data namespace_kernel_authority_amendment_note: String = "THE KERNEL BAR AS FIRST WRITTEN DEADLOCKED ITS OWN SUCCESSOR, and this amendment is the fix (operator ruling, 2026-08-01). The recut landed namespace-binding-kernel with a red_control ending 'no second place in the compiler makes that same decision' and a handback demanding 'evidence that nothing else decides the same question'. That bar cannot be met while the bootstrap seed keeps its own hand-written none/one/many mirror inside the v1 adapter, and that mirror cannot be deleted until generic emission carries the canonical carrier with its required bounds. But namespace-reference-derived-closure DEPENDS on the kernel. So on the day the recut merged, the next step was already unstartable for a reason that had nothing to do with what the next step needs: deriving candidate populations does not require the seed mirror to be gone, it requires the canonical decision to EXIST and be callable.\n\nTHE CUT IS AUTHORITY VERSUS RETIREMENT. Owning the canonical decision and removing every rival implementation of it are separate achievements with separate evidence, and fusing them made an acceptance bar that no amount of correct kernel work could satisfy. The kernel now owns being the one canonical authority; namespace-legacy-choice-retirement owns deleting the older mechanisms, and the seed mirror is named there as one of its rows. A new node was deliberately NOT minted: that node already reads 'delete every other way of deciding what a name means' and already inventories every remaining place that decides, so the mirror is a row it should always have carried, and minting a sibling would have been a second home for one concept.\n\nTHE ADAPTER IS NOT THEREBY BLESSED. It remains a declared scaffold with its dissolution trigger on its own carrier, counted and visible; moving WHERE its retirement is tracked does not lower what is owed. What changes is only that a temporary bootstrap realization no longer gates work that does not depend on it.\n\nTWO ACCEPTANCE SENTENCES WERE ALSO WRONG AND ARE CORRECTED HERE. The red_control said 'a malformed name refuses', but this boundary accepts occurrence identities and derives no name spelling at all, so it named a check no implementation executes — it now reads malformed occurrence TRANSPORT. And the bar now states the two refusals that distinguish a malformed supplied population from a real verdict: a candidate handed in the wrong role refuses distinctly from one that is absent, and the same declaration supplied twice refuses as malformed rather than counting as two. Only two DISTINCT declaration identities are ambiguity. Collapsing either of those into an ordinary verdict would let a defective candidate producer read as a legitimate naming answer, which is the state-space conflation this whole lane exists to remove."

// THE BROAD NAMESPACE NODE WAS TOO COARSE TO CLOSE HONESTLY, and the recut is the fix (operator
// ruling, 2026-07-31). namespace-canonical-binding previously combined two separable things in one
// boundary: working out which declarations a name can see, and calling one decision function on
// them. A check proving only the none/one/many decision could therefore have marked the whole node
// accepted while candidate derivation, reference-derived dependency closure, and the production
// changeover all remained unbuilt — an acceptance hazard, and the exact shape of rung inflation
// gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder forbids, where a carrier named for the top rung occupies the bottom one.\n\nThree
// prerequisites now stand in front of it. namespace-binding-kernel owns the decision alone, on a
// candidate population SUPPLIED to it. namespace-reference-derived-closure owns structural
// exposure, authored order, the candidate index, exact reference-to-declaration binding, and the
// derived dependency edges. namespace-ambiguity-discharge settles the genuinely-many cases from
// real compilation. namespace-canonical-binding KEEPS ITS DURABLE IDENTITY and is now the final
// production changeover only, so historical links resolve and no identity is reused.\n\nWhy the
// split falls exactly there: dependency edges are a PROJECTION OF THE BINDING, not a second
// authored statement. A program that instead authored the missing edges by hand reached 400 of 771
// files at roughly one import per CI floor before it was stopped; the unresolved population was
// evidence that binding and module discovery are coupled at the wrong boundary, not a backlog to
// grind down.\n\nTHE CHANGEOVER AND ITS SUCCESSOR ARE DISJOINT, and an earlier revision of this
// recut broke that (review 45649). It retitled namespace-canonical-binding as 'switch the whole
// compiler over' with a boundary reading 'every place that resolves a name', which swallowed
// namespace-bound-only-consumers underneath it — that node's own boundary is type checking, call
// lookup, and argument-count checks reading the decided answer. Overlapping boundaries are the gunbc.design_argument::minimize_redundancy
// redundancy this document exists to remove, and they are worse on a roadmap than in code:
// completing the parent would already entail most of the child, so either the child can never be
// honestly accepted or the parent was silently read narrower than it was written. The cut is
// PRODUCER versus READER. The changeover node owns the sites that WORK OUT what a name refers to,
// and the deletion of the search-everything fallback behind them. Its successor owns the READERS of
// that answer and their obligation to stop on unresolved or ambiguous. Neither entails the other,
// and each can be accepted on its own evidence.\n\nONE EDGE WAS DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED.
// pderive-source-slot-binding still depends on namespace-canonical-binding, which now means it
// waits for the whole production changeover. It plausibly needs only occurrence transport plus the
// binding kernel, but that is unproven: the dependency moves only once the focused P-derive
// consumer demonstrates it can operate on an exact supplied candidate population. Loosening it on
// the strength of the argument alone would be asserting a fact nobody has measured.

// THE RULE THAT ORDERS THE COMPUTE LANE, and it is a sequencing ruling rather than a design
// preference (operator, 2026-08-07): do not move the present arrangement onto our own machines.
// Move exact computations onto one shared fabric, and DELETE THE DUPLICATED WORK BEFORE increasing
// the number of things asking for it. Handing agents a build capability without deduplication and
// admission would not be a fabric — it would be a tidier way for ten callers to launch ten cold
// builds of one tree, which is the failure the lane exists to prevent. That is why
// compute-deduplication-and-admission stands in front of ci-owned-execution in the graph rather
// than beside it: owning CI adds a consumer, and a consumer added before the duplication is removed
// multiplies the load instead of sharing it.
//
// THE SECOND HALF OF THE SAME RULE APPLIES TO NATIVE EXECUTION. Emitting a native witness bundle
// and running it is the right destination, and the miniature is decisive at the scale it measures —
// direct native calls in single-digit milliseconds against tens interpreted and hundreds through
// warm cargo transport. But the cited production enrolment delivered zero of three native and three
// of three fallback, so the required path took no benefit from it, and native bodies surrounded by
// duplicated preparation would still be bad CI. Native realization and shared preparation are ONE
// programme, not two lanes competing for the same slot; native-selected-witness-bundle owns the
// first, and the discovery snapshot, scoped substrate, early selection and streaming rows own the
// second.
//
// WHY THE MECHANISM ROWS ARE A CHAIN AND NOT A SET. The measured floor is dominated by preparation
// rather than by the work being prepared for: on the clearest full-floor subject, the discovery
// batch spent the large majority of its wall on setup and resolve and a small minority actually
// evaluating witnesses, and the two workers walked the same roots twice. Each row therefore removes
// a DIFFERENT duplicate — the second walk, the second initialised world, preparation that precedes
// selection, and the barrier between preparing and executing — and each is only measurable once the
// one before it has landed. Chaining them with dependency edges is what keeps at most the next one
// startable, so the standing limit on concurrent performance mechanisms falls out of the graph
// rather than being restated as prose that nothing enforces. Width two is deliberately absent from
// that chain and stays parked: the tested implementation shared typed bytes while each worker still
// built its own world, and the architectural prerequisite is that no second private semantic world
// exists.

// THE PERMANENT PRODUCT INTERFACE IS TWO OPERATIONS (operator convergence mandate 2026-08-09):
// gunbc build <program> and gunbc test <program>. DEVBOOT, CI2, CONFIDENCE, CONVERGE,
// materialization and lenses are implementation responsibilities behind those operations, never
// separate user workflows — the caller never chooses runner, cache, affected-set algorithm,
// interpreter, bundle partition, realization provider, lease, ref, store, or host. #8049 owns gunbc
// build (the caller sees Built with program subject, artifact and receipt, or a typed refusal —
// never leases or refs); #8043 owns the reusable v2 test-plan execution behind gunbc test;
// V2-LENS-0 and dirty-worktree verification consume both. An incomplete affected-set answer selects
// the COMPLETE v2 test plan — never zero tests, never the interpreter. CI converges toward gunbc
// test with an exact tested-merge-tree subject: local-versus-CI becomes subject and policy, not
// separate architecture. Cross-process edge-index materialization is SUPPORTING WORK inside
// LENS-0/DEVBOOT, not a sixth program; before it builds, the remaining gates hold: attribute the
// un-decomposed resolve residue to its own seam, reproduce the cold misses in a fresh process,
// compare miss keys across at least two corpus subjects, prove no other in-process consumer
// reconstructs the value — then add a request family to the EXISTING materialization provider,
// never a parallel cache, and only after content-derived SourceFile identity lands (a deserialized
// index and a freshly built one must agree by construction). Artifact reuse identity stays pure and
// process-independent (content, environment, phase, policy, algorithm); producer and consumer
// process coordinates — invocation, host identity, boot identity, pid, process start identity,
// executable digest — live in production and consumption receipts and leases, extending DEVBOOT's
// existing lease and attempt vocabulary, never the artifact key.

// Every node below is ExecutionContractUnspecified: the declared, fail-closed migration frontier
// for gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_execution_contract. A node states the exact validation operations that close it
// before the actuator will spawn for it, so dispatch refuses with a typed environment-admission
// diagnostic rather than guessing validations or dependencies. The prior binding lived on a
// pre-refresh operator-TODO node deleted by the 2026-07-27 authority refresh; re-binding is
// per-node roadmap authoring, never a merge-time default.

// THE FIRST BOUND NODE, and it is bound to an ALREADY-GREEN validation on purpose. Until this row
// existed every node was ExecutionContractUnspecified, so dispatch_environment_admit refused on all
// of them and no part of the workflow below Env had ever executed end to end. A first binding
// therefore has two jobs that pull in opposite directions: prove the Verify path runs at all, and
// prove it discriminates. Those want different nodes, and conflating them is how a green pipeline
// gets mistaken for a working one. This row takes the FIRST job only — the validation it names
// passes today, so an Agent turn that changes nothing still produces a real admitted environment, a
// real derived command, and a real validation receipt. What that proves is the PLUMBING: capability
// admission, argv derivation, and receipt production, independent of whether the provider
// accomplished anything. It deliberately proves NOTHING about discrimination, and must not be read
// as evidence that Verify can fail — the discriminating red belongs on a second node whose
// validation is currently red and goes green when the work lands, and that node is the next
// binding, not this one.
//
// The operation is the transport-clean corpus witness because it is what this ticket's own red
// control describes: 'a new unclassified production construction site reds the census'. It reads
// the live tree (SubstrateInputsOnly), so it is a statement about the repository rather than a
// fixture — a raw shell literal reappearing in that transport module reds it for real.

// THE BINDING NOW DISCRIMINATES. An earlier contract named
// corpus_dag_compile_clean_transport_clean_holds -- an ALREADY-GREEN validation -- so Verify proved
// only that the path RUNS: admission, argv derivation, receipt production. A verifier that returned
// green unconditionally was indistinguishable from a working one, because nothing it ran could
// return anything else.
//
// This contract names a validation that WAS red until the node's work landed: the specimen's setup
// was then usb_gadget_setup_script (deleted by the change that described the transport), which
// prefixed "set -e" and joined rendered shell lines, so the witness asserting no shell control word
// was red, and the red was this node's own acceptance condition rather than a planted fixture: the
// node asks for a described operation instead of written shell text, and the witness asserts exactly
// that no shell text is produced. The transition red -> green WAS the work being finished, and it
// completed on 2026-09-29 -- the witness stays as the permanent regression control, so the red it
// would go now is exactly the regression it guards against.
//
// WHILE THE TEST WAS RED, the witness was enrolled in floor_expected_red, NOT
// QuarantineProbeExpectRed, and the difference was executional rather than stylistic. The sibling
// note above recommends the quarantine cadence,
// and that recommendation is STALE: std.witness_admission records that falsifier.yml -- the
// workflow scheduling QuarantineProbeExpectRed -- was deleted at 611fd02770 (#8283), so every row
// classified into that cadence "has read as covered ever since despite executing nowhere".
// Enrolling here would have put a deliberately-red acceptance test somewhere it never runs, which
// is the failure that note itself documents. The floor executes. When the test greened, the
// floor_expected_red row left by the roster's own removal path -- the counted un-quarantine, not a
// silent pass -- which is why nothing points there now.
fn shell_typed_invocation_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/shell/shell_typed_invocation_witness.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "usb_gadget_setup_emits_no_shell_control_word" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// The node closes only on the nullary wet claim that reads the runner's GITHUB_SHA independently
// through shell.Env.Get, observes checkout HEAD through the existing Git path, and admits only
// their exact match. Binding the contract to the pure fold would permit constructed constants to
// stand in for liveness; binding it to the older population-only witness would prove only that Git
// returned paths, not that the paths belonged to the workflow subject.

fn dogfood_route_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_dogfood_route.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "dogfood_route_acceptance_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

fn v1_rust_source_observation_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/stage0_rust_host_observation_live_witness.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "live_rust_observation_matches_actions_subject" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

data namespace_structural_observations_execution_contract_note: String = "BOUND (this change). The retracted interim below is answered rather than merely quoted: the closing validation now consumes admissions PRODUCED BY AN ORDINARY COMPILE OF ONE FILE and reaches its verdict through assess_reference_binding_observation, never through variant counting. Four StructuralBindingProductionRefused observations green nothing -- a production refusal assesses to ReferenceDerivedClosureRefused, which the set difference keeps in the frontier.\n\nWHAT THE BINDING ADDS BEYOND THE FOUR CAPABILITIES, and it is the half the retraction named as missing: SUBJECT PROVENANCE. Every admission carries the module path the parse itself declared, and the check refuses unless all of them name the one declared subject. Four admissions from four hand-built sources satisfy the capabilities and fail this check, which is exactly the difference between the row as written and the fixture suite that preceded it.\n\nWHAT THE VALIDATION EXECUTES: gunbc.namespace_cut.namespace_structural_observations_production reaches the v1 parser walk through one hermetic host bridge (declared and enrolled seed growth, gunbc.namespace_cut.namespace_structural_observation_bridge_seed_growth), so the witness declares SubstrateInputsOnly truthfully, runs in the required floor, and is not a member of the DeclinedLiveTree arm. Its four red controls are single-edit mutants of the one subject, each refusing exactly the capability whose rule the edit broke.\n\nRETRACTED INTERIM (2026-08-04, operator ruling via loyal-ram-550), kept because it is what this binding had to satisfy: the prior ordinary_compile_structural_closing_contract_holds predicate checked only scenario-variant presence and could green four StructuralBindingProductionRefused observations -- worse than no binding. STALE CITATION CORRECTED (2026-08-18, dead-witness-tree triage): the fixture it cited had no executing consumer since v1_claim_scoped_witness_batch was deleted 2026-08-15 and did not survive the triage; receipt at gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots v1_dead_witness_tree_triage_receipt."

fn namespace_structural_observations_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/namespace_structural_observations_acceptance.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "namespace_structural_observations_closing_contract_holds_on_one_ordinary_compiled_file" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE SIX-ARM CLOSING DISCRIMINATOR for namespace-reference-derived-closure. The validation is
// deliberately RED while its production admission seam carries a typed unavailable row for every
// clause: the closed capability population is the node's own red control, and missing capabilities
// are a derived set difference, so duplicate evidence cannot hide an unexecuted clause and zero
// work cannot verify as complete. Clauses (a-d) wait on #7515's structural candidate producer, (e)
// waits on its reference-derived dependency projection, and (f) waits on the projection's
// pool-membership-independence wall. The paired fixture suite executes the merged P1 kernel for the
// first four clauses and proves every clause rejects its planted wrong output, but the bound
// acceptance witness imports none of those fixtures; it can green only when the gated node supplies
// production observations. It is enrolled QuarantineProbeExpectRed until that transition.

fn namespace_reference_derived_closure_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/namespace_reference_derived_closure_acceptance.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "witness_namespace_reference_derived_closure_closing_contract_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE CLOSING CHECK IS STRUCTURAL, NOT A POPULATION PIN, and that choice is the whole content of
// this binding. The node asks whether the interpreter's dispatch surface is ENUMERABLE and whether
// its roster can silently disagree with the dispatch; it does not ask how large the surface
// currently is. So the bound validation asserts properties that survive the roster legitimately
// growing -- named dispatch sites contribute derived rows, duplicate row keys refuse, shadows are
// exactly the known set BY NAME, every declared row carries its own dissolution trigger, an arm
// carrying no semantic primitive identity stays representable, and an unrecognised form label
// refuses rather than defaulting.
//
// Binding it to counts would have re-created at the acceptance layer the exact defect #7615 removed
// from the witness layer: the five deleted witnesses pinned live-population numbers copied from the
// tree, which gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed rules is not an oracle, and they duly behaved as pure change detectors
// that redded main twice. A closing check that reds on legitimate growth is worse than one that
// does not exist, because it trains everyone to edit the number rather than read the change.
//
// The validation can genuinely fail: removing a dispatch site, dropping a declared row's trigger,
// admitting an unknown form label, or letting a second arm identity shadow a spelling each red it.
// The detectors' own discriminating REDs and positive controls live in
// test.claim.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface_witness and execute beside it.

fn v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_acceptance.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_acceptance_contract_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE CLOSING CHECK FOR v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority. R1 inverts the roster:
// gunbc.v1.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface v1_interpreter_authored_roster_arms is the canonical
// authority as authored InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm rows; v1_interpreter_dispatch_emit derives
// Rust enum variant names from arm identity and generates lookup tables. Compile-time
// exhaustiveness is site-scoped: single-family dispatch sites get a non-wildcard enum match;
// eval_call_bridge and eval_call_native_intercept share one enum per site but expand per-family
// subsets with a required wildcard (missing handler body is runtime unreachable!, not compile error
// — per-family enum split is follow-up). Structural properties that survive roster growth are
// asserted here; R0 discriminating controls remain in
// v1_interpreter_primitive_surface_witness_test.

fn service_evidence_capture_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_service_evidence.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "service_evidence_capture_acceptance_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

fn v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_acceptance.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_acceptance_contract_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE SCM P1 CLOSING DISCRIMINATOR, authored only after the first P1 carrier made the node's whole
// completion condition executable. The validation is deliberately RED: its closed capability
// population is the roadmap node's own bar, and this first slice supplies only the bounded
// candidate-generation model check. Missing behavior is derived set difference, never a
// hand-maintained progress count; duplicate passing rows cannot erase it, and a false row remains
// missing. The contract therefore cannot green on zero progress and cannot confuse a modeled
// carrier with an executed proof kernel. It is enrolled QuarantineProbeExpectRed in
// gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots. Each later P1 slice adds an executing scenario check without weakening the
// aggregate. When the final capability greens, that same change removes the expect-red enrollment
// and promotes the witness to ordinary discovery ratchet.

// The per-node execution binding, shaped as a COMBINATOR rather than a parameter on every
// constructor (the `sign` twin below is the precedent, and it already carries `execution:
// rn.execution` through untouched). Threading an execution argument through
// active/active_small/active_large/authored/derivable/ticket_row would edit seven constructors and
// every one of their ~46 call sites to express a fact that today holds for exactly one node — the
// churn a combinator avoids, and the reason `sign` is a combinator too. A node without this wrapper
// keeps ExecutionContractUnspecified, which is the fail-closed refusal
// roadmap_execution_contract_frontier_note declares, not a default anyone chose.

// A BINDING NAMES THE VALIDATION THAT CLOSES A NODE, so it can only be authored once that
// validation exists. A node without one stays ExecutionContractUnspecified, which is the honest
// fail-closed state rather than a gap: dispatch refuses with a typed diagnostic instead of
// admitting an environment for work whose completion nothing can check. Fabricating contracts to
// make a lane look dispatchable produces exactly the coverage-by-illusion tier — every node
// clickable, every Verify vacuous. The closing validation is written as part of the node's first
// slice; the contract follows the witness, never precedes it.
//
// THE ROSTER IS NOT TRANSCRIBED HERE. This row previously carried a hand survey — 'two of six
// startable roots are bindable' plus the four names and why each lacked a validation — and it
// rotted exactly as a hand-maintained count must: two of the four it named
// (v1-test-hygiene-producer-retirement, pderive-typesafe-nullary-reflection) were accepted while
// the sentence still listed them as unbound, and the leading count was edited twice by unrelated
// changes. startable_nodes_missing_closing_contract() computes the same set from the nodes
// themselves, so read it there and delete nothing by hand. What stays here is the RULE, which does
// not change when the roster does.
//
// v1-test-migration records both sides of that rule: its false-green deletion-guard contract was
// removed, then a behavior-grain validation that can fail on zero progress was authored and bound.
// See v1_test_migration_binding_history_note for that history and v1_test_migration_contract_note
// for the current completion authority.

fn v2_emitter_producer_provenance_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/self_host_emitter_producer_provenance_witness.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "witness_restored_binding_without_executed_receipt_does_not_authorize_reds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// The validation is this node's red control stated almost verbatim. The ticket demands that 'a
// result recorded as made by the new generator, with no receipt from a run that actually produced
// it, has to be impossible to write', and
// witness_restored_binding_without_executed_receipt_does_not_authorize_reds asserts exactly that: a
// restored binding without an executed receipt does not authorize an emitter-produced claim. It is
// chosen over the suite's other twenty-six claims because it is the one that fails if the
// unrepresentability itself lapses, rather than one that checks a roster stayed in step.

// THE CANONICAL CLOSING VALIDATION for v2-emitter-direct-rust-door, bound to
// direct_rust_door_production_group_closing_expectation_holds — GREEN BY EXECUTION since
// 2026-09-06, when the known-red admission row deleted per its own dissolution ("every leaf
// reaches LeafEstablished by execution"), promoting the unchanged group root to the lane's
// permanent regression wall. The production walk is ingest → assemble → infer → emission on the
// real add_probe source and reaches ArtifactProduced: inference derives grounding for the whole
// specimen (declared-inhabitants roster membership, binding denotation, Conj/Arrow product
// introduction, canonical-operations and grammar-productions roster membership, and
// binding-reference derivation from the enclosing arrow's domain), and emission is the
// single-produced-declaration module composition (generate_rust_module_emission_candidate over
// v2.compiler.emit_produced), because a resolved module is a module shell over named
// declarations, never a type record to record-project. All five leaves establish: source
// fidelity byte-equal to direct_rust_door_expected_source, producer identity, seed-emitter
// absence, SourceProduced qualification, and the missing-rule refusal. State the walk claim
// exactly: ONE production implementation authority, ONE production walk per group construction,
// ONE scheduled group construction, measured by
// v2.test.claim.schedule_occurrence_multiplicity_test against the live falsifier schedule.
// Group ALGEBRA remains discriminated by planted-observation controls at zero production cost
// (v2.test.claim.self_host.direct_rust_door_group_algebra). The group's observation is in-memory; the
// written-to-disk artifact surface is mint_written_provenanced_rust_artifact, which rides the
// same module composition.

fn v2_emitter_direct_rust_door_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/long/direct_rust_door_production_group.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "direct_rust_door_production_group_closing_expectation_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

fn v1_seed_honesty_decision_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/seed_honesty_discharge_unavailable.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "v1_seed_honesty_decision_closing_contract_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// The validation names v1-seed-honesty-decision and executes the node's whole handback. Feeding one
// artifact identity as both claim and check refuses with bootstrap_self_verify_same_artifact;
// feeding separately identified artifacts with planted divergent content refuses with
// bootstrap_self_verify_diverged; mismatched source/compiler/hash-pin provenance refuses with
// bootstrap_self_verify_provenance_mismatch; separately identified artifacts with equal content and
// equal provenance admit, proving the refusals are discriminating rather than unconditional. The
// final conjunct requires seed_honesty_decision to carry one of the two operator verdicts whose
// rationale is NonEmptyStr by construction. That conjunct was SeedHonestyUndecided until
// 2026-08-02, so the closing validation was deliberately red and enrolled QuarantineProbeExpectRed
// and could not report done over the missing half; the operator verdict FixedPointTrustSufficient
// greened it and the enrollment was deleted in the same change (see
// v1_seed_honesty_decision_acceptance_note). The undecided pole did NOT retire with the quarantine:
// the conjunction is now a function of the decision, so
// seed_honesty_undecided_would_keep_closing_contract_red still executes it against
// SeedHonestyUndecided and reds if that arm is ever weakened. PRODUCTION-WIRING TRIGGER, STILL OPEN
// AND NOT DISCHARGED BY THE VERDICT: the realized-comparison and regen paths do not yet route their
// artifact identities through seed_self_verify_check. This contract proves the decision procedure
// and gates completion, but it is not yet the live trust-path authority. The verdict took the
// second branch of the choice this sentence set out -- fixed-point trust ruled sufficient -- and
// the rationale therefore disposes of the unwired path explicitly rather than implying it is
// protected, alongside the two other residuals it accepts (a fixed point does not defeat a
// self-reproducing defect; rollback is not fix-forward). Routing the realized artifacts through
// this check belongs to the generation-admission program, which is unbuilt. The full independent
// rebuild remains out of scope here.

// v1-test-migration WAS DELIBERATELY UNBOUND after its former binding to
// test_migration_delete_guard_holds was removed: that binding produced a false green, as reading
// what the guard actually computes showed.
//
// The guard is DIFF-SCOPED. cli_run.rs test_migration_delete_guard_uncovered_deletes_inner resolves
// a (base, head) pair, returns an empty violation list when base_rev == head_rev, returns an empty
// list again when neither rev resolves and GUNBC_CI_DIFF_BASE is unset, and otherwise inspects only
// the v1 test paths DELETED between those revs. Violations are empty whenever a change deletes no
// uncovered legacy test file, so the guard answers true. Measured on the tree that carried it: the
// guard passes today while test_migration_debt_live_module_count() is 81, so a dispatched agent
// could do no migration work at all and Verify would still go green. A validation that cannot fail
// on zero progress cannot close a node (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed — a wrong answer must be loud, and 'done' asserted
// over undone work is exactly the silent wrong answer).
//
// The guard was KEPT at the time this note was written, as a per-change deletion wall. IT IS NOW
// DELETED (2026-08-12, V1-CONSUMER-DRAIN-1): test_migration_delete_guard_holds,
// test_migration_delete_guard_uncovered_deletes and the whole guard body are gone from cli_run.rs,
// from the primitive registry, from the interpreter dispatch surface and from the v1 type env. The
// reason is not that the analysis above was wrong — it was right, and it is why the node was
// unbound — but that the guard's SUBJECT stopped existing: it authorized deletions by checking a
// stem against _retired.dag / _retained.dag carriers, and gunbc#8146 deleted every such carrier
// when the authority inverted from classifying departures to declaring residents. A per-change wall
// over an empty authorize-set refuses nothing. The deletion wall it provided is SUPERSEDED, not
// dropped: an undeclared or stale module now reds through the identity join in
// v2.lens.test_migration_debt retained_rust_kernel_wall_holds, which does not depend on anyone
// remembering to classify a departure. The paragraphs above are retained as the reasoning that
// unbound the node, not as a description of live code.
//
// The node's own bar — 'the per-file coverage mapping with nothing unmatched' — required a closing
// validation at the grain of legacy test BEHAVIOR, not modules: an admitted typed disposition for
// every discovered legacy test function, with unclassified as the derived set difference reaching
// zero. The module count is a trend metric that overstates debt by construction, because
// classification is exact-stem filename matching (chosen fail-closed after fuzzy matching wrongly
// reported an unrelated witness as covering `pipeline`), so a real witness under a different name
// still reads as debt. That missing graph once made the node honestly ClosingContractMissing in
// startable_nodes_missing_closing_contract. It now exists and the node is bound to it by
// v1_test_migration_execution_contract; v1_test_migration_contract_note records why that
// validation, rather than the deletion guard, is the completion authority.

fn v1_test_migration_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/manual_test_migration_debt.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "retained_rust_kernel_wall_holds_against_live_tree" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE CLOSING CHECK FOR roadmap-receipt-continuity. Acceptance history is the ROADMAP EVENT LOG:
// one chain per node, appended only through gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_issue_command, and
// roadmap_acceptance_receipts is a replay projection of those recorded/revoked events only. The
// authored JSONL carrier and its seal count/digest are deleted with it, and so is the merge-base
// prior_history read (git.Core.Show over the carrier file): there is no prior revision of a mutable
// log to address — a chain's parent is an event id in the same log, and the reader REFUSES rather
// than answer with an empty history (PriorHistoryRevisionEvaluationRequired dissolved with the
// carrier it guarded). The bound contract is the inhabitance leaf
// witness_deleted_history_event_refuses (a removed record with no withdrawal refuses). The other
// operator reds named in red_control — prefix law on non-empty observed prior, empty-prior bypass
// discriminant, digest-omitted field mutation, wrong prior digest, revocation while live, duplicate
// revocations, exact revocation admit, criteria rewrite, and the typed
// load/projection refusal chain — are separate test fns in the same entry, discovered by the floor,
// not re-executed by this contract. The live git-observed integrity witness
// (test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_receipt_continuity_live_witness) goes with the authority-level
// integrity wrappers it called: they read the PRIOR acceptance history out of the deleted
// observation carrier, revision-addressed through git. The event log has no such prior — a
// chain's parent is an event id in the same log — so the honest replacement is the log's own fold
// law plus roadmap_acceptance_migration_verify, not a live git witness of a carrier that is gone.

// SHELL→DAG MIGRATION BATCH 1 execution contracts. The ten shell-dag-* nodes were authored
// without contracts, so launch admission refused them execution_contract_missing; these ten rows
// bind each one at authoring time. Each names a worker-authored witness file that does NOT exist
// yet — the dispatched worker authors it under its node's M0. Verification runs only after the
// worker commits, when the file exists; until then an unauthored witness fails verification as
// oracle-missing, which is the truthful outcome for work not yet done.

// REAL BINDING RESTORED 2026-09-20: the seeded red acceptance witness for this node has landed
// (dag/test/claim/shell/shell_dag_cron_entry_line_builder_witness.dag, enrolled red in
