      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Derive each file's dependencies from what its names resolve to",
          boundary: "For every reference, record which declaration answered it. Derive each file's dependency set from those answers alone, identical whichever unrelated files are loaded. This absorbs cross-file provenance (clause e) and pool independence (clause f).",
          displaced_cost: "Hand-written dependency statements can disagree with what files actually reference, and hundreds were patched by hand to keep them in step.",
          first_slice: "Replace one typed-unavailable row in the six-arm witness's admission seam with a production observation from the ordinary compile route (producer #11461/#12186/#12048), starting with clause (e).",
          red_control: "The six-arm witness (dag/test/claim/namespace_reference_derived_closure_acceptance.dag) stays red until all six clauses come from production observations. A pool perturbation that changes an answer while the file set stays the same is caught.",
          out_of_scope: "Bounding the producer's memory; ambiguity discharge; any wave.",
          handback: "The witness green on production and its expect-red enrolment retired."
        ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: witness is expected-red on production seams; next step is an XL-4 producer, not a bounded fix."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. Reuse v2.lens.module_graph::reference_derived_resolution_facts and the six-clause production witness. The producer already exists; remaining work is replacing unavailable admission observations and proving the qualified-only route, not implementing a second closure walker. Generated-provider demand and occurrence loss remain distinct questions.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: namespace_reference_derived_closure_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "Dependencies derived from resolved references are what make a file's closure independent of which unrelated files are loaded."),
      centering: plan(text: "One module only, in the native-seven closure: derive its dependency set from the declarations its qualified references resolve to, compare it to the set its import list produced, and hand back the two sets and their difference with a reason per differing module. The six-arm acceptance witness stays red; this slice establishes one arm (pool independence) on one real module."),
    ),
