      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Settle the names that genuinely could mean two things",
        boundary: "Using the real answers from the step before — not a count taken by searching text — go through every name that genuinely has more than one candidate and either refuse it on purpose or say which one is meant, by renaming or by writing it out in full.",
        displaced_cost: "Counting these by searching for text gives a number that is wrong in both directions, so it cannot tell anyone how much work is left or whether it is finished.",
        first_slice: "Produce the real list from actual compilation, then settle the first genuine group.",
        red_control: "Every genuinely ambiguous name is either deliberately refusing or explicitly spelled out, and no rule is added that quietly prefers one candidate over another.",
        out_of_scope: "No preference rule, no nearest-match, and no sizing the work from a text search.",
        handback: "The real list, the settled groups, and proof that no tie-breaking rule was introduced."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: needs XL-4 production first."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. Under the chosen fully qualified rule there is no independent global ambiguity-cleanup campaign. Keep only the retirement receipt; duplicate declarations belong to ingest refusal and lexical shadowing belongs to resolver controls.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
