    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_HPYW6X0NEMYVNAKZJFA6TQPK0Q",
      id: "namespace-legacy-choice-retirement",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/names_without_imports.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Delete every other way of deciding what a name means",
        boundary: "Once all ordinary consumers use the one rule, remove the older mechanisms: name-string matching, walking up the parent chain, the global pool of bare names, the import retry, and the hand-written seed mirror that counts none/one/many for itself inside the bootstrap compiler. Owning that last one HERE, rather than in the node that defines the canonical decision, is deliberate — see namespace_kernel_authority_amendment_note.",
        displaced_cost: "Leaving them in place means one name can still get different answers from different code paths.",
        first_slice: "Inventory every remaining place that decides what a name refers to, and remove one complete family.",
        red_control: "The inventory refuses anything it cannot classify and must reach zero before this closes; the seed mirror is one of its rows and is not closed by anything upstream of it.",
        out_of_scope: "Code that merely stores where things are written, without choosing meanings, stays.",
        handback: "The zero-remaining inventory plus proof the compiler still behaves the same."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: after seed retirement per interlock."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The resolver still contains ambient and global-bare branches. Deletion is contingent on the qualified resolver and migrated callers, with physical seed mirror deletion owned by v1-interpreter-delete. Avoid charging the same fallback removal here and in names-bind-to-the-unique-declaration; this node owns the final absence check and remaining legacy mechanisms.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "Every rival way of deciding a name is deleted in one motion."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_F7X5W11359B0PQ90BYD7V73VJA",
      id: "names-bind-to-the-unique-declaration",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/resolve.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Layer 0: every declaration reference is fully qualified, a bare name is a lexical binder or unbound, the ambient tables are deleted, and the closure is read from the references",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.names_without_imports, layer 0 (section 3), under gunbc.design_ruling::declaration_references_are_fully_qualified and gunbc.design_ruling::source_is_ingested_into_one_universe_and_files_are_discarded (2026-11-17). In v2.compiler.resolve a declaration reference is admitted only through the qualified door (try_resolve_qualified_name_node, qualified_head_scope_binding), binding by the path's one declaration and refusing, located and typed, when the path has no declaration or two providers; a bare head is answered by a lexical binder (parameter, let, match or lambda binder, type parameter) or refuses as unbound; the four AmbientBindingTable arms and their census are deleted, and no occurrence resolution is BoundAmbient afterwards. A subject's closure is the declaration-demand fixed point: the authored qualified references seed it and the compiler's generated demands (std.generated_provider: conversion routes, list and map heads, template heads, canonical operations, target support) extend it (namespace-reference-derived-closure); the ingest step realizes it by reading, and the seed's entry closure is read from the same demands in place of its import closure (declared_import_closure), which is the one seed change this layer owns.",
          displaced_cost: "Measured 2026-11-16 (gunbc.plans.names_without_imports section 7): 110 bare sites in the native-seven closure, 304 in the gate closures and 4,974 across production bind today only through a stopgap table or not at all, and 42,011 qualified references already exist beside them; the program review of 2026-11-17 found that binding bare names by repository-wide spelling uniqueness would be an ambient namespace, which the 2026-10-15 ruling forbids. One spelling for every declaration reference removes the question and every table with it.",
          first_slice: "The seed loads by qualified references: one native-seven module with its import lines deleted and its references spelled by path, loaded and typechecked by the seed and by v2 through the qualified door; its RED the same module with one reference left bare, refusing as unbound in both.",
          red_control: "A bare head no lexical binder answers refuses as unbound, never falls to a table; a qualified reference to an absent path refuses naming the path; two providers for one path refuse naming both, and neither wins by load order; after the tables are deleted no occurrence resolution reads BoundAmbient and the census fold has no rows; a subject's demand closure equals the closure its former import list produced for every module in the native-seven closure, generated demands included, or the difference is listed by declaration with its cause.",
          out_of_scope: "Declaring homes for names that have none (layer 1 and after); deleting the import grammar corpus-wide (import-grammar-and-lines-deleted); any shorter spelling or sugar.",
          handback: "The qualified-only resolver with its discriminating claims, the four table arms deleted, the seed loading one module by its references, and the bare-name reading over the native-seven closure showing no site bound through a table."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. v2.compiler.resolve already carries occurrence resolutions and a qualified-path route. AmbientKernelTypeSpelling, AmbientKernelCanonicalSymbol and AmbientPrimitiveAuthority still have live branches. Residual is eliminating those fallback authorities and establishing the seed reference-only loader, not creating qualified lookup from scratch. The same binding comparison serves names-homing; do not charge it once per spelling.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "Layer 0 of gunbc.plans.names_without_imports: the one rule that replaces the ambient tables and is the semantics import deletion needs."),
      centering: plan(text: "Seed loader slice only, on a fleet host under the memory envelope: run gunbc --dry-run run --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/lexical_scope.dag --function <claim> once per claim, unchanged (29 claims; the Bool is in each run's refusal line), then with the entry's import member lists stripped, then with its import lines deleted and its references spelled by path. Hand back the three verdict sets and nothing else; the ruling on the seed loader is the operator's from those three. Change no production source."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_9PXMHJ474EV2TEQ6MKEG198ZDJ",
      id: "native-seven-names-homed",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/roster_import_sweep.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Layer 1: every name the native-seven closure uses has one declared home, and every declaration reference in the closure is spelled by its path",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.names_without_imports, layer 1 (section 3), and native-seven directly (gunbc.design_ruling::n7_requires_only_its_own_closure). Every non-roster call in the native-seven closure must reach its declared contract. The historical 54-spelling, 161-module reading is an inspection population, not 54 missing declarations: first already maps to std.algebra::list_head, map_get to map_lookup and flat_map to list_flat_map through roster_head_rows. Reuse those contracts and mappings. Only uncovered contracts require semantic-owner work (std.host_text for host-text operations and std.algebra for lists, maps and sets under the existing rulings); only uncovered signature transformations require new policy rows. Classify overloaded spellings by the actual caller contract. Then the generator rewrites every declaration reference in the closure to its fully qualified path, with the current import semantics as its oracle, and the import lines leave those modules in the same landing (gunbc.design_ruling::declaration_references_are_fully_qualified). No import is added anywhere.",
          displaced_cost: "Native-seven stops at the first unbound name per module, and 1,229 bare sites of names with no declaration sit in its closure; the waves so far homed layer 3 names (substring, char_at corpus-wide) while the closure still stops on split and starts_with. The program review of 2026-11-17 found that homing with an import at each site creates work layer 3 deletes; under the qualified rule no such bridge exists.",
          first_slice: "Start at the measured chars_to_string refusal inside std.host_text::text_of_chars: reconcile its existing whole-list realization admission without a recursive rewrite. Use the recorded caller classes and existing roster mappings. Extend the shared generator to qualified references, then validate occurrence bindings including method/pipeline forms and lexical binders. Reconcile text/nonempty-pattern and optional/scalar results at their existing owners; code_point on a Symbol is not a Char path rewrite.",
          red_control: "A name homed without its calling modules' claims green under both compilers is not homed; a home whose signature differs from the builtin's without a policy row is refused in review; a module in the closure that still carries an import line or a bare declaration reference at handback keeps this open; the resolved-reference comparison identifies each target declaration and every explained semantic difference; same-spelling grep alone cannot establish homing.",
          out_of_scope: "Names and modules outside the native-seven closure (compiler-closure-names-homed-and-types-merged, corpus-names-homed-and-collisions-discharged); the resolver and loader rule itself (names-bind-to-the-unique-declaration), which lands first.",
          handback: "Every declaration reference in the native-seven closure resolves to its intended declared contract, every module is import-free, and native-seven's recorded first stop is no longer a name; include binding comparisons and calling-module claim receipts."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. Source inspection of the import closure at this revision reaches 161 modules with no missing import module. This is a source population, not the compiler demand fixed point. roster_head_rows already covers first, list_push, fold, map_get and key-specific sort_by. The shared missing generator behavior is qualified references rather than inserted imports. Text crossings, scalar/optional results and shape-bound collection calls need separate contract work; an empty-delimiter installer call outside this closure is not native-seven work."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Caller classification at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c, source inspection rather than a resolved binding receipt. (1) Existing declarations: qualify decl_ref, empty_map, map_insert, map_contains_key, skip, length, string_contains and list_push after confirming their occurrence binding; declaration existence is not a new implementation. (2) Existing rename contracts: first/list_head, last/list_last, reverse/list_reverse, flat_map/list_flat_map, map_get/map_lookup and list get/list_at_optional; fold also renames init/f to empty/cons, and sort_by selects an existing order-specific row. Pipeline first uses must be included: counting only calls followed by parentheses misses them. (3) Text compatibility: starts_with can reuse std.algebra::is_prefix_of plus declared character equality after the text crossing. split and replace can reuse v2.std.text::string_split and string_replace, but need host/scalar conversion, renamed labels and a nonempty delimiter/needle. The 27 explicit split calls inspected here contain no literal empty delimiter; dynamic prefix and case-mapping inputs still require their nonempty evidence. to_string's observed callers render numeric values; reuse std.integer::int_to_decimal_string and the declared Nat-to-Int crossing, not a new universal formatter. code_point has both text inputs and a Symbol input in v2.std.compilers.target_model::source_atom_char_projection_from_node, so a single Char cast is not a valid batch rewrite. char_at changes to an optional result and Nat position; substring/string_length also cross carriers. from_code_point already has a typed Result contract and its callers handle it; preserve those refusals. (4) Collection semantics: concat/count/map/join rows currently name collection shapes, not ordinary callable equivalents. any/all/filter/enumerate, map key traversal and sorted keys must consume their declared algebra contracts with ordering/short-circuit behavior preserved. std.algebra::map_support_keys cannot be assumed to supply sorted_map_keys order. (5) Existing unresolved authority: gunbc.primitive_egress.dispositions_collection::dispositions_collection_rows identifies absent set templates and unmodeled discriminant reflection; dispositions_text_rows distinguishes the windowed chars_to_string operation from whole-list text_of_chars. Reuse those semantic decisions and owners rather than inventing new same-spelled functions. atom_identity_hash is a content-hash contract, not an arbitrary path alias. (6) Exclusions: callable parameters such as cons, key_eq, predicate and on_no_literal stay lexical; declaration self-calls at host realization seams are not ordinary recursive callers to rewrite. This classifies the source cases for dispatch; the shared generator still owes resolved occurrence coverage, method/pipeline forms and before/after binding equality. Neither the old 54-name count nor this lexical reading is that oracle."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Measured first stop at source 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c on srv1, 2026-11-19: the exact native-seven label selects eight tests, all prepare-refused by unbound chars_to_string in std.host_text::text_of_chars, propagated to tokenize_prepared. This occurrence is the whole-list kernel realization of an already declared text crossing; replacing it with text_of_chars would be self-recursion. First reconcile declaration-identity admission of that realization with gunbc.primitive_egress.dispositions_text::dispositions_text_rows, preserving its linear whole-list contract and discriminating round trips. Do not charge a new crossing declaration or silently equate the arbitrary-window primitive with the whole-list operation. Any additional windowed operation is separate contract work only when its callers are demanded. Then rerun the same native label and follow its next located refusal. Receipt and compiler provenance are recorded on native-seven.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "Layer 1 of gunbc.plans.names_without_imports: the unresolved call contracts and reference rewrites between native-seven and its typed endpoint."),
      centering: plan(text: "First slice: inspect starts_with, first, split, replace, to_string and code_point in the native-seven closure against the declared contracts and roster_head_rows. Credit first's existing list_head declaration and xs rewrite; classify the text calls by actual carrier, labels and empty-input behavior. Hand back the compatible batch, the missing semantic contracts and the uncovered mappings, each with callers and evidence. Extend the existing generator to qualified references once for the batch (it currently inserts imports); no new import and no new declaration just to match a spelling. Rerun gunbc test //v2/test/claim/parse/expression_bodied_fn_decl_parse:all before and after and report changed bindings, affected claims and first stops. The residual closure work and its ordering live in roadmap_decomposition, not a uniform per-name allowance."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_T8N6SCYHTV6MAJQDQW7KVNG5G3",
      id: "compiler-closure-names-homed-and-types-merged",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/roster_import_sweep.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Layer 2: the two compiler closures use only declared names, spelled by their paths; the dual std type declarations are merged on their own evidence",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.names_without_imports, layer 2 (section 3), and SelfHostCorpusEmitsCleanly over the two retained closures (gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_interlock). The 278 modules of v2.compiler.source_root_eval and v2.cli.compile_cli: only the unresolved contract delta after layer 1 is homed; the historical 80-name, 2,316-site population is not an additional 80 implementations, and sort_by's existing key-specific mappings are reused, and the generator rewrites every declaration reference in both closures to its path and removes their import lines (gunbc.design_ruling::declaration_references_are_fully_qualified). SEPARATELY, and not gating this handback: the dag std types redeclared under src/v2/std (String against v2.std.text, Int, UInt8 and PositiveInt against v2.std.integer, FilePath, Unit, SourceSpan, TerminationProof) are merged so that a compiler-side projection constructs or reads the one declaration and never redeclares it (kernel-type layer rule, 2026-10-18); under the qualified rule each duplicate has its own path and is a design debt, not an ambiguity, so the merges are accepted one type at a time on their own claims (the program review of 2026-11-17 asked that operation homing and type-authority merges not be fused).",
          displaced_cost: "The emitter chain (second-generation onward) emits what resolves natively; a closure that still binds through tables or carries import lines cannot be emitted as one program under the ruled grammar.",
          first_slice: "Inspect the two closures' residual contracts after layer 1 by declaration identity and argument type, separating already-mapped names such as sort_by from uncovered key contracts; rewrite the compatible delta in one batch and rerun the self-host instrument before and after.",
          red_control: "A name in either closure with no production declaration keeps this open; a module in either closure that still carries an import line or a bare declaration reference at handback keeps it open; a type merge that changes a declaration's signature without a policy row is refused in review; the ambiguous-import column of the reading is retired under the rule and is not an acceptance input.",
          out_of_scope: "The rest of the production corpus (corpus-names-homed-and-collisions-discharged); emission itself; the type merges' own acceptance, which is per type and not this node's handback.",
          handback: "Both closures resolve every declaration reference to its intended contract, are import-free, and have binding-comparison and affected-claim receipts; the self-host instrument is at its previous or better stop."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. Reuse the native-seven generator and binding oracle. The additional population is the union of source_root_eval and compile_cli demands minus resolved declarations already migrated, not an arithmetic 80 minus 54. Type mergers remain with one-standard-library. No evidence yet supports a concrete number of additional semantic contracts.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "Layer 2 of gunbc.plans.names_without_imports: what the compiler closures need before they emit with one meaning."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_M4EY6JW75D1BTSJ8R9SFHG23NH",
      id: "corpus-names-homed-and-collisions-discharged",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/roster_import_sweep.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Layer 3a: every production module uses only declared names, spelled by their paths, and the corpus is rewritten in one landing",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.names_without_imports, layer 3 (section 3), under gunbc.design_ruling::declaration_references_are_fully_qualified. Across production, tests and fixtures, only unresolved caller contracts after both closure layers require semantic work. The historical 432-spelling, 46,923-site and 5,910-production-module counts describe inspection and verification scope, not additional implementations: credit existing contracts and mappings, and exclude runtime exports with no caller. Extend the policy table only for uncovered transformations; then the generator run once over the corpus, test and fixture modules included, rewriting every declaration reference to its path and removing every import line, with the current import semantics as the oracle: the rewritten tree resolves and typechecks to the same bindings, module by module, or the difference is listed with its reason. Collisions are not a population under the rule: two declarations with one spelling have two paths, and the 1,617 import members the 2026-11-16 reading called ambiguous need no discharge.",
          displaced_cost: "A corpus rewritten in pieces leaves two grammars live for the whole interval and every landing in it paying for both; one generated landing with an oracle is the replacement-migration doctrine applied (gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration).",
          first_slice: "The generator's oracle: for one production subtree, the rewritten modules' bindings equal the pre-rewrite bindings by declaration identity, with one planted divergence refused.",
          red_control: "A production module with a bare head that has no declaration keeps this open; a module whose post-rewrite bindings differ from its pre-rewrite bindings by identity is listed with its reason or the landing refuses; a merge that changes a declaration's signature without a policy row is refused in review; the claim corpus is green under both compilers at the landing head.",
          out_of_scope: "Deleting the import grammar (import-grammar-and-lines-deleted), which follows this landing so that a file with an import line can still be read while the oracle runs.",
          handback: "The shared generator's corpus-wide run receipt, every declaration reference resolved to its intended contract, zero import lines, relocated policy facts with their governed subjects, and the claim corpus green under both compilers at the landing head."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. Corpus expansion reuses both closure migrations. Remaining contract exceptions and policy-subject moves differ: relocating a live_tree_disposition is not implementing a library function. Counts of modules and runtime exports are not independent repair counts. Preserve the existing staged inspection and charge only the residual callers and unresolved governing subjects.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "Layer 3a of gunbc.plans.names_without_imports: the corpus state that makes the import cut one landing."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_SR452WVJTR99AYEWSNT29J5Y6K",
      id: "import-grammar-and-lines-deleted",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/parse.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Layer 3b: the import concept is gone: no import production in either compiler's grammar once the corpus is rewritten",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.names_without_imports, layer 3 (section 3), gunbc.design_ruling::imports_are_deleted_before_v2_is_accepted, gunbc.design_ruling::declaration_references_are_fully_qualified and gunbc.design_ruling::source_is_ingested_into_one_universe_and_files_are_discarded. After corpus-names-homed-and-collisions-discharged has rewritten the tree, the v2 grammar loses its import production and its module-header production: an import line or a module header refuses at parse with a located diagnostic naming the replacement (each declaration spells its own full path), and the seed's parser refuses them the same way (2026-10-15 rule 2: v1 mirrors v2). Loading is already by declaration demands from layer 0, so this node deletes grammar and nothing else.",
          displaced_cost: "Two ways to see a name, an import closure deciding the compiled population by accident, and an import retry are each a second authority the design forbids (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority); every landing until the cut pays for keeping them agreed.",
          first_slice: "The grammar production removed from v2 with a parse-refusal claim over a planted import line, and the same refusal in the seed.",
          red_control: "A .dag file containing an import line or a module header refuses at parse in both compilers after the cut; a tree with neither parses, resolves and typechecks identically before and after the grammar change; the claim corpus is green under both compilers at the landing head.",
          out_of_scope: "Any meaning change at a site (the policy table, per name, before this); the loader (layer 0); any shorter spelling or sugar.",
          handback: "Both grammars without the production, the parse-refusal claims, and native-production-admission consuming this node."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. ImportScoped and import acquisition remain live, and the production parsers still admit imports. This is actual deletion work after compatible callers and the sole resolver, with a refusal in both grammars. Module-header deletion is a separate syntax case in the same batch; native-production-admission consumes the controls, while seed mirror deletion waits for interpreter retirement.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "Layer 3b of gunbc.plans.names_without_imports: the cut that ends the import concept before v2 is accepted."),
    ),

    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_E414RDCS728VRFA9QZ0NX76SYN",
      id: "pderive-typesafe-nullary-reflection",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/v2-self-hosting.md"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Stop the compiler from mixing up one type with another",
        boundary: "When the compiler asks 'what are the possible values of this type?', the answer comes from that actual type. Asking about one type and receiving another should be impossible to express.",
        displaced_cost: "The old mechanism passed a bare name and an unconstrained answer type, so it could hand back the values of a completely different type and nothing would notice.",
        first_slice: "Replace the loose lookup with one that carries the type, and move its first caller across.",
        red_control: "Asking about one type while requesting another either cannot be written down or refuses outright.",
        out_of_scope: "No rules specific to one feature baked into this general mechanism.",
        handback: "Both the working case and the mismatched-type case, actually run."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-emitter-production", contribution: "Type-safe nullary reflection removes one class of emitted-type mixups."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_HVYDDT9844FY806ZKBDV5KVQDR",
