    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_KSJNTEDB15YG37HBQXP8P62XJ8",
      id: "v2-emitter-producer-provenance",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/self_host/emitter_producer_provenance.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Record which generator actually produced each result",
        boundary: "Every result says which generator made it and how far it got, as two separate facts. Claiming the new generator made something, without the evidence that it did, has to be impossible to write down.",
        displaced_cost: "Right now everything is made by the old generator, and the count we track reads as if the new one made it. We are measuring the wrong thing, so we cannot tell how far along we are.",
        first_slice: "Relabel the existing rows as made by the old generator, and replace the single count with separate counts per generator in the same change.",
        red_control: "Where a file sits is not evidence of what made it: a result recorded as made by the new generator, with no receipt from a run that actually produced it, has to be impossible to write down rather than caught afterwards. Every row in the frontier roster is recorded as made by the old generator, because that is what made them — stated without a count on purpose, since the roster grows and a transcribed number goes stale (it read 'six' while the live roster held twenty-seven). Taking the old generator away proves nothing at this step, because nothing the new generator made exists yet — that check belongs to the two steps below, where there is finally something to compare.",
        out_of_scope: "Nothing changes which generator makes it here, and no check gets loosened to keep a number looking good.",
        handback: "The relabelled list, the retired count, and a demonstration that recording a result as made by the new generator, with no receipt from the run that made it, is refused outright rather than accepted and corrected later."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: v2_emitter_producer_provenance_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-emitter-production", contribution: "Recording which generator made every result as a fact that cannot be claimed without its receipt is the lane's progress measure: the transition from old generator to new is countable, not asserted."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_B7PXF6JQRHY19AEQPXGBP12DCT",
      id: "v2-emitter-direct-rust-door",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/self_host/candidate_generation.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Have the new compiler write out Rust source itself",
        boundary: "Read the source, work out the types, translate, and write real Rust to disk without the old generator deciding any of it. The old runner may still be what executes this; it just stops making the decisions.",
        displaced_cost: "Until the new compiler can write Rust on its own, every improvement has to go through the generator we are trying to delete.",
        first_slice: "Get the real inferred tree through emission. Reading the source and working out the types already succeed; translating and writing out the Rust is where the real path stops, and the fixture route never exercised that step because it starts from a hand-written tree.",
        red_control: "A deliberately missing Rust rule must refuse rather than guess, and taking the old generator away must leave the written source unchanged.",
        out_of_scope: "Not building the new generator as a native program yet, and no second set of Rust rules beside the ones we already have.",
        handback: "The written source, the compile result, which generator made it, and proof the old one was never called."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Awaiting the operator's acceptance event: direct_rust_door_production_group_closing_expectation_holds (dag/test/claim/long/direct_rust_door_production_group.dag), reported green since 2026-09-06."), on: "2026-10-12", note: "Returned at the operator's acceptance review (2026-10-12), not accepted. direct_rust_door_production_group_closing_expectation_holds passes over the Rust source as an in-memory string; the handback promises the written source and its compile result, and neither is produced. Handback owed: the source written to a file, rustc's result on it, and the missing-rule refusal executed on that same route."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. v2.compiler.self_host.v2_emitter_direct_rust_door_contract::direct_rust_door_production_group already observes the production candidate and its leaf assessments. Reuse it. The stronger work item asks for written source, a bound rustc result and missing-rule refusal through that artifact route; an in-memory ArtifactProduced observation does not discharge those obligations.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: v2_emitter_direct_rust_door_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-emitter-production", contribution: "Carrying the real inferred tree through translation and writing Rust with the old generator deciding nothing is the capability this lane exists to name: the new compiler writes the source the factory is built from."),
      centering: plan(text: "Returned at the operator acceptance review on 2026-10-12. Keep direct_rust_door_production_group_closing_expectation_holds as regression evidence for the in-memory route. Extend that same production route to write its Rust source to a file, run rustc on it, and execute the missing-rule refusal there, retaining producer identity and proof the seed emitter was not called. Extend the closing validation to execute these obligations. Hand back the written source, compile result, producer evidence and refusal receipt at a named head. A green in-memory receipt alone does not close this node; if blocked, return the missing capability and diagnostics."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7QF2XN5BJH0K3VDPMWR8CZT6AY",
      id: "v2-emitter-production-compatible-corpus-module",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/self_host/stage0_production_target.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Make the new generator able to produce one real module the seed crate can use",
        boundary: "One real module from the repository, read off disk the way the crate's own modules arrive, comes out of the new generator in a form the existing crate accepts: visible where the crate calls across module boundaries, carrying the integer the crate's other files already carry, and with every expression in that module's body actually written out. Whether production ever selects it is the step after this one.",
        displaced_cost: "The step below assumed a real module was already producible and it is not, so without this the flip has nothing to flip. Measuring it here stops a milestone being recorded against a module the generator cannot write.",
        first_slice: "Take the smallest subject the census finds: one of 1,573 single-declaration corpus modules under dag (excluding test, tests, instruments), narrowed to the sole one the seed crate carries across a boundary and passes an i64 through, gunbc.rust_decl_type_overlay -- and walk its first refusal repeatedly: emit it, name the exact shape that stopped, add that one shape, emit again.",
        red_control: "Each capability is separated by its own failing control rather than one generic bad-output check: an item emitted without visibility must fail where the real caller reaches it, and the wrong integer must fail at the exact position the crate's existing files fix. Emitted text alone is not accepted -- the module has to stand in for the real file in a copy of the real crate, build there, and answer a table of inputs the same way the current one does.",
        out_of_scope: "Not changing which generator production selects, not matching the old generator's bytes, and not widening to modules with several declarations -- that widening waits for a consumer that needs it, and would not by itself make the large integer module producible.",
        handback: "The source tree and module named, the emitted source, the build result in the real crate, the behavioral table, and the remaining shapes still refused."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "In progress: #12623, #12443 and #12715 merged."), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: active lane work; scope moves with each emit PR."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. v2.compiler.self_host.stage0_production_target::stage0_production_target_model exists. Reuse the direct door and select one real corpus declaration; only emission refusals observed on that subject justify added shape work. Do not price all corpus forms before the first subject is chosen."), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Census corrected (warm-fox-517, detached checkout of origin/main): single-top-level-declaration corpus modules under dag, excluding test, tests and instruments, number 1,573; intersected with the generated v1-compiler mirror set they leave exactly 2 (dag/gunbc/rust_decl_type_overlay.dag, dag/std/float.dag); the boundary filter (callable, called across a module boundary, carries the crate i64) leaves 1, gunbc.rust_decl_type_overlay. An earlier figure of 134 was the byte count of a listing line, not a module count.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-emitter-production", contribution: "One real module the seed crate consumes, emitted by v2, is the first production use of the door."),
