    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_K10Q43JPP25KVS998JX8QWZZRV",
      id: "v2-core-emitter-lowers-conjunction-in-value-position",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/std/compilers/target_model.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The core emitter writes a type-shaped expression in value position instead of refusing it",
        boundary: "The core emitter's body-expression lowering refuses with the reason target_value_expr_reason_transform_shape_invalid when a TypeNode Conj, Disj, Arrow or Instantiation, or a ComputationNode, reaches value-expression position. It is raised in src/v2/std/compilers/target_model.dag (two sites, in the TypeNode and ComputationNode arms) and mirrored in src/v2/compiler/target_serialize.dag. The subject that produced it is dag/gunbc/rust_decl_type_overlay.dag: an outer Conj in value position, where the authored node is a leaf, is not a closed alias, and has resolved children. This row decides what each of those shapes lowers to, or names a refusal that says why none exists. The unary case is claimed explicitly: the Rust operator-realization catalog in dag/std/rust.dag has rows for or, and, comparison, arithmetic and coerce but none for not, and no render of a one-operand prefix operator has been observed (all realized operators are infix), so prefix-operator support is unproven and is not assumed. Regression surface, by name: src/v2/test/claim/emit/bind_tail_is_an_expression.dag, src/v2/test/claim/body_cast_node.dag, src/v2/test/claim/compiler/branch_slot_readers.dag, and the population row dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/a_possibly_empty_producer_enters_a_nonempty_consumer.dag, which counts 10 instances of the reason and says to re-measure and update when the refusals clear. Condition: this is a change to the single body-expression lowering every v2 emission goes through, so if it needs src/v2 lowering changes under the freeze, its brief goes to the operator before it is staffed.",
        displaced_cost: "The v2-emitter-production-compatible-corpus-module row cannot name a corpus subject that reaches an emitted artifact while this refusal stands, and each corpus module that hits it is a hand-found dead end. Until the shapes lower, the population row's ten instances stay uncountable as cleared.",
        first_slice: "Decide the outer Conj in value position on the census-forced subject dag/gunbc/rust_decl_type_overlay.dag by its prefix-free Conj core: the outer conjunction of the bound is-leaf operand and the resolved-child-count comparison lowers to the existing infix and realization, and the prefix-not operand together with the prefix-not claim, the two precedence controls and the three corpus controls named in red_control have moved to v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position. The row is done when a prefix-free Conj subject emits, which is achievable and not a weakening because conj_binary_emits and disj_binary_emits already pass at head 59fedef65b8 of PR 16957 as executed evidence that the Conj and Disj arms lower. Re-measure the population row a_possibly_empty_producer_enters_a_nonempty_consumer when the remaining refusals clear.",
        red_control: "OPEN as a before/after pair, to be recorded as data. Historical RED: the witness entry src/v2/test/claim/self_host/stage0_production_corpus_probe.dag at the head of gunb-ai/gunbc#16930 (69854784fe7) carried three claims, corpus_probes_refused_at_emission_holds, corpus_probes_first_refusal_is_transform_shape_holds and corpus_probes_production_ingest_has_off_disk_refs, first refusal reason target_value_expr_reason_transform_shape_invalid, executed on the released runner 9cb21df4c20325fc53ba4187cf4c55bd08037862a45d3900c5cc5519e360a177 at 69854784fe7 and at main 4a63370f. Those three corpus claims and the done-when corpus_probes_emits_holds are gated on prefix emission because the subject gunbc.rust_decl_type_overlay carries a prefix-not operand, so they now belong to v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position and are retired or inverted there. This row's done-condition is now a prefix-free Conj subject emitting, achievable and not a weakening because conj_binary_emits and disj_binary_emits already pass at head 59fedef65b8 of PR 16957 as executed evidence that the Conj and Disj arms lower; the prefix-free Conj subject is the conjunction of two well-typed Bool operands, the shape of src/v2/test/claim/self_host/conj_value_subject_fixture.dag. The inner-named-reason condition is re-targeted to the emission-time nested refusal and is met-as-executed: conj_prefix_inner and disj_prefix_inner refuse at emission carrying the standalone prefix reason while their prefix-free forms emit, witnessed by conjpre_stage_is_emission, conjpre_reason_equals_prefix_reason, disjpre_stage_is_emission and disjpre_reason_equals_prefix_reason PASSing on witness entry src/v2/test/claim/self_host/stage0_prefix_inner_reason_probe2.dag at tree 9dfda4f26c2 on HOST srv1 BOOT c095c0cd with claim_batch sha256 9cb21df4c20325fc53ba4187cf4c55bd08037862a45d3900c5cc5519e360a177 and real exit status one. No green_at sha is claimed for the prefix-free Conj subject yet; the row is done when it emits with the same instrument.",
        out_of_scope: "Not choosing the corpus subject for the compatible-corpus row, not widening any other lowering arm, not any change to the seed, and not prefix-not or prefix precedence: the prefix-not operand, the prefix-not claim, the two precedence controls and the three corpus controls named in red_control all moved to v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position.",
        handback: "The decision per shape (lowered, or the named non-generic refusal) for the prefix-free Conj core, the green_at head and claim_batch sha256 for the prefix-free Conj subject emitting, and the regression-surface claims run at that head. The prefix-not and precedence claims, the three corpus controls and their executed evidence are handed back on v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position."
      ), on: "2026-11-23", note: "red_control re-pointed from four claim names that are absent from main to the three claims at the head of #16930 (69854784fe7); every claim name in this row was checked against #16930's head (69854784fe7): the three refusal-side names and the three regression-surface claims exist there; the done-when claim corpus_probes_emits_holds is named here and added by the realizing PR. No verdict or sha is newly measured here."), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Dependency relayed 2026-11-23 by neat-badger-614 from warm-fox-517's evidence (not recorded in gunbc.design_ruling): the emitter row v2-emitter-production-compatible-corpus-module has a census-forced subject, gunbc.rust_decl_type_overlay, the only cross-boundary i64 carrier among 1,573 single-declaration modules, whose top-level conjunction in value position the generator refuses before emitting anything (target_value_expr_reason_transform_shape_invalid in target_model.dag), executed on the released runner 9cb21df4 at 69854784fe7 and at main 4a63370f. The emitter row's stand-in, input table and two mutated-build controls therefore have no artifact until this row lands. This row owns the lowering; the emitter row's first_slice 'add that one shape' is not to be read as owning it, and the emitter row now depends on this one by edge."), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Per neat-badger-614 final split ruling of 2026-11-24, relayed by warm-fox-517 on PR 16957. Two claim groups move out of this node to the new row v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position: the prefix group, being the prefix-not emit claim and the two precedence controls, and the corpus group, being the corpus emit claim and its two refusal controls, because all are gated on prefix emission while the census-forced subject gunbc.rust_decl_type_overlay carries a prefix-not operand. The Int-wrapper nwrap claim is retired from this node; its wrapper behaviour moves to the prefix row as a named second gap awaiting that row ruling, and is not written here as correct behaviour. This node done-condition becomes a prefix-free Conj subject emitting, achievable and not a weakening because conj_binary_emits and disj_binary_emits already pass at head 59fedef65b8 of PR 16957 as executed evidence that the Conj and Disj arms lower. The inner-named-reason condition is re-targeted to the emission-time nested refusal, met-as-executed by conjpre_stage_is_emission, conjpre_reason_equals_prefix_reason, disjpre_stage_is_emission and disjpre_reason_equals_prefix_reason PASSing on witness entry src/v2/test/claim/self_host/stage0_prefix_inner_reason_probe2.dag at tree 9dfda4f26c2 with claim_batch sha256 9cb21df4c20325fc53ba4187cf4c55bd08037862a45d3900c5cc5519e360a177 on HOST srv1 BOOT c095c0cd and real exit status one. The compatible-corpus emitter row depends on this row for the outer Conj lowering and additionally on v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position for the prefix-not operand its census-forced subject carries; both dependencies are declared as edges in the edge list, which is the authority for them, and the corpus row stays blocked until both parents close. This criteria rewrite establishes no implementation or acceptance; earlier receipts must be assessed against the live criteria digest.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-emitter-production", contribution: "A real corpus module reaches an emitted artifact without the generic transform-shape refusal."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7M2KQ4VDE9P1TXY8SRB3NLCW0A",
      id: "v2-core-emitter-emits-prefix-not-in-value-position",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/std/compilers/target_model.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The core emitter cannot render a one-operand prefix-not in value position, so the prefix and precedence claims stay red on an unenumerated emission refusal",
        boundary: "This row owns every claim gated on rendering the unary bang in value position: the prefix-not emit claim, the two precedence controls comparing the grouped and flat conjunction against the grouped and flat negation, and the three corpus controls for the subject dag/gunbc/rust_decl_type_overlay.dag, all migrated out of v2-core-emitter-lowers-conjunction-in-value-position because the corpus subject carries a prefix-not operand. As executed (probe1 and probe2), a bare one-operand prefix operand reaches emission and refuses there, and that refusal is not attributed to any of the thirteen enumerated primitive-apply, operand-wire, catalog, realization and transform-shape reasons; the operator-realization catalog rust_primitive_realization_rows in src/v2/extdeps/languages/rust.dag carries rows for or, and, the comparison family, add, sub, mul, div and coerce but none for not, and no one-operand prefix render has been observed, so prefix-operator support is unproven, while the lexical prefix forms used for parsing do exist in extdeps/languages/rust/emit.dag and as the bang PrefixOperatorSpec in extdeps/languages/rust/syntax.dag. The standalone negate of a numeric operand refuses at emission with its own named reason target_value_expression_emit_primitive_apply_arity_invalid, which satisfies the clause that an operand form the catalog cannot spell refuses with its own named reason rather than the generic transform-shape bucket. Named second gap, explicitly not classified as correct behaviour and awaiting this row ruling: a well-typed wrapped negate, a numeral plus a negated operand, refuses before emission at the inference stage because op_negate has no catalog row, instead of the inner named reason surfacing at emission, witnessed by nwrap_stage_is_inference PASSing while nwrap_reason_equals_negate_reason FAILs. Precedence claims must be fail-closed: when emitted_text_for yields nothing the claim must refuse rather than compare two empty strings as equal or search for a substring in empty text; the two current precedence failures are exactly that vacuous pattern.",
        displaced_cost: "The prefix-bearing corpus subject stays unemitted while the prefix render is missing, which is the single reason the corpus emit control is red, and the relative precedence of conjunction against negation cannot be pinned by emitted body text until a prefix body is produced.",
        first_slice: "Name the prefix emission refusal from executed text via a narrow diagnostic dump of the refusal families in src/v2/std/compilers/target_model.dag, namely target_concrete_token_kind_invalid_diagnostic, target_value_projection_bundle_malformed_diagnostic, target_value_projection_field_missing_diagnostic, the operand-wire path in target_value_expr_primitive_apply_wire_schema_valid through target_value_expr_operand_wire_malformed_diagnostic, target_value_template_node and the positional-arity check in target_type_expr_emitted_validate_positional_arity, run on the prefix subject src/v2/test/claim/self_host/prefix_not_operand_subject_fixture.dag, then rule whether prefix-not is emitted with a one-operand prefix render or refuses under a named reason that is not the generic transform-shape one. Record the named second gap, the inference-stage wrapped negate, against this row. Re-specify the two precedence controls fail-closed so that an empty emitted body refuses.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at and green_at for the lexeme-naming first pair are not yet measured, and green_at is not measured and no sha is claimed for it. The row is dispatched to name its own prefix emission refusal, so the first red_at and green_at pair would be a claim that the prefix subject src/v2/test/claim/self_host/prefix_not_operand_subject_fixture.dag emits, red while the prefix operand refuses at emission on an unenumerated lexeme. Executed RED backing that refusal, from claim_batch over witness entry src/v2/test/claim/self_host/stage0_prefix_inner_reason_probe2.dag at tree 9dfda4f26c261b1b37cd95359c5e687cf8260252 on HOST srv1 BOOT c095c0cd, claim_batch sha256 9cb21df4c20325fc53ba4187cf4c55bd08037862a45d3900c5cc5519e360a177, real exit status one, fifty-six witness verdicts. Seven pass verbatim: negate_lex_is_arity_invalid_holds, nwrap_stage_is_inference_holds, corpus_reason_equals_prefix_reason_holds, conjpre_stage_is_emission_holds, conjpre_reason_equals_prefix_reason_holds, disjpre_stage_is_emission_holds, disjpre_reason_equals_prefix_reason_holds. The prefix, corpus, negate and nwrap emit claims fail and all thirteen lexeme probes for the prefix and corpus subjects fail, so the prefix subject reaches emission and refuses on a lexeme outside the enumerated set rather than being absent from the pipeline. Stage pins from the earlier witness entry src/v2/test/claim/self_host/stage0_prefix_inner_reason_probe.dag at tree e948da35ce0 with thirty-one witnesses: the standalone negate refuses at emission with target_value_expression_emit_primitive_apply_arity_invalid. The migrated corpus group closes on the positive claim corpus_probes_emits_holds on the subject gunbc.rust_decl_type_overlay, which the worker does not rename, together with its two refusal controls corpus_probes_refused_at_emission_holds and corpus_probes_first_refusal_is_transform_shape_holds, which retire or invert on this row once prefix-not renders and which are red here because that census-forced subject carries a prefix-not operand. The row is done when the prefix subject emits, or refuses under a named reason that is not the generic transform-shape one, and the precedence controls compare two non-empty emitted bodies with grouping present in the grouped form.",
        out_of_scope: "Not the Conj and Disj outer-lowering work, which stays on v2-core-emitter-lowers-conjunction-in-value-position; not the seed; not hand-written seed Rust; not choosing the compatible-corpus subject.",
        handback: "The prefix emission decision, a one-operand prefix render or a named non-generic refusal, with the refusal lexeme from the executed dump; the two precedence controls re-specified fail-closed and comparing non-empty emitted bodies with grouping; and a ruling on the named second gap, the inference-stage wrapped negate. Record HOST, BOOT, the real exit status, the claim_batch sha256 and the hit count for every executed claim."
      ), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Proposed by operator principal 116084671989231734979 by the neat-badger-614 split ruling relayed by warm-fox-517 on PR 16957. The prefix-not claim, both precedence controls and the three corpus controls migrated here from v2-core-emitter-lowers-conjunction-in-value-position because all five are gated on prefix emission.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-emitter-production", contribution: "The one-operand prefix-not operator, never realized by the infix-only Rust catalog, is emitted by v2 in value position."),
    ),
