      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Every rostered emitted module holds its own .dag contract on a discriminating corpus",
          boundary: "The interlock milestone SelfHostEmittedContractsHeld (gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_interlock), read by gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_status from the latest deliberately taken behavioral-equivalence receipt identity-joined to the behavioral transport roster: every module the emitter roster names holds its own .dag contract when the emitted build is driven on a discriminating corpus. The seed is the regression oracle, never the specification (gunbc.design_ruling::v2_better_than_the_seed): a divergence is a v2 regression or a recorded seed correction, and matching bytes is not evidence.",
          displaced_cost: "The milestone is a prerequisite of SelfHostSeedRetirement and until this change no work item discharged it, so the program could not say what remained between generation two and deleting the seed.",
          first_slice: "Take one behavioral-equivalence receipt over the current emitter roster at a named head and read the milestone from it, whatever it says; an empty series (BehavioralEquivalenceSeriesEmpty) is the first red.",
          red_control: "A module named by the roster with no receipt row, or a row whose contract run was not taken deliberately at the receipt's head, keeps the milestone Outstanding; a seed divergence with no disposition keeps it Outstanding; no row is minted from matching bytes.",
          out_of_scope: "Admitting the successor (v1-emitter-fixed-point) and deleting the seed (v1-emitter-delete); widening the roster.",
          handback: "SelfHostEmittedContractsHeld reads CLEAR in gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_status, with the receipt it was read from."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.self_host_behavioral_equivalence_receipt explicitly returns BehavioralEquivalenceSeriesEmpty. Existing receipt types and milestone readers can be reused; the required work is producing a nonempty current emitter-roster series and reading its actual standing, not manufacturing a CLEAR milestone.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-emitter-production", contribution: "A v2-built compiler is not a successor until every module it emits holds its own contract; this is the interlock prerequisite between generation two and seed retirement that had no work item."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
