      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_rust_host_observation.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "See the hand-written files as they actually are, from the host",
        boundary: "The set of tracked Rust files is read from the repository itself at a known revision, not transcribed. Reading it can fail, and when it does it says so rather than returning a shorter list.",
        displaced_cost: "Every count of what is left to move was previously taken from whichever files someone had looked at. That understates, silently, and it understated twice here -- so no schedule built on it could be trusted.",
        first_slice: "Read the tracked set live and refuse, with a reason, when the read does not succeed.",
        red_control: "A read that fails must not come back as an empty or partial set. Discovery and classification are separate axes and are checked separately: finding every tracked file is one question, and every found file carrying a disposition is a different one, so a roster that is complete but unclassified fails the second while passing the first.",
        out_of_scope: "Deciding what each file's fate should be, and the product-reachability question, both belong downstream. This node only makes the population honest.",
        handback: "The live observation, its typed refusals, and a count that comes from enumerating the tracked set rather than from inspection."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Awaiting the operator's acceptance event: live_rust_observation_matches_actions_subject (dag/test/claim/stage0_rust_host_observation_live_witness.dag)."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.stage0.stage0_rust_host_observation::current_stage0_rust_source_observation already calls the tracked-source observer, with typed read refusals. Residual begins with the existing live witness and producer provenance, not implementing git enumeration again. A source count alone is not deletion acceptance.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: v1_rust_source_observation_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "v1-deletion-program", contribution: "Reading the hand-written population from the repository at a known revision -- and refusing a failed read -- is what makes the deletion frontier a count from observation instead of from inspection."),
      centering: plan(text: "Run dag/test/claim:stage0_rust_host_observation_live_witness_test. Confirm live_rust_observation_matches_actions_subject is green; it reads the live tree, so record the head it observed. Change nothing. Hand back the receipt. Stop if DeclinedLiveTree on the route you have."),
    ),
