      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Work through the remaining hand-written files the products need",
        boundary: "Move the hand-written files the shipping tools still depend on. Anything that genuinely has to stay gets an explicit reason.",
        displaced_cost: "The main command-line tool is itself one of these files, so 'the products still build' is not something we can honestly claim until this is done.",
        first_slice: "Move the next complete family and run it.",
        red_control: "A file the products reach that has no stated reason to remain blocks progress. The count of what remains is derived by enumerating the observed tracked set, never by counting the files someone happened to touch -- an inspection-based count understates and has done so twice. A file whose only consumer is a test is not product-reachable and must not be counted as if moving it shortened this queue.",
        out_of_scope: "No hitting the number by baking Rust into templates.",
        handback: "The shorter queue, the replacements running, and the reasons for whatever stays."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: population comes from the re-cut frontier."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The hand queue is a remaining-family population, not a uniform number of files. A family needs a replacement owner and an executing consumer before deletion. Keep the next complete-family inspection; no defensible cardinality or per-family implementation estimate was established by this review.")),
