      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/v1/v1_deletion_plan.dag"), carrier(path: "dag/test/claim/retained_symbol_index_route_refusal.dag")),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A retained v1 Rust test names an executed refusal for its route and a testable way to retire",
        boundary: "Follow-up to v1-test-migration, whose accepted criteria stay as they are. For the retained module declaration_named_in_module_reexport_test (src/v1/tests/src/declaration_named_in_module_reexport_test.rs, the v1 SymbolIndex internals), author an executed .dag claim that tries to reach that route from a claim fixture and is refused; and give every retained row in dag/test/retirement/model.dag a retirement trigger a worker can test, beyond the unbound dissolution arm.",
        displaced_cost: "Today the retained row says no claim can import v1.compiler.* as a sentence, not a run, so a route that later opens goes unseen, and the row cannot say what retires it other than going unbound.",
        first_slice: "Measure first: author test.claim.retained_symbol_index_route_refusal, run it with the released claim_batch, and record whether the compile refuses.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at and green_at are not measured. The first pair would be the refusal claim passing on the refused route (green) and the same claim with a planted reachable import that still expects refusal, failing (red), both at one tree with the released claim_batch in one heavy-slot wrapper. If the route does not refuse, this row is a red handback, not a green one.",
