      id: "dp-m1-dissolvable-rows-retired",
      owner: "debt",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/floor_expected_red.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "DP-M1: every roster row that is dissolvable now is retired",
          boundary: "The join of each roster against this tree has no dead identities: v2.workflow.floor_expected_red chunk_11/chunk_12 and floor_expected_red_is_live deleted (21 dead rows, filter gone); the gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots witness_exclusion_frontier rows that match no tracked file deleted (the synthetic_orphan_admission RED fixture stays); gunbc.rung_drop.measurement_bankruptcy retired; the gunbc.seed_growth_admission orphan justifications rostered or deleted; the stale row of extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io filesystem_absence_establishment_adoption_standing removed.",
          approach: "One worker per roster, each bound to the roster's existing witness; grandfathered-roster removals wait until the dead set is measured by a live population join (a name-grep join flags 76 identities, most synthesized).",
          red_control: "A roster row that is deleted while its identity is still live, or a dead identity left in a roster, keeps this open.",
          displaced_cost: "A dead row is a second representation of a fact git already holds (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority), and every consumer of the roster pays to read it.",
          handback: "Each roster re-joined against the tree with no dead identities, named by the witness that joins it."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "debt-payoff", contribution: "Rows whose own dissolution condition already holds are the cheapest debt there is: retiring them is deletion with an existing witness."),
