      line: ticket(t: updated(t: level_fields(
          headline: "DP-M3: extdeps-scope closure halved",
          boundary: "The legacy extdeps scope manifest (dag/gunbc/legacy_extdeps_scope_frontier.tsv via gunbc.extdeps_scope_frontier) halved, and gunbc.instruments.extdeps_scope_placement_gate enrolled on an executing route before anything is counted.",
          approach: "Enrol the gate first (a gate that runs nowhere is an inert lens, gunbc.design_argument::how_to_work), then drain one extdeps file per change: add its ExternalModelScope and delete its manifest line together.",
          red_control: "A manifest line deleted without its file declaring its scope, or a count taken while the gate runs nowhere, keeps this open.",
          displaced_cost: "An undeclared external-authority placement is a gunbc.design_argument::single_authority citation nobody can check.",
          handback: "The gate enrolled and the manifest at half its current size."
        ),
          on: "2026-11-16",
          note: "Accepted for its literal hand-back: the placement gate enrolled on an executing route and the legacy manifest halved from 352 rows to 176 (wc -l on dag/gunbc/legacy_extdeps_scope_frontier.tsv; gunbc#16511, c7efe927c4f6). The migrated subjects are storage-grain scaffolds, not resolved references: 833 files carry 844 subject: ExternalSubjectRef rows and no consumer asks whether the named module declares the named thing, so a phantom costs one keystroke and passes every existing witness. Until dp-m3-subject-ref-resolved lands its consumer over the full carrier population, no further bulk drain runs against this milestone."
        )),
