    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_S0M7BKWYNQ2HD8JSZ6B79VF5CC",
      id: "corpus-sweep-excludes-directories-by-name-and-reports-no-excluded-count",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs"), carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/derived_row_roster.rs")),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The corpus sweep silently drops whole directories, so the parse-clean count cannot be reconciled against what is on disk",
        boundary: "v1_compiler::cli_run::run_dag_parse_sweep: its roots constant DAG_PARSE_SWEEP_ROOTS, its discovery walk, and DagParseSweep.parse_clean. Reporting and accounting only; finding kinds, severities and the exit-status contract do not move. The reported count differs from the files on disk by two silent adjustments in opposite directions, and neither is printed. MINUS: the discovery walk drops any directory named target and any directory named fixtures whose parent is tests, by a bare continue; the fixtures exclusion is deliberate, since those hold inputs malformed on purpose for the parser's own tests. PLUS: for a ledger row directory the walk contributes a module with no file on disk, one roster rendered in memory under the reserved identity <row dir>/roster.dag by acquire_dir_files in cli_run/derived_row_roster.rs, qualified by the compiled-in table DERIVED_ROW_ROSTERS (five entries at the main this row was filed against: gunbc/recurring_failure_mode, gunbc/rung_drop, gunbc/guarantee_stall, gunbc/layout_namespace_row, gunbc/integration_concern). A file that genuinely fails to parse is NOT hidden: the else branch emits a located diagnostic per entry through the span authority and the sweep returns Err. This is accounting, not error handling, and the exclusion rules and the derived roster contribution themselves must not change, only be reported. The PLUS half lives in the second carrier, src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/derived_row_roster.rs (acquire_dir_files and DERIVED_ROW_ROSTERS), and that is the code that must be made to print a list. Witness: the v1_src_dag_parse binary (bin target declared in src/v1/stage0/Cargo.toml, source src/bin/v1_src_dag_parse.rs); main takes no arguments, so the only lever is the working directory, which must be the tree root or the relative roots silently cover nothing.",
        displaced_cost: "A file the walk never opened contributes zero findings, so anything counted from this sweep treats it as clean: a zero that means unknown. The acceptance of runner-throughput-witness-imports-absent-members turned on zero findings naming dag/test/claim/runner/runner_throughput_qualification_witness.dag, which only means something if that file was in the judged set, and nothing the tool prints lets a reader check it.",
        first_slice: "Count and name what the walk excluded, per root: files_found (from the walk itself, not from a caller), parsed_ok, parse_failed (named), and excluded (named, each with its reason: tests/fixtures, target, other); also name the derived rosters contributed. Refuse to print the summary line unless parsed_ok + parse_failed + excluded == files_found, and print the reconciliation line either way. Keep the exclusions themselves exactly as they are.",
        red_control: "red_at bef04740bb51142a8d591f93c9e432cba5c712ea; green_at OPEN, the head whose summary prints the reconciliation line with every input named, not yet measured and no sha claimed. OBSERVED at red_at, with the binary built at that tree (srv1, heavy-slot, cwd the worktree root): the tool printed 10176 file(s) parse-clean while a find over the four sweep roots counted 10178 .dag (src/v1 69, dag 8209, src/v2 1899, test/primitive_runtime_body 1; git ls-tree -r agrees at 10178; no tracked .dag sits under a target/ directory), exit status 1, 524 finding lines. MINUS 5, excluded and never named: src/v1/stage0/tests/fixtures/fact_cardinality_split_brace.dag, src/v1/tests/fixtures/non_ascii_perf.dag, src/v1/tests/fixtures/whole_tree_wiring_enum/common.dag, src/v1/tests/fixtures/whole_tree_wiring_enum/mod_a.dag, src/v1/tests/fixtures/whole_tree_wiring_enum/mod_b.dag. PLUS 3, the in-memory derived rosters: dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode, dag/gunbc/rung_drop, dag/gunbc/guarantee_stall (at that tree derived_row_roster.rs read DERIVED_ROW_ROSTERS: [&DerivedRowRoster; 3] = [&RECURRING_FAILURE_MODE, &RUNG_DROP, &GUARANTEE_STALL]; the other two entries joined later). So 10178 - 5 + 3 = 10176, exactly the tool's own number. Honest limit: the three derived rosters came from the table and the tree, not from the tool, which prints no derived list at all; that inability is part of what this row asks to fix. RED is N parse-clean that nothing the tool prints reconciles to the input population. GREEN is every input accounted for by name (files_found, parsed_ok, parse_failed named, excluded named with reason, derived named) with the counts reconciling on one tree with one binary, raw output and the command's own exit status pasted, never a pipe's.",
        out_of_scope: "Any change to which findings are reported, to CITED-* or IMPORT-MEMBER-ABSENT semantics, to the sweep root list, to the exclusion rules, or to the exit-status contract. Also out of scope: whether the excluded fixture files belong in the corpus, and whether derived rosters should count as sources at all; both are correct as they stand and this row is about the tool hiding the two adjustments.",
        handback: "Before and after sweeps at the same tree with the summary lines verbatim, the named excluded list, the reconciliation line, and each command's own exit status."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A parse-clean count names every file it did not judge."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_ZGWTH1RA7BXGQN9ZWZK3QZF2B0",
      id: "acceptance-history-parser-seed-builtin-deleted",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/roadmap_acceptance_history_carrier.rs"), carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_acceptance_history_carrier.dag")),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Delete the hand-written seed builtin that parses the acceptance event history, once nothing models a call to it",
        boundary: "The seed builtin parse_roadmap_acceptance_event_history_jsonl and its Rust body parse_roadmap_acceptance_event_history_jsonl_builtin in src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/roadmap_acceptance_history_carrier.rs, with the sites that exist only to reach it: its registration in src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs (the free_call arm), its signature in src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer_method.rs and src/v1/04_method.dag, its entry in src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated.rs, and the declared scaffold roadmap_acceptance_event_history_jsonl_parser_seed_scaffold in dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_acceptance_history_carrier.dag (a Disposition that dissolves to RealizationDispatch and binds the builtin). Today the one modeled caller is parse_roadmap_acceptance_event_history_carrier in that same module, which the loaders load_roadmap_acceptance_event_history_from_carrier_text and its importers reach. GATED on the receipt-line read going through the modeled member readers (sharp-bear-582's PR1, not yet merged): until it merges that wrapper still calls the builtin and the claim of zero callers is false. The first act of this row is to establish the caller set by name at the merged revision with bounded git grep over src/v1, src/v2 and dag, state what was inspected and what remains unknown, and not to infer absence from the PR title. The deletion is governed by cli_run hollowing (gunbc.plans.cli_run_hollowing_plan) and serves the v2 self-host program, which is what admits a v1 seed change (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing); it changes no behaviour of the modeled readers.",
        displaced_cost: "A hand-written seed parser stays a second authority for one fact, how an acceptance event line decodes, beside the modeled readers, and its Rust tests keep the seed carrying a function nothing modeled calls. Each live copy is something the next change to the event shape must update twice.",
        first_slice: "At the revision where PR1 has merged: list the callers of parse_roadmap_acceptance_event_history_jsonl across src/v1, src/v2 and dag with the exact command and revision; if the only remaining reference is the wrapper, re-point or remove that wrapper in the same change, then delete the builtin, its three registration sites, its dispatch entry and the scaffold row together, since a scaffold binding a deleted declaration would dangle.",
        red_control: "OPEN as a before/after pair, to be recorded as data; no red_at or green_at sha is claimed. Before: the builtin is registered and a call to it evaluates. After: the same call from a fixture source refuses as an unknown free call, the modeled readers still decode the same carrier text to the same events (the existing modeled witnesses over RoadmapAcceptanceEventHistoryLoad pass unchanged), and the bounded caller grep at the head returns no reference outside the deleted files. Run on srv1 under heavy-slot, not in a session container.",
        out_of_scope: "Any change to how the modeled readers parse or to the event shape, the PR1 change itself, other cli_run hollowing chunks, any other seed builtin, and the handback_to_json declaration, which is a separate listed seed declaration.",
        handback: "The caller command, revision and its output before the deletion, the files and registration sites removed, the unknown-call refusal and the unchanged modeled-reader results at the head, and the remaining shapes in the carrier module if any."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v1-deletion-program", contribution: "A hand-written seed builtin with no modeled caller leaves the population the deletion frontier counts."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_Q3X3MA0XF1FQRFQ3D17QEYDFZ7",
      id: "foreign-whole-root-primary-source-root-admitted",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "gunbc compile admits a whole-root primary source root from a declared foreign repository",
        boundary: "gunbc compile admits a primary --source-root belonging to another repository when the caller declares it. Today process_workspace_root (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs; it panics when no workspace root resolves) requires a Cargo.toml and a dag/ workspace, and root-admission in compile_emission_over_inner (cli_run.rs) refuses any primary root outside it, ignoring the --repository and --measured-root-demands declaration, although the governor already joins on (repository, primary_root, dependency_pools) in whole_corpus_compile_admission (src/v1/stage0/src/memory_governor.rs). When the declared repository differs from the interpreter's own, admit a real directory of .dag modules under the process cwd and key its modules under the DECLARED repository id, so no foreign module can collide with a gunbc module path; namespace safety, not containment, is what the check protects. Blocked: ctrl's 11 whole-root compiles (9 in scripts/run-ctrl-dag-tests.sh, plus run-scheduling-gate.sh and run-image-publish-gate.sh), which pass today only because ctrl's pin 60b137cf predates both checks. Operator approved this direction (A+C) in chat on 2026-11-23; a seed change, admitted because it serves the v2 self-host program (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing).",
        displaced_cost: "ctrl cannot advance its gunbc pin past 60b137cf without losing eleven compiles, and carries a locus fixture in scripts/lib/gunbc_toolchain.sh as the stand-in.",
        first_slice: "Admit the primary root when --repository is declared and differs from the interpreter's own, the root is a real directory of .dag modules, and it lies under the process cwd; key its modules under the declared repository id. Keep every other refusal as it is.",
        red_control: "The admitting arm: a whole-root compile whose primary root is outside the workspace root, inside the cwd, declared with a foreign --repository plus a projection naming it, admits, with module paths namespaced under the declared id; RED before the change, GREEN after, as a historical before/after pair with red_at and green_at shas and exit statuses (the claim_batch built at each tree). Three refusals stay green across the change: no --repository refuses WholeCorpusCompileRepositoryUndeclared (raised in compile_emission_over_inner, cli_run.rs); a projection for another repository refuses RefusedDemandsForAnotherRepository (whole_corpus_compile_admission, memory_governor.rs); a root outside the cwd refuses. No measurement exists yet: the pair is OPEN, to be measured.",
        out_of_scope: "Containment of foreign modules, any change to the three standing refusals, and ctrl's own pin advance (ctrl owns it).",
        handback: "The change, the measured before/after pair for the admitting arm, the three standing refusals green at both trees, and the node id given to ctrl so it deletes its locus fixture (the R12 marker in scripts/lib/gunbc_toolchain.sh names this node) in the commit that advances its pin past this node."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A seed compile admits a declared foreign root without losing its namespace refusals."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_D3470QB6GPYD3PWSJMNGGMFV27",
      id: "native-emit-match-binding-keeps-its-type",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/04_infer.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "A value bound by a match arm on a generic enum keeps its concrete type through native emission",
        boundary: "Found on 2026-11-15 by the demand-serve-program-image work, emitting the roadmap serve entry natively. A match arm that binds a field of a GENERIC enum variant (Optional<NonEmptyStr> matched as Present { value: v }, then v as String) leaves the bound variable typed by the enum's type parameter rather than the concrete argument, so at emit it renders erased and the as crossing lowers to compile_error!(UNRESOLVED_CompilerError). Typecheck and interpretation accept the same program, so the defect appears only at native emission and is below the floor (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder). The cause, measured in PR #16534 against a pattern-side substitution pass: the seed's kernel Optional mint (v1.compiler.infer kernel_optional_type_node) declared no type parameter and typed Present.value unbound, so the existing generic substitution received an empty slot map. Scrutinee expansion in src/v1/04_patterns.dag is not at fault and needs no second substitution pass. The first production site is gunbc.runner.runner_slot_retirement host_interruption_reason, which blocks emitting the roadmap serve entry.",
        displaced_cost: "Every program that matches on a variant and converts the bound value cannot be emitted natively, so native serving and any other native target is blocked by an ordinary pattern the rest of the compiler accepts.",
        first_slice: "The mint carries its parameter: kernel_optional_type_node declares params [t_param] and types Present.value as that parameter, so the existing substitution binds it, and kernel_mint_shape_diagnostics judges the mint by the same facts as the declaration. No change to src/v1/04_patterns.dag. The stage0 mirrors come from heal.",
        red_control: "Executed pair, RedObservedOnMain: red_at 4e270740af598a12b97351f87b86f72b7fcab343, green_at 4a63370f4a677ae8541cdbf2655e0f4ba131226b. The four fixtures of test.claim.emitter_generic_match_field_binding_witness, run with the released claim_batch 9cb21df4: three FAIL (rc 1) at red_at and all four PASS (rc 0) at green_at (measured by calm-swift-579 and warm-fox-517 on srv1; the fix is #16535 b650f52c, preceded by #16534 319886d9, so the outcome landed). The row claims the generic case only: a match arm binder of a generic enum variant keeps the scrutinee's concrete type. The kernel_optional_mint_shape_witness KernelMintShapeMismatch control is struck: kernel_optional_mint_shape_witness (7 claims) and generic_result_match_binding_witness (11 claims) PASS at both trees, so they cannot flip and are preservation evidence only. The diagnostic half is withdrawn: the arm that would emit it is unreachable because func_env_declared_func_sig and func_sig_from_direct_call in src/v1/04_infer.dag answer before the census arms, and no claim takes that text as subject. Second pair, as data (warm-fox-517): witness native_emit_match_arms_default_arm_all_bind_binder claim arm_binding_keeps_the_scrutinee_type, red_at 4e270740af598a12b97351f87b86f72b7fcab343 (claim_batch built at that tree, sha256 f05bbc4edefa8aca0ac4d59a6244b19ebb149392e9d33a86bd3e4e42f99dcf60; raw line: FAIL native_emit_match_arms_default_arm_all_bind_binder.arm_binding_keeps_the_scrutinee_type: match arm binder 'v' is bound as Shared(String(\"dyn::core::unknown_type\"))), green_at 4a63370f4a677ae8541cdbf2655e0f4ba131226b (claim_batch built at that tree, sha256 3dfe06f25c9f7b2409fa6f4dce8cbc0c43c25d5463b2ac4771d59d90cea89385). generic_let_binder_stays_unbound in the same module PASSes at both trees and is not a control.",
        out_of_scope: "Other native-emission refusals in the roadmap serve entry's closure; each is found and fixed under demand-serve-program-image.",
        handback: "The fix site and reason; the historical before/after pair for test.claim.emitter_generic_match_field_binding_witness (pre-fix tree 4e270740af59 FAIL x3 PASS x1 EXIT=1; main 4a63370f4a67 PASS x4 EXIT=0; fix #16535 b650f52c after #16534 319886d9); the mint-shape and generic-result witnesses kept as preservation evidence (PASS at both trees, not red controls); the red_at/green_at pairs above with their EXIT statuses; the failure-mode row; and the roadmap serve entry's next refusal, if any."
      ), on: "2026-11-15", note: "PR #16534 carries this slice."), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Red control narrowed to the generic case evidenced by the pairs; diagnostic half and mint-shape mutation withdrawn (warm-fox-517)."), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Outcome landed via #16534 (disposition accept-as-landed, to be recorded in the roadmap event log after the lab advance); red_control replaced with the executed pair at 4e270740af59 and 4a63370f4a67, mint-shape control struck (neat-badger-614).")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "Native emission accepts what typecheck accepts for variant bindings."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_5Y4YAYGG7Y4EVCDN7T9XT1Z89P",
      id: "fleet-converge-artifact-closure",
      owner: "debt",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/live_deploy/intent.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Fleet convergence refuses to enable a unit whose read artifacts it has not installed",
        boundary: "deploy-intent-owns-artifact-closure makes the deploy closure check generic over an enable authority and each unit's declared reads, and applies it to gunbc.live_deploy.spec deployment_owned_steps. Units enabled by fleet convergence rather than by the deploy are not in that roster: board-function-converge (gunbc.fleet.board_function_admission), gpu-power-cap (gunbc.fleet.gpu_power_cap_converge) and the serving replicas (gunbc.serving.srv1_serving_launch). The gpu-power-cap unit runs from the board-function converge snapshot, so a converge that enables it without that snapshot fails it the same way lab bug 5 failed the drain.",
        displaced_cost: "A fleet unit whose artifact convergence did not install fails only at run time, and the cause is found from that unit's logs.",
        first_slice: "Name the fleet-converge enable authority for each of the three units, and declare each unit's reads in its own module.",
        red_control: "A fleet convergence whose enabled units read an artifact it does not install refuses before enabling any of them, naming the unit and the artifact; RED on main.",
        out_of_scope: "The deploy roster, which deploy-intent-owns-artifact-closure covers, and moving any srv1 unit.",
        handback: "The enable authority per unit, the read declarations, and the control with its red run on main."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "A fleet convergence cannot leave a unit without what it needs."),
