    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_V2SSDWZR3G2KNSQ1BGRARSKTE2",
      id: "fleet-no-route-masks-a-running-unit",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "No built runner route masks a unit that is still running",
        boundary: "fleet-cap-bracket-keeps-running-units repairs the cap bracket's masking pass. The recurring failure mode gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload still lists built routes that mask an active unit: drain_runner_slot_over with MaskWhileRunning, the default slot_drain_plan, and withdraw. Masking a running unit drops its drop-ins at the next reload, which failed required CI on srv4 runners. The class's rung is the minimum across its routes, so it stays below ceiling until every route is repaired.",
        displaced_cost: "A masked running runner fails required CI jobs at random, and each failure costs a rerun and someone reading the log.",
        first_slice: "Decide whether any route needs to mask an active unit; if none does, delete the MaskWhileRunning arm so the state cannot be constructed. A busy slot is drained without masking (for example a runtime Restart=no drop-in, then waiting for its job to end); until that route exists the cap bracket on a busy host refuses, a liveness cost #16519 declared (review 95796).",
        red_control: "For each listed route, a pass over a fixture host with a running runner unit issues no mask for that unit and a stopped unit is still masked; RED on main for each route that masks today. The failure-mode row's rung is raised to what the executed evidence shows.",
        out_of_scope: "The cap bracket's own masking pass (fleet-cap-bracket-keeps-running-units).",
        handback: "The decision on MaskWhileRunning with its reason, the per-route controls with red runs on main, and the updated failure-mode row."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-bringup", contribution: "A host's runner slots stay healthy across its own convergence."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7KQF3TB9WD4XMH2C8SVA6UYGPN",
      id: "fleet-mask-grants-cover-slots-the-model-keeps",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/runner/runner_slot_retirement.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "srv4's mask authority reaches three slots the model keeps",
        boundary: "Found 2026-11-18 while landing the cap bracket's drain stop leg. The sudoers mask lines are rendered from host_maskable_units (gunbc.runner.runner_host_grants), which is the operator interruption authorization's ENUMERATION for the host, not the retire delta derived from the width authorities (gunbc.runner.runner_width_transition). srv4_transition_interruption_authorization was authored 2026-09-12 when that transition's target was width 12, and it enumerates srv4-13..21. The model today keeps srv4-01..15 -- that is exactly the population the activation grants render -- so provisioning/srv4/gunbc-ghrunner.sudoers carries 'systemctl mask --now' over srv4-13, srv4-14 and srv4-15, units no retire route names. Authority with no consumer, the run-time dangling shape under gunbc.design_argument::consumption: nothing masks those three today (the retire actuator masks only what the obligation tells it to, and the drain stop leg's host_drain_interruption_authorization names 13..15 as slots to stop and RE-ADMIT), but the grant advertises a retire intent the model does not hold, and a later route could consume it. srv3 has no such gap: srv3_width_cut_interruption_authorization (#16665) enumerates srv3-14..21, which equals its derived delta.",
        displaced_cost: "A reader, or any future actuator that trusts the grant list instead of the obligation, treats a kept slot as retired; and every review of srv4's sudoers has to re-derive why three lines are dead.",
        first_slice: "Narrow srv4_transition_interruption_authorization to the derived retire set (srv4-16..21) and re-render provisioning/srv4/gunbc-ghrunner.sudoers. Do not move that grant set under a live bracket: land it only after srv4's cap bracket has restored its slots.",
        red_control: "A claim that every mask line in a runner host's committed sudoers names a unit that host's required retirees names: RED on main, failing on srv4-13, srv4-14 and srv4-15, GREEN once the authorization equals the derived delta.",
        out_of_scope: "The cap bracket's drain stop leg, which lands without touching this authorization, and srv3, whose enumeration already agrees.",
        handback: "The narrowed authorization, the re-rendered srv4 sudoers, and the grant-versus-obligation control with its red run on main."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-bringup", contribution: "A host's runner slots stay healthy across its own convergence."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_QYEUEURHHNC6K26XR4ZZCSFKJA",
      id: "fleet-converge-receipt-counts-owed-work",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_converge_plan.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The converge apply receipt counts the work it withheld and the work it never meant to do",
        boundary: "fleet_converge_apply_terminal's FullHostConverge arm builds its terminal from REFUSAL counts alone, so a plan that owed work and a run that did none of it print the same receipt. On srv1 apply run 44428803079 (plan 44423114994) the plan listed 2 cap drop-in CHANGEs and 4 runner-slot REMOVEs (srv1-10/11/12/14); the apply was correctly fail-closed and did none of them -- the cap axis is never emitted into apply.sh (gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_plan::fleet_converge_cap_apply_shell_note: drop-in writes are live_deploy authority, per the MemoryMax SINGLE AUTHORITY note in gunbc.host.host_axis_caps::host_axis_caps_note) and the 4 teardowns echoed __GUNBC_CONVERGE_WITHHELD__ cause=no retirement evidence because srv1-07/08/09 were still running. The receipt still read partially_applied|7|slot=5 cap=0 ... activation=2, exit 0, 'applied', because a withheld row and a plan-only row are counted as NEITHER applied NOR refused. The arm's own comment in gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_plan::fleet_converge_apply_terminal names this exact failure mode: 'the plan says work is needed, nothing does it, the terminal reports applied' and the LiveDeployMemberBasis arm is guarded against it -- a non-empty plan gives AwaitingCapability, never FullyApplied. FullHostConverge has no such guard. Adjacent and admitted by the same note: the cap rows are rendered into plan.txt as ADD/CHANGE/REMOVE MUTATIONS although converge never acts on them, and the CHANGE line says 'content drift' for a whole-file byte compare (gunbc.host.host_axis_caps::cap_member_value_eq over gunbc.host.host_axis_caps::cap_dropin_content) without naming the directive or either value. That compare is NOT producing a false positive here -- the plan's own observed baseline (artifact fleet-converge-plan of run 44423114994) reads MemoryMax=23622320128 and MemoryHigh=22548578304, the pre-ruling 22/21 GiB bracket srv1's drop-ins still carry at mtime 2026-10-30, while the model has demanded 26843545600 for BOTH directives since the operator ruling of 2026-11-04 (#15850). The drift is real, live_deploy has not written it, converge is forbidden to write it, and the receipt counted it nowhere.",
        displaced_cost: "The one number an operator trusts about a converge run is wrong in the safe-looking direction: a converge that did nothing reports applied, so the next dispatch is chosen from a receipt that hides both the withheld teardowns and the cap rows that were never converge's to do. The retirement-evidence gate -- the thing that withheld the 4 teardowns and is the reason the run was safe -- is invisible in the receipt, which reads as though there were nothing left to wait for. And 2 plan-only cap rows presented as mutations teach the reviewer that converge owns a live_deploy write, which is the authority split the cap note exists to protect; the 25 GiB envelope srv1 has owed since 2026-11-04 is reported as 'content drift', which names neither directive nor value and cannot be acted on.",
        first_slice: "The FullHostConverge arm carries a WITHHELD count and a PLAN-ONLY count beside the refused count, FullyApplied requires all three to be zero, and the receipt line names each; the withheld and plan-only counts are counted from what the renderer actually renders, not re-derived beside it. The cap rows render as plan-only: live_deploy authority rather than as mutations, and the drift line names the managed directive and the observed and desired values instead of saying 'content drift'.",
        red_control: "A full-host request whose slot teardowns are withheld for want of retirement evidence yields a terminal that is NOT FullyApplied and a receipt that names the withheld count; the same request with the guard reverted reproduces the 44428803079 receipt shape (partially_applied, the 4 teardowns counted applied, no withheld or plan-only term). A plan whose cap axis is non-empty and whose slot axis is clean is likewise never FullyApplied, and a cap drift row names its directive and both values -- the srv1 pair reports MemoryMax 23622320128 -> 26843545600 and MemoryHigh 22548578304 -> 26843545600, and a drop-in whose managed directive already parses to the desired value is not reported as needing a value change.",
        out_of_scope: "Converge does not gain a cap drop-in actuator -- writing the drop-ins stays live_deploy's authority, and the fix is to stop rendering them as converge's mutations, not to start performing them. No new withholding cause and no relaxed one: what the retirement-evidence gate decides, it decides. live_deploy's own cap converge (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_cap_converge, live cgroup readback) is untouched, as is who has to write srv1's 25 GiB envelope.",
        handback: "The srv1 apply that reported 'applied' over 4 withheld teardowns and 2 plan-only cap rows now reports both counts and is not FullyApplied, and a srv1 converge whose plan really is empty still reports fully_applied -- the receipt says what the run did, in numbers, in both directions.",
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-bringup", contribution: "A host's runner slots stay healthy across its own convergence."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7QW3NVBMKHTCJ6Y2XDRPE5V0GT",
      id: "converge-plan-lists-the-withholds-the-obligation-and-actuation-gates-emit",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/runner/runner_slot_provision.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "plan.txt lists the obligation and ungranted-actuation withholds it today only echoes into apply.sh",
        boundary: "A host convergence plan's teardown script carries five kinds of withheld line: the required-retiree obligation gates (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision::obligation_withheld_line and gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision::obligation_withheld_scripts), the ungranted-actuation gate (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision::ungranted_actuation_withheld_scripts), and the tree-removal gate (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision::slot_removal_withheld_line). Only the last has a plan.txt row behind it -- plan.txt is rendered from the membership actions -- so on srv1 apply run 44428803079 the plan listed 4 REMOVEs while apply.sh echoed 43 __GUNBC_CONVERGE_WITHHELD__ lines. fleet-converge-receipt-counts-owed-work makes that gap VISIBLE as its own named number on the receipt; it does not close it, and it must not be read as having closed it. THIS ROW IS NOT DISPATCHED and waits on that one, because the gap cannot be closed by rendering those lines as REMOVE rows: a plan row asserts a member the plan wants REMOVED, and the obligation and actuation gates withhold units the plan does not want removed -- they are the standing obligations of a width reduction, not this plan's removals. Rendering them as REMOVE rows would move the member-set fingerprint, making the plan artifact assert a member-set it does not own. They need a grain of their own. THE OPEN QUESTION THIS ROW CARRIES: whether they belong in plan.txt beside the removals in a section named for what they are, or on the observation side of the plan, beside the other units whose retirement the host is waiting on.",
        displaced_cost: "An operator reading plan.txt sees 4 pending removals and no trace of the 39 other units the apply script will report as withheld; the only way to learn they exist today is to read apply.sh, after it has run.",
        first_slice: "Render the obligation and actuation withholds into a plan.txt section of their own -- named for what they are (units whose retirement this host owes and has not actuated), not as REMOVE rows -- and state which side of the plan they belong to and why.",
        red_control: "A width-reduction plan for a host with retiring slots lists the withheld obligation units in that section, and the section is EMPTY rather than absent when nothing is withheld; RED on main, where plan.txt is silent about them entirely.",
        out_of_scope: "The receipt's own numbers, which are the other row's; any change to the member-set fingerprint, which this row must not move; the retirement evidence the withholds are waiting on.",
        handback: "The section's grain and its place in the plan, the fingerprint's verdict on whether it moved, and the control with its red run on main."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-bringup", contribution: "A host's runner slots stay healthy across its own convergence."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_C9W3QF7HX2KD8M5TPR1VN6ZBL4",
      id: "fleet-converge-expected-revision-names-the-plan-revision",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_converge_workflow.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The fleet-converge dispatch tells the operator that expected_revision is the plan's revision, not main's",
        boundary: "The srv1 lab cutover (node lab-converges-release-pair) lost three cutover attempts because the operator passed expected_revision = the current main tip to the apply and deploy dispatches. The plan runs in its own earlier dispatch at revision P; the plan-revision job then emits P, and build, apply, dashboard_deploy and desired_instance_deploy all check out needs.build.outputs.revision, which is P (not github.sha). admit_optional_expected_revision is a cross-check of that checkout, so it compares the supplied expected_revision against P: a main tip M != P refuses with RunRevisionRefused naming expected M, observed P, and the cutover stalls even though every changed path since P was unrelated to the plan. The fix is NOT to relax that gate (no admission-rule change): dispatching with expected_revision = P already passes every gate whatever main does, proven on deploy test run 44488679086 (dispatched --ref main at 4c2f3046 with expected_revision = the plan revision 2561d29e; the 'Verify the checkout is the plan receipt's revision' step and every pointer admission passed). What was missing is the operator-facing statement. The dispatch input description (data `fleet_converge_expected_revision_input`) and the checkout-model comment above it in dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_converge_workflow.dag already say the checkout is the plan's revision and expected_revision is only a cross-check; they must now SAY TO THE OPERATOR that for apply, dashboard_deploy and desired_instance_deploy the value to pass is the plan's revision P (the same value plan-revision emits), never the current main tip, because the checkout is P and main's tip refuses by name. runbook docs/runbooks/roadmap-event-log-cutover.md:1092 states expected_revision is never omitted but does not say which revision it must name once a prior plan run exists.",
        displaced_cost: "Every future plan-then-apply-then-deploy cutover that reads expected_revision as 'the sha I dispatched at' re-loses the race, stalls on an admission that is correct, and burns a 37-minute plan plus a 22-minute apply before the deploy refuses; and a reviewer has to re-derive the checkout-at-P model from the workflow each time.",
        first_slice: "Amend the fleet_converge_expected_revision_input dispatch description and the checkout-model comment in fleet_converge_workflow.dag to state that at the plan-executing modes expected_revision must name the plan's revision (the value plan-revision emits into needs.plan-revision.outputs.revision), not the dispatched main tip, and regenerate .github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml through generated_artifact_gate main_wet. Add a sentence to the runbook's dispatch section. No change to admit_optional_expected_revision or any gate.",
        red_control: "A witness on the single shared admission admit_optional_expected_revision_given, modelled on the apply/deploy dispatch where the run's event sha (run_revision) is a main tip M but the checkout the build emitted (execution_revision) is the plan's revision P: expected_revision = P admits and the admitted revision is P; expected_revision absent admits and the admitted revision is P (proving the checkout followed the plan, not main); and RED — expected_revision = M (the main tip, != P) refuses with RunRevisionRefused naming expected M and observed P. The third arm is the red control: a cutover that names main's tip is refused by name, exactly the stall the docs now warn about.",
        out_of_scope: "Any change to the admission rule (admit_optional_expected_revision stays an exact cross-check; the earlier closure/semantic relaxation investigated on the prior slice of this row is ruled out by the 44488679086 result), the boot job's event-sha-only checkout, and the unrelated 30-minute downstream step timeout that later failed 44488679086 (proud-bat-272's).",
        handback: "The amended dispatch description and checkout-model comment, the regenerated fleet-converge.yml, the runbook sentence, and the admit_optional_expected_revision_given witness with its main-tip red arm green on srv1."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-bringup", contribution: "A host's runner slots stay healthy across its own convergence, and the cutover that converges them dispatches the plan's revision whatever main is."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_EP54CSQWDFDY1JRAD5Q0HJV8F8",
      id: "per-function-claim-run-loads-string-dispatched-names",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A per-function claim run reaches every function the modeled-realization dispatcher calls by name",
        boundary: "Found on 2026-11-15 while executing the fleet-cap-bracket-keeps-running-units controls (PR #16519). gunbc run --claim-run --function <fn> builds fn_nodes from the entry's import closure, but the modeled-realization dispatcher in the seed interpreter (run_in_context_with_args) looks up modeled_realization_admitted_in, operation_realization_duplicate, operation_realization_index, operation_handler_selection and virtual_clock_after by string. Those names are outside an isolated per-function closure that does not import them, so a witness whose closure misses the dispatcher's implicit dependencies refuses under a per-function run while the same function passes under a whole-tree claim_batch. Not every modeled-frame control is affected: #16519 recorded per-function controls that got past the dispatcher and failed on an ambient filesystem read instead. Adding a runtime_key_readers row and entry does not fix it, because realization_of has no caller on the run path (probe seed 087bf2bb). Repro: gunbc run --claim-run --source-root dag --source-root src --entry dag/test/claim/modeled_filesystem_witness.dag --function two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold fails on main (measured on #16519: about 75 s, 2.3 GiB). For an affected control the route that runs today is a whole-tree claim_batch (measured on #16519 at about 15 GiB and 30 minutes, and refused on page thrash on a busy shared host). v1 is semantics-frozen (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing); this is admitted only if it serves the v2 self-host program by making witness evidence executable. The claim-execution cutover deleted --claim-run; the per-function form is now `gunbc test --wet //test/claim/modeled_filesystem_witness:two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold`, and whether that route shares this loader defect is not measured.",
        displaced_cost: "An affected control has to be run as a whole-tree batch instead of a per-function run, and a per-function false failure is easy to mistake for a real one.",
        first_slice: "Name the string-dispatched functions as roots of the run's loaded index (or have the dispatcher realize through a declared import), so the per-function closure contains what the dispatcher calls.",
        red_control: "two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold passes under a per-function --claim-run and agrees with its whole-tree claim_batch verdict; RED on main.",
        out_of_scope: "The whole-tree claim_batch memory cost.",
        handback: "The route by which the dispatcher's callees enter the run's index, the control passing per function and failing on main, and the v1 standing classification."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A witness's verdict does not depend on how much of the tree the run loaded."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_S1393FFYNJXN8S95HKX6P1KSM8",
      id: "per-function-claim-refuses-after-admission",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Name the refusal a per-function claim run raises after admission for a witness that passes whole-tree",
        boundary: "Observation only; the fix is deferred. two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold passes under a whole-tree claim_batch (REAL_EXIT=0 at 6d2115d1e6e7; receipt ~/scratch/merry-deer-252/whole_6d2115d1e6e700671f0ee8317ae6a2e1dfa66da6.out on srv1) yet refuses under a per-function run. The refusal is raised after the run is admitted, by the seed interpreter after admission (v1_interpreter.rs, no symbol cited because none was named), in one of three places: envelope, identity or binding resolution. This row exists to say which, because per-function-claim-run-loads-string-dispatched-names names the string-dispatched callees as the cause and this witness may refuse for a different reason or an additional one. Measured at main 6d2115d1e6e7 (gunbc sha256 145e3307be263deba49d35d4833b864fb715525588a6d049e192bf65b70c66c2, claim_batch sha256 3dd8653479dae40d4bf07292d163adb55318931d2cd3d4abe42b10123b7ea249; merry-deer-252 via warm-fox-517): gunbc run --claim-run --source-root dag --source-root src --entry dag/test/claim/modeled_filesystem_witness.dag --function two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold prints exactly three lines, \"user_work_scope: skip wrap into gunbc-user-work.slice (BoundedByObservedCgroup)\", \"[workspace-root] discovered: /home/briansrls/scratch/merry-deer-252/gunbc\" and \"FAIL two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold\", with REAL_EXIT=1. There is no reason string: the path prints a verdict and nothing else, so the refusal is not observable today, which is the gap this row names. The whole-tree run of the same function at the same head returns \"PASS two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold\", REAL_EXIT=0; cite its re-run, not the first run, whose output a helper truncated to six lines and kept only the exit code. v1 is semantics-frozen (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing); nothing here authorises a seed change.",
        displaced_cost: "A per-function false failure reads as a real one, and the whole-tree batch that agrees costs about 15 GiB and 30 minutes; until the refusal is named, a repair aimed at the dispatcher's callees may leave this witness red.",
        first_slice: "A witness that runs the per-function command for two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold and names the refusal: the text, the position it is raised at and which of envelope, identity or binding resolution raised it, with the command, the sha and the binary hash. Because the path prints no reason, naming it needs an observation (a probe build or a debugger), not a log read; making the path print its reason is the fix and is deferred.",
        red_control: "The same function run whole-tree at the same sha passes and the per-function run refuses; both results are pasted raw with their exit status.",
        out_of_scope: "Any fix, any change to the interpreter, and a census of other witnesses that refuse per function.",
        handback: "The refusal's text, raise site and class (or, if no observation can name it, the statement of that), both raw runs with exit status, and whether per-function-claim-run-loads-string-dispatched-names covers it or needs a sibling repair."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A witness's verdict does not depend on how much of the tree the run loaded."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7JJ0WJ2PQXHREPZVSNDTMZFEYV",
      id: "per-function-claim-loader-modeled-dag-route",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/std/witness_evaluation.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "A per-function claim run reaches the names the modeled-realization dispatcher resolves by string through a declared .dag edge, and its refusal reason is observable",
        boundary: "Relayed, not recorded in gunbc.design_ruling (an authoring is in progress on another branch; cite its symbol in a follow-up when it lands): operator to neat-badger-614, relayed, verbatim '16910 - yeah agreed with your recommendation', at about 2026-11-23T22:12Z, the recommendation being no hand-written seed Rust for #16910's seed update or for the per-function claim loader. So this loader capability is modeled in .dag and no seed Rust grows. Measured by merry-deer-252 (held PR 16912 head e11f468a49bb, main 6d2115d1e6e7, gunbc sha256 145e3307be263deba49d35d4833b864fb715525588a6d049e192bf65b70c66c2, claim_batch sha256 3dd8653479dae40d4bf07292d163adb55318931d2cd3d4abe42b10123b7ea249, srv1 under heavy-slot): a per-function run's loaded index holds a declaration only when the closure REFERENCES it, and a listed-but-unreferenced import loads nothing, so names the dispatcher resolves by string are absent from an isolated closure. The five names are v2.std.operation_realization::modeled_realization_admitted_in, operation_realization_duplicate, operation_realization_index, operation_handler_selection and virtual_clock_after, consumed by v2.std.witness_evaluation::evaluate_in_witness_frame; their dependency is an undeclared fact (a string lookup) and a declared reference is the only edge the run's demand index follows. Only modeled_realization_admitted_in is demonstrated to fail to resolve at main; the other four read PASS on a probe that reads only the FIRST refusal reason, so they are UNMEASURED. A .dag-only edit referencing the five from v2.std.witness_evaluation moved exactly one limb (modeled_realization_admitted_in_resolved, per-function FAIL at main, PASS on the branch) but did not close the claim: two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold still fails per-function with REAL_EXIT=1 on the branch and passes whole-tree with REAL_EXIT=0. The admission predicate was never the refusal (the admission_predicate_admits_hermetic, _refuses_wet and _refuses_record limbs pass identically on unedited main). The remaining refusal sits after admission in the seed dispatcher (admit_modeled_realization onward in v1_interpreter.rs) and is UNOBSERVED: a per-function run prints no reason and the refusal is an Err that claims cannot observe. The refusal reason must be surfaced through a modeled .dag observation point, not by instrumenting the interpreter. Control asymmetry: gunbc run has no --hermetic (unexpected argument, exit 2) while claim_batch accepts it. The loader that decides what a per-function run loads today is seed Rust (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/demand_acquire.rs, seed-growth receipt gunbc.run_demand_acquire_seed_growth::run_demand_acquire_seed_growth_justification), and no modeled .dag claim-loading authority has been identified (UNMEASURED, not shown absent), so the row does not assume one. NOT MEASURED: any cost baseline for the per-function cells, the count of string-dispatched names corpus-wide (five is this dispatcher's, not a census), and the whole-tree wall and memory (about eleven minutes and ten gigabytes is recalled, not logged). The one recorded figure is two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold cpu=13ms wall=13ms eval_steps=2821 from the whole-tree witness line. closure_files=581 and demand_acquired_modules=581 on the real claim. Every figure is at main 6d2115d1e6e7 and stale for current main. Read by merry-deer-252 (relayed by warm-fox-517; read-only in a worktree that is not current origin/main, so re-read at the dispatch sha): a modeled .dag demand-acquisition authority EXISTS, v2.compiler.module_acquisition (decisions in v2.compiler.source_authority, closure checked by v2.compiler.reference_closure::reference_closure_ownership); its requestable set is imports and qualified references, and it states that a String literal is never a module reference and a bare name is not requestable. So the route is a declared reference, not a widening of that authority to read strings. v2.lens.module_graph is a lens over the same edges. Still UNMEASURED: whether any .dag authority models a per-function claim run's loaded index specifically (derived_roster and witness_admission claims were not read), the post-admission refusal reason and its observation point, and the four names other than modeled_realization_admitted_in.",
        displaced_cost: "An affected control runs only as a whole-tree claim_batch, and a per-function false failure prints a verdict and no reason, so it reads as a real failure and costs a slot to diagnose.",
        first_slice: "Establish whether any modeled .dag claim-loading authority exists (read, name its symbol as module::decl, or record that none does), then route the dispatcher's five callees to the run's index through a declared reference, and surface the post-admission refusal reason through a modeled .dag observation point.",
        red_control: "Red measured by merry-deer-252 (relayed by warm-fox-517; srv1 under heavy-slot, main 6d2115d1e6e700671f0ee8317ae6a2e1dfa66da6, gunbc sha256 145e3307be263deba49d35d4833b864fb715525588a6d049e192bf65b70c66c2, claim_batch sha256 3dd8653479dae40d4bf07292d163adb55318931d2cd3d4abe42b10123b7ea249; raw logs under srv1 ~/scratch/merry-deer-252/, not re-read here). Per-function, exit 1, one line FAIL two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold, no reason printed: gunbc run --claim-run --source-root dag --source-root src --entry dag/test/claim/modeled_filesystem_witness.dag --function two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold (via scripts/claim_batch). Whole-tree, exit 0, same claim PASS: claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/modeled_filesystem_witness.dag --functions two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold. Both are stale for current main, so the pair must be re-measured at the dispatch sha before it is relied on. Green: the per-function run passes and agrees with the whole-tree verdict at one sha, with the run's index containing the dispatcher's five callees; no green sha exists and none is claimed. OPEN: the observation-point pair (where the post-admission refusal is raised), which cannot be written until the observation point exists.",
        out_of_scope: "Any seed Rust, any change to the dispatcher's semantics or to the admission predicate, the whole-tree claim_batch memory cost, and a corpus-wide census of string-dispatched names.",
        handback: "The answer to whether a modeled claim-loading authority exists, the declared route by which the callees enter the run's index, the observation point and the post-admission reason it shows, and the per-function and whole-tree verdicts agreeing at one sha."
      ), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Red control made concrete and the row made dispatchable on measurements relayed by warm-fox-517 from merry-deer-252 (neat-badger-614: a row becomes dispatchable by a planning PR that writes a measured red_control). The red pair is stale for current main and is re-measured at the dispatch sha; green and the observation point stay OPEN. A dispatch is an ad hoc worker with acceptance owed until ctrl can mint work items for rows added after 2026-11-21.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A witness's verdict does not depend on how much of the tree the run loaded."),
    ),
    // Admitted 2026-11-24 by cool-crane-531 on royal-newt-240's finding in review 97779 (gunbc#16976): a run
    // has no channel for the value a function RETURNS, so every report in the corpus is delivered as a refusal
    // and a reading is told from a refusal by nothing but the words inside the refusal's sentence.
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_4LN7JV4MB3L2WLM67DC4Z0EHEI",
      id: "gunbc-run-success-output-surface",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs"), carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/main.rs")),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(fields(
        headline: "gunbc run has a success-output surface for a function's result, distinct from refusal",
        boundary: "MEASURED 2026-11-24 on main 8b434ce74d6cfbabe8efba0c55b0fea5fb4c4a4a with the release binary `gunbc b9f54f8f9cf3b50ad8ef29c2641d3ebe509c55a1` (sha256 c7e45d37a4c01418bade432d0bc25f636ed819b29bd0dd492e38205dd809f05a, whose `src/` is byte-identical to main: `git diff --stat b9f54f8f9cf origin/main -- src` prints nothing). One entry per invocation: `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 [--source-root <probe dir>] --entry <file> --function <name>`, the run's own progress lines stripped, stdout and stderr captured apart. A report and a refusal are ONE observation: exit 2, ZERO bytes on stdout, the payload only inside an error sentence on stderr. (i) the corpus report `floor_cost_debt_population_report` (src/v2/workflow/floor_cost_debt.dag:1158) -- exit 2, stdout empty, stderr `error: function `floor_cost_debt_population_report` returned `floor_cost_debt population: proven=311 censored=62 straddling=2 total=375`, not `ProcessExit`.` then `cause: the host maps a run's verdict to an exit code, and only ProcessExit carries one.` then `status: refused -- printing the value and exiting 0 would report success for a run whose outcome is unknown.` (ii) a probe returning the String `REFUSED: roster row 3 has no backing document` -- exit 2, stdout empty, the same wrapper sentence around the same position: a refusal stated as a value separates from a report by nothing but its words. (iii) a probe returning `ExitFailure { code: 2, reason: \"measured probe: a genuine refusal that carries code 2\" }` -- exit 2, stdout empty: the code a report is forced into is a code a genuine refusal may carry, so the status is not the tell either. (iv) a probe returning `ExitFailure { code: 1, reason: \"...\" }` -- exit 1, stdout empty, its reason on stderr. (v) a probe returning `ExitSuccess` -- exit 0 and NOTHING printed on either stream: the one shape that reaches 0 carries no bytes, so a successful run cannot report anything. (vi) a probe returning the String `line one of the report` + newline + `line two mentions `ProcessExit` and a quote` -- exit 2, stdout empty, and stderr prints the value across TWO REAL LINES with its own backticks unescaped inside the wrapper's backticks (stderr reads: `returned`, an opening backtick, the report's own two lines, a closing backtick, `, not`, a backtick-wrapped `ProcessExit`, a full stop): the wrapper's quoting is the value's quoting, so a reader cannot tell where the report ends. THE MAPPING, at file:line: `cli_run::classify_exit` (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs:18145) ends at cli_run.rs:18182 with `other => ExitClass::NotProcessExit { type_name: ctx.format_value(other) }` -- the returned VALUE is filed in the class field named for a type name -- and `exit_status_for_class` (cli_run.rs:18383) turns that arm into status 2 plus the message quoted in (i), at cli_run.rs:18398-18406; `Verdict::apply` (src/v1/stage0/src/main.rs:999-1008) prints every message with `eprintln!` and exits through `end_process_without_teardown(self.status)` at main.rs:1007. So the caller's payload arrives on stderr, mid-sentence, unquoted. THE SURFACE ALREADY EXISTS FOR ONE CARRIER, WHICH IS WHY THIS IS A GAP AND NOT A NEW INVENTION: `CliWirePrintable { bytes, exit }` (dag/gunbc/cli_wire.dag) is bound in the run verb and its bytes go to STDOUT with the exit the carrier itself declares (main.rs:1433-1460, `classify_cli_wire` and `cli_wire_outcome` at cli_run.rs:18224 and cli_run.rs:18327) -- measured: a probe returning `CliWirePrintable { bytes: \"wire report: 4 rows, 2 unbacked\", exit: ExitSuccess }` exits 0 with exactly those 31 bytes on stdout. Kernel `String` -- the type every report in the corpus returns -- has no such arm, so a report has to be delivered as a refusal. WHY THIS IS NOT COSMETIC: the criteria_digest an acceptance receipt pins is `roadmap_model::node_criteria_digest` (dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_model.dag:267) rendered by `serialize_content_hash(hash: Fnv1a64(...)) as String` (as dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_log.dag:573 does), and the only way to obtain it from the binary is a String-returning print: measured, a probe returning `h.digest as String` for the declared node `roadmap-criteria-digest-validated-at-write` exits 2 with the digest only inside the refusal sentence -- measured: `error: function `plan_digest_report` returned `roadmap-criteria-digest-validated-at-write digest 435db3716c37517d`, not `ProcessExit`.` at exit 2 with stdout empty. Two of the three legs the operator needs for one receipt (node, digest, red-control evidence) therefore arrive on the refusal channel, and a digest that reads back empty or truncated is indistinguishable from a run that genuinely refused. The row `roadmap-criteria-digest-validated-at-write` asks for exactly that command and does not have it (\"the runnable print command reproduces node_criteria_digest for a named node\"), and the cutover runbook records the ceiling one level up (docs/runbooks/roadmap-event-log-cutover.md:1434-1437: the runner \"cannot enter at all\" `roadmap_retired_node_ids_load` and `roadmap_acceptance_event_history_load` (dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_authority.dag:8339, :8313) \"because `gunbc run` requires a `ProcessExit`\", \"those three return DATA\"). THE WORKAROUND IS WRITTEN DOWN AS THE READING: src/v2/workflow/floor_cost_debt.dag:1142-1145 (\"The run REFUSES ... and it prints the returned String in the refusal, which is the reading\"), dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_launch_admission.dag:1191 (\"it refuses a String return and prints it, which is the read-out\"), dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_result_returned.dag:515-516 (\"a String because `gunbc run` prints a String return inside its typed envelope\"), dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_cli.dag:417-419 (the nonzero exit with the value quoted in the refusal text is \"the sanctioned way to read a value out of a run\"), dag/gunbc/instruments/instrument_registry_emit.dag:179-180 (a generated artifact's bytes come out through the refusal), and the split report of open PR gunbc#16976 carries the same admission -- the gap royal-newt-240 raised in review 97779 there. Sibling half, same shape one layer down: gunb-ai/gunbc#16995, \"a shell.Exec.Run payload never reaches stdout\", whose named consumer is ctrl -- its model entry points print their answer as a heredoc through `ctrl_report_script` into `shell.Exec.Run` for drivers to parse, and it registers a Rule 12 keystone `gunbc run answer channel` in `scripts/INVARIANTS.md`'s keystone registry with that issue as the dissolution trigger (gunb-ai/ctrl#2521 is the named follow-up for the models still printing). So ctrl is a NAMED CONSUMER of this row's hand-back and this channel is that keystone's trigger: when it lands the file-record channel retires, the models answer directly, and the exit code stays verdict-only. That ctrl side is not citable from ctrl's `origin/main` today -- `git grep -i \"answer channel\" origin/main` returns nothing there and `ctrl_report_script` is absent at that ref -- so ctrl is named as a consumer whose registration is ctrl's act to record, not as a fact this row asserts about ctrl's tree. Realization receipts, on the same measurement basis: the carrier a run's verdict reaches an operator through is `ProcessExit = ExitSuccess | ExitFailure { code, reason }` (dag/std/process.dag:10-12) and NO arm of it carries bytes, which is why a `String` has nowhere to go; `gunbc.cli_wire_host_admission` already names the capability that retires its own hand items -- delete `CliWireOutcome`, `cli_wire_outcome`, `exit_status_for_class` and their tests \"when std models a process's standard output and exit status as a carrier the .dag side can produce directly, so a command entry returns the whole host effect and the seed only executes it\" (dag/gunbc/cli_wire_host_admission.dag:178) -- and states that the seed-growth receipt \"does NOT admit them: the realization disposition is an operator judgment and fails closed in its absence\" (dag/gunbc/cli_wire_host_admission.dag:10); and `gunbc.cli_run_hand_rust_area_ledger` records that no emitting entry point can be named for any of its sixteen areas, so no `GenerateNow { emitting_entry }` row exists today (dag/gunbc/cli_run_hand_rust_area_ledger.dag:81). Boundary: WHICH CHANNELS `gunbc run` gives a function's RESULT, and which it gives a verdict. Not what a report says, and not how a refusal reports itself, which `ProcessExit` owns today and this row leaves where it is.",
        displaced_cost: "Every caller that wants a value out of a run pays twice: it must parse an error sentence, and it cannot use the exit code to notice a real failure, because the exit a reading arrives on (2) is a code a genuine refusal also carries (measured leg (iii)). The conflation is already written down elsewhere: dag/gunbc/hermetic_mock_fidelity.dag:110 records that a Bool return is refused -- \"returned true, not ProcessExit\" -- with the same status whether it returned true or false, and dag/test/claim/approve_ios_vectors_envelope_witness.dag:25-26 has to warn its own wrappers that a Bool false under `gunbc run --function` \"exits 2, which means \"did not return a ProcessExit\" and is NOT a verdict\". A report whose text holds a newline or a backtick misparses, since the value is spliced into the sentence raw (measured leg (vi)), so each caller invents its own quoting rule. And the acceptance recorder writes a throwaway module for every digest it needs, because `roadmap-criteria-digest-validated-at-write` makes its red control a runnable command that reproduces `node_criteria_digest` for a named node, \"so a recorder needs no throwaway module\" -- and there is none to run today.",
        first_slice: "Give `gunbc run` ONE success channel for the result a function returns: the value reaches stdout and the run exits 0, while a refusal keeps a non-zero status and its reason on stderr. Which return shapes own that channel, and what a refusal must still return to stay distinguishable, is the decision the implementation PR hands back; the existing `CliWirePrintable` arm (main.rs:1433-1460) is the precedent to engage with rather than re-coin, so the change mints no second bytes-to-the-operator authority beside `gunbc.cli_wire` (dag/gunbc/cli_wire.dag:1) and the render authority `std.render` (dag/std/render.dag:1) on `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority`, and it leaves `classify_exit` refusing whatever is not a `ProcessExit` verdict (the non-`ProcessExit` arms at cli_run.rs:18155-18158 and cli_run.rs:18172-18176). REALIZATION ROUTE, named rather than left to the implementer: the channel is modelled in `std.process`, where the run's verdict carrier already lives, and `src/v1/stage0/src/main.rs` is regenerated from the `.dag` authority that generates it (its first line reads `Generated by v1 compiler -- do not edit.`) and is never typed by hand; a hand-written arm in `classify_exit` / `exit_status_for_class` is hand seed Rust, so that route is the FALLBACK and needs the operator's realization ruling BEFORE the implementation PR. One return shape reaching the channel, under the two controls below, is the slice; migrating the corpus is not in it.",
        red_control: "RED, MEASURED 2026-11-24 at main 8b434ce74d6 with the binary named in the boundary: a String-returning function's result is readable ONLY from refusal text. `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/workflow/floor_cost_debt.dag --function floor_cost_debt_population_report` exits 2 with 0 bytes on stdout and the report inside the stderr sentence `error: function ... returned `floor_cost_debt population: proven=311 censored=62 straddling=2 total=375`, not `ProcessExit`.`; a function returning the String `REFUSED: roster row 3 has no backing document` exits 2 with 0 bytes on stdout in that same wrapper, as does `ExitFailure { code: 2, reason: ... }` -- so neither the channel nor the status separates a delivered report from a refusal. GREEN AT OPEN, to be named by the implementation commit: the same String result on stdout with EXIT 0, while each genuine refusal -- the `ExitFailure { code: 1 }` leg and the `code: 2` leg -- still exits non-zero, prints its reason on stderr, and puts nothing of the report on stdout.",
        out_of_scope: "Migrating the callers is a follow-up per caller, named here, not this row: floor_cost_debt_population_report (src/v2/workflow/floor_cost_debt.dag:1158); the split report of open PR gunbc#16976 (src/v2/workflow/floor_preparation_split.dag:62-66 on that head, whose comment admits the same reading); expected_design_rulings_md (dag/gunbc/design_ruling.dag:1534); instrument_registry_generated_text (dag/gunbc/instruments/instrument_registry_emit.dag:183); result_returned_report (dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_result_returned.dag:519); roadmap_event_standing_report (dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_cli.dag:420); roadmap_retired_node_ids_load and roadmap_acceptance_event_history_load (dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_authority.dag:8339, :8313), which the runbook says the runner cannot enter at all; launch_admission_contract_digest_hex (dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_launch_admission.dag:1204); unary_not_eval_receipt (src/v2/test/claim/unary_not_eval.dag:43); never_eliminator_native_receipt (src/v2/test/claim/never_eliminator_native.dag:106); floor_cost_distribution_report and floor_cost_envelope_report (dag/gunbc/instruments/floor_cost_distribution_instrument.dag:451, :626); parse_acceptance_census_for_paths (src/v2/compiler/parse_acceptance_census.dag:35); roster_import_sweep_for_paths and roster_import_sweep_lock_control_verdicts (src/v2/workflow/roster_import_sweep.dag:824, :4617); srv1_render_replica_engine_args (dag/gunbc/serving/srv1_serving_replica_layout.dag:2218); paired_timing (dag/gunbc/instruments/list_append_concat_paired_timing.dag:49); changed_surface_impact_report (dag/gunbc/instruments/module_impact_query_front_door.dag:414). Also out of scope: what a report says; how a refusal reports itself, which `ProcessExit` owns; the `gunbc.cli_wire` render authority itself; and the non-`ProcessExit` arms of `classify_exit` (cli_run.rs:18155-18158, cli_run.rs:18172-18176). Also out of scope, and named as a consumer's follow-up rather than this row's work: ctrl moving its file-channel models onto this channel -- the four already converted to a typed file record and the three gunb-ai/ctrl#2521 still prints -- and retiring the `gunbc run answer channel` Rule 12 keystone that landing this row triggers; and the `shell.Exec.Run` payload path gunb-ai/gunbc#16995 names as this row's sibling.",
        handback: "The interface change -- which return shapes reach stdout and with which status, and what a refusal must return so a reading and a refusal stay distinguishable -- written into the run's own contract with the file:line of the arm that implements it; plus both controls run at the named commits: the report readable on stdout at exit 0, and a genuine refusal still non-zero."
      ), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Admitted from royal-newt-240's finding in review 97779 on gunbc#16976. Every leg of the boundary was executed on 2026-11-24 by cool-crane-531 against `gunbc b9f54f8f9cf` at main 8b434ce74d6, one entry per invocation; the probe modules are quoted inline above so the legs reproduce without a checked-in fixture."), on: "2026-11-24", note: "REALIZATION ROUTE named in first_slice with its receipts in the boundary, and ctrl named as a consumer with gunb-ai/gunbc#16995 as this gap's sibling half -- both at neat-badger-614's instruction after review 97964. The route named is `std.process`, because the authority that admitted the `CliWirePrintable` precedent lists that exact capability as the trigger retiring its own hand items (dag/gunbc/cli_wire_host_admission.dag:178): minting the channel in seed Rust instead would keep an item its own receipt already plans to delete. The seed route stays available, but only behind the operator's realization disposition, which that same authority says fails closed in its absence (dag/gunbc/cli_wire_host_admission.dag:10).")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "An operator who runs a report gets the report on a success channel, so a non-zero exit means the run refused -- and never both.")
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_RS81HSP5Y9RCE4TE935FXJE1PM",
      id: "seed-claim-loader-loads-modeled-realization-callees",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The seed's per-function claim loader puts the modeled-realization dispatcher's callees in the run's index",
        boundary: "GATED on the operator's pending ruling on seed growth; not staffed and not dispatchable until that ruling is recorded by the operator. Measured by warm-fox-517 on srv1 under heavy-slot (PR 16912 head e11f468a merged with main 6d2115d1, gunbc 145e3307, claim_batch 3dd86534): the per-function run of two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold FAILs with REAL_EXIT=1 on main and on the branch, while the whole-tree claim_batch PASSes on both. The branch-side change does not close it, so the repair is on the seed side: the loader that builds a per-function run's index. This row owns that seed-side loader; per-function-claim-run-loads-string-dispatched-names keeps the verdict (the per-function run agrees with the whole-tree one) and depends on this row. v1 is semantics-frozen (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing): a seed change is admitted only when it serves the v2 self-host program, and a SeedGrowthJustification (gunbc.seed_growth::SeedGrowthJustification) is owed with the change. The carrier is the seed interpreter named in the sibling row; the exact loader function is to be verified by the worker.",
        displaced_cost: "Every affected control runs only as a whole-tree claim_batch (about 15 GiB and 30 minutes on #16519), and a per-function false failure reads as a real one.",
        first_slice: "Verify the loader entry point on the sibling row's carrier, then make the run's loaded index contain the functions the dispatcher looks up by name, with a SeedGrowthJustification naming the dissolution trigger.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at and green_at are not yet measured. The measured disagreement to turn green is two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold: per-function REAL_EXIT=1 and whole-tree claim_batch PASS, at the same sha, on main (gunbc 145e3307, claim_batch 3dd86534). Green is the per-function run passing and agreeing with the whole-tree verdict.",
        out_of_scope: "Any change to the dispatcher's semantics, the whole-tree claim_batch memory cost, and the branch-side change of PR 16912.",
        handback: "The loader change with its SeedGrowthJustification, the per-function run and the whole-tree run agreeing at one sha, and the v1 standing classification."
      ), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Relayed, not recorded in gunbc.design_ruling: operator to neat-badger-614, verbatim '16910 - yeah agreed with your recommendation', about 22:12Z; the recommendation was no hand-written seed Rust for the per-function claim loader. This row's seed-side route is therefore not the route; the capability is owned by per-function-claim-loader-modeled-dag-route. The measurements here stay as the record. Its disposition (withdrawn or kept as the abandoned route) is not decided here."), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Superseded by per-function-claim-loader-modeled-dag-route (rationale only; this text records no disposition and claims no standing). The operator ruled out hand-written seed Rust for the loader (relayed, not yet recorded in gunbc.design_ruling), so this seed-side route is not a pending route. Its measurements are kept as the record. The edge from per-function-claim-run-loads-string-dispatched-names to this row is removed in the same change, so the verdict does not depend on a rejected route (gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration). The ruling symbol replaces 'relayed' in a follow-up when the row merges.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A witness's verdict does not depend on how much of the tree the run loaded."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_H7RRZ8VBRSZ4Z7TFQTECZ5PF9F",
      id: "whole-corpus-diagnostic-census-callable-from-dag",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A .dag claim can count a diagnostic class across the whole corpus",
        boundary: "Requested by neat-badger-614 from bold-ibex-678's measurement for gunbc#16895 (floor-exhaustiveness-refusal). compile_dag_diagnostic_census takes one source string and the corpus walk is internal to the seed Rust, so no claim can count a diagnostic class across the corpus; a roster-equality claim can therefore only check a bounded fixture. The capability as currently shaped is seed Rust, which needs the operator's seed-admission call before anyone is staffed (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing); the relayed operator position against hand-written seed Rust for loaders is not recorded in gunbc.design_ruling, and this row does not assume a route. The roster-equality claim of floor-exhaustiveness-refusal is the first consumer that could become a whole-corpus check; no edge makes that row wait on this one, because it stands without it. The carrier names where the census entry point lives today and is to be verified by the worker. Nothing about the entry point's present signature beyond the one-string input is measured here.",
        displaced_cost: "A diagnostic class cannot be shown absent or exact across the corpus by a claim, so each such check rests on a fixture and a population change goes unseen.",
        first_slice: "Observation and design only until the admission call: read where the corpus walk lives, and name the smallest interface a .dag claim could call to count one diagnostic class.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at and green_at are not measured. The first pair would be a claim counting one diagnostic class over the whole corpus, red while no .dag-callable census exists.",
        out_of_scope: "Any seed edit before the operator's admission call, and the exhaustiveness refusal itself.",
        handback: "The admission call, then the interface by which a claim counts a diagnostic class over the whole corpus, with the claim run at one sha."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A witness's verdict does not depend on how much of the tree the run loaded."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_JN1Q7V9M3F0T7M0S358FWJQJSM",
      id: "release-bins-retention-witness-18-failures",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/test/claim/long/fleet_release_bins_key_witness.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The release-bins retention witness passes: its fake curl stub is well formed and its emission is accepted",
        boundary: "Observed by stern-wren-746 on srv1 with the released claim_batch b691 (main b6915594), --wet, at gunbc#16908 head 498089a4 (that PR only fixes the file's imports and the fixture's emitted-bin members): 18 FAIL and 44 of 62 PASS in dag/test/claim/long/fleet_release_bins_key_witness.dag, the #16596 retention family. Before #16908 main could not resolve the file (missing int_*/rooted imports), so these claims were unrun, not green. FAIL names (prefixed release_bins_): retention_over_cap_deletes_only_the_oldest_family_member, retention_delete_failure_is_typed_not_silent, retention_at_cap_has_nothing_due, retention_full_chore_deletes_from_its_own_answer, retention_parses_fractional_seconds, retention_orders_mixed_timestamp_shapes, retention_orders_within_a_second_by_fraction, retention_over_bound_types_total_and_deletes_nothing, retention_paged_delete_reaches_past_one_page, retention_window_spares_pr_ref_entries, retention_duplicate_ids_refuse_all_deletions, retention_stale_scratch_cannot_delete_on_failed_get, retention_page2_failure_refuses_to_delete, full_step_hit_reports_restore_and_nothing_due, full_step_zero_due_keeps_the_keep_window, full_step_get_fail_types_and_ignores_the_stale_answer, full_step_miss_builds_then_runs_the_chore, full_step_over_page_types_over_cap_and_promotes_anyway. Observed causes: (1) the fake curl stub (fake_curl_answering via fake_tool, #!/bin/sh) emits a broken loop, 'Syntax error: \"then\" unexpected (expecting \"do\")', so its answer file is never written (jq: Could not open file .../ws/release-bins-retention-answer.json); the suspect is the quoted-argument escaping in the for-loop line. (2) retention_stale_scratch_cannot_delete_on_failed_get: 'runtime error [type-error]: symbol_lexeme requires a Symbol argument', reached through v2.std.diagnostic diagnostics_reason_lexemes from a Rejected emission, so some retention part's bash emission is also refused. The raw log is srv1:~/scratch/stern-wren-746/out8/release_bins_key.log.",
        displaced_cost: "The retention chore's behaviour is covered by claims that cannot pass, so a regression in it is invisible and a reader cannot tell a broken stub from a broken chore.",
        first_slice: "Fix the fake curl stub's emitted loop so it writes its answer file, find which retention part's bash emission is Rejected and why, and re-run the file.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at and green_at are not measured on main. The measured failure is the 18 FAILs above at #16908 head 498089a4 with released claim_batch b691; green is all 62 claims PASS at one sha with the same binary.",
        out_of_scope: "The #16908 import and fixture fixes, the retention policy itself, and weakening any claim to make it pass.",
        handback: "The two causes repaired, the file's 62 claims passing with the raw PASS/FAIL lines and exit status, and the binary and sha they ran at."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "ci-end-to-end-execution", contribution: "A claim in the required population passes or is named as failing."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_8C203SGK4BRDSWTPEM7J0BPQD4",
      id: "serve-entry-verdict-path-is-per-run",
      owner: "demand-engine",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/live_deploy/pre_swap_admission.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The fleet-converge plan's artifact location is a per-run input carried through the plan, the swap and the workflow, not a constant under /tmp",
        boundary: "Ruled by neat-badger-614 to be a plan-to-swap contract change, not a step-local fix; requested by warm-fox-517 from gentle-tern-663's measurement. gunbc.live_deploy.pre_swap_admission serve_entry_verdict_path joins gunbc.fleet.fleet_plan_artifact_location fleet_converge_plan_artifact_dir, the constant /tmp/fleet-converge-plan, with serve_entry_verdict.json: no argument, spec field or environment override. The same row is consumed by the fleet_converge_workflow artifact upload and download, the fleet_converge_plan_cli directory creation, and observe_plan_serve_entry_verdict, where the swap job reads the verdict back from another job, plus the generated fleet-converge.yml. So a per-run path must be carried through the plan into the swap and the workflow, not changed at one step. Measured on srv1 (raw lines at https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16891#issuecomment-7103879443): the demand-serve step command ran 943.26 s (15:43) at 8,639,588 kB and exited 1 with Permission denied writing that shared fixed path, after a 12-minute witness had completed. Consequences: any two runs on the machine collide on one filename, a person-owned run cannot complete at all, and demand-serve-entry-compile-time is blocked on it because its restated red_control requires that program to complete on srv1 with its receipt. Measuring around it (mount namespaces, a CI substitution) is refused. gentle-tern-663 lands the fail-closed writability preflight separately; this row is the unblocking half. The generated fleet-converge.yml changes only through its authority and regeneration, never by hand",
        displaced_cost: "A run that did all its work fails at the last write because another session owns the fixed path, and two concurrent runs overwrite each other's verdict.",
        first_slice: "Make the artifact location a field of the plan (or run input the plan names), consume it at the verdict writer, at the swap job's read-back, in the artifact upload and download and in the plan CLI directory creation, and regenerate the workflow through its authority; no constant /tmp default remains a shared fixed path",
        red_control: "Red measured by eager-bat-800 on srv1 under the heavy-slot ledger at main 8b434ce74d6cfbabe8efba0c55b0fea5fb4c4a4a (acquisition 2026-11-24T07:00:09Z slot 4/12; HOST=srv1 BOOT=c095c0cd-1eaa-4bc7-861d-2bd9756c2bc4; systemd scope heavy-slot-240271.scope; interpreter /home/briansrls/scratch/eager-bat-800/gunbc/target/release/gunbc BUILT FROM 8b434ce74d6cfbabe8efba0c55b0fea5fb4c4a4a (cargo build --release -p v1-compiler --bin gunbc exit 0 in 9m50s; that tree git status shows 0 tracked changes, only the untracked scratch driver under dag/test/claim which is not part of the compiled crate) sha256 b76b09f242c71e9226d3fce1ae8a6d20e03fad3880ac8cd7816a78df0e4c92d3; raw log srv1 ~/scratch/eager-bat-800/red_probe_main.log). Two facts at main. (1) One shared path, no run input: the symbol serve_entry_verdict_path in pre_swap_admission.dag joins the symbol fleet_converge_plan_artifact_dir in fleet_plan_artifact_location.dag (the constant /tmp/fleet-converge-plan) with serve_entry_verdict.json and takes no argument, so the interpreter evaluates it to the single fixed path /tmp/fleet-converge-plan/serve_entry_verdict.json for every run (that fixed path appears verbatim in the refusal below). (2) The collision: running, as a non-ghrunner identity (briansrls), the production first branch of record_plan_serve_entry_verdict_for — probe_serve_entry_verdict_dir then serve_entry_verdict_dir_refusal_text then exit_failure — against current main, the fixed dir is held by the lab serve run (drwxr-xr-x 2 ghrunner ghrunner, serve_entry_verdict.json written 05:20 the same day), so the probe write fails: started Filesystem.Write /tmp/fleet-converge-plan/.serve_entry_verdict.probe (0 bytes); live_deploy: record_plan_serve_entry_compile_verdict — the verdict directory /tmp/fleet-converge-plan is not writable (Permission denied (os error 13)); refused before the served-command witness ran, so no verdict can be lost at the final write; REFUSAL_RC=1. A direct write by that same identity to the two fixed files (touch .serve_entry_verdict.probe, and truncate serve_entry_verdict.json) is likewise Permission denied, rc=1. This is the Permission-denied collision gentle-tern-663 measured (https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16891#issuecomment-7103879443, 943s and 8.6 GB spent before that final write), re-measured on current main. Green: a witness in which two concurrent runs with distinct run inputs each write and read back their own verdict without clobbering the other; RED is that same witness with the fixed path (proven above). green_at is not measured and no green sha is claimed.",
        out_of_scope: "The 15:43 and 8.6 GB cost of the step, the verdict's content, and any change to what pre-swap admission decides.",
        handback: "The run-input route chosen, the two-concurrent-runs witness with its raw PASS/FAIL lines and exit status, and the old constant's consumers named."
      ), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Red_control filled (red only, per neat-badger-614; STEP 2 not started). Measured by eager-bat-800 on srv1 under heavy-slot at main 8b434ce74d6c with an interpreter built from that same commit (cargo build --release -p v1-compiler --bin gunbc, tree 0 tracked changes, interpreter sha256 b76b09f242c71e92...). The fixed path /tmp/fleet-converge-plan/serve_entry_verdict.json takes no run input, and a non-ghrunner run's production probe refuses Permission denied (os error 13) at rc=1 — the collision gentle-tern-663 measured, re-measured on main. green_at stays OPEN; no green sha claimed. No mount namespace and no CI substitution was used (the row refuses both).")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "The served program is materialized once per key and reused across restarts."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_KS6BDNA0MQ3EYSS115JRW3GRPG",
      id: "standing-names-the-revision-it-evaluated",
      owner: "factory",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_serve.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A standing names the plan revision and carrier sha it was computed from, and a stale one refuses instead of rendering as accepted",
        boundary: "Requested by vivid-swift-693 and endorsed by neat-badger-614. The /standings.json response (StandingsJsonHandler in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_serve) carries no statement of the plan revision or carrier sha its standings were computed from. A standing whose row criteria_digest differs from the row at the revision a consumer reads must not render as accepted: it refuses as stale, naming both digests. Evidence: the lab runs c48e06d826 (2026-11-16) whose roadmap_authority.dag is 776,180 bytes against main's 1,160,496, and the srv1 carrier is 02c95a06 (2026-10-03), so an acceptance recorded against an old row can read as current against a new one. Single authority for the digest: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model node_criteria_digest; no second digest path is invented. srv1 ~/shared/node-digest already holds a digest probe that uses it (exit 2 when its controls fail, exit 3 on a lab move or a missing node, an empty value counted as failure) and a block gate (row block at two revisions, VERDICT=IDENTICAL or DIFFERS, self-test against planted mutations); those are existing evidence, not a second authority. A refusal is by exit or typed refusal, never by empty output, and the control outcome is carried next to the digest in the standing. Distinct from the carrier sync and lab advance themselves, which this row does not perform.",
        displaced_cost: "A consumer cannot tell an acceptance of the current criteria from one of criteria since edited, so a stale accepted reads as done.",
        first_slice: "Add the plan revision and carrier sha to the standings response, compute each digest with node_criteria_digest, carry the control outcome beside it, compare each accepted standing's recorded criteria_digest with the row's digest at that revision, and render a mismatch as a stale refusal naming both digests.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at and green_at are not measured. The control is a standings read where a row's recorded criteria_digest differs from its digest at the read revision: RED renders accepted, green refuses as stale naming both digests; and a matching digest still renders accepted.",
        out_of_scope: "Advancing the lab, syncing the srv1 carrier, and re-recording acceptances against edited rows.",
        handback: "The response fields, the stale refusal with both digests named, and the mismatch and match controls with their raw PASS/FAIL lines and exit status."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The daily workspace shows only what the tree at its revision supports."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_Y2N706Z00ETP0V247F1XECBY0B",
      id: "acceptance-recorder-names-its-durable-destination",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_cli.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The acceptance recorder prints the commit sha and ref it pushed, so its output alone verifies the effect",
        boundary: "Found by royal-newt-240 (run 02:17:11Z, GUNBC_EXIT=0): roadmap_acceptance_record_cli prints `started Filesystem.Write /tmp/gunbc-roadmap-event-snapshot.<id>/events/<node>/<hex>.json` and exits 0, and never prints the commit sha it pushed or the ref it pushed to. The durable store is the gunbc GitHub branch refs/heads/roadmap-events (the event 64bd9f29 is commit 10723280198ff955289ddd45240ff8e1cbf055e5 on it); the /tmp snapshot is the staging tree for that commit, so the run was NOT defective. But a reader of the output alone cannot verify the effect, which is how a false non-durability claim was published against the srv1 checkout at 02c95a06 (2026-10-03), 85 commits behind the branch. The earlier reading that acceptances were not durable is retracted and not cited. Boundary: what the recorder's success output names. Not the receipt grammar, not the digest computation, not the carrier sync policy, which is the operator's carrier item.",
        displaced_cost: "A reader cannot tell from the recorder's output where the event went, so a stale checkout is mistaken for a lost acceptance.",
        first_slice: "On success print the pushed commit sha and the ref, and on a push that did not complete exit non-zero naming the snapshot; carry it with the existing recorder work rather than as a separate surface.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at and green_at are not named as commits. The control is that the success output names a commit sha that is an ancestor of refs/heads/roadmap-events and contains the event file; the output today names neither (royal-newt-240, run 02:17:11Z).",
        out_of_scope: "The receipt grammar, the digest computation, the carrier sync, and the unresolvable witness module of #16914.",
        handback: "The recorder output naming sha and ref, and the control with its raw lines and the ancestor check against refs/heads/roadmap-events."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "ci-end-to-end-execution", contribution: "A claim in the required population passes or is named as failing."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_P9G8YTMA3YVQTW194Z3MBG3RM8",
      id: "list-append-refuses-an-element-argument",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/04_infer.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "list_append refuses an element where a list is required",
        boundary: "Found on 2026-11-15 by the deploy-artifact closure work (PR #16535, side chat finding F2). std.algebra list_append takes two FreeMonoid<T> values, but list_append([\"a\"], \"bc\") is accepted by the claim run and evaluates to [\"a\", \"bc\"]: a String reaches a FreeMonoid<T> parameter unchecked. This is below the ordinary floor (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder: values inhabit declared types), and it hides the list_push/list_append mix-up that authors make. Repro module: import std.algebra { list_append }, std.list { list_cover }, std.types { String, List, Bool }; fn eq_str(a: String, b: String) -> Bool { a == b }; test fn probe() -> Bool { list_cover(held: list_append([\"a\"], \"bc\"), expected: [\"a\", \"bc\"], eq: eq_str) } passes and must be refused. argument-type-compatibility-grounding covers the v2 exemption, not this generic-parameter case.",
        displaced_cost: "A wrong-type argument to a generic list operation runs and returns a plausible list, so the mistake is found only by a reviewer or a wrong answer downstream.",
        first_slice: "Find where the generic parameter binding admits a non-collection argument for FreeMonoid<T> and make it refuse with a located argument-type diagnostic.",
        red_control: "RED IS OBTAINED BY EXECUTION, NOT BY READING. WITNESS, MODULE AND LEGS BY NAME: dag/test/claim/text_at_free_monoid_run_carrier_witness.dag, seventeen legs, run on the claim route as separate operands -- gunbc test //test/claim/text_at_free_monoid_run_carrier_witness:<leg> -- with the batch own exit status on its own line and every leg named in its own HELD outcome=Pass line. THE PAIR THAT DECIDES THIS ROW: text_actual_at_run_of_string_is_refused_naming_the_right_parameter is the wrong case refused, naming the argument and the parameter it belongs to, and the_same_call_over_two_runs_is_not_refused is the right case accepted. list_push_takes_an_element_where_an_element_is_required keeps the element position working, so the wall cannot be bought by breaking list_append in general, and an_int_at_an_element_the_sibling_run_grounds_is_refused keeps a sibling argument from grounding the run carrier. RED AT is a commit on main where the repro is accepted: the parse control is executed with main released binaries and the claim route with a main-built gunbc labelled main-built, manifest-unmatched, with its sha256 read from disk in the same log as the heavy-slot acquisition line, and red counts only with identical failure text at the same main sha. GREEN AT is the node head reporting seventeen claim(s), seventeen held, zero did not hold, zero unobserved, rc 0.",
        out_of_scope: "Other generic-parameter positions, unless the same rule covers them.",
        handback: "The rule repaired and where, the controls, and a recurring_failure_mode row for the class."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "Generic collection parameters refuse a non-collection argument."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_9VRS5PZJDA30H78V0QH694Q70W",
      id: "effect-summary-env-carries-listed-imports",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/listed_imported_free_fn_named_like_an_algebra_method_has_no_effect_join_callee.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The effect summary finds a callee through the module's own imports",
        boundary: "PR #16555 repaired gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::listed_imported_free_fn_named_like_an_algebra_method_has_no_effect_join_callee by letting the census gates yield to a listed import. Its next trigger remains, scoped to the environment it was measured in: when an entry's effect summary runs over the sparse, namespace-only function env (129 parents, none declaring the imported skip, on the approval_broker_tree_install effect join reaching portable_remote_words), the env carries none of the module's listed imports, so callee identity there depends on the census fallback, while the resolve pass over a richer env (194 parents) binds the same call. Entries whose graphs supply the richer env already resolve: #16555 recorded a_binary_only_plan_installs_and_restarts_without_publishing_the_tree and a_twin_apply_neither_writes_nor_restarts_the_host_broker reaching host_effect_realize green on main. In the sparse env the two passes can disagree on which declaration a bare call binds to.",
        displaced_cost: "In the sparse env a call that resolves can still refuse effect joining, which blocks whole entries at resolve, as it blocked an_unbound_revision_refuses_before_any_observation until #16555.",
        first_slice: "None owed: the env change landed with #16555 and its listed-import witnesses (#16884, 8d3338b2). This is a coverage row: it records what is preserved and claims no red control.",
        red_control: "No red control is claimed, and none may be recorded for this row. Coverage: dag/test/claim/effect_summary_listed_import/listed_import_witness.dag claim listed_import_binds_the_effectful_declaration (roots dag and src/v2) PASSes at the parent a1948a5c923b2bc780fe6651aabfd04e8dd243fd and at 2eec3413d95b, claim_batch built at each tree (parent binary sha256 609b76cf2570141f17a57b2b0777dcb2bee1c709618122f1f4fc3feed7304b3b, exit 0; closing-candidate binary sha256 645418e1ed4ff9bb059c03bd9be249c405a892d3a5dcafc234f1e1ab52e3494d, exit 0). The six witness files were absent at both trees and only added, so the greens are not produced by code the PR brought, and the claim was never red at that pair: there is no closing commit to name. The two other limbs, s1_method_template_witness and s2_generic_witness, refuse to load at both trees (equality admission for an empty declaration identity cannot be judged, exit 1), a load refusal and not a verdict; they carry no pair, and claiming them is a separate choice for planning. The census fallback is not a control: call_target_for_direct_call and func_env_declared_func_sig answer before census_declaration_identity and func_sig_from_global_bare, so a probe cannot make its presence observable; whether its miss branch is reachable is established under effect-join-census-fallback-arm-removed.",
        out_of_scope: "Routing of non-imported method-template names to the method bridge.",
        handback: "The coverage record above, and the failure-mode row's rung stated at what the executed evidence shows."
      ), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Reclassified as a coverage row: the listed-import witness was never red at the candidate pair (warm-fox-517, quick-wolf-263)."), on: "2026-11-23", note: "RETIRE (warm-fox-517, quick-wolf-263): no isolable break exists, so no red control can be recorded. At b696faab46ac the witness asserts values (rival_marker() == \"rival-marker\" && shared_listed_probe_fn() == \"listed\") while an effect summary carries effects; both join failure arms are resolve-time diagnostics, not values (callee_edge_of_semantics and unjoinable_callee_edges in src/v1/04_service.dag emitting ResolvedCalleeRegistryRowAbsent, rendered in src/v1/04_infer.dag), and callee identity comes from the same inference call_semantics wiring that feeds the summary, so any cut hiding listed imports from the summary also destroys identity. A break yields either a refusal (the EntryResolveRefusal::ClosureDiagnostics arm of claim_batch, not a control) or a silently skipped join that still binds and answers PASS. The only false-answer path is binding a bare call to the rival declaration, which needs the closure-census fallback restored, a multi-site change and not a minimal break. Executed: witness PASS exit 0 at 2eec3413d95b with claim_batch 645418e1 and at a1948a5c923b with 609b76cf; FAIL with a closure-diagnostics refusal at break a41eeef9d6ea over red_base b696faab46ac with binary fd775eb0. The retirement itself is a roadmap event-log event, not a row edit; the service-mock and shape question has no owning row yet.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "Resolve and effect summary agree on a call's callee."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_X5XSR3QY6G0J91JHYJ0S317PFS",
      id: "fabric-slot-roster-covers-srv3",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/runner/runner_slot_allocation.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The fabric slot roster and the released-set control agree on which hosts carry fabric slots",
        boundary: "test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness a_fabric_slot_is_never_in_the_released_set fails on main: it requires a nonempty srv3 fabric population, but gunbc.runner.runner_slot_allocation fabric_execution_slot_identities lists only the two srv1 slots, so runner_host_fabric_member_units(\"srv3\") is empty. Either the roster is missing srv3's fabric slots or the control names a host that carries none. Found during PR #16519 (88 of 89 controls pass; this one was red before and after).",
        displaced_cost: "A control that is red on main for a data reason trains readers to ignore red in the witness, which hides a real regression.",
        first_slice: "Read srv3's current runner layout and decide whether it carries fabric slots; correct the roster or the control to match.",
        red_control: "a_fabric_slot_is_never_in_the_released_set passes over a nonempty fabric population for the host it names; RED on main.",
        out_of_scope: "Moving any runner unit on srv3 or srv1.",
        handback: "The srv3 layout reading with its source, the corrected roster or control, and the control passing."
      ), on: "2026-11-18", note: "THE CONTROL WAS THE STALE SIDE; THE ROSTER WAS FRESH.\n\nThe srv3 layout reading the handback asked for is a ruling, not an observation to go fetch: gunbc.design_ruling::srv3_srv4_fabric_slots_serve_ci (operator, 2026-11-09) retired srv3's and srv4's fabric execution slots and gave every committed slot on either host to GitHub Actions, gunbc.runner.runner_slot_retirement runner_fabric_slot_retirement_carries_removal keeps each retired cell refusing a grant, and gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision (the slot 11/12 reading) states that the host carrying a fabric member today is srv1 ALONE. The same population is asserted at length two elsewhere: test.claim.runner.runner_slot_retirement_witness pins fabric_execution_slot_identities to two members, and test.claim.runner.runner_service_activation_witness says outright that it holds no srv3 member at all. So the roster's two srv1 members (13 microVM shakedown, 14 revision job) are correct, and runner_host_fabric_member_units(host: srv3) being empty is the ruling rather than a hole in the roster.\n\nWHAT WAS FIXED, THEN, IS THE CONTROL: it named srv3 as a literal, so it failed on a host the operator had emptied instead of on the release it claims to check. It now takes its subject from fabric_execution_slot_identities and refuses when that roster is empty -- an empty population has no unit to keep out of the released set, so the disjointness would be vacuously true; an emptied roster is a finding, not a pass. That keeps the fix from being undone by the next ruling that moves a slot. The stale restatement in gunbc/runner/runner_host_file_converge.dag that transcribed srv3/srv4 slots 6 and 7 as fabric members now names the roster instead of copying it.\n\nEVIDENCE AND STANDING: red on main reproduced at d3e46b86c4ef (FAIL a_fabric_slot_is_never_in_the_released_set); the corrected control passes by claim-run, one function per process, and the sweep of the file's other controls was waived by the dispatching manager on the ground that this edit adds no helper, edits no other control, and leaves the roster it reads untouched -- so nothing else in the file could have moved. NOT accepted -- the standing here is fixed-pending-review; acceptance stays with the operator and the belt observes it.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-bringup", contribution: "The slot roster matches the hosts that carry slots."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_20NKA9WYGMKXA5JPA4YM8KXD5X",
      id: "deploy-release-roster-carries-every-owned-step",
      owner: "debt",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/live_deploy/member_observe.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The release roster observes every member the deploy owns, so an all-kept plan clears the artifact gate in production",
        boundary: "Found while landing the deploy-artifact closure gate (PR #16587, 2026-11-17). The gate (gunbc.live_deploy.apply_legs deploy_artifact_closure_gate) counts an artifact as present when the release plan verified it KEPT, through plan_kept_owned_artifacts. gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe deployment_member_roster does not carry two of the deploy's owned steps: the attempt-unit drain path unit (AttemptUnitDrainPathUnit) and the approval broker front door (ApprovalBrokerFrontDoor). The production verifier therefore never emits a KEEP row for them. A plan that keeps everything halts at the gate on their reads (the launcher snapshot directory; the broker release tree and its digest env file) even when they are installed. That is fail-closed, not a false admission. The witness test.claim.live_deploy.live_deploy_apply_plan_witness all_kept_roster appends both members by hand to show the gate's keep coverage, so that control does not exercise the production roster for these two.",
        displaced_cost: "An unchanged redeploy of srv1 halts at the artifact gate until someone writes the two members into the plan by hand or forces a rewrite, and each halt costs a read of the refusal.",
        first_slice: "Give each of the two member kinds its own desired and observed identity, grounded in what it is: the drain path unit is a systemd unit file, and the broker front door is a Tailscale serve route. gunbc.live_deploy.emit identity_member_of_step binds both as DirectoryRoot today, and member_observe reads a DirectoryRoot as a directory's standing, which verifies neither. Then add both to deployment_member_roster through that per-kind identity. Adding DirectoryRoot rows to the roster does not satisfy this node.",
        red_control: "(1) Through the production observation path (desired_member_identity and observed_member_on_host over a supplied host reading), each member kind yields KeepMember when its installed identity equals the desired one, and a rewrite when it differs (a drifted unit file; a route serving another backend). RED on main, where neither kind has an observation of its own. (2) As a separate consumer check, the_all_kept_plan_clears_the_deploy_artifact_gate passes with the production deployment_member_roster and no hand-appended members. converged_effect_plan assigns KeepMember without observing, so (2) alone does not accept this node.",
        out_of_scope: "Reader ordering after the tree converger (integration concern deploy-readers-must-order-after-tree-converger).",
        handback: "The per-kind desired and observed identities with the upstream each is grounded in, the observation controls (keep and drift for each kind) passing and red on main, the gate consumer check on the production roster, and all_kept_roster deleted from the witness."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "A redeploy that changes nothing proceeds without a hand step."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_3E5NJVBW4DA73A581DTT7APKC7",
      id: "factory-dogfood-route",
      owner: "harness",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_dogfood_route.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "One request travels the whole factory and comes back as an independently reviewed, published candidate",
        boundary: "The dogfood route as one acceptance case: request, immutable subject, shared computation, placement grant, isolated execution, durable result, metering, independent review, candidate published, cleanup, result returned (production order: the belt reviews a head before publishing it) -- each established by its own typed record from the durable records the real srv2 route wrote for ONE attempt (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dogfood_route DogfoodRouteReceipt). The start receipt is the first complete attempt, selected in refname order, by the first successful recorder to observe one (scanning durable attempt history), recorded once, create-only; attempts operated by hand before the route existed do not qualify.",
        displaced_cost: "Without one executable case the factory is a set of stages that each pass alone while no request has crossed them all, and the operator's confidence -- the gate for the first external customer -- has nothing to rest on.",
        first_slice: "The receipt and its acceptance function, red with three stages owed, each to the change that writes its own record: G1 cutover (immutable subject, shared computation) and G5 isolated execution, owed to a record binding the granted unit's observed start and exit to its grant and fence. Produced and carried through the complete arm and the start receipt: the request (G4 request-binding record), placement grant and cleanup (G5, cleanup returning the placed grant and fence), metering (a Final G3 metering record), and the result returned (G4, a published result answering the request's claim at the submission's head). The start receipt also pins the attempt's joined service evidence (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_service_evidence) bound to its launch record",
        red_control: "A reading set with a stage missing or read twice is malformed, not judged; one owed or refused stage withholds the receipt and names it; an unreadable attempt population does not pass.",
        out_of_scope: "MicroVM isolation (a capped systemd unit plus a lease is the dogfood bar, operator ruling 2026-10-03); billing and pricing; a reviewer on a different model (same model, separate context window, operator ruling 2026-10-03).",
        handback: "The dogfood start receipt: the first attempt on srv2 whose DogfoodRouteReceipt is complete, read by the acceptance function."
      ), on: "2026-10-03", note: "Operator ruling 2026-10-03: the dogfood clock is what matters most for the first-external target."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. dogfood_route_receipt already derives gaps from stage readings. The remaining work is one complete real attempt after G1 and isolated-execution producers land, plus the start receipt. Reuse the acceptance function and retain explicit owed stages until evidence exists.")),
      execution: bound(contract: dogfood_route_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The factory is proven by one request crossing every stage on the real route, not by each stage passing alone."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_8JYZHD6GVDME0EYZ3PX0QRBD0Z",
      id: "dogfood-g1-shared-computation-record",
      owner: "harness",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_dogfood_route.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Dogfood G1: the immutable subject and the shared computation are each established by their own record, read by the route's receipt",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.factory_dogfood, layer 2 (section 3). The stage factory-dogfood-route's first slice owes to G1: one attempt's verification runs through the materialization provider over the bounded store, and the receipt reads an immutable-subject record and a shared-computation record written by that run (the reader gunb-ai/gunbc#13097 declared as a frontier, shared_computation_observe_for_attempt, consumed by DogfoodRouteReceipt). Lands alone against main after factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease, so there is one writer of attempt records to bind to; never as a stack.",
          displaced_cost: "gunb-ai/gunbc#13097 carried this work and closed unmerged on 2026-10-09: a stacked PR whose base moved, a conflict in the generated emit file, and seven witness failures identical on main. Until the record exists the route's receipt is withheld at this stage and the dogfood window cannot start.",
          first_slice: "The reader consumed: DogfoodRouteReceipt reads the shared-computation record of one real attempt, with SharedComputationAbsent typed by its closed cause, and refuses on an attempt that has none.",
          red_control: "An attempt whose verification did not go through the provider yields SharedComputationAbsent with its cause, never a complete stage; a receipt read over a record from another attempt refuses; deleting the reader's consumer makes the route's acceptance red.",
          out_of_scope: "Metering (G3, landed), result returned (G4, landed), isolated execution (G5, its own node); the belt-to-fabric cut itself.",
          handback: "The two records written by one real attempt on the route, the receipt reading them, and the stage no longer owed."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dogfood_route::DogfoodStageReadings still types immutable_subject and shared_computation as ProducerPendingReading. The route cannot construct evidence from those placeholders. Implement the real attempt records and bind the reader; service-evidence-capture reuses that producer rather than building it again.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "Layer 2 of gunbc.plans.factory_dogfood: the one dogfood stage whose record was attempted and lost to a stacked base."),
      centering: plan(text: "One real attempt only, after factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease: verification through the materialization provider over the bounded store, the shared-computation record written by that run, DogfoodRouteReceipt reading it, SharedComputationAbsent typed on an attempt without one. Lands alone against main; never as a stack. Hand back the records and the receipt's reading."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_X05JQFPT0MQG81ASDVDNMXTXAF",
      id: "dogfood-g5-isolated-execution-record",
      owner: "harness",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_dogfood_route.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Dogfood G5: a record binds the granted unit's observed start and exit to its grant and fence, and cleanup returns both",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.factory_dogfood, layer 2 (section 3). The stage factory-dogfood-route's first slice owes to G5: one attempt runs as a capped systemd unit under a placement grant and a fence (the dogfood bar, operator ruling 2026-10-03; microVM isolation out of scope), and a record binds the unit's observed start and exit to that grant and fence; cleanup returns the grant and the fence and is its own record. The receipt reads both.",
          displaced_cost: "Without the record the route can show a placed grant and a finished unit without being able to say they were the same attempt, so isolation is asserted, not observed; the stage is owed and the receipt withheld.",
          first_slice: "One real attempt's unit start and exit observed and bound to its grant record, read by the receipt; its RED a unit record naming another attempt's grant, refused.",
          red_control: "A unit record whose grant or fence names another attempt refuses; an attempt with a grant and no unit record is owed, never complete; cleanup that does not return the placed grant keeps the stage owed.",
          out_of_scope: "MicroVM isolation (F5, microvm-runtime-durable-state); the G1 records; billing.",
          handback: "The binding and cleanup records of one real attempt, the receipt reading them, and the stage no longer owed."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. DogfoodStageReadings still marks isolated_execution pending while placement and cleanup have typed readings. Residual is observing start/exit and binding them to the same grant/fence, with foreign-grant refusal. Do not rebuild placement or charge cleanup as an unrelated new allocator.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "Layer 2 of gunbc.plans.factory_dogfood: the dogfood stage that had no record and no node."),
      centering: plan(text: "One real attempt only, on srv2's capped-unit route: bind the unit's observed start and exit to its placement grant and fence in one record, have DogfoodRouteReceipt read it, and plant a record naming another attempt's grant to show the refusal. Hand back the record, the receipt's reading, and the planted refusal."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_TCZ82BX9PRSBAW1Z4WVSFQT023",
      id: "fabric-worker-event-log",
      owner: "harness",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/fabric/fabric_event_log.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Publish each attempt's worker events to the fabric event log",
        boundary: "The harness's per-attempt worker events, today appended only to a host-local provider-events.jsonl that gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_provider_events reads, are appended to gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log as a new payload kind over its existing partitions (product.capacity.event_chain), one partition per attempt. Any consumer then reads an attempt's events from the fabric rather than from a file on the worker's host.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it, every live view depends on sharing a filesystem with the worker, and streaming cannot go through the fabric as ruled.",
        first_slice: "Define the worker round/item payload over the existing fabric event log, connect its append producer, and project one attempt after a cursor through event_log_read_partition_with.",
        red_control: "An attempt's events read from the log equal the events the harness produced, in order, with no gap or duplicate across a reader restart; an append the log refuses is a typed refusal, not a silent drop.",
        out_of_scope: "The held-open HTTP response, any change to what the events are, and any second transport.",
        handback: "The payload kind, the append and read paths, and the order, gap and refusal receipts."
      ), on: "2026-10-05", note: "Not yet centered: needs a centering plan: authored 2026-10-05 with no attempts. Owner ruling 2026-10-05: event streaming goes through the fabric, not a tail of a host-local file. This row is the prerequisite of serve-held-open-response, declared as a dependency edge."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log::event_log_append_with and event_log_read_partition_with already provide generic storage mechanics. Residual is the worker event payload, its attempt/cursor reader and order/gap/refusal evidence. Avoid implementing a second log or charging generic append/read from scratch.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "A worker's events must be readable from the fabric before any live view can stream them without sharing the worker's filesystem."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_92JGQNTZK8FJC0X8C6AS7HZRYS",
      id: "serve-held-open-response",
      owner: "harness",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/extdeps/http/server.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Let the server keep a response open and send events as they happen",
        boundary: "gunbc serve gains a response kind that stays open and writes a sequence of events, beside today's whole-body response (extdeps.http.server ServeHttpResponse has only body: String). It delivers one attempt's events as read from the fabric's event log (gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log over product.capacity.event_chain), never from a file on the serving host. The first consumer is the per-attempt event cursor: the same events the cursor poll returns, delivered as they are appended.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it, every live view polls and rebuilds its whole answer every two seconds, and a progress view can only be as fresh as its poll.",
        first_slice: "One held-open route that reads one attempt's events from the fabric from a given cursor and resumes from the last one the client saw.",
        red_control: "A reconnect with a cursor never repeats or skips an event; a closed client releases the server's resources; a handler that cannot stream refuses instead of buffering silently.",
        out_of_scope: "No second transport beside the fabric, and no change to what the events are.",
        handback: "The response kind, the route, and receipts for resume and disconnect."
      ), on: "2026-10-04", note: "Not yet centered: needs a centering plan: authored 2026-10-04 with no attempts. Owner ruling 2026-10-05: event streaming goes through the fabric, not a tail of a host-local file. Read on that date: gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log is generic over its event payload, but its only payloads are pool, redemption and pair-serving authority events; a worker's events live in a file its attempt owns (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_provider_events). Publishing them to the fabric log is its own row, fabric-worker-event-log, and this row's declared prerequisite edge."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. extdeps.http.server::ServeHttpResponse and ServeWireResponse carry a complete String body. They do not model a held-open event response. This node needs the response domain and realization before the resumable route, with disconnect cleanup; ordinary static response support is reused.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "Live views of working agents need events delivered as they happen, not rebuilt on a timer."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_VQ8RGFT438E36PHK9WXJ5TCJMC",
      id: "v2-compiler-live",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: [
        Pointer { label: "authority", path: "dag/gunbc/compiler_frontend_program_interlock.dag" },
        Pointer { label: "plan", path: "dag/gunbc/plans/v2_self_host.dag" },
      ],
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "The new compiler is the one that runs",
          boundary: "v2 reads, names, types and emits the whole corpus. It builds itself, then rebuilds itself. It is the required native route, admitted for production, and the v1 seed is retired. No work sits on this node; the work lives in its eight member projects.",
          approach: "Order: frontend first (the native seven, then the whole corpus), then generations (a second build made by the built CLI), then the native route made required and admitted (D10), then the seed retired. gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_interlock owns this order, and this node does not restate it.",
          red_control: "Seed retirement stays unreachable while any SelfHostSeedRetirement prerequisite in gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_status reads OUTSTANDING. A v2 task whose membership walk does not reach this node refuses as unrooted.",
          displaced_cost: "v2 work is spread over about 12 disconnected roadmap components, and the page's focus filter hid most of them. So nobody can tell whether a v2 PR moves the compiler closer to running.",
          handback: "SelfHostSeedRetirement reads CLEAR in gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_status, and every member project's handback is met."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "gunbc-project-root", contribution: "Self-hosting is the root's identity. This program makes the self-hosted compiler the one that actually runs, and it ends when the old seed is gone."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_5A53SMVX18G72TGH0215TV1HYM",
      id: "universe-ingest-replaces-file-acquisition",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/module_acquisition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "The bundle is ingested into one universe of declarations and the files are discarded",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.v2_self_host, the vision-realized milestone (its second done-when list), layer 5. gunbc.design_ruling::source_is_ingested_into_one_universe_and_files_are_discarded: one ingest step takes the source bundle, parses it, publishes every declaration by its full path into the universe, keeps a declaration-to-text mapping for literals and locations only, and discards the files; v2.compiler.module_acquisition and v2.compiler.source_authority become that step's realization, gunbc.source_layout and the two-tree layout become its mapping, and nothing after ingest names a file. Two providers for one path refuse at ingest. A test declaration is an ordinary declaration whose selection is a property of the subject.",
          displaced_cost: "Every stage after acquisition today can name a file, a tree or a module header, so meaning depends on where a declaration was stored and the compiler carries file concerns everywhere; the operator's vision is a file-less system where things are purely named.",
          first_slice: "One subject ingested from a bundle, every stage after it reading declarations by path only, with the text mapping answering one literal's location; its RED a stage that reads a path after ingest, refused in review by the phase-admission domain.",
          red_control: "A declaration moved between files in the bundle changes no identity and no behavior; two bundles with the same declarations in different files yield the same universe; a duplicate path refuses at ingest naming both providers; no stage after ingest consumes a file path.",
          out_of_scope: "Fracturing the universe (one universe for now); sugar for headers or shorter spellings.",
          handback: "The ingest step executing on the native route with its controls, the stages after it free of file names, and the mapping as the only survivor of the files."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. v2.compiler.module_acquisition already has HeldSourceRead, acquire_closure_of and acquire_verified. Those are reusable acquisition machinery, not proof that later stages read only a declaration universe. Residual is the bundle/universe boundary and removing actual post-ingest acquisition dependencies while preserving diagnostic mappings.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The vision's first separation: code from the files that carried it."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_YXN3SJDH0F69CMYJSVDK1R9RA5",
      id: "one-declaration-identity-carrier",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/std/decl_ref.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "One structural declaration identity, rendered with dots, used by every consumer",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.v2_self_host, the vision-realized milestone (its second done-when list), layer 5. std.decl_ref DeclarationRef (module path, declaration name, tagged member coordinate) and v2.std.qualified_name QualifiedName (a symbol sequence) become one carrier: a nonempty path plus a tagged member or type-parameter coordinate; equality, hashing, dependency edges, citations, generated-provider demands and resolver output all use it; dots are its one rendering, citations included, and `::` is retired from std.decl_ref's display key, the citation grammar and the sweep. A path names exactly one thing (zero violations today).",
          displaced_cost: "Two carriers for one identity, and two spellings for one path, are a fork by gunbc.design_argument::single_authority; std.decl_ref itself warns that its display key can collapse distinct references.",
          first_slice: "The merged carrier with the equality and rendering laws as claims, and the sweep's citation check reading it; the citation grammar accepting dots.",
          red_control: "Two references equal by rendering and distinct by structure refuse to compare equal; a citation with `::` refuses after the cut; a path that is both a prefix and a declaration refuses.",
          out_of_scope: "Shorter spellings or sugar.",
          handback: "One carrier, its laws executing, `::` gone from the tree."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. std.decl_ref already owns equality, ordering, member coordinates and identity. declaration_ref_display_key still renders ::, so dotted rendering/grammar migration remains. Reuse the existing laws; preserve field versus type-parameter coordinates rather than flattening both to ambiguous text.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The vision's identity law: one structure, one rendering."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_M9XZQ1K5Y7756T4C5FWQ8Z3CKS",
      id: "sealed-phases-and-the-checked-carrier",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/normalized_tree.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Four sealed phases, and evaluation and emission consume only the checked carrier",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.v2_self_host, the vision-realized milestone (its second done-when list), layer 5. gunbc.design_ruling::phase_admission_is_a_conformance_pattern and the conformance domain conformance-phase-admission: the compiler has four phases, parsed, resolved, checked, emitted, each a sole_constructor carrier (ParseTree stops being a bare Node alias); a CheckedProgram exists whose constructor proves every reference resolves, every obligation is discharged, every target-required operation has a realization and no provider is unavailable; evaluation and emission accept nothing else. A partial analysis (GroundingNotDerived, an unresolved provider) may exist for tooling and never reaches a build.",
          displaced_cost: "A bare Node can be handed to any stage as if a phase had established it, and partial facts reach emission; the alternative kept today is a roster of tolerated unknowns, which the operator ruled out as a ratchet.",
          first_slice: "ParseTree sealed, with the RED a resolve called on a Node that no parse produced.",
          red_control: "A stage constructed from a raw representation refuses at the type; a program with one not-derived grounding has no CheckedProgram; the evaluator and the emitter have no input type but CheckedProgram.",
          out_of_scope: "What each phase establishes (its own module); the eight-phase ladder the audit sketched (four is the ruling).",
          handback: "The four carriers sealed, CheckedProgram consumed by both the evaluator and the emitter, and the last roster of tolerated unknowns deleted."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. v2.compiler.normalized_tree::NormalizedTree is already sole_constructor. Do not charge sealing it again or infer that all phase boundaries are sealed. The remaining CheckedProgram proof obligations and evaluator/emitter consumers need a real end-to-end constructor path with failure controls.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The vision's phase law: states are types and transitions are their only constructors."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_914G3PJ530KJHSZT5K1EV78SCE",
      id: "typed-refusals-own-control-flow",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/std/diagnostic.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Production code branches on typed refusals; diagnostics render them",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.v2_self_host, the vision-realized milestone (its second done-when list), layer 5. Every v2 production outcome that a caller branches on is a closed refusal type with its located evidence; a Diagnostic is a rendering of such a value for an audience and is read by no production module to decide anything. The 32 production modules under src/v2 that read diagnostics_fatal_reason today (2026-11-17 count) branch on the typed value instead.",
          displaced_cost: "A rendered reason symbol stands in for a closed type at 32 sites, so message wording is semantics and a renamed reason is a silent behavior change.",
          first_slice: "One resolve outcome made a closed type, its two production readers moved to it, with the RED a reason-symbol read that no longer compiles.",
          red_control: "No production module under src/v2 reads diagnostics_fatal_reason or matches a rendered string; a refusal's wording can change with no claim changing.",
          out_of_scope: "Diagnostic rendering policy (audience, wording).",
          handback: "Zero production readers of reason symbols, the closed refusal types, and the renderer as their only consumer."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The resolver has typed outcomes and diagnostics, but existing diagnostic reason readers are not all control-flow authorities. Group actual decisions by owning outcome, retain renderers, and move compatible consumers together. The old module count does not establish the number of missing variants.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The vision's failure law: typed, located, rendered after."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_88E7PHHNRJ71E3ZB8JHSM3FDM8",
      id: "one-text-carrier",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/std/text.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "One text carrier, a sequence of Unicode scalars, with the host crossing as its only wrapper",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.v2_self_host, the vision-realized milestone (its second done-when list), layer 5. v2.std.text String (FreeMonoid<Char>) and the kernel String are one carrier for one meaning; bytes decode to it with stated fidelity; identifiers and symbols are not arbitrary text; a host string appears only at an explicit effect or wire boundary through the one declared crossing (gunbc.structural_realization_bindings UnicodeScalarSequenceUnfold); gunbc.rung_drop text_boundary_identity_wall is retired by that crossing executing on the native route.",
          displaced_cost: "Two String declarations and an identity wall at the tokenizer mean the same source can carry two meanings of text, and every string operation has had to be homed twice.",
          first_slice: "The tokenizer reading host text through the one crossing with its claims, and one of the two String declarations deleted in the native-seven closure.",
          red_control: "A host string reaching a structural position without the crossing refuses; a second String declaration in the retained closures keeps this open; the rung drop is retired by its own restoration trigger, never by prose.",
          out_of_scope: "Diagnostic text and path text roles beyond the crossing (later wrappers, if a consumer needs them).",
          handback: "One String, the crossing executing natively, the drop retired."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. std.host_text and v2.std.text expose different carriers and APIs: char_at returns Optional<HostText>, while scalar text uses FreeMonoid<Char>. Residual includes non-literal crossing and compatible caller migration. It is not a blind String path replacement; charge shared crossing work once and reuse it for names-homing.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The vision's text law: one carrier, explicit crossings."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_BAE8SV9B7FFF0908MPZ9RHY2QG",
      id: "operations-are-declarations",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/std/primitives.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "An operation is a declaration with a realization row, and operators lower to references",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.v2_self_host, the vision-realized milestone (its second done-when list), layer 5. gunbc.design_ruling::operations_are_declarations_with_realizations: the five mechanisms that carry operations today (68 std.primitives contracts, 120 builtin_registry_surface_names, 40 primitive_projection rows, the CanonicalOperation enum consumed by infer, target_serialize and the three target models, and the seed's 134 v1_rt functions) converge on one shape, a declared fn with a per-target realization row as std.algebra fold_list already has; a surface operator lowers to a reference to the declared operation of its operand's algebra; the only primitives are v2.std.node's five connectives and six behaviors.",
          displaced_cost: "One shape spelled five ways is five places meaning is decided; each wave that homes a name has had to touch several of them.",
          first_slice: "CanonicalOperation's Add arm replaced by a reference to the declared add of the operand's algebra, with the checker, the serializer and one target consuming the declaration; the RED an operator whose algebra declares no such operation, refusing typed.",
          red_control: "No enum, table or roster answers an operation by spelling; a target without a realization row for a demanded declaration refuses typed; the seed mirrors each move.",
          out_of_scope: "Deleting the seed's runtime (dies with the seed); new operations.",
          handback: "The five mechanisms reduced to declarations and realization rows, the operator lowering executing natively."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. v2.std.compilers.target_model::CanonicalOperation has five mechanisms, not five equally sized functions. The Add vertical shares checker/serializer/target wiring; inverse composition, ordering, equality and coercion have different contracts. Reuse existing algebra declarations and price uncovered semantics, not variant count.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The vision's operation law: declarations and realizations, nothing primitive but the substrate."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_MC7EJBANKKA6XYYEQJTXDVK1D9",
      id: "one-standard-library",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/std/integer.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "The retained compiler closures contain no two declarations for one concept",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.v2_self_host, the vision-realized milestone (its second done-when list), layer 5. Every pair across dag/std and src/v2/std is classified: the same concept collapses to one declaration (integers, optionality, collection carriers, scalars, algebra); the same carrier in a different role gets a role wrapper over one carrier; a genuinely different concern is renamed into the compiler's own namespace so it is not called the language's standard type. v2.std is not a second standard library. Under the fully-qualified rule each pair is already distinct by path, so this is design debt with its own acceptance per type, not an ambiguity.",
          displaced_cost: "Two authorities answer one semantic question, and every consumer of the pair chooses one by habit.",
          first_slice: "Int: std.integer and v2.std.integer merged or the compiler's renamed, with the Oct 18 kernel-type layer rule's claims executing.",
          red_control: "A second declaration for one classified concept in either retained closure keeps this open; a renamed compiler-internal type no longer spelled as a standard type.",
          out_of_scope: "Types outside the two retained closures.",
          handback: "The classification table executed: zero same-concept pairs in the retained closures."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. std.integer::Int is the canonical NonNegative/Negative carrier; its comment freezes the distinct v2.std.integer Int until migration. That is a real representation/consumer change. Text is owned by one-text-carrier; aliases can be rewritten in a batch without a separately priced merger for every spelling.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The vision's library law: one std."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_RW47VTM7V7K4MZ0GYB9D8Y9TTZ",
      id: "one-source-tree",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/one_source_tree.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "One source tree: dag/ is the only tree, no module is named v2, and users name declarations rather than paths",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.one_source_tree (gunbc.design_ruling::one_source_tree_and_the_v2_namespace_dissolves, 2026-11-22). Owns the storage layout, the v2 namespace and the CLI's source-naming boundary. It does not own the compiler's post-ingest file-freedom (universe-ingest-replaces-file-acquisition) or the binding rule (gunbc.plans.names_without_imports); the std reconciliation is the existing one-standard-library, consumed here.",
          approach: "Members in dependency order: the root manifest (source-workspace-manifest), the test harness (harness-runs-in-the-workspace), the other callers (workspace-derived-source-roots), the one-tree cut, then the uncontested renames and the extdeps reconciliation beside one-standard-library, then the namespace's last trace (v2-namespace-dissolved).",
          red_control: "Met only through its members: the intention's done-when holds on the tree (no src/v2, no v2.* module, no root-passing caller, every surveyed pair resolved).",
          displaced_cost: "Two trees and two standard libraries answer one question; every caller restates the split by hand and fails when it drops a root; a reader cannot tell which Int is the integer.",
