    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_5CQTJHEEPD2TXTARM3W7CNR50D",
      id: "external-specimen-compiles",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/instrument_targets.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "A program outside the compiler's own closure compiles natively, using features the closure does not select",
          boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.v2_self_host, the vision-realized milestone (its second done-when list), layer 5. One specimen program that is not part of any compiler closure, chosen to exercise constructs the compiler's own source never uses, compiles, checks and runs through the native route with its claims green; it is an instrument row (gunbc.instrument_targets) judged by the emitted binary, never a lane handing the corpus to the seed. Native-seven is the first specimen of the native route and never the definition of the supported language.",
          displaced_cost: "A self-hosting closure defines the supported language by accident: whatever the compiler happens to use works, and nothing else is known to.",
          first_slice: "The specimen chosen and its unselected features listed against the closure's construct census; one construct passing natively.",
          red_control: "A construct the specimen uses and the closure does not is refused early and precisely or passes; the specimen's claims are green on the native route; the row is judged by the emitted binary.",
          out_of_scope: "Choosing more than one specimen; performance.",
          handback: "The specimen's native run receipt and its construct list."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The instrument-target registry supplies a route, but this node still needs a named external specimen and its unselected construct list. Do not count an internal emitter fixture as external behavior. Selection determines scope; the native receipt follows it.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The vision's completeness law: the language is what is specified, not what the compiler uses."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_BOHQKYIY2BDOAKSVCY2WUPKA6A",
      id: "floor-calibration-rate-bound-to-an-instrument-target",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/instrument_targets.dag"), carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/floor_eval_step_calibration.dag")),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The rate every claim ceiling derives from is transcribed in prose rather than produced by a bound instrument target",
        boundary: "The required floor prices every claim against a figure whose producer is prose. In src/v2/workflow/floor_eval_step_calibration.dag the type EvalStepCalibration is a PinnedSpecimenCalibration whose instrument member is a written-out claim_batch command, whose host member is a prose rate sample, and whose readings, specimen_eval_steps and steps_per_ms members are hand-transcribed. src/v2/workflow/required_floor.dag reads that figure through claim_ceiling_eval_step_budget, and required_floor_claim_work_envelope_ms, required_floor_per_subject_cpu_line_ms and required_floor_new_witness_envelope_ms each return a millisecond count multiplied by it. What this row asks for is a binding, not a number. DECLARING AUTHORITY, named so the compiled-in registry can see it: the row is authored as `fn floor_eval_step_calibration_binding() -> TargetBinding` among the rows of `gunbc.instrument_targets::instrument_bindings()`, which IS the authority, following the nearest precedent `gunbc.instrument_targets::dag_emit_real_grammar_round_trips_binding` with its `..._label()` and `..._entry()` helpers -- a Label whose package is `gunbc.instrument_targets::instruments_package()` and a producer naming the specimen entry dag/test/claim/floor_eval_step_calibration_specimen.dag. `gunbc.instrument_targets::instrument_test_target` is NOT the route: it builds a BuildTarget for the `gunbc test` surface, not a registry row, and naming it here would create a second, non-authoritative spelling of the same subject. The registry at src/v1/stage0/src/instrument_registry_generated.rs is EMITTED from that list by `gunbc.instruments.instrument_registry_emit::instrument_registry_generated_rs`, and its own header says regenerate rather than edit, so the row owes that regeneration alongside itself, proved by `test.claim.instrument_registry_artifact_rendering_witness::the_committed_instrument_registry_artifact_equals_the_rendered_bytes`. SEQUENCING, live at the time of writing: PR 17018 (tidy-hawk-691) regenerates the same artifact for four targets registered in the .dag but absent from the generated .rs, so whichever of the two lands second owes the regeneration and that witness by name -- discovered by the worker as a red CI run otherwise. Cite the symbol, not the position. This row re-pins nothing, and the pinned rate keeps its recorded provenance, including the file's own note that the specimen was reduced so that it sits under the ceiling the calibration derives, because a measuring stick exempt from the tier it defines is the escape hatch gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed forbids.",
        displaced_cost: "Every ceiling figure inherits a constant no reader can reproduce from the tree. The recorded rate is 110,011 eval steps over 152ms on a self-hosted CI runner, written down as steps_per_ms, and the file states the rate is a property of the machine rather than of the depth, so checking it means re-running a command string by hand on the right machine class. Executed instance my lane was handed rather than paid for: one claim of v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return measured 11,894,377 eval steps and 51,556ms cpu, about 16 seconds of allowance at that rate against the 361,500 steps a grandfathered identity is granted and the 72,300 an ungrandfathered one is; the source is PR 17026 issuecomment-7150285687, released binary dbcf0419f7a67b5d127b0b6249e119c9172937554aea1374b5e46ace706e5d58, srv1 slot 9/12 acquired 2026-11-24T23:52:24Z, and that identity is in no grandfathered list, so it was priced by nothing. A worker reading through that figure already has to declare it ungrounded: floor-ceiling-roster-cut-completeness carries standing TranscribedUncited with a read obligation precisely because the citation this repository has not earned is the binding this row asks for.",
        first_slice: "Five steps, each with a named surface so none of them is a judgement call. 1. Author the binding row in gunbc.instrument_targets as described in the boundary: `floor_eval_step_calibration_label()`, `floor_eval_step_calibration_entry()` and `floor_eval_step_calibration_binding() -> TargetBinding`, appended to `gunbc.instrument_targets::instrument_bindings()`. 2. Regenerate src/v1/stage0/src/instrument_registry_generated.rs through gunbc.instruments.instrument_registry_emit -- never by hand -- and show committed equals rendered. 3. Add the grounding surface to v2.workflow.floor_eval_step_calibration, modelled on the pair that file already carries, `specimen_steps_grounding` and `specimen_steps_grounding_holds`: a `CalibrationInstrumentGrounding` coproduct with a grounded arm naming the binding and an `UngroundedInstrument { cited: NonEmptyStr }` arm, plus `calibration_instrument_grounding(calibration: EvalStepCalibration) -> CalibrationInstrumentGrounding` reading the declared population through `gunbc.instrument_targets::instrument_bindings()` and `calibration_instrument_grounding_holds(grounding: CalibrationInstrumentGrounding) -> Bool`. 4. Change the calibration record's instrument member to cite that binding by symbol rather than restating a command, and say in the record what the citation is resolvable against. 5. State field by field which members become produced and which stay prose, the rate sample included.",
        red_control: "The witness is dag/test/claim/floor_eval_step_calibration_instrument_witness.dag, module test.claim.floor_eval_step_calibration_instrument_witness, authored by this node's first slice, because no claim exists today that asserts the calibration's instrument member names a row the authority declares: v2.workflow.floor_eval_step_calibration declares no test at all, and the test fns of dag/test/claim/floor_eval_step_budget_witness.dag are ceilings, rosters and dispositions (a_cost_between_the_ceilings_passes_for_a_grandfathered_identity, the_roster_is_not_truncated, a_roster_addition_refuses and their siblings), none of which reads the instrument member. Its two discriminating claims are named here so a worker arrives with something to run rather than something to invent: `the_calibration_citation_refuses_an_undeclared_instrument` -- calibration_instrument_grounding_holds is false and the ungrounded arm names the cited instrument, when the record cites an instrument the authority does not carry -- and `the_calibration_citation_accepts_the_declared_pair` -- it is true and the grounded arm names the binding this row adds. Both legs execute under claim_batch with --entry test.claim.floor_eval_step_calibration_instrument_witness and the two names in one comma-joined --functions value, each leg's own rc printed on its own line, never a pipe's. red_at is a scratch tree whose ONLY change is the calibration record's instrument member set to a label instrument_bindings() does not carry; green_at is the head. Red is obtained by mutating the citation and never by deleting the specimen, so the control cannot be satisfied by removing the thing measured. The control leg is a named module and function, not a phrase: dag/test/claim/instrument_registry_artifact_rendering_witness.dag, function `the_committed_instrument_registry_artifact_equals_the_rendered_bytes`, green at both heads, which is also the receipt that the regeneration is committed rather than local. Before either leg, INSTRUMENT CHECK FIRST in the same log: the claim_batch path, its sha256 read from disk, and a nonzero grep -ac count for the arm the leg is about to test for -- a zero there is reported as instrument absent, never as a verdict. Each new claim prints its own eval_steps and the module maximum must sit at or under 72,300, the figure `src/v2/workflow/required_floor.dag::claim_ceiling_eval_step_budget` gives new work at the NewWitnessTier: two claims in a sibling witness passed under claim_batch at 96,910 and 110,099 steps and were refused on the routed route, and that is the pattern this line exists to prevent.",
        out_of_scope: "Re-pinning the rate or re-measuring it; changing any derived ceiling or allowance; a per-host calibration table; and admitting any module to the required gate, which is a disposition decision this row neither makes nor presupposes.",
        handback: "The binding row, the regenerated registry proven equal to the rendered bytes, the calibration record citing the binding by symbol, the executed red and green legs with their own rcs and the named control leg green at both heads, the instrument-check-first lines for each leg, the per-claim eval_steps with the module maximum shown beside 72,300, and the field-level list of which calibration members are still transcribed after the change. Any pre-flight gate for a refusal claim in this node runs at --target rust and says which target it used."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The factory's per-claim allowance is only as honest as the figure it is derived from, and a figure nobody can reproduce is an allowance nobody can audit."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_4DXSRQ0TDK36EBTJHKF9YFRJ3A",
      id: "v2-frontend",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/infer.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "v2 reads, names and types its own source",
          boundary: "Parse, body lowering, literal and construct elaboration, occurrence identity, resolve and type inference in src/v2/compiler, measured on the production ingest route. Emission and namespace policy are not part of it.",
          approach: "Converge first on the native seven, the seven native test modules v2 must parse and type end to end. Then work down the whole-corpus refusal roster by root cause, never file by file (gunbc.design_argument::earliest_unjustified_boundary). The first big root was the construct tag that refused v2.compiler.tokenize.",
          red_control: "Any native-seven module refusing before type inference keeps this red. Later, a whole-corpus self-host run with any refusal that no named row owns keeps it red.",
          displaced_cost: "Each refused file is a module v2 cannot compile, so the seed must keep compiling it. Every frontend gap extends the seed's life.",
          handback: "The native seven typed end to end, then the self-host whole-corpus run (gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:self-host) with its refusal population at zero or fully rostered with triggers; the interlock milestones SelfHostWholeCorpusPopulationDerived and SelfHostCorpusEmitsCleanly are cited, not restated."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "Nothing downstream can be real until v2 can read, name and type its own source. Today the whole-corpus run refuses roughly 720 to 1,000 files, and this project owns bringing that number down."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_QDPV7AJRJDYKTD4R22N67BRCXK",
      id: "v2-shared-type-check",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/infer.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "v2 type-checks every construct with one relation",
          boundary: "v2.compiler.infer judges declared returns, record fields, lets, matches, optionals, generic records and cross-module declarations through the single inhabitance relation from #12566. There is no inline per-construct check beside it.",
          approach: "Extend the one relation construct by construct. Landed so far: #12379, #12566, #12601, #12763, #12806. Next: lets and match binders (#12582, #12637, #12641).",
          red_control: "A construct kind that neither derives nor refuses turns the per-kind coverage census red, which was v2-node-kind-derivation-coverage's bar. A second inline check beside the relation is a gunbc.design_argument::single_authority fork and is refused in review.",
          displaced_cost: "Each construct checked its own way means a wrong program passes wherever the local check is weaker. That is the \"accepted on well-formedness alone\" class.",
          handback: "The per-kind coverage table with no generic accept arm, and the member tasks accepted."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-frontend", contribution: "Typing is where most refusals that survive resolve end up. One shared check means a type fact is decided once, not once per construct."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_FE4ZD7DWESKYT47F704VFZHRG3",
      id: "native-route-to-live",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/rung_drop.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "The native route gates every landing and becomes the production route",
          boundary: "The v2-native-frontier ratchet runs as a required merge_group step, which retires gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path and v2_native_frontier_nightly_cadence. Then the whole-route NativeProductionAdmission verdict (D10) admits it, with every refusal and divergence dispositioned. The effects the route needs (D11: Filesystem plus the Gap-B host facts) are a prerequisite, not this project's work.",
          approach: "Mint the roster first (v2.workflow.native_frontier_roster is RosterUnminted), then add the merge-queue-only step inside an existing lane (operator ruling Q4, 2026-09-30: accepted, no new job). Admission comes after that. v1/v2 disagreements are investigated and neither side wins by age (D10).",
          red_control: "A landing that grows the native-frontier debt roster refuses, once the lane is required. Admission refuses on any refusal or divergence left undispositioned.",
          displaced_cost: "Nothing runs the ratchet today, so native regressions land silently. The nightly job was deleted (#12439), and the lane is not yet required.",
          handback: "SelfHostNativeRouteRequiredLane CLEAR, both drops retired, and NativeProductionAdmitted over the required subject denominator."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The native route is what the live compiler runs on. Until it gates merges and is admitted as production, v2 is an experiment beside the real build."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_2AFHMH4Q2RZV8C9KNXXT2R62Q6",
      id: "demand-engine",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/demand_engine_program.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "Run programs through one demand engine, paying only for what changed",
          boundary: "gunbc.plans.demand_engine_program milestones M1.b to M7 plus D13 (derived dependency demand and composition-root binding). Already landed: M0 (#11428), M1.a (#11447), D9 partition (Pkg7), M3a (#12401, inferred), D11/E2 (#12391), D12 (#11528). The plan is the design authority. These rows are its milestones as work.",
          approach: "Replanned 2026-11-23 as an intention (gunbc.plans.demand_engine_program section 5). Work items are selected against the tree and name that intention; the milestone rows demand-m1b to demand-m7 are superseded and await the operator's retirement.",
          red_control: "A milestone that lands without deleting the route it replaces refuses in review, per the plan's own replacement-migration law. A cache without a derived identity is refused (gunbc.design_argument::demand_before_materialization, gunbc.design_argument::earliest_unjustified_boundary).",
          displaced_cost: "Stage-wide folds recompute unchanged facts on every run, and hand-authored widths and schedulers sit where derived demand belongs.",
          handback: "The plan's section 5 done-when, each condition read on the tree."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The live compiler's driver is a demand over its universe, so a run pays only for what changed. The engine is how v2 stays affordable as the required route."),
    ),
    // ---- heal's regeneration round, realizing gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence (2026-11-22, operator, after an
