    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_EVMFH44TKERABG6DZCB7RHWYX7",
      id: "stage0-crate-partition-covers-every-emitted-module",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The stage0 crate partition covers every module the emitter writes, so a seed-input edit is not refused",
        boundary: "Reported by vivid-swift-693 from a measured trace and approved by neat-badger-614; re-measure before closing. Every regen round checks whole-population coverage (required_regen_host.rs, the Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered check). At main, 13 emitted modules are in no GeneratedPartitionCrateRow (gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs) and not in the host shell: extdeps_exec_command, extdeps_tools_ls, extdeps_posix_shell_command_language, extdeps_filesystem_filesystem_io, extdeps_tools_env, extdeps_exec_program, extdeps_posix_process, gunbc_remote_shell_command, extdeps_access_posix, std_operation_argv, std_template, std_env_binding, dry_run. So any change that edits seed-input src/v1 sources is refused with 235 endpoints uncovered; gunbc#16910 is the first casualty and depends on this row. The owner decides package-row versus host-shell placement per module and regenerates through the named authority (v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition via generated_artifact_gate main_wet, informed by the stage0_partition_rebuild_* claims of regen_convergence_transaction); the generated file is never hand-edited. Owner is ci-control because it owns the heal rows that read this check; if the heal and seed lane is another owner, the manager should redispatch.",
        displaced_cost: "Every pull request that edits seed-input sources is refused until someone hand-routes around the refusal; the refused one waits on a partition nobody owns.",
        first_slice: "Decide, per each of the 13 modules, package row or host shell, and regenerate the partition through its authority.",
        red_control: "EXECUTED matched pair, run by bold-lark-538 on srv1 under the shared heavy-slot limiter (BOOT printed from /proc as c095c0cd); same instrument on both legs: claim_executor sha256 d1e84294616d796bea05a7d8c14bef017a222b8982cabded7eb6e49df476aacc, base mirror f990441e4aae05b83080f8c55142c41488f4b292, control claim_executor --regen-round-cost --base-mirror --regen-affected-scope over --source-root dag --source-root src/v2. RED leg (tree 4c61f5a33b4ce0f8d778b3ca8c9f37c5ef5b7b9b, the gunbc#16910 head, which is main f990441e plus a seed-input edit, WITHOUT the twelve-row carrier): refuses at rc=1 naming Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered with 235 emitted edge endpoint(s) across 14 modules, std_template named with 10; red_at = 4c61f5a33b4ce0f8d778b3ca8c9f37c5ef5b7b9b, red_base = f990441e4aae05b83080f8c55142c41488f4b292 (a main sha). GREEN leg (tree 0d29c21d8d3649cada56ca1d1f90bc3a15980f80, which is 4c61f5a3 plus exactly the two carrier files src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag blob 10f1c11a and dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_crate_partition_generated.dag blob 318dc912): the same instrument prints 22 emitted edge endpoint(s), residual per module, verbatim, 18 v1_tests_claim_v1_source_chars_once_identity and 4 dry_run, with std_template absent (count 0); green_at = 0d29c21d8d3649cada56ca1d1f90bc3a15980f80. green_at is rc=1 not rc=0: at 0d29c21d the round still refuses overall because 22 endpoints remain, and those 22 belong to two modules outside the carrier of this node; the green this row claims is not a global admitted-edges line but that the placement of each module owned by this node drives its own contribution to zero -- all twelve did, reduction delta 213 = 34+26+24+19+18+17+16+15+14+13+10+7 exactly, and the two modules outside the carrier held their counts across both legs (dry_run 4, v1_tests 18 unchanged), which shows the emitted-edge admission reads the committed carrier and not a seed snapshot. The executed population is 14 modules and 235 endpoints, not the 13 the row originally enumerated: v1_tests_claim_v1_source_chars_once_identity (18 endpoints) did not exist when the row was written and its rostering belongs to v1-source-chars-converted-once (gunbc#16910), and dry_run (4 endpoints) belongs to adhoc-132254e5-c25 per the operator ruling; neither is in the carrier of this node. The red-control probe that admitted edges=353 and then crashed at the seed cargo build (could not read std_operation_argv.rs, cargo exit status 101) is NOT this control and is not cited as red; bare main f939aa6dd75d3b8eb302632b8a4547dd76b30ceb under this instrument never reached a refusal -- the unmodified-main control voided at NoAffectedMirrors rc=0 before the admission, and the probe admitted 353 then crashed. CI corroboration, executed by CI and not by this node: heal run 45166820438 at 9995af78ec27 and heal run 45437920300 at 4c61f5a3 (admission line at 17:30:26.69Z before the 60-minute cancel), each printing 235 emitted edge endpoints across 14 modules.",
        out_of_scope: "Hand-editing the generated partition file. Changing the coverage check itself. Any module the emitter does not write. Producing an emitted body for a module that no authored source references, and any change to the seed's emission reachability: that half is carried by gunbc.rung_drop.crate_row_names_a_module_the_emitter_has_no_reason_to_write, whose restoration_trigger is an operator ruling on seed growth, so a worker on this row neither writes seed Rust nor reruns the round hoping for a different verdict.",
        handback: "The placement of each of the twelve owned modules with its reason, and the partition regenerated through v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition, plus the executed matched pair on one instrument: claim_executor sha256 d1e84294616d796bea05a7d8c14bef017a222b8982cabded7eb6e49df476aacc, base mirror f990441e4aae05b83080f8c55142c41488f4b292, control claim_executor --regen-round-cost --base-mirror --regen-affected-scope over --source-root dag --source-root src/v2, with both legs' real exit statuses pasted -- RED at red_at 4c61f5a33b4ce0f8d778b3ca8c9f37c5ef5b7b9b printing Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered over 235 emitted edge endpoint(s) across 14 modules with std_template named with 10, GREEN at green_at 0d29c21d8d3649cada56ca1d1f90bc3a15980f80 printing 22 endpoints with std_template absent and reduction delta 213 = 34+26+24+19+18+17+16+15+14+13+10+7 exact. THE HANDBACK STOPS AT THE ADMISSION-COUNT LEG. What this row certifies is that each module it owns drives its own uncovered-endpoint contribution to zero over the DECLARED partition, which is the population a round with --regen-affected-scope reads. It does not certify, and no longer asks the worker to claim, that a heal or regen round reaches the seed's fixed point: at green_at the round still refuses overall because 22 endpoints remain, and the build behind a round's own emit fails whenever a crate row names a module with no emitted body -- measured 2026-11-25 on origin/main with the counts printed, all 100 modules named by the GeneratedPartitionCrateRow blocks have a body on disk in src/v1/stage0/src and 0 are missing, while the thirteen modules this row names have none between them. That convergence half is carried as a dependency and not as a promise: gunbc.rung_drop.crate_row_names_a_module_the_emitter_has_no_reason_to_write holds it, and its restoration_trigger is an operator ruling on seed growth. This row does not close on the admission count alone while that drop stands. The residual 22 endpoints keep their named owners: dry_run (4 endpoints) to adhoc-132254e5-c25 per the operator ruling, and v1_tests_claim_v1_source_chars_once_identity (18 endpoints) to v1-source-chars-converted-once (gunbc#16910), whose coverage route is the host shell rather than a crate row -- measured the same day, 0 claim-test modules appear in the generated carrier or in src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag, while 14 claim-test bodies exist in the seed root and are named in src/v1/stage0/src/lib.rs, the host shell the admission's own Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered text names as the alternative to a partition row. This node unblocks gunbc#16910 for its own slice only."
      ), on: "2026-11-25", note: "Narrowed 2026-11-25 by vivid-swift-693 (lane manager) on neat-badger-614's ruling, after the operator escalation msg_f631425e CLOSED HOLD BY DEFAULT. His report of it, verbatim: \"msg_f631425e closed as Hold by default. That's no seed growth, a non-answer rather than a design ruling.\" A timeout on an ask is not a ruling, so no operator words exist to record and no gunbc.design_ruling entry is claimed. handback now stops at the admission-count leg certified at green_at 0d29c21d; out_of_scope now excludes producing an emitted body for an unreferenced module; the convergence half is carried by gunbc.rung_drop.crate_row_names_a_module_the_emitter_has_no_reason_to_write as a dependency with an operator-ruling trigger. red_control is UNCHANGED because it is an executed matched pair and still describes what was measured. One diagnosis in this row's earlier prose was corrected by measurement rather than argument: a round does not build before it emits -- in the host realization of v2.workflow.required_regen the round calls emit_generated_surface, then write_emitted_tree, then reaches seed_cargo_build at its round.rebuild_from_installed sites -- so a body missing at the build is a body the emitter was never given a reason to write, which is why the gap is typed as a rung drop instead of a step a worker can reorder.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "A heal or regen round covers the whole emitted population, so a seed-input edit reaches its read set instead of a refusal."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_A1AZBS250N7JM8DQ0O6C1ON5YD",
      id: "placed-module-gets-its-body-emitted-or-a-typed-refusal",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/required_regen.dag"), concat(carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag"), carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs"))),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A module the round places into a stage0 package row gets its body on disk, or a typed refusal names it before the build",
        boundary: "Reported 2026-11-24 by bold-lark-538 from an executed regen round, directed into the plan by neat-badger-614, recorded by vivid-swift-693. The emitted-edge coverage check, owned by stage0-crate-partition-covers-every-emitted-module and under re-measurement, printed edges=353 admitted with zero uncovered at head f0c3c72dfb7337bccf1fba53a1691bce46a0ea07 with the twelve-row carrier committed, but that line does not discriminate -- a one-row probe carrier printed the identical figure -- so this row makes no coverage claim, and the round then refused downstream at round.rebuild_from_installed: cargo build exit status 101, couldn't read src/v1/stage0_std_core/src/../../stage0/src/extdeps_exec_program.rs: No such file or directory, at src/v1/stage0_std_core/src/lib.rs:190 which declares pub mod extdeps_exec_program;. The round writes the crate-root declaration and does not write the body, so a placed module is a compile error waiting for the whole-compiler rebuild. Anchors in src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs: seed_cargo_build(workspace, 'round.rebuild_from_installed') at :7516, :7624 and :9195; install_convergence_stage :9123 and install_convergence_stage_with_backend :9205; the install admissions admit_install_target :1507, admit_install_destination :1536 and admit_install_boundary_population_from_model :9575. This is NOT the half recorded by dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs.dag: that capability was delivered 2026-11-12 by PR #16377 and its remaining ceiling is that no compiled-in crate-root renderer should be called at all. Nothing in the plan owns the placement-then-body step, which is why a coverage fix lands green on coverage and red on build. The specimen needs the twelve-row carrier to exist first, which is stage0-crate-partition-covers-every-emitted-module's product; that is stated as prose rather than an edge because this row is workable the moment such a carrier exists, and an edge would hold an executable repair behind an unaccepted row.",
        displaced_cost: "Every seed-input change is refused twice in sequence: first for coverage until the partition covers the emitted modules, then again at the rebuild because placing the module wrote no body. gunbc#16910 is the second casualty, unblocked from coverage and still refused at rebuild.",
        first_slice: "For ONE module that the round places into a package row, make the round write its body .rs beside the declaration it already writes, or refuse earlier with a typed refusal naming the module and its row, so round.rebuild_from_installed no longer meets a missing file. One module, one refusal name. REALIZATION ROUTE: the body is emitted by the .dag authority -- src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag, which owns the emitted-crate partition and its emission, realised through v2.workflow.required_regen -- so the .rs bytes reach disk as generated output. src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs is HAND-MAINTAINED seed Rust with no Generated header (it is the host realization of v2.workflow.required_regen) and changes there only as regenerated or transport output; any hand edit to it needs an operator ruling BEFORE implementation. This row claims no such ruling and lands no hand-written seed Rust.",
        red_control: "EXECUTED, off-main: the A6b round at head f0c3c72dfb7337bccf1fba53a1691bce46a0ea07 (session branch session/bold-lark-538, never merged; srv1 heavy-slot slot 8/12, 2026-11-24T10:00:39Z to 10:51:03Z; log 89,739 B over 343 lines; BOOT printed from /proc) prints emitted-edge admission admitted edges=353 with zero uncovered and then ROUND_REAL_EXIT_STATUS=1 refusing at round.rebuild_from_installed with cargo exit status 101 on couldn't read .../stage0/src/extdeps_exec_program.rs at src/v1/stage0_std_core/src/lib.rs:190. The cargo-check folded into the same slot printed rc=0 but ran AFTER a checkpoint restore -- porcelain 0, the mirror blob back to main's 41586473, the crate-root pub-mod count back to 55 -- and is recorded as a NON-RESULT, never as a green.",
        out_of_scope: "Hand-writing the twelve body .rs files, which an operator ruling forbids; the emitted-edge coverage check itself, owned by stage0-crate-partition-covers-every-emitted-module and under re-measurement; the partition placement decisions, owned by stage0-crate-partition-covers-every-emitted-module; and removing the compiled-in crate-root renderer, owned by the recurring_failure_mode row named above.",
        handback: "The round emits the body for every module it places, or refuses typed earlier naming the module and the row; a round reaches rc=0 at a fixed revision with the twelve-row carrier committed; and gunbc#16910 is no longer refused at round.rebuild_from_installed."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "A round that places a module leaves a tree that compiles, so coverage and buildability become one fact instead of two refusals in sequence."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_996VCB1C1184A2HK3XJV2T0CXT",
      id: "commit-sha-has-one-validating-constructor",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/std/types.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "CommitSha has one validating constructor, so a placeholder sha cannot be written",
        boundary: "Reported by vivid-swift-693, approved by neat-badger-614. std.types declares CommitSha = String, and its own comment says commit_sha_text_holds is a check a caller must remember to run, not a construction wall, dissolving when CommitSha gains one validating constructor (the predicate then deletes). Effect: claim-side and .dag-declared sha-typed data can carry a placeholder sha that parses, typechecks and runs, and nothing refuses it. Measured by vivid-swift-693 at main df072970: a census of sha-typed literals in src/v2 and dag found zero placeholders today (hundreds checked), so this is an exposure, not an incident. The roadmap recorder and status already validate and are the pattern to follow, not a target: roadmap_event_cli refuses a malformed --red-at, --green-at or --red-base, and roadmap_status requires commit_sha_text_holds on both shas plus red_at != green_at.",
        displaced_cost: "A wrong sha in claim-side data is found only by whoever reads it (a 64-hex binary hash was mistaken for a commit in this very planning work); nothing in the type refuses it.",
        first_slice: "The constructor itself: one validating constructor for CommitSha, with claim-side and .dag-declared sha-typed data reaching it.",
        red_control: "NONE OBSERVED YET as a recorded pair: no sha is claimed. The control is a claim-side CommitSha literal holding a non-40-hex placeholder, executed to typecheck and run today at a named revision, and refused at construction after; red_at and green_at are OPEN.",
        out_of_scope: "The roadmap recorder and status (already validating; leave them alone). Any change to what a sha means.",
        handback: "The constructor, the call sites now reaching it, the placeholder literal executed and pasted before and after with their commits, and the deletion of commit_sha_text_holds."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A recorded commit identity is constructed valid, so a claim's evidence cannot carry a placeholder."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_YCJZ8HFPSSXRQEZAJ0NACMY1HE",
      id: "acceptance-recorder-four-positional-call-is-accepted",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_cli.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The call at roadmap_model.dag:726:98 takes the positional arguments it is given",
        boundary: "Measured by royal-newt-240 at main 5ed201b4a5267dc841eda350af91a199f7959954: reaching past the receipt grammar, `--entry dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_cli.dag --function roadmap_acceptance_record_cli --dry-run` fails at dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_model.dag:726:98, this value call takes at most 1 positional argument, not 4, a post-expansion span. SOFTENED after royal-newt-240's correction: the entry itself resolves at af4a6e54 and 5ed201b4 (resolve_failed=NO, 491 closure files, resolve_entry_graph_inclusive 88810 ms), and rc=1 on a placeholder receipt is a legitimate refusal, so this is a pre-existing error reachable only past the receipt grammar, not a regression and not a claim that recording is broken. Whether the lab advance changes recording is not established. The recorder keeps recording on the durable branch refs/heads/roadmap-events. Distinct from required-check-named-witnesses-runs-no-claim-module, which owns running claim modules in the required check.",
        displaced_cost: "A real receipt that clears the grammar reaches a four-positional call that the typechecker refuses, so the failure appears only at the last stage of recording.",
        first_slice: "Find the call at roadmap_model.dag:726:98, correct its arguments, and run the entry past the receipt grammar with a grammar-valid receipt in dry-run.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at and green_at are not named as commits. Observed at 5ed201b4a5267dc841eda350af91a199f7959954 (royal-newt-240, built sha256 a2f5732a816830ba5d62e0431c593aed0a560c49a5c565ff484f122ccce00721, released sha256 d5a807756bb1379767c64d37a12be63e424144866e3bcf192588ddeb4caa40d0): a dry-run past the receipt grammar refuses with the four-positional cause above. Green is the same dry-run with a grammar-valid receipt exiting 0 at one sha.",
        out_of_scope: "Any change to what an acceptance records, and the lab advance itself.",
        handback: "The call corrected, and the dry-run past the receipt grammar exiting 0 with its raw lines and the binary it ran under."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "ci-end-to-end-execution", contribution: "A claim in the required population passes or is named as failing."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_TEPF94H0G69RRZEM7TYJSAMMT6",
      id: "required-check-named-witnesses-runs-no-claim-module",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/witness/compiler_gate_workflow.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The required check named witnesses accounts for the claim modules it never ran",
        boundary: "Reported by royal-newt-240 from executed commands and from reading the generated file. The required workflow witnesses.yml declares one job, v2-bootstrap, whose steps are checkout, read-set cache restores, fast-lane classify and the compiler-gate stamp (gunbc run --function run_v1_program_check_compiler_gate_stamp); no step invokes claim or claim_batch over dag/test/claim, and the only claim_batch sites under .github are two build sites. At 3aa21469096445d75857a9bc70902885b9fa6094 the GitHub checks v2-bootstrap, heal-generated-artifacts and the hosted-runner shadow gate configuration reported success while a claim module in the corpus did not resolve under royal-newt-240's executed run (see red_control for what that run does and does not establish). witnesses.yml is GENERATED: its authority is gunbc.witness.compiler_gate_workflow (compiler_gate_workflow, expected_compiler_gate_yml), regenerated through gunbc.instruments.generated_artifact_gate main_wet, so the change belongs in that .dag authority and the yaml is never patched by hand. Same class as corpus-sweep-excludes-directories-by-name-and-reports-no-excluded-count: a reported pass that does not account for what it never looked at. Distinct from required-lane-exit-on-refused-phase and required-floor-passes-with-a-failed-phase, which the operator is deciding and which this row does not touch.",
        displaced_cost: "A green required check is read as the corpus resolving, and a broken claim module merges under it; the cost is paid later by whoever finds it (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed, a check that selects no consumer is not one).",
        first_slice: "Decide what the required check is entitled to say about claim modules, then make the generated workflow either run them or state in its own output that it selected none, through compiler_gate_workflow and its regeneration.",
        red_control: "PENDING, pair-ready (royal-newt-240, executed): red_at 5ed201b4a5267dc841eda350af91a199f7959954, green_at OPEN, to be named by the commit that makes the claim module typecheck. At red_at, `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/roadmap/roadmap_red_control_tree_witness.dag --claim-run` exits RC=1 under both binaries, with 35 stderr lines and 0 stdout lines, so none of the module's 8 test fns executes. BUILT at that tree (binary sha256 a2f5732a816830ba5d62e0431c593aed0a560c49a5c565ff484f122ccce00721, --version \"gunbc 5ed201b4a5267dc841eda350af91a199f7959954\"): cause dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_status.dag:141:33, '==' compares an optional value with a required one (no declared coercion lifts T into T?). RELEASED (sha256 d5a807756bb1379767c64d37a12be63e424144866e3bcf192588ddeb4caa40d0, --version \"gunbc 23523235c601a102e79a753294ea9f7c9c3a36d7\", 309 commits behind): cause dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_cli.dag:100:56, a direct call argument for parameter red_at is declared String and produced Optional<String> (also :100:76, :104:56, :104:76, :104:96, :104:117). The two binaries print different first causes on one tree because the typechecker changed across those commits, so identical failure text at one sha must also name the binary. The check named witnesses stays green because its single job v2-bootstrap runs no claim module. The natural green is this row's own implementation: adding claim coverage to the generated workflow makes CI fail on that module, and the commit that fixes it is green_at. The control must be a --claim-run, never --function, which resolves only the graph reachable from the function and proves nothing here. A plant inside this unresolvable module cannot discriminate (royal-newt-240's plant produced a byte-identical resolve failure); a plant belongs in a module that currently --claim-runs green, showing the claim refuses while the witnesses check still passes. The generated witnesses.yml is changed only through its authority gunbc.witness.compiler_gate_workflow (expected_compiler_gate_yml) and regenerated through gunbc.instruments.generated_artifact_gate main_wet, never edited",
        out_of_scope: "Whether the required lane exits on a refused phase (the operator's rows). Hand-editing witnesses.yml. Making the required job run the whole corpus if the answer is to say it selected none.",
        handback: "The decision and the change in the generating .dag authority, the regenerated workflow produced through generated_artifact_gate main_wet, the executed output showing the check now runs or names what it did not run, and the red control restated from the finished measurement."
      ), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Evidence relayed 2026-11-23 by neat-badger-614 from vivid-swift-693's census: 139 claim files under src/v2/test/claim have no import lines, the same class as the gunbc#16942 control, which called dag_language_model and span_index_extent bare and could never run (two roots: unresolved v1 imports, rc 1; three roots: the effect checker refusing 'no established callee identity', rc 1) while sitting ungated in manual/. The obligation this adds to the row: every claim file is executed by some instrument at least once, or is refused as unexecutable with a typed reason. The 139 is a starting census, the command to reproduce it is to be obtained from vivid-swift-693 and is not recorded here."), on: "2026-11-23", note: "Measured evidence relayed by neat-badger-614 from vivid-swift-693's lane (worker tidy-fox-641): the required gate admits v1-importing controls it cannot execute under its two roots. Run 45266527662 at head fce895e5, whose parse-population step uses two roots (dag, src/v2) with no src/v1, prints 'parse-verdict reuse: ancestor=none reused=0 miss_identity_absent=10561', and grep -c 'PASS ' over the whole log is 0. Displaced cost: an agreement control can be admitted by required_gate_admits while nothing in CI executes it. Cross-reference: claim-three-source-roots-shared-index. tidy-fox's control only ever executed at three roots, so the two-root gate and the three-root SharedIndex refusal are two halves of one cost. Relayed figures, not re-measured here; no edge added.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "ci-end-to-end-execution", contribution: "A green required check says what it ran, so a landing it gates is not trusted for modules it never selected."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_BPQ3Q3CTSK0TP02ECZC74B8ZDP",
      id: "heal-noop-before-regenerator-build",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/heal_workflow.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Heal decides a no-op before it builds the regenerator",
        boundary: "gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence P7 (2). After recovering any interrupted round, heal decides whether any of its products (mirrors and seed-build artifacts) needs work, and a valid no-op ends the job before the regenerator's cargo build. A no-op needs valid inputs AND valid outputs (the plan's section 2.3): an unchanged read set does not excuse a missing or hand-edited product. A change that touches a seed build input still builds and runs its own regenerator.",
        displaced_cost: "About 5 minutes of cargo build on every heal run whose answer is that nothing needs regenerating.",
        first_slice: "Answer the scope with an already-built binary that is valid for the question (main's native CLI from the fast-lane unit, as P7 (2) names), then move the regenerator build behind that answer in gunbc.heal_workflow.",
        red_control: "A planning-only change ends before the regenerator build with a NoAffectedMirrors receipt; a change to a seed build input still builds; a missing or hand-edited mirror under unchanged sources is not a no-op; an interrupted round's journal is recovered before a no-op is declared.",
        out_of_scope: "Bootstrap-executable reuse for affected rounds (heal-bootstrap-seed-reuse).",
        handback: "The four control outputs, a real planning-only heal log with no regenerator build step, and the diff."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "Deciding validity before paying for the producer is the demand engine's order: a valid product costs a lookup, not a build."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M8629XZJZ9KFZDFNS3AE6BFF",
      id: "heal-mirror-convergence-under-unbuildable-checkout",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/heal_workflow.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Heal converges a stage0 mirror even when the checkout cannot build its own regenerator",
        boundary: "gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence P7 (2): a no-op needs valid inputs AND valid outputs, and an unchanged read set does not excuse a missing or hand-edited product -- dag/gunbc/heal_workflow.dag is the one place that decides whether a regeneration is excused. DESIGN.md 'Reference: building and checks' (gunbc.design_document::ci_contract_blocks) makes heal the job that converges the stage0 mirrors to the seed. Today heal builds the regenerator from the pull request's own checkout before it converges them, so a pull request whose hand-written seed consumes a change to a .dag type can never be converged: the tree that must be repaired is also the only tree the builder is allowed to come from. Measured at PR 16895 head 9291d66130369c4509f08f3baa8df618310eeaac: src/v1/00_core.dag:399 declares ExhaustivenessUnknown { scrutinee: String, declaration: String, module_path: String, span: SourceSpan } and :713 destructures all four fields, while the generated mirror src/v1/stage0/src/v1_std_core.rs:695-698 carries only scrutinee and span (uses at :1114, :1209, :1414) under its own 'Generated by v1 compiler -- do not edit' header, and src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/compile_clean.rs:219 destructures the two absent fields; the heal job ends E0026 rc 101 building its own regenerator. This is not a mirror that drifted: ExhaustivenessUnknown appears 0 times in src/v1/00_core.dag on main and 0 times in the mirror on main, so a two-field body was hand-authored into a do-not-edit file inside the very pull request that introduced the source, disagreeing with it by two fields. A generated file that forbids hand edits and contains one is detectable by a four-line body extraction with a printed lines and bytes count -- and nothing in this repository runs it: CI cannot, because heal's regenerator cannot compile, and the generated-artifact gate does not own stage0 mirrors. Human review found this one. A product repaired by a hand-written approximation is not converged: the repair must REPLACE it with generator output. A second hole sits under the first and makes the first survivable: the sanctioned regeneration route has no registry row for any stage0 mirror, because those paths are COMPOSED rather than declared -- data stage0_src_repo_prefix: String = \"src/v1/stage0/src/\" at dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_rust_source_lifecycle_scaffold.dag:306 -- so a literal grep for a mirror path finds no declaration anywhere under dag/ (measured: 9 hits, all prose in unrelated rows) and the registry is silent on the whole class (measured: 0 rows reaching stage0 mirrors, 0 rows reaching stage0_src_repo_prefix). That silence has three consequences, all exit-honesty failures and all observed on PR 16895: a regeneration pass asked to converge an unregistered path is a no-op that returns normally, so \"I ran the regen tool\" is compatible with \"the tool wrote nothing\"; an author facing a grep that finds nothing reasonably concludes the file is hand-written and authors it by hand, which the repository has been bitten by before (dag/gunbc/rung_drop/regen_producer.dag:14 records a change whose \"only reachable green was a hand-authored mirror\"); and CI cannot catch it either, because heal triggers on src/v1/** (.github/workflows/heal.yml:8) yet a green check says nothing about a mirror its own regenerator cannot produce -- CI judged it and CI never looked are indistinguishable in the UI for this class.",
        displaced_cost: "Every pull request whose seed hand-edit consumes a .dag type change deadlocks: heal cannot converge it, the branch cannot compile, and the only way a worker can proceed is to hand-write the generated file -- the exact state that broke it. Observed on PR 16895: heal run 45331640599 rc 101 at the regenerator build, four of that node's seven priced acquisitions consumed without converging the mirror, and the repair then needed a manager ruling about which tree a producer may be built from -- a question the plan should have answered itself. The composed-path hole has its own measured cost: a lane spent two heavy slots and about sixty minutes believing a regeneration was in progress when the pass was a normal-returning no-op over an unregistered path.",
        first_slice: "Split producer from consumer: build the regenerator from a revision whose checkout builds -- the merge base is the one the plan already trusts for mirror work, HEAL_BASE_MIRROR_COMMIT at .github/workflows/heal.yml:115-116 -- and run that binary against the HEAD's .dag sources to replace the stale mirror, keeping the head's sources as the input and the base's binary as the producer. Prove the product is generator output and not an edit: emit twice, diff the two, require zero lines with both sha256 printed, and show the diff against the committed mirror so the arriving fields are visible on the record. Then build the head's checkout and record its real exit code. Where the emit closure for the file differs between the two revisions, refuse the base-built producer rather than trusting it globally. The slice must also close the registry hole for the file it converges: the producer names the mirror path in its own list of files to install, so a pass over it cannot silently write nothing.",
        red_control: "A checkout that cannot build its own regenerator still converges, with the empty re-diff, both sha256 values and the head build's exit code recorded. A mirror hand-edited under unchanged sources is still refused as a no-op rather than excused. A producer whose emit closure differs between the two revisions is refused instead of used. A regeneration pass asked to converge a path that no registry row reaches refuses and names the path, instead of returning normally having written nothing. And a pull request that can build its own regenerator today is unaffected, so heal cannot silently stop building one.",
        out_of_scope: "Changing where generation 0 starts for the seed build: the row carrying id: heal-bootstrap-seed-reuse (cited by symbol, not position: 4146 on main and 4163 at this PR head, because inserting a row above it moves its line) puts 'Changing where generation 0 starts (the base-start ruling stands)' out of scope, and this row collides with that protected ruling -- escalated to the operator as msg_bb054e96 with Hold recommended; the operator ruled on 2026-11-24 with the words \"yeah your recommendations are fine\" against that recommended HOLD, recorded in gunbc.design_ruling as heal_mirror_convergence_held_until_merge_base_build_is_measured_2026_11_24, so the hold stands and no worker starts until this row measures whether the merge-base build actually collides with the base-start ruling. Also out of scope: the main_wet_one artifacts .github/workflows/witnesses.yml and src/v1/stage0/src/compiler_tests.rs, which carry their own separate authorisation; heal's other rounds and their budgets; and what counts as a seed build input.",
        handback: "The four control outcomes; the converged mirror before and after at located lines; the producer binary's sha256 read from disk together with the revision it was built from; the empty re-diff with both sides' sha256; the porcelain line count showing only the intended path changed; the head build's real exit code; the diff; and the operator's own words recorded in gunbc.design_ruling, not only in a PR comment."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "Heal can converge a generated product even when the checkout it repairs cannot build the producer"),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7ETF92EY55VC9N781F531F4NSD",
      id: "heal-planning-only-in-a-minute",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/read_set_convergence.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A planning-only heal completes in about a minute, including plan-file additions and deletions",
        boundary: "The acceptance of gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence P7, unchanged in owner and in bar: a real planning-only pull request's heal completes in about one minute with a NoAffectedMirrors receipt and no regenerator build, a one-module edit still regenerates exactly the mirrors the dry run names, and a seed-input edit still builds and runs its own regenerator. The evidence is broadened so an edit-only example cannot stand for the whole claim: one real pull request that edits a plan file, one that adds one, and one that deletes one.",
        displaced_cost: "Every planning-only pull request pays 10 minutes of heal, or about 35 if it adds a file, for no regenerated byte.",
        first_slice: "Run the three planning-only pull requests and the two ordinary controls once the members have landed, and record the receipts.",
        red_control: "Any of the three planning-only heals taking a regenerator build or selecting a mirror fails acceptance; the one-module edit selecting more or fewer mirrors than the dry run fails it; the seed-input edit skipping its regenerator fails it.",
        out_of_scope: "Affected-round savings: reuse and terminal-emission elision are accepted on their own.",
        handback: "Five heal run receipts with their step timings, at one named revision."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "The first consumer whose cost is visibly denominated in the change: a planning edit costs heal a minute."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_SWYW46X2J67VK4597BVQ2CGJ80",
      id: "heal-observation-reuse-by-subject",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Heal observes its source closure once per identified subject and carries the observation",
        boundary: "One heal run computes the stage0 source closure several times: the scope child, the checkpoint-subject child and every generation's corpus load. Share one file observation with correctly identified views, each naming its source snapshot, roots and discovery population, parser and resolver semantics, configuration, and the relation it supplies. The dag+src/v2 versus src/v1+dag shared-index refusal is a real subject mismatch and stays a refusal. Carry compact identities, edges and digests across processes, never a resident previous generation.",
        displaced_cost: "About 3.5 minutes for the checkpoint subject and about 3.5 minutes per generation re-deriving a closure an earlier step of the same run already observed.",
        first_slice: "State the observation identity and its validity contract, then carry it from the checkpoint subject to generation 0.",
        red_control: "A reused observation under a changed root set, resolver identity or source snapshot is invalidated and re-observed; a generation whose generator changes parsing or name resolution invalidates the views it computed; an observation offered for a different pool refuses; the slot's memory peak does not rise.",
        out_of_scope: "The cheaper relation itself (heal-scope-relation-without-typecheck); bootstrap-executable reuse.",
        handback: "The invalidation control outputs, before/after phase times and peak memory from one affected heal run, and the diff."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "One observation per subject, reused only while its identity holds, is the demand engine's reuse rule applied to heal's own inputs."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_R4QMB048BX168JHDZZXXV355HW",
      id: "heal-bootstrap-seed-reuse",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Heal reuses the base-policy bootstrap executable under its complete build identity",
        boundary: "Round 1 builds the seed from the base commit's whole src/v1/stage0 crate on every affected heal run, and pull requests on one base build the same artifact. Reuse a valid artifact, or build that same artifact on a miss: a miss changes how it is obtained, never which bootstrap policy runs. Its identity is every effective build input (restored base crate, kept head-added paths, manifests and lockfile, toolchain, target, profile, flags, relevant environment), through the existing materialization identity (std.materialization_provider request_key, std.computation_identity), not a new cache key.",
        displaced_cost: "4 to 5.5 minutes of identical cargo build per affected heal run on a shared base.",
        first_slice: "Write the bootstrap artifact's identity from the existing materialization authority and show that two heal runs on one base derive the same identity and different bases derive different ones.",
        red_control: "A changed toolchain, lockfile, build flag or head-added path under stage0 invalidates the reuse and rebuilds; a reused artifact whose digest disagrees with its recorded identity refuses; the base-start policy is unchanged on a hit and on a miss.",
        out_of_scope: "Changing where generation 0 starts (the base-start ruling stands). A store that needs a new CI job or a raised budget is not admitted here and goes to the operator first.",
        handback: "The identity derivation, the invalidation control outputs, two heal runs on one base with the second reusing, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Cost measured on an UNAFFECTED heal run, 2026-11-24, at the manager's GO so this row is not duplicated by a new one. Proud-fox-90 ran heal's Converge the stage0 mirrors on srv1 at the head of pull request 16964 (01a27929) with the round-cost entry and recorded: round.built_seed_regen wall_ms=1022544, about 17 minutes, of a 1260658 ms total, then partition-rebuild RebuildScopeRefused with cause NoChangedMirrorsToRebuild, changed_paths=0 and first_generation_equal=true at planned=176 executed=176. So about 17 of those 21 minutes bought nothing: the run rebuilt the whole src/v1/stage0 crate from the base seed and then refused because no mirror had changed. On a loaded runner that is what pushes heal past the job cap, now being raised to 90. This is an ORDERING question and not a missing verdict, which is why it lands here rather than in a new row: the refusal already exists in the model -- counted by me with timeout 60 grep -rn over src/v1, src/v2 and dag/gunbc at origin/main 61d340d55cce4707c6c5ece828e41c5c0ab5158f, rc 0 each, the population being the 12,093-file tree extracted by git archive, and what remains unknown is any hit outside those three paths, which I did not inspect: RebuildScopeRefused with cause NoChangedMirrorsToRebuild carrying 10 hits in dag/gunbc/stage0_partition_rebuild_scope.dag with a witness at src/v2/test/claim/stage0_partition_rebuild_scope_witness.dag, and regen-round-cost has 75 hits across dag/gunbc/heal_workflow.dag and dag/gunbc/heal_publication_boundary.dag while regen_affected_scope has 4 hits in src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_executor.rs. The question this row now owes an answer to: can changed_paths=0, or the empty affected set, be DECIDED BEFORE the seed rebuild, failing closed to the full round whenever it cannot be decided? If the answer is yes, the reuse this row already plans makes the empty case free as a side effect. If the answer is no -- emptiness is only knowable after building -- then a separate row is justified and this one stays as written. Nothing in brief, red_control or handback was edited here, and roadmap_criteria_digest in dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_model.dag hashes those three alone while updated() copies them unchanged, so this node's identity and any digest quoted by evidence do not move. heal is a gate: measure, then decide, and do not hurry an implementation."), on: "2026-11-25", note: "REVERT OBLIGATION, dated 2026-11-25 (bright-seal-652), from the operator's temporary-cap ruling. Operator decision message msg_ae0f349b-384e-4b0e-801e-b1b87a9a74bc on escalation msg_2e4d9bcb-468e-42b4-9a54-3395f77ea143, verbatim: \"Raise heal+witnesses to 90 until seed-reuse lands, then back to 60\". The 90-minute v2-bootstrap (RosterGate / gunbc_roster_gate) and heal CI caps were a TEMPORARY deviation, granted only until THIS row lands (gunbc.design_ruling::heal_and_v2_bootstrap_ci_timeouts_raise_is_temporary_2026_11_25; policy gunbc.design_ruling::ci_job_budgets_closed_to_growth). WHEN THIS ROW LANDS, THE SAME CHANGE returns gunbc.ci.repository_ci_profile::gunbc_repository_ci_profile gunbc_roster_gate timeout and heal.timeout to minute(60) and regenerates .github/workflows/heal.yml and .github/workflows/witnesses.yml back to 60, and the fleet-converge.yml host-cap bracket derived from them (gunbc.runner.runner_fleet_job_timeout_census::fleet_targeted_wait_bound) falls back with them. Do not land seed reuse without that revert. This note is the roadmap-side view of the typed ruling; it is an updates layer only -- brief, red_control and handback are untouched and roadmap_criteria_digest is unmoved.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "A build product reused under its derived identity is the materialization ladder's provider step, admitted only once the identity is complete."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_23V8SF4BCP22Y499DQE08TZCAE",
      id: "heal-terminal-emission-elision",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/workflow/regen_convergence_transaction.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Heal's convergence skips a terminal emission only when the next emitting computation is established to be unchanged",
        boundary: "A stopping rule inside the existing planner (v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction regen_plan_next_stage), keeping its compatibility and stage-admission rules. Compare the executable that would perform the next emission, after all required installations and builds, with the executable that produced the retained candidate, and validate that candidate's complete emission inputs and result binding at the same boundary; only when both hold is the next emission skipped. Correct mirrors on disk are not evidence about the producing executable. Skipping an emission never skips an undischarged build or publication obligation. The first identity is the executable's own.",
        displaced_cost: "An affected round pays a final confirming generation (about 15 minutes) whose answer an earlier fact already established; heal run 44976008640 is the specimen to read, not a proof that its passes were redundant.",
        first_slice: "The discriminating pair below as planner-level controls, then the stopping rule.",
        red_control: "Positive: the next producer and the complete emission inputs are unchanged, so no further emission runs. Negative: the head's mirrors are correct on disk but the candidate came from the older base-built producer, so the round must advance. A terminal stage whose final candidate has not been built still builds.",
        out_of_scope: "A semantic-equivalence classifier for producers; caching, scoping and the bootstrap policy. It does not depend on heal-bootstrap-seed-reuse or heal-observation-reuse-by-subject.",
        handback: "The pair's outputs, one affected heal run's receipt showing the elided generation and the build still performed, and the diff."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "demand-engine", contribution: "Not recomputing a result whose producer and inputs are unchanged is the demand engine's first question, asked of heal's own fixed-point loop."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_CFZ5DNH7FEND59ZAXKRZS55XAR",
      id: "convergence-coverage",
      owner: "debt",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/convergence-coverage-program.md"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "Cover every production convergence path until the ensure chain reaches the execution boundary",
          boundary: "Own scope: the compiler-enforced ensure chain D14 intended (qualified operands, restricted construction, completion from root bindings) applied to production observe/decide/apply/readback/mint paths. An operation cannot be admitted without its complete prerequisite chain, and cannot consume success until that chain has established the required facts. It continues prior ensure-chain and compiler-architecture work; it does not redesign them. Member of debt-payoff (operator 2026-10-11): known gaps and RFMs retired against their triggers. Dual membership is refused. Daily-workspace (factory) value is named on the contribution, not a second parent.",
          approach: "Census production paths first (cc-path-census). Then one leaf per deepest cause: ordinary compiler floor (A), generic structural carriers (B), environmental facts as required operands (C), observation distinctions that decide repair (D), lifecycle ownership including failure and retirement (E), selection-to-use of scope and policy (F), evidence that reaches its consumers at subject identity (G), guaranteed cleanup of held resources once the owner is proven ended.",
          red_control: "A production path in the census whose consumer still type-checks after its prerequisite-producing ensure is deleted keeps this open. A leaf that restates D14 or mints a second ensure syntax is refused in review.",
          displaced_cost: "Useful convergence procedures exist, but forgetting a prerequisite still compiles and runs. Harm is paid later as silent wrong actuation, unrepairable members, and green CI over an unestablished serving or sudoers closure.",
          handback: "Every census path either consumes a qualified operand minted on the D14 effectful route or carries a named gunbc.design_argument::conformance exclusion, and each member leaf's handback is met."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "debt-payoff", contribution: "Debt payoff: known gaps and recurring failure modes retired against their rostered triggers -- covering the ensure chain to the execution boundary, including guaranteed cleanup of held resources, is that retirement rather than a parallel lane. Daily-workspace (factory) value: a lab or live dashboard that cannot release seats, units, attempts or lease files after the owner ended keeps charging the host that lands work. Compiler floor: a live compiler that accepts an operation without its complete prerequisite chain makes incomplete convergence cheaper to ship (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder ordinary floor first)."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_K6TBWN5T4J6FV5B2X0HN3VHCW4",
      id: "cc-path-census",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/convergence-coverage-program.md"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Census every production convergence path against the missing execution-boundary guarantee",
        boundary: "Enumerate production observe / decide / apply / readback / mint paths. Classify each: does removing a prerequisite-producing ensure deprive the consumer of a required operand? One roster row per path (route, subject, supplied vs established, covering leaf or named exclusion). The roster is the denominator later leaves consume.",
        displaced_cost: "Without a derived population, each leaf invents its own list of paths and the uncovered remainder is invisible.",
        first_slice: "One roster carrier over the production ensure and effectful-converge folds already named in D14 section 10 and the operator review (srv3_ensure_apt, ensure_host_tool, converge_typed_remote_file, RunArgv family), each classified supplied vs established. Cause-F instance/target slice is sourced from valiant-gull-69 (entry wrappers pinning srv1_live_dashboard_instance over *_for_instance cores: belt 16, serve 10, dispatch_actuator 5 plus two srv1-layout data pins, dashboard_instance_apply 2, launch_deployment_cli 1, dispatch_preflight 1, dispatch_selection 1 fixed in gunbc#13720); do not re-derive that census.",
        red_control: "A production path that uses gunbc.ensure or std.realization_reconcile and is absent from the roster keeps this red. A row that restates D14's target list instead of naming a corpus route is not a census row.",
        out_of_scope: "No repair, no new ensure syntax, no HostBlueprint work.",
        handback: "The roster, the identity-join that later leaves read, and a planted omitted path that reds the census."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "Coverage is an identity join over paths, not a count of findings. The census is the program's denominator."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: a roster carrier consumed by later cc-* leaves. (1) Do not redesign D14 or v2-compiler-architecture. (2) First slice: classify the production folds D14 section 10 and the operator review already name -- srv3_ensure_apt, ensure_host_tool, converge_typed_remote_file, RunArgv / RunArgvStdin / RunArgvOutcome -- as supplied-report vs established-operand. (3) Ingest valiant-gull-69's cause-F wrapper census as sourced inventory; do not re-count srv1_live_dashboard_instance pins. (4) Plant one omitted path that reds the census. (5) Acceptance: a claim process over that roster once bound; until then ExecutionContractUnspecified is honest."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_XW56ZS6QC1081AFR252PR2RBPS",
      id: "cc-compiler-floor",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "An ordinary type obligation cannot stay unresolved while execution proceeds",
        boundary: "The ordinary compiler floor (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder) on the path that let a list of SystemdRunProperty inhabit a list-of-String formal (F19/F36). Confirmed shape: dispatch_worker_unit_properties_for_plan to session_placement_record_write. Not established: list element types aren't checked -- direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags exists. Weakness: a record at a scalar formal can yield InhabitanceUndecidable, and DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided is GateAdvisoryTypecheck, so it does not block. Class: gunbc.recurring_failure_mode product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted. The SystemdRunProperty-in-list path needs a discriminating execution. The seed finding must not be silently transferred to v2; the native route needs its own executed negative control.",
        displaced_cost: "Zero blocking errors is read as every declared type obligation being established. Wrong programs then run.",
        first_slice: "A native-route negative control that the SystemdRunProperty-in-list (or an equivalent record-at-scalar-formal) case refuses, plus the existing class's RED staying enrolled.",
        red_control: "A planted record at a scalar formal that the native route accepts keeps this red. A seed-only red cited as v2 coverage is rung inflation.",
        out_of_scope: "Not the whole compiler-guarantee program, not a claim that list element types are unchecked, and not transferring seed diagnostics onto v2 by transcription.",
        handback: "The native negative control green-by-execution, the class's RED still enrolled, and a stated rung that matches executed evidence."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "The ensure chain is a type obligation. If the ordinary floor does not block, qualified operands cannot be required."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: gunbc.recurring_failure_mode product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted, native-route negative control. (1) Do not claim list element types are unchecked; direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags exists. (2) Discriminate the advisory InhabitanceUndecidable / GateAdvisoryTypecheck arm. (3) Execute the SystemdRunProperty-in-list path or an equivalent record-at-scalar-formal fixture on the native route. (4) Do not transfer the seed finding to v2 by citation alone."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_59AP6NKF1MH8GB1VNDYRHEK9X0",
      id: "cc-structural-carriers",
      owner: "language-integrity",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/extdeps/languages/bash_build.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A generic structural carrier cannot drop admitted children into plausible partial output",
        boundary: "bash_build_subshell accepts any Node body. bash_fold_flatten_stmt_list reads positional children 0 and 1 only, so an or_else body keeps left and drops right with no refusal (v2.extdeps.languages.bash_build; v2.workflow.bash_command_fold_serialize). F37. The body carrier does not establish grammar membership; the serializer fabricates partial output (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed). bash_build_subshell_from_stmts is a caller fix and leaves other consumers (conditional bodies) able to drop behavior. Durable repair: establish shape at construction, preserve every admitted child, refuse malformed input. No new Bash representation.",
        displaced_cost: "A forgotten branch is emitted as a shorter script that still runs.",
        first_slice: "The shared flatten/read of statement lists refuses an or_else (or other extra-child) body instead of dropping the right child, with a planted RED and a well-formed two-child positive control.",
        red_control: "An or_else node as a subshell or conditional body that serializes without refusal, dropping a child, keeps this red.",
        out_of_scope: "No second Bash IR, no per-caller wrappers beside the shared reader, and no change to D14's operand model.",
        handback: "The shared reader refuses malformed input, preserves every admitted child, and both controls stay enrolled."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "A convergence plan that is a Node the serializer silently truncates never reached the execution boundary as authored."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: v2.extdeps.languages.bash_build and v2.workflow.bash_command_fold_serialize shared statement-list reader. (1) Repair construction and reading, not a new Bash representation. (2) Caller-only bash_build_subshell_from_stmts is out of scope as the durable fix. (3) Plant or_else-as-body RED; keep a well-formed two-child control."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_Q73CZQQFQHZKC9VP6ZEW6AAW8W",
      id: "cc-qualified-operands",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/ensure-closure-design.md"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "An operation asks for the established capability, not an optional description of the environment",
        boundary: "Environmental facts as required operands (F02, F07, F14, F16, F35, F43-F44). The reversal belongs once at the operation's owning boundary: the operation asks for the established capability, the selected provider induces further requirements, the compiler carries them outward, the root answers policy and placement. Specimen: srv3_ensure_apt takes subject and package separately; install uses package, readback checks subject (D14 section 10). Continue D14's qualified results and restricted mint. Do not mint a parallel operand vocabulary.",
        displaced_cost: "A path, secret location or package spelling compiles while the principal, readers or package identity were never established. Unrelated mutation can happen before readback rejects it.",
        first_slice: "Close the srv3_ensure_apt subject/package fork so install and readback are one authority, using D14's existing mint shape.",
        red_control: "A call that supplies a package spelling different from the presence subject and still applies keeps this red. A new operand type that restates InstalledPackage / MaterializedProgram is a gunbc.design_argument::single_authority fork.",
        out_of_scope: "Not D14 landing steps 1-7 as a whole, not grants or leases (those stay their authorities), not inventing HostBlueprint here.",
        handback: "The specimen's single authority, the census paths this leaf owns marked established-operand, and the RED enrolled."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "D14's replacement is qualified operands. This leaf applies that replacement at the owning boundaries the census names."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: gunbc.host.host_effect_realize srv3_ensure_apt, continuing D14 section 10. (1) One authority for install and readback. (2) Use existing qualified-result / mint shapes; do not mint a parallel vocabulary. (3) Grants and leases stay their own authorities. (4) Event-carrier and tailnet-door directory demands are precedents, not this leaf's rewrite."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_6EVP7PRFRA1V1WDS1WA1137XCX",
      id: "cc-observation-distinctions",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/a_deploy_that_observes_its_own_service_cannot_repair_it.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Observation must distinguish holds, absence, repairable drift, conflict and unobservable",
        boundary: "F11 and related F01, F46, F52. ProcessRunningRelease carrying a revision, or ProcessNotRunning carrying an active flag: an active service whose /healthz fails becomes MemberUnobservable, which decide_member refuses (gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe, member_identity). There is no representation of an observable, owned, active service with a broken health/release endpoint. Class: gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_deploy_that_observes_its_own_service_cannot_repair_it. Needed distinctions: desired holds; demonstrably absent; owned repairable drift; ownership/identity conflict; unobservable. An arbitrary 403 is not absence. Domain assessment owns the decision; a generic satisfaction Boolean is insufficient (D14).",
        displaced_cost: "Repair requires the damaged service to cooperate. Unobservable is collapsed with broken, so dependent actions are refused or, worse, guessed.",
        first_slice: "Represent owned-and-active-with-broken-health as distinct from MemberUnobservable, without treating 403 as absent.",
        red_control: "A planted owned active member whose health endpoint fails that is classified only as unobservable, with no repairable-drift arm, keeps this red. A 403 classified as absent keeps this red.",
        out_of_scope: "Not inventing a generic satisfaction Boolean, not best-effort over an incomplete exclusive-capacity census, not the whole deploy rewrite.",
        handback: "The distinction arms, the class's RED still enrolled, and decide_member consuming the new arm rather than collapsing it."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "Ensure policy cannot choose Apply vs Refuse if observation has already erased the distinction the decision needs."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe / member_identity and the existing failure-mode row. (1) Add the owned-active-broken-health distinction; do not collapse it into MemberUnobservable. (2) 403 is not absence. (3) Domain assessment owns the decision (D14); do not add a generic satisfaction Boolean. (4) Keep the class RED enrolled."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_WWHPSKXKDTFH62WJ1D6VD3HJ04",
      id: "cc-lifecycle-ownership",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/live_deploy/emit.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Convergence owns failure, retirement and crash gaps, not only selected successful transitions",
        boundary: "F12/F39, F13, F17, F20/F21, F24. identity_member_of_step leaves belt, publication, fabric-storage, approval-front-door and tailnet-door artifacts outside the identity-aware route; deployment_apply_plan reconciles them against observed: [] (unfinished per-member-kind migration). Dropping a unit from desired does not retire one an earlier deploy owned. Serving closure is checked only after switching. Attempt/container activation has incomplete recovery; dispatch and cleanup observe different populations. Mutation-to-projection causal dependencies were hidden by a clock. A foreign listener is found only by failed activation or revision mismatch. Moving the record write after creation swaps the crash gap. gunbc.design_argument::selection_precedes_convergence: the effectful admission-actuation-observation cycle has no consumed home yet; the fleet admission spine is the named first consumer. This leaf covers production paths; it does not mint that home.",
        displaced_cost: "Owned artifacts survive undeleted, invalid candidates become live before their closure is accepted, and a crash leaves one side of an activation without the other.",
        first_slice: "Name activation identity for one unfinished member kind currently reconciled against observed: [], and refuse promotion until that candidate's serving entry and closure are accepted -- consulting F39's annotation refusal before switch, not after.",
        red_control: "A member kind still reconciled against observed: [] after this slice's chosen kind is migrated, without a named remaining-kind row, keeps this red. Consulting serving-closure refusal only after switch keeps this red.",
        out_of_scope: "Not minting the gunbc.design_argument::selection_precedes_convergence cycle home, not adding an enqueue after every mutation without a durable causal relation, not finishing every member kind in one change.",
        handback: "The first migrated member kind on the identity-aware route, promotion gated on accepted serving closure, and remaining kinds rostered by identity."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "An ensure chain that only covers the happy transition leaves retirement, crash gaps and late refusal outside the compiler's reach."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: gunbc.live_deploy.emit identity_member_of_step / deployment_apply_plan unfinished per-member-kind migration. (1) One member kind off observed: []. (2) Serving closure before promotion (F39). (3) Do not mint the gunbc.design_argument::selection_precedes_convergence cycle home. (4) Do not 'fix' crash gaps by swapping record-write order."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_QXKD8Q0EHNVEQKS6Q7N0FF946R",
      id: "cc-selection-to-use",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/rung_drop/fleet_converge_named_revision_and_branch.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Selection of environment, candidate, principal and store is consumed at the effect, not described beside it",
        boundary: "F03/F04, F18, F22, F33, F45; admission F25, F26, F31, F47; instance/target F63. Which environment, candidate, principal, state store and source tree belong to this attempt is not answered by the host. F04 correction: the operator allowed branch development operations; the declared restoration is binding revision and branch to an admitted identity (gunbc.rung_drop fleet_converge_named_revision_and_branch). Restoring universal main-only does not satisfy it. Grants, leases and security context keep their own authorities (D14). The compiler makes those distinct prerequisites unavoidable in the same dependency graph. Instance/target inventory sourced from valiant-gull-69, not re-derived: wrappers pinning srv1_live_dashboard_instance over *_for_instance cores (belt 16 including belt_claude/codex_preflight, belt_attempts_observe, tick and spawn; serve 10; dispatch_actuator 5 plus dispatch_worktree_root and dispatch_codex_home; dashboard_instance_apply 2; launch_deployment_cli 1; dispatch_preflight 1; dispatch_selection 1, fixed in gunbc#13720). belt_dispatch_instance_named keeps the srv1-live/srv2-deploy name map.",
        displaced_cost: "A credential, writable path or branch that was selected is not the one the effect uses, and production policy cannot constrain the selection without breaking the allowed dev route.",
        first_slice: "Bind revision and branch to an admitted identity on one production converge path, consumed at the effect, without restoring main-only.",
        red_control: "A converge that runs on an unbound branch while this slice's path claims identity-bound revision+branch keeps this red. A change that restores universal main-only as the F04 repair keeps this red.",
        out_of_scope: "Not making ensure grant itself permission, not promising volatile capacity, not collapsing grants into environmental completion.",
        handback: "The identity-bound selection consumed at the effect, the rung-drop's capability trigger named, and the dev route still authorable."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "Prerequisites that exist only as descriptions next to an effect are not in the ensure chain."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: gunbc.rung_drop fleet_converge_named_revision_and_branch, plus the instance/target wrapper population valiant-gull-69 censused (do not re-derive). (1) Explicit target+candidate selection consumed at the effect. (2) Do not restore universal main-only. (3) Grants and leases stay distinct prerequisites in the same graph, not absorbed into ensure. (4) Wrappers that pin srv1_live_dashboard_instance while the core is already *_for_instance are this leaf's inventory, not a second census."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_6XYMKSJ1TTTE4XQ1RTZMFG19GM",
      id: "cc-evidence-to-consumers",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/rung_drop.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A result qualifies the exact candidate and behavior the next step relies on",
        boundary: "F05, F06, F09/F57, F15, F32, F34, F42, F51, F53, F59. The required job covers two emitted closures and does not evaluate witnesses or compare generated artifacts (gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn), so green CI does not establish serving/deployment closure or the sudoers projection. Witness results that found a regression did not constrain the merge; evidence was for another revision; a projection lost its consuming gate; an unobserved claim supplied no execution evidence; a real type error sat outside the required population. gunbc.design_argument::consumption plus the pairing obligation: supplying inputs may never remove the last execution of the real path.",
        displaced_cost: "Green required CI is read as the workspace being closed. It is not.",
        first_slice: "Name, for one census path (sudoers projection or serving/deployment closure), the exact candidate and instrument whose result the next step must consume, and the typed gap while v1_required_lanes_withdrawn stands.",
        red_control: "A next step that proceeds on green required CI without the named instrument's result for that candidate keeps this red. An inhabitance claim that deletes the last real-path execution stays green -- that is the pairing-obligation RED.",
        out_of_scope: "Not reopening the job-roster-closed-to-growth ruling, not putting the whole witness floor back on the required job in this leaf, not measuring a count copied from the current tree.",
        handback: "The named candidate-qualified evidence join for the first path, the pairing-obligation control, and remaining paths rostered against the census."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "A chain that stops at an unused result has not reached the consumer that needed the established fact."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: one census path (sudoers projection or serving/deployment closure) and gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn. (1) Qualify evidence by candidate identity. (2) Do not reopen the job roster. (3) Pairing obligation: the last real-path execution stays. (4) Remaining paths rostered, not counted from the tree."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_QFTG2N0RXM7R70HPJ8BDDHH045",
      id: "cc-guaranteed-cleanup",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/a_held_compute_seat_has_no_in_corpus_discharge.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Every held resource converges to released once its owner is proven ended",
        boundary: "Modeled as an ensure over std.upsert_decision, not a new decision algebra. Converged = held by a live owner (Noop). Drifted = owner proven ended, still held (Apply). Inaccessible or UnknownRefused = Refuse and keep the charge. Independent readback; a named driver. Instances (ledger 2026-10-11, https://claude.ai/artifact/7AMGHuyVXu1U7bFXDnbG1M): compute seat (F75; Apply = existing gunbc.compute.work_provider_local compute_recover_attempt; class gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_held_compute_seat_has_no_in_corpus_discharge), failed checkpoint unit (F68), spent supervisor unit (F72), half-spawned attempt (F20/F21), lease file the recovery leaves behind. First slice: compute seats. Do not free on doubt (the class already forbids over-admission).",
        displaced_cost: "A host that lands daily-workspace work keeps charging seats, units and lease files after the owner ended; at compute_pool_slots = 2, two orphans consume the appropriation.",
        first_slice: "Drive compute seats through the existing compute_recover_attempt door as the Apply of this ensure, with independent readback that the seat is released only when the owner is proven ended.",
        red_control: "A seat whose owner is proven ended that stays Held with no Apply keeps this red. An Apply that reports success while RecoverySettledButHeld (seat still charged) keeps this red. Freeing on Inaccessible or UnknownRefused keeps this red.",
        out_of_scope: "Not a second recovery door beside compute_recover_attempt, not discharging on doubt, not finishing checkpoint/supervisor/half-spawn/lease-file instances in the first slice, not minting a new ensure syntax.",
        handback: "The compute-seat ensure (observe/decide/apply/readback) with compute_recover_attempt as Apply, the class RED still enrolled, and remaining instances rostered by identity."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "convergence-coverage", contribution: "An ensure chain that never releases a held resource after the owner ended leaves the daily workspace charging the host forever."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_held_compute_seat_has_no_in_corpus_discharge and gunbc.compute.work_provider_local compute_recover_attempt. (1) Ensure over std.upsert_decision: Converged=Noop, Drifted=Apply the existing door, Inaccessible/UnknownRefused=Refuse keep the charge. (2) Independent readback. Named driver. (3) Do not mint a second door. (4) Do not free on doubt. (5) Remaining instances (F68, F72, F20/F21, leftover lease file) rostered, not repaired in this slice."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_AXXFPYZ1SDMHS62PGYAWH6Z2V2",
      id: "compiler-guarantee",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "The compiler refuses what a compiler must refuse, and says how sure it is",
          boundary: "The guarantee ladder's measurement (schema, probe corpus, claims carrier), the ordinary-floor walls (calls, methods, conformance, records, exhaustiveness, parse formation, generic fields), and the acceptance door that makes the floor blocking. Measured on the compiler the floor runs today, which is the v1 seed under gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing, and on v2 where a v2 twin exists.",
          approach: "Measure, then wall class by class, then flip the floor to blocking (accepted-floor-obligation-closure). The extended classes wait until the floor closes.",
          red_control: "Any floor class whose reported rung exceeds its executed evidence (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (rung honesty) rung inflation) keeps this red.",
          displaced_cost: "Without a measured floor, \"the compiler accepted it\" says nothing. Wrong programs are caught late, in rustc or in production.",
          handback: "accepted-floor-obligation-closure accepted, with the ladder census re-derived from receipts."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The compiler that goes live must hold the ordinary floor (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder). A self-hosted compiler that accepts wrong programs only makes those wrong programs cheaper to produce."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_ZBFRF5QZPMSD6FY93DR7GRATHV",
      id: "v2-complexity-analysis-parity",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/v2_complexity_capability_parity.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Give the new compiler the cost analysis the old one had, and let something act on it",
        boundary: "gunbc.plans.v2_complexity_capability_parity phases C1 to C6: v2.lens.cost derives a work, span and space summary for a function, evaluates it on concrete bounded inputs, and feeds a consumer that refuses a change which makes a linear function quadratic. This row also owns three items that plan assigned to the deleted discrete-cost-derivation note: the valuation environment, bounded-input evaluation (C3), and the witness-cost admission consumer.",
        displaced_cost: "The v1 seed can report that a function is quadratic and v2 cannot, so a cost regression in v2-compiled code is found by a slow run instead of at compile time.",
        first_slice: "Decide whether the plan absorbs the three inherited items or drops them, and record that in the plan; then the next unlanded phase after C0.",
        red_control: "A planted accumulator-copy loop that the summary reports as linear keeps this red; so does a blocking mode with no live consumer.",
        out_of_scope: "Not pricing CI lanes or scheduling the fleet, and not restoring the v1 floor's per-claim budgets.",
        handback: "The derived summary on a real function, the bounded-input evaluation, and one live consumer that refused a planted regression."
      ), on: "2026-10-10", note: "Added when the discrete-cost-derivation note was deleted (gunbc#13697). Not dispatchable until the plan records who owns the three inherited items.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A blown complexity bound is one of the classes gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder says the ladder reaches above the ordinary floor."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_M276MK15AHKZ2KWHTPWXR2WMAW",
      id: "declaration-provider-outcomes",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/resolve.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "A closure provider's availability is per declaration; only module admission is module-wide",
          boundary: "Operator ruling 2026-10-14 (Option B). A declaration is available to an importer exactly when the module namespace needed to interpret it was admitted, that declaration resolved, and every declaration outcome its demanded semantics depends on is available; an unrelated declaration's refusal does not make it unavailable. MODULE-WIDE failures stay module-wide: an unreadable or malformed root, an unavailable or ambiguous module header, an incomplete namespace, a cross-tree policy refusing the namespace, or any failure that leaves declaration boundaries or the candidate population unestablished. DECLARATION-LOCAL failures refuse the declaration and its dependents only: an unbound name, an anonymous record with no expected type, an unavailable referenced declaration, an unsupported construct in its body or declared type. The CARRIER changes, not the lookup: v2.compiler.resolve ClosureProviderRefusal is one record per refused module and a refused walk contributes no declarations; it becomes a module outcome (ModuleUnavailable with its diagnostics, or ModuleObserved with a per-declaration outcome map), each declaration Available with its resolved declaration and direct dependencies or Refused with its chain. The closure index holds only available declarations and the refusal index is keyed by declaration identity. Because resolve can bind a reference through the pre-resolution symbol index while its target later refuses, a declaration's own clean walk is not enough: the producer resolves each top-level declaration separately, collects its direct declaration references, propagates refusal over them (strongly connected components to a fixed point), and publishes only declarations whose required closure is available. An import lookup has three outcomes: available, refused with that declaration's chain, or genuinely undeclared (unbound). Ignoring the refusal at the importer is forbidden: it reopens what gunbc#13853 closed.",
          displaced_cost: "Since gunbc#13853 a single unbound name anywhere in a provider module refuses every name imported from it, so one unbound Float in std.algebra blocks Cons, Empty and FreeMonoid; native-seven's prepare stops at v2.std.diagnostic for that reason. The alternative, making every provider module resolve completely before any declaration is consumable, makes the module file the semantic unit only because declarations share a file.",
          first_slice: "Reuse the recorded 13/13 seed-hosted provider controls. Reconcile the production admission projection with the same per-declaration outcomes and refusal chains, then rerun the native label after its measured namespace stop is repaired; the seed green alone is not native acceptance.",
          red_control: "A valid declaration beside an unrelated invalid declaration imports; importing the invalid declaration refuses with its own chain; a declaration depending on the invalid one refuses through the dependency edge while an independent third stays available; two mutually dependent declarations, one locally invalid, refuse together; a malformed header or refused namespace makes every declaration unavailable; a genuinely absent name in an observed module stays unbound, not declarer_refused; reverting to the module-grained provider outcome turns the valid-neighbor control red.",
