root.children` in g_tree_has_arrow_body: v2.std.node does not resolve because `Optional` is ambiguous between std.optional.Optional and std.constructors.Cardinality.Optional (resolve_ambiguous_on_lexical_chain) -- this node's own 'Optional ambiguous (Optional de-fork PR B)' item; the de-fork steps #13178 and #13388 are merged, and the residual is the production lookup counting candidates without asking their kind. Refused files: dag/extdeps/filesystem/filesystem_io.dag (service_realization_unreachable, XL-2) and src/v2/std/integer.dag (normalized_tree_reason_wrapper_retention_not_normalized, new on main, cause not investigated)."), on: "2026-10-13", note: "Re-measured by gunbc test //v2/test/parse/expression_bodied_fn_decl_parse:all at 4816cd57ca (n7/parse-wholefile-import). Cleared: root.children -- v2.std.node_query now names std.constructors.Cardinality.Optional in full and v2.std.node renames its parameter-shadowing let, so both resolve; src/v2/std/integer.dag -- its refusal was an index suffix read across a line break (a `[` list literal on the next line), and the grammar now requires the `[` on its operand's line. The first refusal for every member is infer_reason_projection_receiver_declares_no_fields at e.target in g_tree_has_arrow_body, after infer_reason_fold_member_domain_not_a_collection at root.children: Node.children is std.types List<Edge>, and std.types itself fails v2 resolve (resolve_reason_unbound_symbol at replace and sorted_map_keys, which have no std.primitives contract row, and at none; resolve_anonymous_map_key_text_unavailable at its string-keyed map literal), so the List alias does not unfold even though the fold domain is now read alias-normalized. Only dag/extdeps/filesystem/filesystem_io.dag refuses as a file (service_realization_unreachable). The native census (gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census) at b7c40fa403 counts 101 of the closure's 135 modules as refusal roots, so the remaining walls are mostly the std substrate not yet passing v2 resolve rather than unknown chain links."), on: "2026-10-14", note: "Main regressed twice and both were bisected by this label: gunbc#13905 (grammar Optional import collision, repaired by #13960) and gunbc#13832 (an imported refinement type classified as a value, repaired by #14007). gunbc#13853 then, correctly, refuses names imported from a module whose resolve refused; std.algebra has been resolve-refused in every scoped census, so prepare stops at v2.std.diagnostic's std.algebra imports. Prepare no longer passes on names from refused providers; the next wall is declaration-provider-outcomes (operator ruling 2026-10-14, Option B)."), on: "2026-10-15", note: "Scoped census //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census-scoped (the scoped-census acceptance), base e888d6fe03 against gunbc#14119: 139 modules, scope closed, about 19 minutes with the driver build since gunbc#14077 (before it the run took over four hours and never completed). Cleared at resolve: extdeps.transports.file_declared and shell_declared (the bare none literal). Newly exposed: file_declared infer_grounding_not_derived, shell_declared infer_reason_declaration_body_unavailable; v2.compiler.service_realization now first refuses on its own unbound concat and to_string (line 151). Open roots by fan-out: std.error_primitives Float (its own repair); std.algebra and std.types spelling Map and List across their import cycle (fixed at the declaration homes by the NAMESPACE-XL waves lane under the 2026-10-15 rulings: no built-ins, no resolver alias tier); std.algebra anonymous records with no expected type."), on: "2026-10-15", note: "With declaration-grained publication (gunbc#14029) and its follow-ups (#14055, #14088, #14072) the stop is precise: all eight stop at prepare, first on chars unbound in std.content_hash (seed-era built-in), and behind it Map, NotFound (a stale rename) and the compiler-generated std.algebra.FreeMonoid list head that gunbc#13832's kind eligibility refuses. The resolve wall is the v2-namespace-cutover programme (no built-ins; v2 the authority, v1 only sequences; strict first), not further native-seven-local repairs."), on: "2026-10-19", note: "N7 #13069 LANDED (gunbc#14478) AND THE PHASE B EMIT-GROUNDWORK CLASSIFICATION IS RECORDED HERE AS ITS PLAN CARRIER (gunbc.design_argument::consumption: a prose artifact with no carrier is dangling; the PR plan notes were dropped per review 82859 and their substance folded into this thread and into gunbc.recurring_failure_mode fold_realized_loop_carries_no_iteration_direction, which now carries the 6b re-derivation). PHASE B SHAPE, measured at this head: execution is seed-emit plus the emitted binary, and v2.compiler.source_root_eval says THE RENDERED MAIN CALLS THE DRIVER FOLD AND NOTHING ELSE DECIDES THE VERDICT -- Phase B groundwork is therefore driver-closure groundwork, not emitter work; v1.emit_rust emit_source_root_eval_driver_main_rs renders main as one call into the fold. CLASSIFIED: #13069 fold iteration direction SHIPPED, rung 4 by construction (callback_step_row total match; executed flip evidence on ccr_map_direction_is_read_from_its_step_shape). #13210 NativeTestPassed verdict join is INDEPENDENT of Phase A but manager-gated: later, by manager word; its gap is a fold-produced row, the consumer arm already exists in v1.emit_rust. BLOCKED, DO NOT START: #13284 roster-bound concat evaluation waits on the Phase A concat resolution (kernel-text concat is inside the first_slice chain; the 2026-10-15 service_realization unbound-concat refusal is the record) -- authoring its v2 evaluation meaning now would fork a second authority (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority); and B-emitter-1: once emission reaches shared-type realization the v2 emitter consumes the SAME declaration-identity-keyed sharing authority as gunbc#13936, no re-keying by spelling, blocked on 13936 landing. OPEN QUESTIONS FOR THE NODE OWNER, not pre-empted here: (1) which executor is the lane ONE loop authority -- a fold-carried loop interpreter inside the source_root_eval closure, or v2.extdeps.runtimes.v2_evaluator v2_eval_step_loop / v2.program program_step_loop made shared and pulled into that closure (gunbc.design_argument::minimize_redundancy one-concept-one-executor; the operator holds this call and no work builds on either reading; both handlers refuse every Loop today); (2) confirm #13210 rows means driver-fold-produced verdict rows, given the v1.emit_rust consumer arm already renders them."), on: "2026-11-08", note: "SCOPE RESET (gunbc.design_ruling::n7_requires_only_its_own_closure, operator 2026-11-08): N7 depends only on what its own label closure needs to pass. The 2026-10-15 note routing its resolve wall to v2-namespace-cutover (not further native-seven-local repairs) is superseded and the edge native-seven <- v2-namespace-cutover is deleted; whole-repository namespace work is a separate program that gates nothing here. The tokenizer reads host text and reaches structural text only through the declared unfold (gunbc.design_ruling::tokenizer_lexes_host_text)."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. Separate the all-seven typed receipt from execution. Historical first-stop names in the ticket are not a current measurement. Re-run the exact label at this revision with compiler provenance and record whether the subject was reached; infrastructure or binary freshness refusal does not identify a compiler blocker. Resolver/typing fixes remain on their owning prerequisite nodes."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Native execution on srv1, 2026-11-19, source 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c: fresh seed SHA256 fdcb57ff8c73ea822df684a531bf785c1b71eaacaca10b497039a608f66d1b6c emitted 279 files, closure 1f2e1efb75ed2f198fa92455a13c576d45011a5988f7467a548a5b88492f1311; native compiler SHA256 10b502967af83c4e01f2a9c5c660c10e8db98caccd8f3cc9a1bfaa5de3095f95 built offline with -D warnings a