    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_1ZM59ZX3RGYJX81YEJ6Z22Z2QG",
      id: "declaration-identity-switchover",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/resolve.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "Every name reference carries its declaration",
          boundary: "Resolve records a declaration identity on every reference (v1 Node.declaration #12612; recursive types #12635; type parameters #12690; census #12592). All consumers read that identity and not the leaf name (#12506, #12766), under one declared-scope definition (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode name_canonicalisation_depends_on_the_co_compiled_graph). Absorbs namespace-canonical-binding and namespace-bound-only-consumers. Built in shadow now; its root cut is XL-6.",
          displaced_cost: "Consumers matching leaf names can bind a different declaration than resolve chose.",
          first_slice: "Reuse resolved_reference_identity and generated_reference_binding_entries; identify the remaining downstream re-resolution consumers by occurrence category, then switch one actual remaining family.",
          red_control: "A consumer reading a leaf where an identity exists turns the census red. Unresolved and ambiguous references stop before infer.",
          out_of_scope: "Deleting the old lookup (namespace-legacy-choice-retirement).",
          handback: "The census at zero leaf-matching consumers."
        ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: quiet-hawk-702 lane in flight."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. v2.compiler.resolve::resolved_reference_identity and generated_reference_binding_entries exist; #12735 is in history. Reuse those carriers. Residual is checking downstream readers and all occurrence categories for re-resolution, then moving only the actual remaining consumers; the seven category labels are coverage cases, not seven fresh carrier implementations.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "Every reference carries its declaration, with one definition of 'in scope'."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_ERV25EYAMEVV1G6JQ8XAXWDHAS",
      id: "v2-namespace-cutover",
      owner: "namespace",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v2/compiler/resolve.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "v2 namespaces with no built-ins: every name is a declaration reached by import, and v2 is the authority",
          boundary: "Three operator rulings, 2026-10-15. (1) NO BUILT-INS, NO EXCEPTIONS: every name -- including chars, List, Map, none, concat and host-realized operations -- is an ordinary declaration with one home module, reached by an authored reference only through lexical scope, an explicit import or an explicit qualified path. There is no ambient namespace and no automatic prelude. A host-realized operation still has a std declaration with a type signature; its host implementation is a realization bound to it (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority). Resolve's stopgap tiers (the kernel type-spelling table, collection_roster_rows, the std.primitives last tier) never grow: they shrink and are deleted as names move to their homes. (2) v2 IS THE AUTHORITY, v1 ONLY SEQUENCES: the v1 seed may constrain the order in which a change lands, never the v2 semantics. When v1 cannot carry the v2 design, the permitted responses are to update v1 to mirror the v2 authority, to replace or delete the v1 consumer, or to add a narrow named bridge with a deletion trigger; never a v2 exception or a v2 fallback from identity to spelling. 'stage0 expects this spelling' or 'the seed treats it as built-in' explains a compatibility failure and never justifies a v2 design. (3) STRICT FIRST, LOOSEN LATER: unresolved homes and ambiguity refuse rather than pick, the debt ratchet admits no new finding, convenience (a curated explicit re-export of common names) waits for a ruled need, and any relaxation is a later explicit ruling with its reason. END STATE: declaration identity is independent of leaf spelling, alias, packaging and crate neighbours; imports control visibility and local binding but never identity; a compiler-generated reference carries the identity the compiler selected and needs no source import; provider failure is declaration-grained (declaration-provider-outcomes); later stages (type equality, emission) read the same identity, never a leaf-name reconstruction. SEQUENCE: N0 these rules; N1 a whole-tree census classified into compiler-generated reference defects, formerly ambient names, stale renames or missing imports, and real capability gaps; N2 repair compiler-generated references at their producer; N3 an operator-ruled home table (one declaration and signature source per formerly ambient name: List versus FreeMonoid, structural String versus host text, none, collection operations, host-realized operations such as chars); N4 one generator (gunbc#14017 extended, never a second) driven by the home table, plus a v2-to-v2 binding diff on each sweep's own PR in which the only admitted rebinding is an ambient occurrence moving to its ruled home; N5 one generated corpus cutover regenerated against current main; N6 a shrinking v2 resolve debt ratchet and deletion of the stopgap tiers.",
          displaced_cost: "Names the seed supplies ambiently resolve differently, or not at all, in v2, so native-seven and most of the std closure stop at resolve; each lane that meets one is tempted to add a lookup-table row or an alias tier, which grows a second namespace authority beside the declared one.",
          first_slice: "N2 on its first specimen: a list literal lowers (v2.std.list_introduction lower_list_introduction) to a call whose head is the bare qualified spine std.algebra.FreeMonoid. Since gunbc#13832's kind eligibility a call head excludes a type declaration, so `[]` and `[1, 2]` refuse resolve_reason_unbound_symbol even in a module that imports std.algebra { FreeMonoid } (fixture probe at main 2f87f93d8f). Lowering writes the head as a declaration reference carrying std.algebra.FreeMonoid's identity, and infer already reads that form. Then audit every other compiler-generated reference for the same class.",
          red_control: "An authored name that resolves without a declaration reachable by scope, import or qualified path; a v2 tier that binds by spelling when no declaration is visible; a list literal refusing while its head declaration is admitted; a same-spelled foreign declaration capturing a compiler-generated reference; a sweep whose binding diff shows any rebinding other than ambient to its ruled home; a census finding that appears with no explanation; or a stopgap-table row added rather than removed, keeps this red.",
          out_of_scope: "Float and float-literal lowering (a capability gap with its own repair); the infer frontier behind resolve; per-module stale imports and renames, which go to each module's owner.",
          handback: "Compiler-generated references no longer depend on source import visibility; every formerly ambient name has one ruled home or an explicit open decision; the generator and binding diff run over the whole repository; the generated cutover has landed; the ratchet is active; the stopgap tiers are deleted; and no v1-only namespace authority was introduced."
        ), on: "2026-10-16", note: "N2 first slice landed by gunbc#14209: lowering writes the list head as the marked declaration reference to std.algebra.FreeMonoid, the spelled-spine reader is deleted, and resolve answers every compiler-generated declaration reference by declaring path (indexed, provider refused, or the typed resolve_reason_generated_reference_declaration_absent); caller admission no longer reads a list introduction as a call. Receipt, //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census against base fdd6370d09: generated FreeMonoid rows 142,068 to 0 (44,953 roots, 6,118 modules) whole tree and 2,571 to 0 native-seven; no module inferred at base stops inferring; 1,069 whole-tree modules move from resolve to infer, where infer_grounding_not_derived heads 1,317 roots (the A4 frontier, not ranked until resolve clears). Native-seven first stop unchanged: chars unbound in std.content_hash, so N3 continues with chars. NEXT OBLIGATION, N2b: a compiler-generated declaration reference induces acquisition of its declaration provider. Module acquisition reads the parse tree, where a list literal requests nothing, so a closure acquired without std.algebra refuses the head as generated_reference_declaration_absent (fail closed). The repair is one general generated-reference dependency route, the effect T? already has for std.optional (v2.compiler.module_acquisition acquisition_sugar_member_texts) -- never an authored import of std.algebra and never an ambient built-in."), on: "2026-10-17", note: "N3 HOME RULINGS (operator, 2026-10-17). These settle homes; each wave moves its own names in its own PR through the one generator and the v2-to-v2 binding diff. H1: std.types List, Map and Set are the sole language-facing declaration homes. std.algebra owns their structures, templates, operations and laws, and is not a second source-level type home. The kernel type table and fallback rosters stop supplying them, and same-spelled aliases elsewhere are deleted. The ruling settles homes, not representation: the current algebra-carrier aliases stay separately revisable without changing these identities. H2: dag/std/host_text.dag, module std.host_text, type HostText is the single home of the opaque host-text carrier, the operations whose semantics require it, and their target realization bindings. It is never another String: structural text stays v2.std.text String = FreeMonoid<Char>. v2.std.node stops being host text's semantic home. Only host-carrier operations move there; structural equality, split, join, replace and folds stay with structural text. Signatures use dag-layer types such as List<Char>, because dag/ may not import src/v2. Any seed bridge names std.host_text.HostText as its authority and carries a deletion trigger. H3: none is syntax for optional absence, lowered to a compiler-generated reference to std.optional Absent that carries its identity (the N2 mechanism) and needs no import. T comes from the expected Optional<T> or constraint solving, and with no type information inference stays underived or refuses; it never defaults to Optional<Unit>, a free variable or a host null. Authored Absent stays an ordinary reference. The general null spelling is removed, but JSON, SQL, wire and missing-field nulls stay their own modeled values, and the migration census separates them from optional absence first. H4: std.host_text chars(text: HostText) -> List<Char>, defined as the Unicode scalar values of the host text in source order, not bytes, graphemes, UTF-16 code units or lossy decoding. It is a pure declared operation whose host realization binds by declaration identity; missing realization is a typed refusal at realization. Wave 1 imports std.host_text { chars } at genuine host-to-structural crossings, and deletes a chars call whose input is already structural. Any inverse crossing is a separate declared operation. Sequence: the H2/H4 authority PR (HostText, chars and its realization binding, the structural-result and Unicode-scalar controls, no corpus sweep), then Wave 1 chars, then native-seven rerun, then H3 and the type-name waves as separate migrations."), on: "2026-10-18", note: "KERNEL-TYPE LAYER RULE (operator, 2026-10-18), recorded with the Float cut so Float is not the precedent: every supported language-facing type has ONE canonical semantic declaration in its dag-tree domain module; compiler recognition, literal elaboration, semantic denotation and target realization refer to that declaration by identity; compiler-side projections (v2.std.<t>) construct or read its representation and never redeclare it; authored names receive no ambient privilege from kernel registration; a specialized node or primitive row is added only when a consumer needs it. Homes: H5 Float in std.float, opaque, meaning std.kernel_type_denotation binary64, Rust row keyed on the declaration, no node or roster spelling yet, float literals still refused. Int survives as std.integer Int, with the value carrier separated from its algebraic structure (no blind choice of either current body). Bool moves to dag std.logic, merged with Classical into one carrier (keeping the #12583 single-Bool result), node in v2.std.logic. Char goes to std.unicode.scalar, with its dependencies restructured and no bespoke Rust char row while arbitrary ints can reach it. Json: no kernel std.json; the value model stays extdeps.languages.json.emit JsonValue; the subject marker is a format marker to rename; std.types Json is a separate opaque migration. Symbol to std.symbol with projection v2.std.symbol; Unit to std.unit with v2.std.unit; the HostText node to v2.std.host_text; Bytes to std.bytes; Secret to std.secret. List/Map/Set keep their H1 homes, representation revisable. Order: Float now; then Int and Symbol; then Unit and the HostText node; Bool and Char coordinated; then Bytes and Secret; JSON separate. Drift prevention extends the existing witnesses (identity completeness, import honesty, meaning versus realization, migration completeness through the generator and binding diff) rather than adding another roster. Wave 1 and the N7 measurement are not paused for this."), on: "2026-11-08", note: "SCOPE RESET (gunbc.design_ruling::n7_requires_only_its_own_closure and imports_are_the_terminal_name_mechanism, operator 2026-11-08): this node is the whole-repository program and gates nothing in native-seven, whose edge to it is deleted; native-seven passing resolve is no longer part of this handback. Imports stay as the binding mechanism; import-grammar deletion (namespace-import-deletion, XL-7) is withdrawn and its node deleted. Acceptance criteria naming the retired census and binding diff are superseded by per-wave evidence: the touched modules resolve natively, with a discriminating control.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "namespace-unique-on-chain", contribution: "The cutover that makes v2's declared namespace the only one: no built-ins, v1 only sequences, strict first."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_3TSBT7J8RJ82D478ES4K56B45V",
