    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_3TW5WQJD3K97172C5NN807VQ32",
      id: "native-frontier-required-lane",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/rung_drop.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "The native-frontier ratchet runs on every landing",
          boundary: "Mint v2.workflow.native_frontier_roster (RosterUnminted today) from a //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-frontier run. Then add a merge-queue-only STEP inside an existing fleet lane: no new job, and the job roster stays closed (operator ruling Q4, 2026-09-30). Time budget: about 35 minutes per landing; revisit trigger: re-examine the step if it exceeds about 35 minutes per landing or stops catching regressions. Retires drops v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path and v2_native_frontier_nightly_cadence. The emit-build job was made blocking by #12468 but is still labelled NON-REQUIRED; fix the label.",
          displaced_cost: "Nothing runs the ratchet between the deleted nightly and a lane that is not yet live.",
          first_slice: "Run the whole native subject denominator once and bind its live verdict to the required lane under the recorded no-ratchets rule; do not mint a shrink-only floor.",
          red_control: "A landing that adds a debt row refuses. A green run over an unminted roster refuses.",
          out_of_scope: "Production admission; a new CI job.",
          handback: "The roster minted, the step required, and both drops Retired."
        ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The seed has a whole-universe native frontier invocation; a named instrument is not a required executing lane. Keep the recorded no-ratchets decision and missing-member refusal. Do not reintroduce a shrink-only floor under the old first slice wording.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "native-route-to-live", contribution: "The ratchet running on every landing is what turns native regressions from silent into refused."),
      centering: plan(text: "Roster mint slice only. Run gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-frontier on a fleet host. Capture the [native-frontier-roster] proposal it prints. Open one PR that sets v2.workflow.native_frontier_roster from RosterUnminted to the minted proposal, citing the run. Do not touch CI YAML or rung drops. Stop if the run refuses or prints no proposal."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_YEHRGCZXNVT39XA761ENMGZ4WR",
      id: "native-production-admission",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/demand_engine_program.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
          headline: "The native route is admitted as the production route",
          boundary: "NativeProductionAdmission (gunbc.plans.demand_engine_program D10) over the required subject denominator: result-contract coverage, a refusal census, and divergence disposition (old versus new, neither wins by age). Includes the v2-lens-suite obligation: zero v1 lens-body executions. The namespace receipt identifies the qualified resolver as the sole production declaration resolver and records import rejection by both parsers (gunbc.design_ruling::production_namespace_admission_precedes_seed_mirror_removal).",
          displaced_cost: "The daily build still runs on the seed, so v2 proves a replacement nobody uses.",
          first_slice: "Author the verdict type and compute it once over the current route.",
          red_control: "An undispositioned divergence or refusal refuses admission. A fallback to the interpreter refuses. On the production route a qualified reference must resolve to its declaration and a reference only the seed mirror could answer must refuse. An import accepted by either parser keeps admission open.",
          out_of_scope: "Generator promotion (D9).",
          handback: "NativeProductionAdmitted, with its subject receipts, the sole-resolver control and both parser refusals."
        ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: typed verdict not on main; needs the required lane first."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. NativeProductionAdmitted occurs as a demanded plan/roadmap endpoint, not an implemented verdict in the inspected compiler path. Model and compute it over actual subject receipts after the qualified resolver and both import-parser refusals. Interpreter and seed mirror deletion are later work; no circular prerequisite back to those deletions."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Dependency correction under gunbc.design_ruling::production_namespace_admission_precedes_seed_mirror_removal: replace the whole namespace-project prerequisite with names-bind-to-the-unique-declaration and retain import-grammar-and-lines-deleted. The project contains namespace-legacy-choice-retirement, which waits on v1-interpreter-delete, whose quarantine waits on this admission; expanding the container as a prerequisite would restore the cycle. The grammar prerequisite already consumes corpus homing and the qualified resolver, so their production obligations remain. The existing expansion guard now checks both concrete waits and rejects a dependency on the retirement/container nodes."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Execution reading on srv1, 2026-11-19, planning head eb73204ea12a06431581ab97d830e4e23b459e6d: all four roadmap_real_decomposition_expansion_guard_witness controls passed, including every_real_decomposition_expands and native_production_admission_concrete_waits_resolve. Restoring only the old namespace project wait made the latter fail with exit 1. This validates the scheduling dependency repair, not production compiler admission. Raw receipts: srv1:/tmp/merry-node-review.cMh7pMm0/planning.log and .err, planning-red.log and .err, planning-red.patch.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "native-route-to-live", contribution: "D10: the native route becomes the production semantic route. It absorbs v1-ci-floor-cutover and v1-verification-ledger."),
    ),
