      centering: plan(text: "Written by the dispatch that closed it; kept for the reading. Target witness: dag/test/claim/seed_growth_roster_hygiene_witness.dag, module test.claim.seed_growth_roster_hygiene_witness -- the declared test.claim namespace, beside seed_growth_admission_witness.dag. The path this row first named, dag/test/claim/debt/seed_growth_roster_hygiene_witness_test.dag, was refused by the layout check: namespace test.claim.debt has no declared row, and the rows are emitted by gunbc.instruments.layout_migration layout_namespaces_emit, so a subdirectory for one file was the wrong move. (1) RED arm, permanent: a SeedGrowthJustification value whose declarations the roster publishes no version of is refused. It is PLANTED inside a function body, so it never joins the population it measures. (2) Control, accepting: the rows this node dispositioned pass the same fold, which is what stops the red arm from being satisfiable by a join that refuses everything. (3) Bind this row to the red arm with gunbc_claim_execution_contract. (4) Disposition, per row: roster the justification whose hand Rust still stands, delete the one whose declarations are gone from the Rust and whose module nothing imports. Measured on this line there were THREE orphans, not the two first counted: the two named here plus primitive_runtime_body_seed_growth_justification. The census's other items (kind_reflection_seed_growth, floor_teardown_attribution_seed_growth) do not exist on this line; do not look for them. HAND BACK if the population of SeedGrowthJustification values cannot be enumerated without a host scan: it cannot. The declared population is enumerable (v2.std.decl_index data_decl_type_facts), but no Accepted program can read which declarations a List<SeedGrowthJustification> names -- gunbc.rostered_row_join says so and test.claim.long.host_identity_single_authoring_witness executes the demonstration -- so the join runs on a population HANDED to it, the way gunbc.instruments hands one, and the reverse direction (a value the roster never enumerated) is mitigated by this node's per-row measurement rather than mechanically prevented. The rung above is a reflection surface that carries a declaration's value, or a route putting v1_compiler.cli_run.rostered_row_join run_rostered_row_join on the required path; the census scan that would supply the population costs 10 to 27 seconds over the corpus against a 5000 millisecond fast-lane ceiling (gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots). Do NOT substitute a hand-authored population list: a second enumeration beside the roster is the double-authoring defect this node exists to close."),
    ),
