      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Bind the binary that ran a retirement assessment to the revision the assessment claims",
        boundary: "On the unmerged September closure -- origin/session/still-swift-642 and the session/quiet-moth-644 family, commits ef298b6621c3 and 721fd46dda00 authored 2026-09-19, covering PRs gunbc#11680/#11688/#11699/#11693 closed unmerged by gunbai-bot[bot] 2026-09-20 -- the assessment corroborated the checked-out revision and refused on disagreement; on main no such assessment exists (carrier dag/gunbc/runner/runner_slot_retirement.dag git grep -ci assessment = 0 at 977e12a1b400). What is missing is that the EXECUTABLE which evaluated it was built from that revision. The join reads the running image's own reported build identity and admits it only through the trusted delivery route (the fleet-converge retire job taking release-bins from the build job), never from a self-report alone. Its consumer is the host-retirement assessment closure (blockers, terminal, receipt) -- an UNACCEPTED PREREQUISITE, not landed code: that closure was authored 2026-09-19 (ef298b6621c3, 721fd46dda00) and survives only on origin/session/still-swift-642 and the session/quiet-moth-644 family, never merged, its cited symbols with zero hits on main. fleet-retirement-assessment-closure is that prerequisite row and owns its re-derivation on current main; this join is GATED on that row by a typed prerequisite edge -- declared_roadmap_edges is the single authority for the edge (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority), so no edge is spelled out here -- and is admitted for staffing only when that prerequisite is discharged.",
