      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Finish retiring srv2, from an executor that is not srv2, with a readback that proves it",
        boundary: "srv2's retirement as an explicit obligation over its host spec and owned identities. TWO POPULATIONS, NEITHER DERIVED FROM THE OTHER: seven local slot trees (01-05, 11, 12; 11 and 12 have NO systemd unit, so unit enumeration misses them) and four captured registrations: srv2-02 id 251463 and srv2-05 id 251484 PRESENT on the organization (2026-09-19 reads), srv2-11 id 91529 and srv2-12 id 91513 ABSENT (no DELETE, no receipt claiming one). Also decide the ctrl-runner-reclaim timer's disposition. Remaining: plan and apply reaching the target over SSH, graceful retirement, and the authorized removal with its postcondition.",
        displaced_cost: "srv2 was hand-converged to zero workers on 2026-09-18 and the model could not describe that state: on the September closure branch -- never merged, closed 2026-09-20 -- the assessment refused on an ungrounded local population and an unread roster, and the capacity plan refuses for every host while srv2's registrations are unaccounted for. Until the route can act, every convergence is hand SSH and the next one repeats it.",
        first_slice: "Stand on the closure re-derived by node fleet-retirement-assessment-closure -- that row alone owns the re-derivation (review 98194: one owner), this row does not re-derive it -- then ground and clear the closure blockers against real observations, then bring the plan/apply spine to a target that is not the executor: remove the seven local slot trees (01-05, 11, 12); for the four captured registrations take a FRESH READ of each captured ID (251463, 251484, 91529, 91513) at execution time and delete only registrations confirmed present, owned and authorized, recording observed absence for any ID already absent -- never claim a deletion that was not needed (the 2026-09-19 per-ID reads found 251463 and 251484 present, 91529 and 91513 absent; that is history, not a re-read); and decide the ctrl-runner-reclaim timer disposition.",
        red_control: "PLANNED controls, not observed: the three ungrounded-input cases (an ungrounded local census, an unread roster, an unproven build identity) are controls to be EXECUTED once the re-derived closure (node fleet-retirement-assessment-closure) and the provenance join (node fleet-assessment-build-provenance-join) exist; none has been executed and none is claimed as observed behaviour. Measured on main instead: no assessment exists on the retirement carrier (git grep -ci assessment -- dag/gunbc/runner/runner_slot_retirement.dag = 0), and the route refuses by typed outcomes rather than admitting -- observe_slot_retirement_evidence_wet yields SlotRetirementEvidenceAbsent for unmodeled, refused and zero-width hosts (dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_converge_plan_cli.dag:521-535) and the generic plan CLI exits failure TargetNotASubject for any --target (dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_converge_plan_cli.dag:1480); no current-main entry point is claimed here to admit srv2. Post-repair the same request refuses on each ungrounded input, an unobserved roster refuses rather than reading as empty, and an unreadable build identity refuses as unobserved (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed). Retiring srv2 never requires a runnable srv2 runner, and a registration whose ownership is not established by the host capture refuses rather than being deleted.",
        out_of_scope: "No second actuator beside the reviewed plan/apply spine; no deletion authorized by a name prefix; GracefulRetirement stays MethodUnavailable until implemented rather than being discovered as a surprise. srv2 has NO RunnerHostDeploy row at all -- its width is a typed refusal -- so nothing downstream may assume a deploy exists, and a capacity refusal is never a deletion instruction. One realization precondition, measured 2026-09-19: masking a unit whose fragment lives in /etc/systemd/system REFUSES until the fragment is moved (srv2's timer and service fragments were moved to /var/lib/gunbc-retired/20260919/ before both masked at 15:06:30Z); the retirement operation must handle that rather than fail on it, and BOTH the timer and its service must be masked, since an inactive service is not an inhibited one.",
        handback: "One same-revision transaction: the plan artifact at a single revision, the authorized apply receipts, an independent readback, and a second assessment showing nothing outstanding -- completion finishes only on that evidence, where the closure row may finish on reporting a blocker. The re-derived closure is consumed as the verdict of the fleet-converge retirement route: its typed blocker arms gate the convergence package, its receipt names the executor and the removal postcondition, and fleet-assessment-build-provenance-join is consumed by that verdict as the build-identity blocker (gunbc.design_argument::consumption -- a named consumer over an executing route)."
      ), on: "2026-09-24", note: "The brief before the 100-word re-cut, verbatim (obligations kept in the brief, context here): srv2's retirement as an explicit obligation over its host spec and its owned identities. TWO POPULATIONS, NEITHER DERIVED FROM THE OTHER: seven local slot trees (01-05, 11, 12) and FOUR captured registration bindings (srv2-02 id 251463, srv2-05 id 251484, srv2-11 id 91529, srv2-12 id 91513). 11 and 12 have directories but NO systemd unit, so anything enumerating by unit misses them. Of the four, the 2026-09-19 per-ID reads found 251463 and 251484 PRESENT on the organization and 91529 and 91513 ABSENT, so two need an authorized removal and two need no DELETE and no receipt claiming one. Also in scope: the runner trees and the ctrl-runner-reclaim timer's disposition, which is undecided pending whether it serves anything beyond the retired trees. The assessment route landed; what remains is plan and apply reaching the target over SSH rather than reading it locally, graceful retirement, and the authorized removal with its postcondition."), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Archaeology correction, Manager B premise correction 2026-11-24: the 2026-09-24 update asserted the assessment route had LANDED with its three blockers 'typed and visible on every receipt'. That was FALSE of main. Measured at origin/main 65230868362d in a non-shallow full clone: pickaxe over the main lineage (git log origin/main -S<symbol> -- dag src) gives code hits=0 -- ConvergenceAssessment hits=0, LocalPopulationUnavailable hits=1 and srv2_host_retirement hits=1, both hits being the roadmap prose commit a6f10a8f5d (gunbc#11864) itself; the retirement carrier itself greps assessment hits=0, blocker hits=0. The closure was authored 2026-09-19 (ef298b6621c3 'Retire srv2 as a declared obligation, from an executor that is not the target', 721fd46dda00 'The capture is a binding between four identities, not a name') and survives ONLY on origin/session/still-swift-642 and the session/quiet-moth-644 family: 0 of its 60 September-window commits are ancestors of main, and the covering PRs gunbc#11680, gunbc#11688, gunbc#11699 and gunbc#11693 were closed UNMERGED by gunbai-bot[bot] on 2026-09-20 with zero comments and no closure note in any timeline; the auto-close-on-base-deletion mechanism is ruled out (three bases were main; #11693's base session/quiet-moth-644 still exists at tip e346b877b545, unmerged). The branch is an OFFLINE ORACLE only (gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration): the first slice re-derives the closure on current main, no cherry-pick into the post-gunbc#13783 layout, old witnesses ported as REDs at most. The class is filed at gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_roadmap_row_asserts_landed_code_that_exists_only_on_an_unmerged_branch."), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Recut per Manager B premise correction 2026-11-24 (go-word relayed by silent-swift-73, executed by quick-ant-703): first_slice, red_control and handback re-cut to the re-derive-on-main shape because the old red_control and handback were written against the September closure code that never merged; the red_control is now a behavioural RED observable on current main, never the closure is absent, and the handback names the executing consumer. Previous values, verbatim -- first_slice: Re-derive on current main the retirement-assessment closure authored 2026-09-19 (ef298b6621c3, 721fd46dda00) and NEVER MERGED: the host-retirement assessment that refuses on typed blockers -- an unadmitted local census (the model carries the census date in its cause), an unread roster for want of an organization credential, and unresolved build provenance (that join is node fleet-assessment-build-provenance-join) -- then ground and clear those blockers, then bring the plan/apply spine to a target that is not the executor. The closure does not exist on main: the symbols the earlier text cited have zero hits there, so the closure itself, not merely its admissions, is the work list. The branch code is an OFFLINE ORACLE only (gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration): re-derive on current main, never cherry-pick the September code into the post-gunbc#13783 layout; its old witnesses may be ported as REDs. | red_control: Retiring srv2 must not require a runnable srv2 runner; a registration whose ownership is not established by the host capture refuses rather than being deleted; an unobserved roster refuses rather than reading as empty. | handback: One transaction at one revision: plan artifact, authorized apply receipts, independent readback, and a second assessment with nothing remaining. Second pass (review 98194, same PR): first_slice no longer claims the closure re-derivation; node fleet-retirement-assessment-closure is its sole owner.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-application-authority", contribution: "The fabric decides placement from observed fleet facts; fleet health, convergence and hardware observation are those facts."),
