      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "ENCODING-0: land pure .dag CBOR, DER and X.509 parsing (gunbc#11727)",
        boundary: "Pure .dag CBOR, DER and X.509 parsing, reconciled in quarry/11895, DEFERRED on its witness redesign (supplied pre-parsed values plus one real-bytes inhabitance claim) or the kernel arms. Five acceptance obligations, each with a discriminating control: (1) DER OID arcs bounded before pending * 128 + low overflows; (2) the App Attest bundle-version extension enforced before the ECDSA frontier returns; (3) a BIT STRING with nonzero declared-unused bits refuses; (4) the DER primitive/constructed bit enforced IN BOTH DIRECTIONS (controls: Certificate SEQUENCE 0x30 -> 0x10 refuses; a primitive universal value with the constructed bit refuses); (5) CBOR map keys in deterministic order.",
        displaced_cost: "The attestation parsers sit approved but unlandable, and every consumer of std.octet_span waits on them.",
        first_slice: "Re-draft from gunbc#11895 at its immutable quarry head 8fc4448575cd4955c2b3b6c34ac6e300f41d31f1 (tag quarry/11895) with the redesigned witnesses, repairing the five known defects in the boundary, each with its named refusal control.",
        red_control: "The three mutant REDs of the gunbc#11727 receipt stay red, and each of the five boundary defects has a discriminating input that refuses.",
        out_of_scope: "content_hash consolidation, UTF-8 causes and the bytes seam are their own rows.",
        handback: "Return the landed head and the fresh receipt."
      ), on: "2026-09-24", note: "The brief before the 100-word re-cut, verbatim (obligations kept in the brief, context here): Pure .dag CBOR, DER and X.509 parsing, reconciled in gunbc#11895 at its immutable quarry head 8fc4448575cd4955c2b3b6c34ac6e300f41d31f1 (tag quarry/11895) and DEFERRED, not landed: it waits on its witness redesign (claims supplying pre-parsed values plus one inhabitance claim on the real bytes) or on the kernel arms. The reconciled tree is KNOWN INCORRECT in five ways found by review after the split, each an acceptance obligation of this row with its own discriminating control: (1) DER OID arc accumulation is bounded before pending * 128 + low can overflow -- an over-long arc refuses; (2) the required App Attest bundle-version extension is enforced before the ECDSA frontier is returned -- an attestation lacking it refuses; (3) a DER BIT STRING whose declared-unused low bits are nonzero refuses; (4) element matching (der_is, der_expect, der_expect_universal) enforces the DER primitive/constructed bit IN BOTH DIRECTIONS -- a constructed type encoded primitive refuses (SEQUENCE, SET and constructed context-specific containers; control: the outer Certificate SEQUENCE mutated 0x30 -> 0x10 refuses, the exact reported exploit) AND a primitive type encoded constructed refuses (BOOLEAN, INTEGER, BIT STRING, OCTET STRING, OBJECT IDENTIFIER; control: a primitive universal value with the constructed bit set refuses); (5) CBOR map keys are checked for deterministic ordering -- an out-of-order map refuses."), on: "2026-09-20", note: "Reconciled onto main in gunbc#11895 (quarry head 8fc4448575cd) and SPLIT OUT of its landing (operator ruling 2026-09-21): its whole-object App Attest witnesses parse a 4 KB attestation in the interpreter at ~4M eval steps against the 100ms-equivalent new-witness budget. Re-draft from the quarry head with the claims supplying pre-parsed values (gunbc.design_argument::witness_one_interface standing rule) and one inhabitance claim on the real bytes, or behind the kernel arms.")),
