    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_50P0GN3GQK5MSVMMKCZWWZ8YE5",
      id: "optional-admitted-at-record-literal-field",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "src/v1/04_infer.dag"), carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared.dag")),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A T? written at a bare-T record-literal field reaches runtime instead of refusing at resolve",
        boundary: "optional_at_required_obligation_diags in src/v1/04_infer.dag refuses an optional value standing at a Required position, and the recurring-failure-mode row that records the class names the positions it knows: a direct-call argument, a list element, and a member of a list literal whose type was elected from a Required head element. The record-literal field position is not among them, so a T? written into a bare-T field has no typed refusal and was found at rung 1, a runtime TypeError on the interpretation path. The row itself states the next rung: extend optional_at_required_obligation_diags to the record-literal field position in the T?->T direction, with a red fixture, so the refusal lands at resolve with a typed cause. Measured at origin/main on 2026-11-24, two things make this a re-measurement and not a guess. First, dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared.dag mentions pull request 13179 exactly 0 times, still carries rung RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated }, and its receipts are measurements on main 3fabccc35f -- a String? at a String direct-call parameter and at a List<String> element compiling with only an advisory under UndecidableOptionalCarrier, and a list literal with no expected type judged by 0 diagnostics -- so a reader today cannot tell a wall that has since closed from one still open. Second, the extension is unowned: the function name appears 15 times across the tree (6 in src/v1/04_infer.dag, 4 in the generated mirror src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs, 2 in the row itself, 1 each in src/v1/05_emit.dag and in the rows product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted and bare_value_admitted_where_optional_is_declared) and 0 times in dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_authority.dag, so no node claims it. The two nearest rows do not overlap: egress-optional-at-required-tail extends an already-landed wall to five modules outside every gated closure, and cardinality-optional-declaration is about declaration cardinality. Neither touches a field position.",
        displaced_cost: "From the row's own measured history, which is why the silent arm is not merely untidy: when base64_encode was changed to return String? (the gunbc#11626 chain, NUMERIC-BIT-0 #11643), the approval_device_wire call site produced no diagnostic at all, and the regenerated vectors.json rendered the URL path as id-Present { value: ZXNj... } instead of id-ZXNj..., after which the ci-auto-heal bot committed those bytes as e7b8ad2 on session/royal-stag-544. Fabricated plausible output reached a committed fixture because nothing judged the written value against the declared field type, and an automated healer then certified it.",
        first_slice: "Re-measure before building anything. Resolve main with git rev-parse origin/main and record the sha, then execute the recurring-failure-mode row optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared at that sha and produce a receipt carrying the sha, the command's own exit status on its own line, and the verdict for a T? written at a bare-T record-literal field -- admitted, advisory, or refused with a named typed cause. Then update the row's rung from what was executed, not from the 3fabccc35f receipts it still carries. Every negative claim prints its hit count beside a positive control that demonstrably fires, because the whole class is a claim that a check did not run.",
        red_control: "The row's red fixture fails at main -- admitted with only an advisory, or reaching rung 1 as a runtime TypeError on the interpretation path -- with identical failure text at the same main sha and the command's real exit status on its own line, and then refuses with a typed resolve cause at green, in the same command form both times. A green that cannot be distinguished from the fixture never having compiled is not a green: print what the compiler emitted, the diagnostic count, and the exit status.",
        out_of_scope: "The field-projection trigger that the row already records as landed, and the field-declaration direction beyond T?->T at the record-literal field position. Not enumerating the corpus population: the row's own bounded sweep reports only what it inspected and states that the class cannot be enumerated from outside the checker that is itself failing to enforce it, so no population count may be claimed. Not the neighbour mode optional_payload_never_judged_against_declared_carrier, which is a different invalid state -- a Present payload never judged against the declared T. No hand-written seed Rust, no pinned change and no DESIGN.md change: those come back to the lane manager as an escalation for the operator.",
        handback: "The recurring-failure-mode row re-measured at a named main sha, its receipt carrying sha, real exit status and verdict, with the rung updated from execution rather than from the stale 3fabccc35f text; the red fixture's red and green arms in the same command form with their own exit statuses; the typed cause the refusal produces, by name; the hit count beside a firing positive control for every negative claim; the DESIGN.md section relied on, named; and the smallest gap between current behaviour and this contract, stated before it was closed."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "The floor obligation that values inhabit declared types is enforced where a record field is written, not only where an argument is passed"),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
