    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_XMKDEM3GM4NYQ4QXPEDVK4H6MB",
      id: "action-runtime-epoch-observation",
      owner: "generated-artifact",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/extdeps/github/action_runtime_policy.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Notice when the platform's runtime epoch has moved, and when a runner overrides it",
        boundary: "The node-runtime policy epoch is dated and cited, but nothing reads that date against a clock and nothing observes the override variable set in a runner HOST's environment rather than in a workflow. Give the epoch a standing that refuses once a newer cited epoch exists, and observe the runner-side override on the fleet's own runner units.",
        displaced_cost: "The ban on provider-substituted action runtimes holds only while the epoch row is current. When GitHub moves again, the corpus keeps answering Exact until a human notices a warning -- the exact interaction the ban exists to end.",
        first_slice: "Observe the override variable on the runner units and refuse a workflow admitted under an epoch the fleet's runners no longer match.",
        red_control: "An epoch row older than an observed platform change refuses; a runner carrying the override refuses.",
        out_of_scope: "Guessing GitHub's next deprecation date.",
        handback: "Return the epoch standing, the runner-side observation and both refusals."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "ci-end-to-end-execution", contribution: "The required run is the factory verification half; a gap in what it counts, bills or reports is a gap in every landing it gates."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_YTGNRT7FAP4G13E0W9JXDECQ4Y",
      id: "generated-artifact-gate-red-at-main",
      owner: "generated-artifact",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/instruments/generated_artifact_gate.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The generated-artifact drift gate is red at main with eight drifted paths",
        boundary: "At main 91d657a62d72 (and at the head of gunbc#16950, 53ad50a2d8c5, with the identical list) the generated-artifact gate exits 1 on eight paths, each reported as committed content that differs from authority: .github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml, .github/workflows/heal.yml, four fixtures/roadmap_authority/events/ files (scenario-accepted 01-acceptance, scenario-superseded 01-acceptance, 02-revocation and 03-retired, scenario-absent-node 01-acceptance) and provisioning/srv14/gunbc-ghrunner.sudoers. DESIGN.md is read by the gate and is not in the list. Reported by jolly-lark-58, observed on srv1 on 2026-11-23 with the command: target/release/gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/generated_artifact_gate.dag --function main, run from a checkout of the tree with gunbc built from that same tree. Not established: whether the drift predates 91d657a62d72 or is a fixture/binary mismatch in that observation.",
        displaced_cost: "A gate that is red at main on every checkout cannot tell a change that drifts a projection from one that does not, so authors either ignore it or regenerate by hand without knowing which of the eight their change moved.",
        first_slice: "Establish the cause before any regeneration: run the same command at the parent of 91d657a62d72 and at one earlier revision with a binary built from each tree, record per path whether the drift is present, and name the first revision at which each path drifts or that the observation is a binary/fixture mismatch. Then regenerate through generated_artifact_gate main_wet only the paths the cause says are genuinely drifted.",
        red_control: "OPEN: no executed pair is recorded. The red observation is the eight-path output at 91d657a62d72 cited above; the green is the same command exiting 0 at a named later revision, recorded as data when it exists.",
        out_of_scope: "Editing any generated file by hand, and changing the gate's comparison. The required job's membership.",
        handback: "Return the cause per path, the revisions compared, the regeneration (or the finding that none is owed) and the green run of the gate at the resulting revision."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "ci-end-to-end-execution", contribution: "The required run is the factory verification half; a gap in what it counts, bills or reports is a gap in every landing it gates."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_GXK7JBRQS1EQA7YMMXX4Z66QBE",
      id: "self-host-promotion-admission-witness-does-not-compile",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/test/claim/self_host_promotion_admission_witness.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A claim module about self-host promotion admission does not compile, so none of its claims run",
        boundary: "Reported by warm-fox-517 from loyal-carp-337's base-to-head join on gunbc#16897 (base 68dfd570fc02, head e679a90e670b): dag/test/claim/self_host_promotion_admission_witness.dag does not compile at either side, error at line 348 column 14, empty list literal: expected type is not a collection (the empty: [] argument of the fold_list in pa_closed_over, as read at main 6d6fc857e3aa). The reporter counts 19 claims in the module, each FAILing with identical text on both sides, so the failure is invisible in a join. The 19 is the reporter's count from the join, not a scan. Not established: whether any roster or coverage count now quoted includes these claims.",
        displaced_cost: "A check module that cannot compile reads as FAIL with the same text before and after every change, so nobody sees it is dead, and any coverage figure that counts its claims counts claims that never run.",
        first_slice: "Scan every claim in the module at main, reproduce the compile error with the exact command at one named sha, and state whether any roster or coverage count in circulation includes the claims; then make the module typecheck without weakening its assertions.",
        red_control: "OPEN: red_at is the compile error reproduced at a named main sha with the command; green_at is the same module compiling and its claims executing PASS at a named later sha. Neither is recorded yet and no sha is invented here. The first_slice scan states, as part of the control, whether a quoted coverage count includes these claims.",
        out_of_scope: "Judging the severity of the finding. Changing what the claims assert.",
        handback: "Return the reproduced error and sha, the per-claim scan, the statement about quoted counts, and the module compiling with its claims run."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "Primitive egress, interpreter cost and self-host admission are what the self-hosted compiler needs before it is the one that runs."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_63KX4CB2GGD5BA5C6J56NBPV5E",
      id: "bignat-bit-widths-typed-as-bit-width",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/std/bignat.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Carry bit widths in dag/std/bignat.dag as the std.measure BitWidth, not as bare Int",
        boundary: "Reported by warm-fox-517 from review 97694 (claude provider, gunbc#16960, request_changes at f5eb4cffb569cc5163b5cb81f965d4b7f5fea972 over a new BignatBitBuffer field carrying bits as Int). Counted by the reporter at origin/main: zero occurrences of BitWidth in dag/std/bignat.dag, seven bare width or bits fields typed Int, and every width-taking signature (bignat_to_octets, bignat_fit_octets, bignat_limb_bits, bignat_pad, bignat_truncate, montgomery_r_squared, montgomery_modulus) takes Int. std.measure already declares BitWidth (Measure<Information, One, Nat>) with bit_width and bit_width_count. A grounding defect: a bare Int stands where the shared quantity model has the type. Not established: which of those width parameters count bits and which count limbs or octets; only a bit count is a BitWidth, so the first slice classifies each before any retype. The counts are the reporter's, not re-measured here.",
        displaced_cost: "A bit width and a limb or octet count are both Int, so a caller can pass one for the other with no refusal, and each new field in the module copies the bare convention.",
        first_slice: "Classify each of the seven fields and each width-taking signature as bits, limbs or octets with the exact command and revision of the count; then retype only the bit counts to BitWidth through its declared constructors, as one change to the module.",
        red_control: "OPEN: no executed pair is recorded. Obligation, not optional: a retype can move interpreted step counts, so the before and after of the p256 verification baseline (48,296,785 eval_steps for one member at tree 91d657a62d72, reported by warm-fox-517) and of the cut (p256-verify-cost-cut) are both re-measured with one binary on the same tree, and no step comparison across binaries is accepted. A caller passing a limb count where a BitWidth is demanded refuses at typecheck.",
        out_of_scope: "Doing the retype inside the p256-verify-cost-cut row or any row whose red_control is a step threshold. Changing what any bignat function computes.",
        handback: "Return the classification, the retyped signatures, the one-binary before and after step counts for the p256 baseline and the cut, and the refused wrong-unit caller."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "Primitive egress, interpreter cost and self-host admission are what the self-hosted compiler needs before it is the one that runs."),
      centering: plan(text: "Timing relayed 2026-11-23 by neat-badger-614 via warm-fox-517 (not recorded in gunbc.design_ruling): file non-dispatchable; sequence after p256-verify-cost-cut lands and after the P-256 witnesses stop being interpreted, since the interpreter's per-step cost is what the numbers are sensitive to."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_BJ10YHEPG9ESNJ7YV7VD9KWYTF",
      id: "compiler-identity-invariant-under-corpus-commit",
      owner: "v1-performance",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/typed-module-cross-run-materialization.md"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Compiler identity that does not move with the commit SHA, so cross-push reuse becomes reachable",
        boundary: "std.interface_summary typed_module_key consumes a compiler identity it does not author, and its realization today is v1_compiler.closure_identity transform_content_digest -- the content hash of the RUNNING BINARY. src/v1/stage0/build.rs embeds GUNBC_BUILD_IDENTITY, the checkout's commit, into that binary through cargo:rustc-env, so a rebuild at ANY new commit re-keys every entry, including a corpus-only .dag commit. Derive the identity from what the TYPECHECKER actually is instead.",
        displaced_cost: "Every cross-push reuse claim in the materialization design depends on this and none of it is reachable without it. The store as landed delivers same-build cross-process reuse only, and that limit is a property of this derivation rather than of the store.",
        first_slice: "Establish which producers consume the identity (the resolved-graph subject digest and the typed-module key both do), then change the derivation in ONE place and test it through a normal .dag-only rebuild -- an actual changed-commit experiment, not one commit rerun warm.",
        red_control: "A v1 Rust change to inference must still miss every entry; a corpus-only .dag commit must hit for unaffected modules. Both directions, or the new identity is either unsound or useless.",
        out_of_scope: "Do not remove build provenance: the SHA stays in the CLI version. Do not run an old compiler to manufacture hits.",
        handback: "The new derivation, its single consuming authority, and the two-direction experiment."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "Primitive egress, interpreter cost and self-host admission are what the self-hosted compiler needs before it is the one that runs."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_A0SYP0J1P3JE8W8OBX6M3BD777",
      id: "roadmap-operator-attested-acceptance",
      owner: "harness",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_operator_acceptance.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The operator can accept a node on a written attestation, kept visibly apart from executed work",
        boundary: "Operator acceptance today (roadmap_acceptance_record_cli in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_cli, the law in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_operator_acceptance) closes a node only on an EXECUTED red control and a DELIVERED handback, so an old or prose-only node with neither can only be Retired (kind=retire, gunbc.design_ruling::operator_may_arbitrarily_retire_any_work_item) and never accepted. Give the operator a typed attestation arm beside the executed arm -- e.g. OperatorAttested { note: NonEmptyStr, author } -- admitted in place of an executed red control, written only by the operator's principal. Every consumer of the receipt must render it as ATTESTED and never as executed: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model (the RoadmapAcceptanceReceipt schema, receipt_evidence_complete, receipt_matches_node), gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_operator_acceptance (roadmap_operator_acceptance_receipt_line, roadmap_operator_acceptance_receipt_is_closable), gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_log (roadmap_acceptance_receipt_members and the standing projection), gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_verification_receipt (the native receipt parser), gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_issue_command (issue_command_acceptance_evidence_law), gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_cli (roadmap_acceptance_record_cli), and the readers gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_presentation (issue_standing_text, standing_chip_nodes) and gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_page (the closing page). A manager or worker principal that attempts to write an attestation is refused with a typed reason; a non-operator must not be able to make a manual acceptance read as tested work.",
        displaced_cost: "Today a node whose evidence no longer exists -- or that never had an executed control -- has no honest closing except Retired, which loses the operator's judgement that it was actually done. Either the operator retires real work or leaves it dangling; there is no way to record a considered manual acceptance without it being mistaken for a tested one.",
        first_slice: "Add the typed attestation arm to the acceptance receipt beside the executed arm -- a distinct variant, never coerced into executed -- gated on the operator's principal, and carry that kind through the standing so it is labeled ATTESTED at every reader.",
        red_control: "A witness admits an attested acceptance carrying a non-empty note and the operator author; a planted empty note refuses; a manager or worker principal attempting to write the attestation refuses with a typed reason; a witness shows standings, the closing page and every reader carry the attested kind distinctly as ATTESTED and never as executed -- a coercion of an attested receipt into the executed arm reds.",
        out_of_scope: "Do NOT coerce the attestation into the executed arm, do NOT weaken the executed red-control/handback requirement for the executed path, and do NOT edit any pinned oracle: widening issue_command_acceptance_evidence_law's closed set to admit an attested arm needs its own design ruling quoting the operator (\"i think manual acceptance should be allowed with a note\", 2026-11-17) and is not taken here.",
        handback: "Return the attested receipt arm with its note and operator author, the typed non-operator refusal, the standing/closing-page rendering that keeps ATTESTED distinct from executed, and the witnesses named above."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The factory's closing half is how work is accepted; the operator needs an honest, distinguishable way to close old or prose-only nodes without pretending they were executed."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_T9WMSXR8TINTG2USDRXH82NQKJ",
      id: "roadmap-criteria-digest-validated-at-write",
      owner: "harness",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_cli.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A mistyped criteria digest is refused when the acceptance is written, not when the page closes",
        boundary: "roadmap_acceptance_record_cli (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_cli) admits an acceptance receipt whose criteria_digest does not equal node_criteria_digest (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model, roadmap_criteria_digest) of the node on the declared plan; only the closing page-join live_receipts_join_declared_nodes (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model, via receipt_matches_node) enforces the digest, so a mistyped digest is admitted at write and fails later -- a fail-closed gap. Refuse, at write time, a receipt whose criteria_digest does not equal the node's plan digest, with a typed located diagnostic. Also give a runnable way to print a node's plan digest: none exists today, so the last recorder had to write a throwaway module.",
        displaced_cost: "Every recorder re-derives the digest by hand or writes a throwaway module to obtain it, and a single mistyped character is admitted silently at write and surfaces only as a page-join failure much later, far from the mistake that caused it.",
        first_slice: "At the write route, compare the receipt's criteria_digest against node_criteria_digest of the node on the declared plan and refuse a mismatch with a typed located diagnostic; add a runnable command that prints a named node's plan digest.",
        red_control: "A receipt whose criteria_digest differs from the declared node's plan digest refuses at write with the located diagnostic; a receipt carrying the matching digest is admitted; the runnable print command reproduces node_criteria_digest for a named node, so a recorder needs no throwaway module.",
        out_of_scope: "Keep live_receipts_join_declared_nodes as the closing backstop -- this moves the check earlier, it does not remove it; and do not change what the digest is computed over (the node's criteria rows via roadmap_criteria_digest).",
        handback: "Return the write-time refusal with its typed located diagnostic, the admitted-on-match case, and the runnable plan-digest print command."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "Acceptance is the factory's closing half; a digest checked only at the closing page admits a bad receipt at write and fails far from the cause -- validating it at write keeps the closing honest."),
    ),
    // ---- dispatch from the simulated execution (gunbc.plans.planning_consolidation, 2026-11-17):
    // The workspace and its workers belong to factory (#gunbc.design_ruling::roadmap_scheduling_units_belong_to_factory).
    // The schedule a read answers -- leaf occurrences, a list schedule over them, the calendar that
    // binds its days, claims that name a leaf, the in-flight set and the realized durations derived
    // from the log, the schedule from now, its bottlenecks and its offer, the leaf-grain frontier and
    // the dispatch that carries a leaf, the typed handback, the projection every reader reads and the
    // page that renders it. DECLARATION ONLY: the rows are the units, each one PR, each with its red
    // control in its own ticket. No leaf is a node here: a leaf has no identity until it is claimed.
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8MY69FQRA0RE37AHAB",
      id: "roadmap-schedule-leaf-expansion",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_decomposition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "A decomposition reads as leaf occurrences with the edges between them",
        boundary: "roadmap_decompositions expands into leaf OCCURRENCES: one per leaf, a FindingsOf family at its declared assumed count carried as a simulation input, and dependency edges between occurrences -- stage k on stage k-1, and each waits_on row aimed into the child's stage. The expansion writes nothing; every schedule and every readiness below reads it.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it a schedule can only count items, so an item with three parallel leaves holds the critical path for one leaf's days and the offer keeps naming work that cannot start. Every unit below reads this expansion.",
        first_slice: "Run roadmap_schedule_leaf_expansion_witness against the current decomposition, including the real factory row and controlled decision barrier; submit the existing expander evidence for acceptance.",
        red_control: "A planted waits_on naming a stage the parent's decomposition does not have refuses by CONSUMING THE CARRIER'S EXISTING CLAIM: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_decomposition's own well-formedness witness is what refuses, and the expansion calls it rather than re-checking a row the carrier has already admitted.",
        out_of_scope: "No scheduling, no calendar, no in-flight set, no dispatch. No leaf is minted as a node in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority: a leaf has no identity until it is claimed.",
        handback: "The occurrence list for one decomposition at a declared count, the refusal output for the planted stage, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. Leaf expansion and its dedicated witnesses already exist, including FindingsOf nonclaimability, invalid waits, decision barriers and the real factory decomposition. Residual starts with executing the current witnesses and acceptance evidence; no fresh expander implementation is justified.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The expansion is what makes a leaf legible at all: a dependency, an estimate and a dispatch all have something to name. What to work on stays the operator's choice (gunbc.design_ruling::planning_scheduling_is_cut)."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8N43DQ0V7XT2EZKX04",
      id: "roadmap-schedule-list-scheduling",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_decomposition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "List scheduling that answers in days, lanes and a critical path",
        boundary: "Over the expansion: longest remaining path first, a worker count taken as an INPUT, and a zero-day Join placed without a worker. It answers, per leaf, its start and finish day; the lane it sits in; how many leaves are in flight each day; and the critical path. Days stay abstract until the calendar unit binds them. The answer is COMPUTED from the decomposition carriers and the item event log; it MAY be cached, and a cache is derived and never authoritative, so every read recomputes it (gunbc.design_ruling::schedule_answers_are_computed_cached_and_re_read, which narrows gunbc.design_ruling::planning_scheduling_is_cut). No schedule type, time-period record, forecast state or synchronized today list is written as such, and the worker count stays an input shown as an input. Its consumers are the bottleneck-and-offer row and the projection.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the days a decomposition carries are an input nobody can test against reality, and there is no critical path to define a bottleneck or an offer. Every later schedule unit reads this answer.",
        first_slice: "Run the existing one-worker and two-worker schedule controls after the shared placement-core change; retain the per-leaf outputs and refusal evidence for acceptance.",
        red_control: "A two-leaf chain under one worker finishes at the SUM of the two days; two independent leaves under two workers finish at the MAX of the two. Both answers come from one run.",
        out_of_scope: "No calendar, no claimed leaves, no decision about who works. The worker count is shown as an input and never becomes a fact.",
        handback: "The schedule output for both fixtures (start and finish per leaf, lanes, in-flight count per day, critical path), the two refusal outputs, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule already computes leaf schedules, now sharing placement machinery with roadmap_item_gantt. Reuse it and run the one/two-worker controls. Remaining evidence and integration should not be estimated as writing another scheduler."), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Estimate basis for the seven existing scheduling/log units reviewed together: one working day each is an evidence-and-consumer-check prior, replacing implementation priors where the function and witness already exist. This does not price a discovered regression at zero or authorize accepting any node without its handback.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The simulated execution is the scheduler; without its answer there is no critical path to bottleneck or offer from."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8PQK11YFYV0QV0SM74",
      id: "roadmap-schedule-calendar-binding",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_decomposition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Day zero is the read date, and a week has five working days",
        boundary: "The schedule's abstract days become dates: day 0 is the date the read was taken, and a week has five working days. The binding is kept out of the scheduler so the scheduler stays testable on days alone and the calendar is read separately. No date here is a dependency or a gate -- the dependency reading is the edges -- and no date is authoritative between reads: a cached date is derived and recomputed on read (gunbc.design_ruling::schedule_answers_are_computed_cached_and_re_read, narrowing gunbc.design_ruling::planning_scheduling_is_cut), and the dated clock stays gunbc.design_ruling::effort_estimates_are_public_and_live_in_gunbc.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the days in the answer are not the days anyone will see: an item finishing on day 0 of a read taken on a Friday would read as a Friday finish.",
        first_slice: "Run the existing calendar witness for a weekday read, weekend read and one-week-later read; retain dated output from the existing calendar binding.",
        red_control: "A leaf finishing on a non-working day reads as the NEXT working day, never as the weekend; the same schedule read one week later moves every date by seven days and changes nothing else.",
        out_of_scope: "No scheduling policy change: the order and the worker count come from the scheduler unit unchanged.",
        handback: "The dated output for one read, the weekend output and the one-week-later output, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule_calendar already binds abstract days to a five-day week and excludes weekends. Reuse it and its witness; no new date arithmetic is needed. Holiday calendars are outside the declared scope.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "A schedule nobody can date is not a plan; the read date is what makes the answer about today."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8QQ2EYRW11GZWGRFTB",
      id: "roadmap-claim-names-leaf",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_log.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "A claim names the leaf it claims, in the decomposition's own spelling",
        boundary: "The Claimed payload names the LEAF PATH -- item, stage index, piece index, and the member index for a family at its declared count -- spelled as the decomposition spells it, the same three indexes the carrier's well-formedness check reads. A path the decomposition does not have refuses at append.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the in-flight set, the realized durations and the offer can only be spoken of per item, which is where the belt stops today: two workers cannot take one item's leaves side by side. A claim that names only its item is refused at append, from the first landing (gunbc.design_ruling::claims_name_their_leaf_from_the_first_landing); what the refusal leaves outstanding is tracked and prioritized rather than admitted.",
        first_slice: "Verify the existing leaf coordinate decoder at append: one real decomposition path admitted, one nonexistent path refused with the log unchanged.",
        red_control: "A planted Claimed whose path is not in the decomposition refuses AT APPEND, by consuming the carrier's existing claim rather than re-checking the spelling here.",
        out_of_scope: "The ruled shape is not reopened here (gunbc.design_ruling::claims_name_their_leaf_from_the_first_landing): no migration arm is built, and a live item-level claim that predates the landing is re-recorded against its leaf or released -- the set of such claims is a work item of its own. No leaf becomes a node.",
        handback: "The accepted append, the refused append output, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_log::roadmap_claim_grain_parse already reads leaf coordinates and preserves pathless history. Residual is proving append admission against a real decomposition and a nonexistent leaf, not adding the leaf field again.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "Every leaf-grain answer downstream is a fact about a claimed leaf, and a claim that names only an item cannot carry one."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8R27QGW6MFE9WB6G4F",
      id: "roadmap-leaf-in-flight-set",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_log.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Which leaves are in flight, derived and never written",
        boundary: "The in-flight leaves are those with a Claimed and nothing after it: no Released, no HandedBack, no Retired, no acceptance. The set is DERIVED from the log and never written down, so it cannot go stale.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it in flight is a list somebody maintains, and the first missed release makes it wrong: the offer and the highlight would both point at leaves nobody holds.",
        first_slice: "Run roadmap_leaf_in_flight_witness against claims, releases and acceptances, then confirm consumers use roadmap_leaf_in_flight_set rather than a separately maintained set.",
        red_control: "A leaf claimed and then released is NOT in flight; the same log replayed without the release puts it back.",
        out_of_scope: "No in-flight record is ever written; what a claim carries belongs to roadmap-claim-names-leaf.",
        handback: "The derived set for the planted log with and without the release, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_log::roadmap_leaf_in_flight_set already derives claims and closures from the log, with a dedicated witness. Reuse this set in consumers; execute release/acceptance controls before claiming completion.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The projection's in-flight column and the page's strip are one derivation from the log; a second copy of that fact is how a projection starts lying."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8S3EY06Q6JCZA2F57G",
      id: "roadmap-leaf-realized-duration",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_decomposition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "A completed leaf's realized duration, read from the log, replaces its prior",
        boundary: "A leaf's claimed-to-accepted working days are read from the log. Where a realized value exists the schedule takes it and REPORTS WHICH VALUE IT USED; otherwise it takes the prior. Realized values replace the declared priors as they accumulate: the priors are simulation inputs.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the plan keeps quoting the day counts it started with, the estimates never meet the work, and the next round of estimates has no source.",
        first_slice: "Run roadmap_leaf_realized_duration_witness and retain its prior-versus-realized output, including an accepted leaf without a claim; reuse realized_duration_fold.",
        red_control: "An accepted leaf with NO claim has no realized duration and the fold SAYS SO in its output -- it does not read as zero days and does not fall back to the prior silently.",
        out_of_scope: "No change to the scheduler's order; no estimate is re-issued here, which is gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_effort_estimate's work.",
        handback: "The fold output for a leaf with a realized duration and for an accepted leaf with no claim, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_leaf_realized_duration::realized_duration_fold already distinguishes realized spans and missing evidence. Reuse it and its witness. The remaining handback must show the chosen prior/realized value, including accepted-without-claim behavior.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The simulated execution is only honest if realized days replace the priors the moment they exist."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01PXNRMP5HTMEKQ8W68JRAQ1D3",
      id: "roadmap-estimates-cannot-contradict",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: [
        Pointer { label: "authority", path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_effort_estimate.dag" },
        Pointer { label: "authority", path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_estimate_derivation.dag" },
        Pointer { label: "witness", path: "dag/test/claim/roadmap/roadmap_estimate_derivation_witness.dag" },
      ],
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "estimates that cannot contradict: one representation, derived upward",
        boundary: "The estimate row and its one conversion table are the whole authority (gunbc.design_ruling::estimates_are_one_representation_derived_upward). A row names either a size or a duration in working days, never both, and one table converts them both ways: size to duration is the range's midpoint, duration to size is the band that contains it, calibrated from the measured rows in roadmap_effort_estimate's header (an easy node is about a week, a hard compiler node 10 to 16 weeks) and re-calibrated when roadmap_leaf_realized_duration shows a band's realized days outside its range. The upward derivation and every contradiction follow CONTAINMENT ONLY -- in_project membership and decomposition-piece membership -- and never a prerequisite edge: prerequisites order siblings, they do not contain them, so two sequential tasks each carry their own price and no shared prerequisite is ever counted into a parent twice. An authored estimate on a node with an estimated descendant is the contradiction, refused BY NAME with both sides carried in the refusal -- the operator's own case, a project at 1w beside one subnode at 2w, is the witness. The dated rows already appended to roadmap_effort_estimate are history: none is deleted or rewritten, and the check reports every conflict with both sides. Decomposed items already price their pieces (WorkPiece.days read through piece_member_days), so those days are that item's leaf estimates and are not restated. A stated size is admissible only as a labelled estimate with a basis, never as a measured fact. No hours anywhere: a duration is the scheduler's marked working-day Int, with its feature/dissolve-on markers. roadmap_sizing's Intricacy x Volume calibration is a derivation input ABOUT a task and not a size OF a node, so it is not a second representation of the same fact; the merge trigger is realized durations per band, at which point the bands re-calibrate from that same population. NOT IN THIS ROW: the sizing of the roughly 290 nodes, which is its own lane and its own session; no new scheduler -- the item-grain answer places rows through the one placement core and answers over RoadmapNodeIds, and roadmap_schedule stays the leaf-grain scheduler of decomposed items, where they meet being declared here: an item that owns pieces takes its work from the sum of its pieces' days and its elapsed from that item's leaf-grain makespan, so no number is ever priced twice; no authored date beside a duration -- start and finish are bound at the read through roadmap_schedule_calendar; no scope total over a project plus its prerequisites, which is a different question for a different row; the belt's spawn input stays roadmap_schedule's next-leaf offer, which this row does not touch.",
        displaced_cost: "an estimate that can sit beside its own contradiction: a project planned at 1w over a subnode estimated at 2w, one node carrying two durations two consumers read differently, and an unsized node priced at zero by a default nobody chose",
        first_slice: "THIS PR (the mechanism, landed green on its own): the conversion table with its six bands and their measured basis, the one representation whose two arms make a row naming both a size and a duration impossible to construct, the size/duration round-trip witness over every band and band boundary, the upward derivation over fixture rows, the typed refusal firing on the operator's own 1w-over-2w case, containment-only (a prerequisite never makes a price a contradiction), and the append-only release a split leaf needs so a stale price cannot haunt it forever -- 27 witnesses. SECOND PR (the item-grain answer, built on the leaf-grain scheduler's own commit so the placement core is shared and this row never grows a second scheduler): the Gantt rows with their four sources, unsized listed and never defaulted, start and finish bound at the read.",
        red_control: "the operator's contradiction refuses by name with both sides carried -- EstimateContradiction naming the authored parent's estimate and the estimated descendant's, durations and all; a size and its bucketed duration round-trip in BOTH directions for every band (size to days to size returns the same size, days to size to days lands inside the band the days came from); an unsized node appears in the Gantt answer as Unsized with no duration and no dates, never priced at zero and never defaulted to a band's floor; two sibling tasks ordered by a prerequisite, each priced, are NOT a contradiction and both prices stand",
        out_of_scope: "sizing the roadmap's roughly 290 nodes, which is its own lane and session; any second scheduler; any authored date beside a duration; treating an unlabelled size as a measured fact; any scope-level (project plus its prerequisites) total, which is a separate question for a separate row",
        handback: "a PR against main with a green dag-check gate; the contradiction report over the 18 rows already appended, every conflict named with both sides, posted to neat-badger-614 rather than resolved by editing history; and the row format the sizing lane hands back to",
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "the estimates the planning page prices with: one representation per node, parents that cannot contradict their children, and one Gantt answer over the whole roadmap"),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_O7KR37AVRN6K46KKYTTZQ5XPQQ",
      id: "roadmap-unprobed-findings-are-unsized",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: [
        Pointer { label: "authority", path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_decomposition.dag" },
        Pointer { label: "authority", path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_estimate_derivation.dag" },
        Pointer { label: "witness", path: "dag/test/claim/roadmap/roadmap_estimate_derivation_witness.dag" },
      ],
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "an unprobed FindingsOf family is unsized, never priced as one member",
        boundary: "A FindingsOf family's member count is not known until its probe runs, so the pricing must not answer it with an Int. gunbc.design_ruling::estimates_are_one_representation_derived_upward rules that unsized is listed, never priced; the current population_members answers FindingsOf with 1 and piece_leaf_days multiplies the family's days by it, so every unprobed findings family is silently priced as exactly one member and that fabricated count reaches the portfolio totals unmarked. The fix removes the fabricated Int at its source (the population cardinality becomes typed, so stages_leaf_days and stages_leaf_count never see a member count for a findings family), and the one derivation refuses to price an item whose pieces include an unprobed FindingsOf family: it returns Unsized with a typed UnsizedWhy::FindingsUnprobed { family, probe } naming both the family and its probe. The leaf-rule check treats a findings family as non-empty by construction rather than by inventing a count of one. There is still exactly ONE pricing function; the item Gantt already refuses these as PiecesFindingsCount, so after this the Gantt and the derivation answer alike.",
        displaced_cost: "Unprobed findings families reach the portfolio totals priced as one member each: 18 of them at this HEAD, unmarked, so every number the planning page and the portfolio total quote carries 18 fabricated single-member prices, and the item Gantt and the estimate derivation give two different answers for the same item.",
        first_slice: "Add the UnsizedWhy::FindingsUnprobed { family, probe } arm and a typed population cardinality; make the derivation return Unsized for any item whose decomposition carries an unprobed FindingsOf family; red first, an item with a findings family answers Unsized naming its probe, and Produced/Reading families still price members x days.",
        red_control: "Red against today's code, which prices a findings family at 1 x days: an item whose pieces include a FindingsOf family answers Unsized { FindingsUnprobed { family, probe } } naming the probe, NOT Derived at 1 x days; a Produced or Reading family still prices members x days; the live roadmap still derives; stages_leaf_count and the leaf-rule check report no invented member count for a findings family. List which live items flip to unsized.",
        out_of_scope: "no change to how Produced/Reading families price; no change to the scheduler's order; no new pricing function; the probe execution itself and the findings table it writes are unchanged; sizing the roughly 290 nodes is its own lane",
        handback: "a PR against main with a green dag-check gate and a red-first witness; the UnsizedWhy::FindingsUnprobed arm with its witness naming the probe; the list of live items that flip to unsized (measured, not asserted); and confirmation the estimates witnesses and the item Gantt's estimate-derivation consumers answer the same, coordinated with tidy-crane-257's #16729",
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "the estimates that cannot contradict must also never price what has not been measured: an unprobed findings family is listed as unsized, not defaulted to one member"),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8TQNENCQJCKVK0TNT1",
      id: "roadmap-schedule-from-now",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_decomposition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The schedule read from today: in-flight leaves pinned, the rest scheduled around them",
        boundary: "In-flight leaves are pinned at their claim day with their REMAINING days; only unclaimed leaves are scheduled around them, under the same policy and worker count. The answer is the schedule as of the read. A claimed leaf's day comes from the item event log, so the pin rests on a realized fact and not on a forecast; the rest is recomputed at the read, and any cache of it is derived and never authoritative (gunbc.design_ruling::schedule_answers_are_computed_cached_and_re_read, narrowing gunbc.design_ruling::planning_scheduling_is_cut).",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the schedule restarts every leaf at today and loses the week already spent: work in flight is scheduled a second time and everything behind it slips by the days already worked.",
        first_slice: "Run roadmap_schedule_from_now_witness with existing pinned rows, the day-two read and capacity refusal; retain the computed output rather than implementing pinning again.",
        red_control: "A leaf claimed three days ago with five days of work finishes at DAY TWO of the read; a leaf whose remaining days cannot be worked out is refused rather than pinned at zero.",
        out_of_scope: "No new scheduling policy; no bottlenecks and no offer, which is the next row's answer.",
        handback: "The from-now output for the fixture with the pinned rows named, the day-two control output, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule_from_now::schedule_from_now already prices holds, pins in-flight work and carries refusals. Reuse its day-two and over-capacity controls rather than building pinning again; verify the consumer uses the same read date.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The plan is read today, not from day zero; work already in flight is the first fact a read has to respect."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8VN1APM29K9AV9YE29",
      id: "roadmap-schedule-bottlenecks-and-offer",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_decomposition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Bottlenecks and the offer, from the schedule as of today",
        boundary: "A bottleneck is an item with an in-flight or startable leaf ON THE CRITICAL PATH. The offer is the unclaimed startable leaf with the longest remaining path, excluding items the belt withholds. Both are computed from the carriers and the log, may be cached as derived data that is never authoritative, and are recomputed on read (gunbc.design_ruling::schedule_answers_are_computed_cached_and_re_read, narrowing gunbc.design_ruling::planning_scheduling_is_cut). The offer is shown on the projection beside the bottlenecks, so what is planned from the critical path stays visible to the operator.",
        displaced_cost: "Without them the schedule is a picture nobody acts on: what to start next, and what is holding the line, are the two questions the projection and the page exist to answer.",
        first_slice: "Compute bottlenecks and the offer for one fixture whose critical path runs through two items, and show both answers.",
        red_control: "With the critical path through X and Y the offer is X's startable leaf, NOT an off-path leaf that happens to start the same day; an item the belt withholds is never offered.",
        out_of_scope: "No dispatch and no capacity arithmetic: the dispatch row reads this offer.",
        handback: "The bottleneck list and the offer for the fixture, the off-path control output, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The scheduler provides a critical path, and the item Gantt shares the placement core. That does not establish the cross-item offer consumer. Residual is composing the existing result into bottlenecks and a startable unclaimed offer, with the off-path control; no second scheduling policy.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "Without this row there is no bottleneck to look at and no leaf to offer; naming the offer is what lets a dispatch be addressed to a leaf at all."),
    ),
    // The barrier fix for the roadmap-Gantt chain (gunb-ai/gunbc#16650). Declared 2026-11-19 after
    // merry-moth-343's planning review found, on main at 82aff98d, that leaf expansion's stage barrier dies across a
    // stage that emits no occurrence. DISPATCHED: this is the work this PR carries.
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_97HADSFM1HMFG14365YY78ZE0G",
      id: "roadmap-schedule-barrier-through-empty-stages",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_decomposition.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A stage barrier carries through a stage that emits no occurrence",
        boundary: "expand_decomposition's stage barrier links each stage to the NEAREST EARLIER stage that actually emits an occurrence, skipping a stage whose only pieces are Decision / Join / Composite (which by design emit none). A waits_on row that names an empty stage on either endpoint resolves to that stage's nearest non-empty predecessor. REFINEMENT (operator ruling 2026-11-19): an endpoint that is WELL-FORMED -- the stage index EXISTS and the parent edge is DECLARED, so the carrier's own well-formedness claim ADMITS the row -- but whose whole span at-or-below the named stage mints NO occurrence (only Join / Decision / Composite) is NOT refused: it is a wait onto a milestone / project Join that has nothing to wait on, i.e. cross-item ordering no lane schedules yet, so it is RECORDED in the expansion's unresolved_waits (side, stage, and an EndpointEmitsNoOccurrence reason naming the kinds the span held) beside omitted_composites, and the item still EXPANDS -- named and counted, never silently dropped (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed). DependencyClaimRefused is RETAINED for a genuinely malformed row only -- a stage index that does not exist, or a parent the item does not declare -- refused by the carrier's well-formedness claim before any endpoint resolves (the pre-#16716 sense and the #16678 red control). The fix lives inside the ONE expander: expand_decomposition, stage_barrier_edges and waits_on_edges; it adds no second expander (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority). The expansion also gains a visible report of every top-level Composite it did NOT expand (the top-level piece's LeafPath and its nested day total read from the ONE count helper piece_leaf_days), so a schedule over an item with Composites SAYS it omits that work instead of undercounting quietly (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed).",
        displaced_cost: "A stage that emits no occurrence today ERASES the barrier across it: factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease has 8 audit leaves at stage 0, a Decision alone at stage 1 and 8 cut leaves at stage 2, and emits ZERO audit-to-cut edges, so the scheduler lets cut start before audit. A waits_on aimed at an empty endpoint is silently dropped today; 16 rows already name an empty endpoint.",
        first_slice: "Expand the REAL factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease and show every stage-2 cut occurrence now waits on the stage-0 audit occurrences it must, where before the fix it emitted none.",
        red_control: "On the REAL fixture, factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease emits an edge from every stage-0 audit occurrence to every stage-2 cut occurrence (8x8 = 64); reverting the barrier change makes that edge count ZERO. An added all-stages-empty item expands to zero occurrences and zero edges WITHOUT refusing, and an added waits_on naming an empty endpoint resolves to that endpoint's nearest non-empty predecessor. REFINEMENT controls (rule change 2026-11-19): an added waits_on naming a WELL-FORMED child endpoint that emits no occurrence EXPANDS and RECORDS an Into-side UnresolvedWait (side, stage, EndpointEmitsNoOccurrence kinds) rather than refusing; a malformed row (a stage the parent lacks) STILL refuses through DependencyClaimRefused; and the permanent guard roadmap_real_decomposition_expansion_guard_witness asserts EVERY real decomposition expands (no allow-list) while the three milestone / project-Join waits (v1-emitter-quarantine, native-production-admission, factory) are each reported in unresolved_waits -- reverting the rule to refuse-by-name blanks their schedules and turns the guard red.",
        out_of_scope: "No scheduler policy change; no cross-item ordering (list-scheduling stays per-item by design). A Composite's NESTED worker pieces are NOT expanded here: the expansion now REPORTS them (their top-level path and nested day total) so the omission is visible, but that work is still not scheduled -- addressing it is the LeafPath model change on roadmap-schedule-composite-nested-addressing, which this row defers. No new occurrence kind or path format.",
        handback: "The edge-count for the real fixture before and after the revert, the all-empty and empty-endpoint waits_on outputs, the refusal output, and the diff.",
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The whole schedule chain reads the expansion's edges; a barrier that silently vanishes across an empty stage makes the critical path, the bottleneck and the offer all wrong for any item with a Decision-only or Composite-only stage."),
    ),
    // DECLARED, NOT DISPATCHED: the frontier that gives the expander's unresolved_waits report a CONSUMER. Until it
    // lands, roadmap_schedule carries the report on the Expansion but no schedule answer reads it (the Consumption
    // authority: a declaration must be consumed now or by a NAMED later change). It waits on the barrier row, which is
    // what creates the report, and bottlenecks-and-offer waits on IT so the surfaced report has a downstream reader.
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_HED0W6FHP53P26Z4RVR45AGWSV",
      id: "roadmap-schedule-surfaces-unresolved-waits",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_schedule.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A schedule surfaces the unresolved waits its expansion reported",
        boundary: "The one expander records every waits_on whose endpoint span is WELL-FORMED (the stage index EXISTS and the parent edge is DECLARED, so the carrier's own well-formedness claim admits the row) but whose span emits NO occurrence -- a wait onto a milestone / project Join -- on the Expansion as unresolved_waits (side, stage, EndpointEmitsNoOccurrence kinds) beside omitted_composites (roadmap-schedule-barrier-through-empty-stages). This frontier gives that report a CONSUMER: the schedule answer carries unresolved_waits beside its placed leaves, so a reader SEES the cross-item ordering a lane cannot yet place. It orders nothing and mints no edge -- surfacing, not scheduling -- so no lane gains the ability to schedule cross-item ordering here (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority); it simply stops the report from being a dangling declaration the scheduler throws away (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed).",
        displaced_cost: "Without a named consumer the unresolved_waits field is a dangling declaration (Consumption: red). The report exists on the Expansion but no schedule answer reads it, so the cross-item-ordering gap it was added to make visible goes unseen again -- the very silence the barrier fix was made to end.",
        first_slice: "The schedule answer for one real item (factory) carries its unresolved_waits beside its placed leaves -- the three milestone / project-Join waits reported, none scheduled.",
        red_control: "An expansion with an unresolved wait yields a schedule answer that NAMES that wait; an expansion with none names none; and no edge or ordering is minted from an unresolved wait -- the placed-leaf set and every edge are identical to the schedule computed without the report. Reverting the surfacing blanks the named waits and turns this control red.",
        out_of_scope: "No lane schedules cross-item ordering; no edge or order is invented for an unresolved wait. Actually SCHEDULING such waits is a further frontier, not this one. Which waits are unresolved is decided in roadmap-schedule-barrier-through-empty-stages, not here.",
        handback: "The schedule answer for factory with its three unresolved waits listed beside the placed leaves, the empty-report item's answer naming none, and the diff showing no new edge or ordering was minted.",
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The frontier keeps the cross-item-ordering gap visible in the schedule answer until a lane can place it; bottlenecks-and-offer then reads it downstream."),
    ),
    // DECLARED, NOT DISPATCHED: the LeafPath model change that would let expansion reach a Composite's nested
    // stages. It must land as a model change to LeafPath BEFORE any nested expansion, so it is held (dispatch
    // defaults to NotDispatchable) until the path change is itself scheduled.
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_8BQKTF2C0H9M4RVDJZ5N7AE3Y1",
      id: "roadmap-schedule-composite-nested-addressing",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_model.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A LeafPath that reaches into a Composite's nested stages",
        boundary: "A MODEL CHANGE to LeafPath, not an expansion change. Today LeafPath { item, stage, piece, member } reaches exactly one top-level piece, and the carrier says a Composite is a container addressed deeper than the path reaches -- decomposition_has_leaf_path REFUSES a path into a Composite -- so a Composite's nested worker pieces carry days but are never occurrences. This row widens the path to address nested Composite stages and pieces, keyed with no invented side-format, so the ONE expander can then emit those nested occurrences; whatever path a claim names must be the SAME path the expansion mints (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority). It waits on roadmap-schedule-barrier-through-empty-stages, which makes the omission visible first.",
        displaced_cost: "15 items contain Composites that hide 47 nested worker occurrences and 5 findings families; a schedule over them undercounts the work and the offer never names it. Until the path reaches them, no expansion change can schedule that work honestly -- which is exactly why the barrier row only REPORTS them today.",
        first_slice: "Extend LeafPath with the nested coordinates and prove decomposition_has_leaf_path and piece_member_days answer CONSISTENTLY for one nested leaf, with every existing top-level path unchanged.",
        red_control: "A nested leaf a Composite declares is addressed by exactly ONE path that BOTH the claim guard and the expansion agree on; an out-of-range nested index refuses by name; every existing top-level LeafPath and every existing witness is unchanged; and every Claimed already recorded in an event log decodes to the SAME LeafPath (or Pathless) as before -- recorded history is bytes, and widening the path must not reinterpret it.",
        out_of_scope: "No scheduler policy change; no change to barrier semantics (that is roadmap-schedule-barrier-through-empty-stages); NO Composite nested expansion until this path exists.",
        handback: "The widened LeafPath, the claim/expansion agreement receipts, the refusal output, and the diff.",
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "Nested composite work is invisible to the schedule until the path can name it; this row carries the model change that makes that work schedulable without inventing a second path format."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8WTDD8SXN0SR7P26C1",
      id: "roadmap-spawn-frontier-leaf-grain",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_readiness.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The spawn frontier at leaf grain, with the item predicate still as the gate",
        boundary: "A leaf is ready when every leaf it depends on is ACCEPTED and its item is dispatchable by today's readiness (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_readiness). The item predicate STAYS the gate: nothing starts a leaf whose item may not start.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the frontier is item-grain, so only the first leaf of an item is visible to the belt and the leaves waiting on a stage-1 sibling stay invisible until the whole item moves.",
        first_slice: "Compute the leaf frontier for one item with two stages and print, per leaf, which dependency leaf is not yet accepted.",
        red_control: "A leaf whose stage-1 sibling is unaccepted is NOT ready even when its item is dispatchable; a leaf whose item is not dispatchable is not ready even when every dependency leaf is accepted.",
        out_of_scope: "No dispatch; the item readiness predicate itself does not change.",
        handback: "The frontier output for the two planted cases, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. Item dispatchability remains the gate. Leaf readiness must consume accepted dependency leaves from the existing expansion/log, not relax item admission. Source inspection here did not establish that live dispatch consumes this frontier, so retain implementation/integration work rather than report completion.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The frontier is where the graph becomes an action; at item grain it under-reads the work the decomposition already declares."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8XJ9DVYGSNMZKP8WKJ",
      id: "roadmap-dispatch-carries-leaf",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_belt_actuate.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "A dispatch names the leaf it dispatches, and one leaf has one dispatch",
        boundary: "The live dispatch row carries the leaf path beside its node_id, and one leaf has one dispatch: two dispatches on one leaf refuse; two leaves of one item are admitted, each in its own dispatch. This is what makes a leaf addressable. The belt takes its desired members from the offered leaf, bounded by BeltCapacity, with the readiness predicate still the gate on what may start at all. That the offer is the belt's selection basis is the INTERPRETATION recorded in gunbc.design_ruling::schedule_answers_are_computed_cached_and_re_read -- the operator's \"the planning we did now is relevant\" read onto this unit's done-when -- an interpretation, not operator words, and correctable by the operator.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the belt cannot put two workers on one item's leaves at all: the item is the only addressable thing, and every schedule above this row stays a picture.",
        first_slice: "Dispatch two leaves of one item in two dispatches, then a second dispatch on a leaf already dispatched, and show all three outputs.",
        red_control: "Two dispatches on one leaf refuse; two leaves of one item in two dispatches are admitted -- both in the same run.",
        out_of_scope: "No new dispatch machinery: the leaf path travels beside the node id it already carries. BeltCapacity's meaning does not change. Whether the offer is the belt's selection basis is not this row's call: it stands as the labelled INTERPRETATION in gunbc.design_ruling::schedule_answers_are_computed_cached_and_re_read, and the operator corrects it.",
        handback: "The three outputs, the capacity bound as observed, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The large belt actuation module still needs a demonstrated leaf-grain live dispatch path. Adding claim coordinates alone does not prove duplicate-leaf exclusion or capacity bounds. Reuse the existing actuation route and execute the three specified dispatch cases.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "This is where the simulated execution touches the fleet: the offered leaf becomes a dispatch, addressed to that leaf, under the readiness gate and the capacity bound."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8Y40BD0A4SBDMW0J60",
      id: "roadmap-typed-handback",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_log.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The handback is typed, and only an accepted handback moves the carrier",
        boundary: "The handback is typed: Close with its acceptance evidence; Split with a replacement decomposition, carried as an edit to the carrier on a branch; ReEstimate with its days; Findings with its members, for a probe leaf. It is accepted by the claim's return_to principal, and the carrier changes only through an accepted handback. A Split is accepted the way any work item is (gunbc.design_ruling::a_split_handback_is_accepted_by_the_manager, on gunbc.design_ruling::work_item_acceptance_is_the_managers_or_an_escalation), and no operator gate stands on a split that lengthens the critical path -- the view flags the moved path so the operator sees it rather than approves it.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the four things a handback can mean are one undifferentiated message, and any handback can rewrite a decomposition on the way past. The authority law says a carrier changes through an accepted change, and the handback is where that is enforced.",
        first_slice: "Accept a Close and a Findings on two planted leaves, and refuse a Findings on a leaf whose evidence is a Builds.",
        red_control: "A Findings handback from a leaf whose evidence is Builds refuses; a handback offered by a principal that is not the claim's return_to principal refuses; the carrier is unchanged after either refusal.",
        out_of_scope: "No operator gate on a Split that lengthens the critical path (gunbc.design_ruling::a_split_handback_is_accepted_by_the_manager): it is accepted as any work item is, and this row's view only has to flag the moved path. A Split stays an edit on a branch, never an in-place rewrite.",
        handback: "The accepted and refused handback outputs, the carrier unchanged on the refusals, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The event log already decodes HandbackEvidence and looks up the claim return_to. That alone does not establish Close/Split/ReEstimate/Findings carrier mutation only after authorized acceptance. Residual is checking the existing vocabulary against those variants and wiring the accepted mutations with refusal controls.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "A leaf that turns out to be four leaves, or ten days, or a finding, has to say so in a form the carrier can read."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR8ZNA89SDC0ZXCHA2DS",
      id: "roadmap-work-item-projection",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_event_log.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "One projection row per work item, served as JSON from the daily workspace",
        boundary: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_work_item_projection serves one row per work item as JSON from the daily workspace, at the path projection.json beside standings.json -- the path a consumer fetches to find the projection, declared here because a reader detects the projection by fetching it. The row's shape is declared here, because it is what a consumer of the projection is built against: node, intention, layer, item_state; leaves -- one entry per leaf occurrence, each with its leaf path as the decomposition spells it, its start day and finish day from the schedule answer, and on_critical_path; in_flight -- the derived set, each entry with its leaf path, its claim's assignee and its claim's return_to; latest_event; acceptance_evidence; events -- the item's past events with the timestamp each one was recorded at (claimed, released, acceptance recorded, retired), read from the event log at the read and kept in no store of this row's own, so a consumer can draw the progress already made and not only the plan ahead; and read_on, the date the document was read, together with the inputs that read used (worker_count, the day priors, the assumed findings counts), each shown as an input and not as a fact. It IS planning_consolidation section 1's projection; every consumer reads this row and keeps no state of its own, and a field this row does not serve is not part of the projection.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it each reader folds the log itself, and the readers are where the drift lives; there is no one place to read what is true about an item on the day of the read.",
        first_slice: "Serve the projection for one item with leaves in flight, then the same item after a planted release, and show both rows against the shape above, field for field.",
        red_control: "A row's in-flight leaves are the derived set and never a stored list, and a served row that omits a declared field of the shape above -- a leaf without its on_critical_path, an in-flight entry without its claim's assignee or return_to, an event without the timestamp it was recorded at, a row without read_on and its inputs -- is not the projection; the events a row carries are the event log's own rows at that read, never a copy this row keeps; a planted binding of this row to an intention that does not exist refuses at load, by the binding carrier's own check.",
        out_of_scope: "No rendering; no operator to-do list on the row -- section 1's projection states, it does not nag. No reader outside this repository is named or bound here.",
        handback: "The two JSON rows, the planted-binding refusal output, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. roadmap_item_gantt supplies computed per-item rows, but the requested projection.json contract also needs log-derived in-flight leaves and binding refusals. Reuse both producers; the served projection and release control are the actual integration work, not another timeline calculation.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The plan is the one mind and the projection is what it shows; every reader reads this and nothing else."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR90N2HGC2XA1WMQFRFK",
      id: "roadmap-timeline-page",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_page.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The timeline, rendered from the projection alone",
        boundary: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_page carries the timeline: one row per item ordered by first start, leaves stacked where they run parallel, the in-flight strip, a read-day line at today, in-flight rows highlighted, bottlenecks in red, and the offer at the top. It renders the roadmap-work-item-projection row and nothing else -- no reader state, no second fold of the log.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the schedule is a dump nobody supervises a week of work with; a projection with no renderer is a file.",
        first_slice: "Render the timeline for one read with two items, one of them in flight, and show the page apart from the JSON it came from.",
        red_control: "Every mark on a row is explained by its projection row: the page reads the projection and nothing else, and a planted value that exists only in the page refuses.",
        out_of_scope: "No schedule, in-flight set or offer is derived here; no consumer outside this repository is bound here.",
        handback: "The rendered page for the fixture read, the planted-value refusal output, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. roadmap_page has ordinary authority-projection rendering, but this review found no timeline/Gantt consumer in it. Implement the timeline from the served projection after that contract exists; keep date/placement decisions in the existing producers rather than the page.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The plan has to be visible to be ruled on; the timeline is where the simulated execution is read."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7NPVR91VNF088PHY2G7X5PK",
      id: "roadmap-return-to-principal-records-acceptance",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_operator_acceptance.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The claim's return_to principal may record the acceptance of that claim's own node",
        boundary: "Acceptances keep being recorded under the operator's principal for now, and the later route gets its own row: the principal a claim carries in its return_to may author AcceptanceRecorded FOR THAT CLAIM'S NODE, under the same receipt law gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_operator_acceptance states. It is gated on the acceptance-guidance carrier planning_consolidation section 7 layer 4 names. This row is the return_to arm of rn_A0SYP0J1P3JE8W8OBX6M3BD777 (roadmap-operator-attested-acceptance) -- one receipt law, two admissible authors -- and it waits on that row.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it every acceptance runs through one principal, so the principal a claim is returned to cannot attest to the work it accepted, and the operator stays in the path of every handback.",
        first_slice: "Let a claim's return_to principal author AcceptanceRecorded for that claim's node under the same receipt, and show the accepted append.",
        red_control: "An AcceptanceRecorded authored by a principal that is neither the operator nor the claim's return_to principal refuses AT APPEND, and the log is unchanged after the refusal.",
        out_of_scope: "The operator's own attestation path does not change; no new claim type appears; acceptances recorded under the operator's principal stay the route until the guidance carrier says otherwise.",
        handback: "The accepted append, the refused append output with the log unchanged, and the diff."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Source review at 398136026b345e087968a9db4ba42ec551c5ca4c (2026-11-19); source presence is not acceptance. The event log can retrieve a claim return_to; the operator acceptance route is a separate authority boundary. Residual is admitting that principal for that claim/node under the existing receipt law, with a wrong-author append refusal. Reading a return_to field is not authorization evidence.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The handback a leaf returns to has to be able to close the leaf; today only one principal can record that it did."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_01M7T844EWSVQJ6A7XMXC6VZ85",
      id: "roadmap-authoring-refuses-prerequisite-into-own-container",
      owner: "planning",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_authority.dag"), carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_estimate_derivation.dag")),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Roadmap authority: authoring refuses a prerequisite edge into the source's own container",
        boundary: "One property of the EXISTING authority graph (dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_authority.dag's edge() / declared_roadmap_edges), not a second walker: it reuses the containment the authority already derives -- MemberOf/UnderParent membership AND the decomposition pieces a container holds (the same pieces the rollup restates in roadmap_estimate_derivation.dag) -- and refuses a prerequisite edge whose TARGET is a containment ancestor of its SOURCE, naming BOTH the edge and the container. The item Gantt read already surfaces this as BlockedCause WaitsOnItsOwnContainer (tidy-crane-257, #16729); this lifts it onto the authority's own edge graph as a validator property refused by name. ENFORCEMENT ROUTE: the check is a property of the authority graph validator, executed on the claim/validator route today (witnesses over the declared graph); the required-path `roadmap_authority_projection` gate that refuses the live graph is a named follow-up, blocked only until the single containment walk this law reuses is lifted into a module the projection can import without a cycle (the walk now lives in roadmap_estimate_derivation.dag, which nothing imports) -- a one-line call once liftable.",
        displaced_cost: "Today a row waiting on its own milestone/project/decomposition container is admitted by the authority, so the contradiction is caught only at the Gantt read: an author sees a graph that validates and then a blocked cell that cannot be scheduled, and no name is put on the edge until the view runs. A parent waiting on its own child is the REDUNDANT case, not the contradictory one -- the child already gates the container, so the edge is harmless; it is FLAGged for the planner and NOT refused. The refuse-vs-flag line and the single containment walk (extended with decomposition pieces, keep_all style) live with the edge graph; the Gantt read stays the display.",
        first_slice: "A model-side claim over the declared edge graph + the derived containment: a planted prerequisite edge whose target is its source's MemberOf parent is REFUSED naming the edge and the container; a planted edge into a container that holds the source only as a decomposition piece is REFUSED identically (same claim, no second walk); a legal cross-item edge still passes; a planted parent-waits-on-own-child edge is reported as redundant and NOT refused. RED-FIRST against live data: run the claim on current main and list every existing violating edge; if any exist, STOP and send the list -- fixing data is a planning decision.",
        red_control: "A fixture where a leaf declares a prerequisite on its own project/milestone ancestor refuses and names both sides; a fixture where the leaf's only link to the container is decomposition-piece membership refuses identically (the walk counts pieces, proving MemberOf-only is NOT the whole containment); a legal cross-item edge passes; a planted container->contained-child edge is flagged redundant, not refused; and the live authority passes once data is clean.",
        out_of_scope: "Fixing any live violating edge (a planning data decision, not this row); refusing a container that waits on its own contained child (redundant, not contradictory -- flag only); rewriting the item Gantt read or its BlockedCause enum; a second containment walker beside the authority's own.",
        handback: "The named-refusal report: each violating edge as (source -> target) plus the container named, and the single containment function reused (the authority's own, now covering decomposition pieces); plus the RED-FIRST live-data verdict listing every existing violating edge."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The estimates the planning page prices with: an edge graph whose prerequisites cannot contradict the containment the same authority derives, so authoring refuses what only the Gantt read used to catch."),
    ),
    // ---- gunbc.plans.derived_types_keep_their_name (sharp-stag-549, 2026-11-19) ------------
    // The how the intention holds out of itself. Three selections against it; the binding in
    // roadmap_intention_binding links each to the intention. Carriers point at the plan module.
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_47NBQ2XDRDLSB56VT99NDAOO4D",
      id: "derived-type-argument-inhabitance-root",
      owner: "nominal-typing",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/derived_types_keep_their_name.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "One root inhabitance rule preserves the declared type relationship",
        boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.derived_types_keep_their_name under gunbc.design_argument::declared_intent and gunbc.design_ruling::type_relationships_are_declared_and_transparent_reference_is_explicit_2026_11_23. ONE v2 inhabitance judgment with resolved declarations preserves an explicitly transparent reference, a constraint and a nominal distinction according to their declared relationship and conversion direction; a common representation cannot choose among them. A reference to Compose retains its full constrained type under machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier. Generic versus nongeneric syntax grants no exemption. The existing equals form's observed behavior does not settle transparent-reference syntax. Any seed mirror remains subject to gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing, not seed feature completion.",
        displaced_cost: "The recorded v1 probe admitted String variables at NonEmptyStr, PathSegment, MyStr = String and nominal_opaque parameters. Constraint or nominal erasure can defeat the declared contract, while deliberately transparent same-identity acceptance is legitimate. Treating all four observations as defects would replace one silent reinterpretation with another; the real v2 result is still owed.",
        first_slice: "Obtain the real-path v2 verdict for an already settled constraint or nominal contract over the actual standard-library declarations, and repair the shared judgment where that evidence identifies erasure. Independently, settle and record the transparent-reference surface on a small comparison with existing reference features, ordinary value binding, constrained construction and nominal introduction; only reference-specific semantic changes or migration wait for that choice. The operator's a = b copy intuition is a reader expectation, not a physical-copy rule; type A = B is not selected by habit. Preserve each observed result separately from the selected semantics.",
        red_control: "Controls for settled contracts can execute now: base-at-base and correctly constructed values remain accepted, a base value lacking required construction or evidence refuses at a constrained or nominal position, and the full width composition is not erased into its base. Once the reference surface is recorded, add the explicit transparent-reference positive controls for both a nongeneric type and a generic expression; all controls are required for full acceptance. The earlier MyStr = String acceptance is not itself a RED. Preserve the unrelated Int-at-record, String-at-record and Int-at-String refusals. Run the real in-scope v2 acceptance path, not only two-declaration stand-ins, and distinguish the two crossing directions under the declared conversion authority.",
        out_of_scope: "Choosing transparent-reference syntax from current parser behavior; a blanket alias ban or blanket refusal of MyStr = String; generic-form exemptions; checked-constructor implementations owned by the successor nodes; a new link taxonomy; reimplementing the width intersection's owning model; seed changes outside the purpose test.",
        handback: "The recorded surface decision, bounded affected relationships, and exact-path v2 receipts for the positive and negative controls, identifying the shared inhabitance judgment and any remaining declared gap. Update the recurring failure mode's owed v2 claim only to the scope actually executed; report any justified v1 mirror separately."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "The shared argument judgment preserves the authored relationship: transparent identity remains usable and constraints or nominal distinctions do not disappear."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_KUYADI8UNNQF12O7TCOWBFG3L0",
      id: "nonempty-str-becomes-a-checked-nominal",
      owner: "nominal-typing",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/std/types.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "NonEmptyStr reached only through a checked constructor, never a where-predicate",
        boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.derived_types_keep_their_name. NonEmptyStr keeps its nonempty contract through checked construction returning Optional, or carried evidence admitted by gunbc.design_ruling::nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved; remove the where declaration under where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors. Any expected-type literal introduction establishes that same contract rather than an unchecked transparent conversion. Retire literal_only_refinement_judgment_is_interim only when its replacement capability holds. This settled constraint is independent of the pending transparent-reference spelling; reference-specific migration waits for that choice. Boundary v2 frontier + std; seed mirrors only under the v1_seed_standing purpose test.",
        displaced_cost: "The recorded v1 probe admitted an unproved String variable at NonEmptyStr, so its predicate was not established on that observed path. The real v2 verdict remains owed until the prerequisite executes it; a new constructor name alone would not repair the consumer boundary.",
        first_slice: "Take one real NonEmptyStr consumer and its literal and variable introductions; establish their actual v2 behavior, then migrate that bounded slice under the already ruled checked-construction or admitted-evidence contract. This independent work need not await transparent-reference spelling, but reference-specific migration does. Use source inspection to bound the next migration slice and report unknowns; no global count is a prerequisite for this first repair. Full acceptance still requires the shared-root controls and the existing dependency graph.",
        red_control: "A String-typed VARIABLE without evidence at a NonEmptyStr parameter refuses; the checked constructor returns Present for x and Absent for empty text; the unproved as crossing refuses. An admitted nonempty literal and a correctly constructed value remain accepted, while an empty literal cannot be introduced as NonEmptyStr. Explicit transparent references to the SAME full NonEmptyStr type remain accepted and do not turn it into String. The prerequisite's relationship controls remain green on the real v2 path.",
        out_of_scope: "Other branded contracts and their constructors; choosing or banning alias syntax; inventing a new literal policy; erasing the nonempty obligation because a reference is transparent; seed changes outside the purpose test.",
        handback: "The checked constructor's executing Present/Absent controls, real v2 argument and literal results, the bounded migrated consumer slice and remaining migration obligation, plus evidence that the relationship controls still hold. The interim scaffold is retired only with its named capability established."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "The hottest derived type reached only by a checked constructor, so its non-emptiness is constructed, not assumed."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_ZD5REPL430O15K4AVE4I82JSD7",
      id: "brands-reached-by-checked-constructors",
      owner: "nominal-typing",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/std/types.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Branded contracts survive checked construction and retirement of where",
        boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.derived_types_keep_their_name and gunbc.design_ruling::type_relationships_are_declared_and_transparent_reference_is_explicit_2026_11_23. For each migrated brand, state its actual constraint or nominal contract, introduce the checked constructor required by where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors and retire its where form without erasing that contract. PathSegment, CommitSha and FilePath consume their existing authorities; their names do not authorize inventing new validation. Integer widths remain the constrained intersections governed by machine_width_composition_has_an_intersection_carrier, never generic aliases exempted from enforcement. Boundary v2 frontier + std; seed mirrors only under v1_seed_standing.",
        displaced_cost: "The recorded v1 PathSegment probe shows an unproved String admitted at a branded boundary; the real v2 behavior and other brands require their own scoped receipts. Treating all brands as aliases or all aliases as brands loses the distinction the operator wants preserved.",
        first_slice: "Take PathSegment and one actual consumer, state the contract its current authority owns, and run construction and unproved-base controls through real v2, including an invalid-value case only where that contract excludes values. Introduce the constructor required by that contract and the where-retirement ruling, then migrate the bounded consumer slice. Expand to the known sibling brands only against their own contracts, rather than a guessed rule derived from their spelling.",
        red_control: "At each migrated brand, an unproved base value refuses where the declared contract requires construction; construction accepts valid inputs and refuses invalid ones where the contract excludes values. A nominal-only distinction requires explicit introduction, not an invented validity predicate. Correctly constructed values and explicit transparent references to the same branded type remain accepted. A width reference retains the full intersection and cannot authorize an out-of-range or unproved base crossing. The shared relationship controls from derived-type-argument-inhabitance-root remain green on the actual in-scope v2 path.",
        out_of_scope: "NonEmptyStr's own constructor; a blanket alias retirement or generic exemption; a new taxonomy of links; inventing contract constraints from a brand's name; independently redefining the width intersection; seed changes outside the purpose test.",
        handback: "Each migrated brand's named contract, checked-construction and argument receipts, bounded consumer migration and remaining trigger, with the shared relationship controls preserved. Report v2 and any justified seed evidence separately; source observations are not execution guarantees."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "Every branded carrier name is reached by a checked constructor, so the brand means something the checker enforces."),
    ),
    // ---- gunbc.plans.gunb_ai_served_from_gunbc (merry-eagle-717, 2026-11-24) ---------------
    // The site's source and deploy move into gunbc and gunb-ai/frontend is archived, then the content is
    // refreshed. The cutover is one node because the authority transition is one motion
    // (gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration); the refresh waits on it so it is written once, in gunbc.
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_F8YSNN55TQSIEP8DDD5X8O218I",
      id: "gunb-ai-served-from-gunbc",
      owner: "site",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/gunb_ai_served_from_gunbc.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
        headline: "gunb.ai is served from gunbc, and gunb-ai/frontend is archived",
        boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.gunb_ai_served_from_gunbc under gunbc.design_ruling::gunb_ai_deploys_from_gunbc_2026_11_24. Owns where gunb.ai's served bytes come from and how they are deployed, and the content refresh that follows. It does not own the DNS zone (gunbc.cloudflare.zone; no record changes), the brand mark's geometry (gunbc.design.brand_mark), or the lab and daily workspace, which are served elsewhere.",
        approach: "Members in dependency order: the cutover (gunb-ai-deploy-cutover), then the refresh (gunb-ai-content-refresh), which edits only gunbc's typed site modules.",
        red_control: "Met only through its members: the intention's done-when holds (gunb.ai serves gunbc's render at a named main commit, the frontend repository is archived with no gunbc file naming it as a source, and the operator judges the content current).",
        displaced_cost: "Two repositories answer what gunb.ai says: the frontend repository hand-maintains the served files and gunbc keeps a transcribed model plus committed copies to compare against, so every site change is written twice.",
        handback: "gunb.ai deployed from gunbc on merge, the frontend repository archived, and refreshed content."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "gunbc-project-root", contribution: "The public site states what the project is; one source for it means a change to what the project says is one reviewed change here."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_S4YN3WB8XG94FDD2RPELEDGR5G",
      id: "gunb-ai-deploy-cutover",
      owner: "site",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/site/gunb_ai_page.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "One cut: an emitted gunbc workflow deploys gunb.ai from the site modules' render, and gunb-ai/frontend stops being a source",
        boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.gunb_ai_served_from_gunbc under gunbc.design_ruling::gunb_ai_deploys_from_gunbc_2026_11_24. A new workflow emitted from a .dag model (beside the existing emitted workflows, enrolled in the drift watch's artifact roster) that, on main only, renders the site and publishes it through the GitHub Pages actions. THE PUBLIC PATH LIST IS EXPLICIT and is the four files the page links: index.html (gunbc.site.gunb_ai_page), assets/site.css (gunbc.site.gunb_ai_css), assets/cards.js (gunbc.site.gunb_ai_deck) and assets/mark.svg (gunbc.site.gunb_ai_mark). The frontend's publish step (gunb-ai/frontend .github/workflows/pages.yml at 3152d4c) also stages five PNG icons under assets/ and CNAME; neither is carried. The PNGs are linked from no served file, and the operator chose to drop them (gunbc.design_ruling::gunb_ai_deploys_from_gunbc_2026_11_24), so gunbc.design.brand_mark_assets is not built by the deploy; nothing off the path list enters the Pages artifact. The custom domain is a setting of the destination repository's Pages site, not a staged CNAME file: GitHub ignores a CNAME file in a custom-workflow deployment. In the same change: delete the parity comparisons against dag/test/fixture/gunb_ai/live_* and those fixtures, keeping each discriminating claim that does not depend on the copy; delete every comment that names gunb-ai/frontend as where a value is re-derived from. DNS records are not edited.",
        displaced_cost: "Each site change is edited in gunb-ai/frontend and re-transcribed into gunbc's model and fixtures; the two can disagree and only a parity witness, run by hand, notices.",
        first_slice: "Confirm the render against the served files at gunb-ai/frontend 3152d4c (its head since 2026-06-16). site.css and cards.js are compared byte-exact. index.html and mark.svg are compared under the differences their writers already enumerate (gunbc.site.gunb_ai_page parity_nullities, seven rows; gunbc.site.gunb_ai_mark mark_parity_nullities, the self-close spelling), and any difference those rows do not name fails. Then the workflow's model and emission, with its time and memory budgets stated in the pull request for the operator under gunbc.design_ruling::ci_job_budgets_closed_to_growth.",
        red_control: "Before the domain moves: a planted guard refusal in the page render (an href the URL guard refuses) makes the workflow fail having uploaded nothing, and the unplanted render, from a named main commit, deploys to gunbc's project Pages URL, where every path on the list is fetched and equals that commit's artifact byte for byte. Only then, with the operator asked immediately before: remove the custom domain from gunb-ai/frontend, set it on gunbc's Pages site, and read back that gunbc's Pages site holds the domain, that the served deployment is the named commit, that HTTPS is enforced, and that every public path at gunb.ai and www.gunb.ai equals the artifact byte for byte. Matching bytes alone do not show which repository served them, so the Pages binding readback is required. Until all of that holds, the frontend's last successful deployment stays restorable (its workflow is not disabled and the repository is not archived). Then, before archiving: close gunb-ai/frontend#2 (an earlier operator-selected pitch around multi-target emission, still open) with a note recording that gunbc.plans.gunb_ai_served_from_gunbc and gunb-ai-content-refresh supersede it, and record that comment's permalink, because an archived repository's pull requests are read-only. Disabling the frontend's deploy and archiving the repository are the last steps.",
        out_of_scope: "Any content change (gunb-ai-content-refresh); DNS record edits (the apex and www behavior is verified, not changed; gunbc.cloudflare.zone records the GitHub Pages addresses only from the historical Namecheap transcription, and its origin readback is pending); a pull-request or merge-group trigger; carrying workpad.html, legacy/, docs/, scripts/, PROPOSAL.md or DESIGN.md across; modeling the deck's retained JavaScript further.",
        handback: "The emitted workflow and its run URLs (project-URL deploy and custom-domain deploy), the deployed commit, the per-path byte comparisons at the project URL and at gunb.ai and www.gunb.ai, the Pages binding readback, the deleted fixtures and parity comparisons with the claims kept, the permalink of the supersession note closing gunb-ai/frontend#2, and the archived frontend repository."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "gunb-ai-served-from-gunbc", contribution: "The authority transition itself: after it, gunbc is the only place gunb.ai's bytes come from."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_LZGDD7HEJWFT7KDW6EWM56YLSS",
      id: "gunb-ai-content-refresh",
      owner: "site",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/site/gunb_ai_content.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "gunb.ai's pitch redone from first principles: architecture determines which mistakes a program can make and which work it has to do",
        boundary: "Serves gunbc.plans.gunb_ai_served_from_gunbc. Operator, 2026-11-24: the theming may be fine but the terms and pitch are outdated, to be reconsidered from first principles; the highlight is the separation of business intent from the implementation, which the current page does not make clear. Direction given by the operator: the page is about how a program's architecture determines which mistakes it can make and which work it has to do. First principles is the method, separation of concerns is what the programmer does, and safety and performance are the consequences the page demonstrates. The reader is engineers who design and maintain systems. The three-card deck is replaced by one worked example a reader can inspect, and the first action is 'Trace the build decision'. The first draft's example is the development-build reuse decision: gunbc.devboot.subject::BuildSubject separates the source tree, the requested product, the target and the build settings; gunbc.devboot.outcome::record_matches_request and gunbc.devboot.outcome::reuse_decision_from_match decide reuse; gunbc.devboot.produce::live_reuse_report calls that decision on the production path; and test.claim.devboot_subject_identity_witness covers a matching request, another subject with bytes available, and a matching record without bytes. Each claim on the page names the declaration or receipt that evidences it, and the page claims no more than those establish (on a valid hit the service avoids a build; a request for another target cannot receive that executable). Changed only through gunbc.site.gunb_ai_content, gunbc.site.gunb_ai_page and gunbc.site.gunb_ai_deck (which may be replaced or removed); the theme (gunbc.site.gunb_ai_tokens, gunbc.site.gunb_ai_layout, gunbc.site.gunb_ai_css, gunbc.design.gunb_ai_hues, gunbc.design.gunb_ai_live_scale) is kept unless the new structure needs a change. The earlier pitch in gunb-ai/frontend#2 is superseded by this direction; the cutover closes that pull request with a supersession note before archiving, and this item links that note's permalink from its handback. Operator, 2026-11-24, on a text draft: too much copy; the page leads with clear pictures and diagrams, with words reduced to a headline, one sentence and labels, because the concept is simple enough to show.",
        displaced_cost: "The site pitches codegen from one description ('describe the system once, let the compiler derive the rest'), which is no longer what the project argues; readers meet a project that does not match it, and the separation of intent from implementation, which the operator names as the highlight, is not visible.",
        first_slice: "Agree a diagram-first mockup with the operator, starting from the review draft for operator approval (headline 'Make the rules of your architecture executable.', the 'Can we safely skip this build?' example), with each claim tied to its declaration; on the operator's approval, rewrite the content model and page, replace the deck with the diagrams as static markup, and render; the operator reviews the rendered page before merge.",
        red_control: "The render served at gunb.ai after merge equals the merged commit's render; each claim on the page names a declaration or receipt that resolves at that commit, and a planted claim citing a declaration that does not exist fails the content witness; the operator's review of the rendered page is the acceptance of whether it is current.",
        out_of_scope: "The deploy route itself; DNS; new served pages beyond what the operator asks for; the Google-operation example, which stays in DESIGN.md.",
        handback: "The merged content changes, the deployed commit, the operator's review of the rendered page, and the permalink of the cutover's supersession note on gunb-ai/frontend#2."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "gunb-ai-served-from-gunbc", contribution: "The reason for the move: the site is out of date, and after the cut it is updated in one place."),
    ),
    // ── The boot and management edge program (2026-11-20) ────────────────────────────────────────
    // Bring srv4 up as the site's boot and management edge, then retire mtcollins1's boot duties.
    // Nothing in the authority covered it: no boot row, no PXE-install row, no mtcollins1
    // boot-retirement row -- the only earlier records of this program were the now-closed gunbc#15350
    // and gunbc#15287. The intention each row serves is the plan carrier
    // gunbc.plans.new_server_bringup, registered at gunbc.plan_registry the day these rows landed.
    // Every PR state below is a live read through
    // gh pr view <n> --json number,state,isDraft,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,updatedAt,mergedAt,headRefName,title
    // on 2026-11-20, not a restatement of any brief or plan line; where a handed-down state and the
    // live read disagreed the row records the live read and names the correction in its own updates
    // thread.
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7BQM3KZT4VW1XN8RJC5YD6AP2S",
      id: "site-boot-and-management-edge",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/new_server_bringup.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
        headline: "srv4 carries the site's boot and management edge, and mtcollins1's boot duties retire",
        boundary: "The program, not the keystrokes. It owns the repository's claims about how a bare host becomes a serving member of this site: srv4 (the SitePxeEdge at gunbc.network_boot_delivery) serving DHCP/PXE/TFTP for installs, the machine-intake arrival chain admitting the host, the one-shot network install dispatching, and the management duties mtcollins1 still carries (boot, arrival, BMC reach, runner legs) moving onto modeled rows that converge. Physical actions -- power, cabling, console, Apply, GO -- are the operator's and stay out.",
        approach: "Four lanes, each a row under this one, sequenced by the plan carrier: (a) the PXE edge carries installs and bobo (srv15) is the first host installed; (b) butch (srv14) reaches the executor route under the standing CI-substrate ruling; (c) srv4's edge artifacts move from hand-placed staging into modeled rows with an operator Apply; (d) mtcollins1's boot legs -- arrival budgets, dispatch/collect/deregister, qualification, disk rows, the handless repeat -- land so its boot duties can be retired. Operator-held decisions are their own decision-gate rows, so a blocked lane names the person who unblocks it instead of pretending to be agent work.",
        red_control: "Met only through its members: every lane row is either accepted or refused with a reason, and the fleet's own reading of the boot and management edge carries no unmodeled dependency -- srv4 declared as the edge, no host depending on a hand-tended mtcollins1 boot duty that no row models.",
        displaced_cost: "A second hand-tended boot path that nothing converges and nothing witnesses. Today a new host's path runs through notes and an operator's hands, so a wrong MAC, a stale prior life or a hand-placed TFTP artifact surfaces as a failed install on the floor rather than as a RED witness, and nobody can say from the repository whether mtcollins1's boot duties are still load-bearing.",
        handback: "A boot and management edge the fleet's own reading accounts for: srv4 declared and converging as the edge, bobo installed through the modeled chain, mtcollins1's boot duties retired with their last consumer moved, and each lane's live state readable from its row rather than from a chat."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-application-authority", contribution: "The site's boot and management edge as fleet-owned claims: what the repository asserts about how a host boots, arrives and is managed here, held to the same convergence and reading as every other fleet authority."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_2HWDKX9TQ5LZ8C3VJMR6YE17PN",
      id: "bobo-arrival-door-refusal-carrier",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/machine_intake/mtcollins1_boot_run.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The arrival door's epoch reading returns its refusal as a value (gunbc#16736)",
        displaced_cost: "A refusal the arrival door drops instead of returning is a refusal nobody sees: the door reads as having decided when it never did, and the install path behind it is graded on a reading that quietly failed.",
        boundary: "The carrier-at-scalar class, site 1 of the 2 remaining: the arrival door's epoch reading returns its refusal as a value rather than swallowing it. One reading, one return path; no change to what the door decides.",
        first_slice: "Nothing left to cut: gunbc#16736 merged 2026-11-20T01:59:39Z, with the epoch reading returning its refusal as a value and its witnesses run on the post-wall binary before the operator landed it. The row stays as the record of what the install lane stands on, and the second site of the carrier-at-scalar class stays out of it.",
        red_control: "A door reading that fails while returning nothing refuses once the refusal is a value the caller must match; the swallowing form is the control's RED case.",
        out_of_scope: "The second remaining site of the same class; the live srv15 arrival run; the install dispatch; the host's runner join, which is another session's; any change to what the door admits.",
        handback: "An arrival door whose every reading, including its refusals, reaches the caller -- so the install path behind it is graded on readings that cannot go missing."
      ), on: "2026-11-20", note: "Head of the install lane, and its first prerequisite. Live read 2026-11-20, re-read after main moved: gunbc#16736 MERGED 2026-11-20T01:59:39Z (earlier read the same morning: OPEN, not draft, mergeable MERGEABLE, merge state CLEAN, updated 2026-11-20T01:41:43Z), branch dev/carrier-at-scalar-remaining-two, title 'fix(dag): the arrival door's epoch reading returns its refusal as a value (#16717 class, site 1 of 2)'. Correction to the hand-down: the brief labeled it 'wall-site carrier fixes'; what it changes is the arrival door's epoch reading on bobo's arrival path, and it is site 1 of 2 of the carrier-at-scalar class -- the second site is still owed and is not in this PR.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "site-boot-and-management-edge", contribution: "The install path's first reading is made un-skippable: a door that refuses says so to its caller."),
      centering: plan(text: "new_server_bringup_plan: the install path can only be graded on readings that reach their caller, so the arrival door's epoch reading must return its refusal as a value before any host is dispatched at it. Target: the arrival door behind dag/gunbc/machine_intake/mtcollins1_boot_run.dag."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_9FTR4ZKC6XQ2N8MVHJD7YB3S5W",
      id: "bobo-arrival-converge-budget-fold",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/fleet/site_pxe_edge_converge.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The arrival-converge step is budgeted as a fold over the door's declared legs (gunbc#16691)",
        displaced_cost: "The arrival-converge step runs on a budget no fold over the door's own declared legs produced, so its minutes are a guess: an arrival either dies on a step budget nobody admitted, or it runs long and nothing said it would.",
        boundary: "One PR, one shape: the arrival-converge step's budget derived as a fold over the legs the door itself declares, so the budget follows the model instead of a hand. Data plus one fold; no new budget mechanism.",
        first_slice: "Nothing left to cut: gunbc#16691 merged 2026-11-20T03:59:52Z, so the arrival-converge step's budget is the fold over the door's declared legs and its witnesses ran before the operator landed it. The row stays as the record, and as the prerequisite the mtcollins1 grants row names by id.",
        red_control: "An arrival-converge step whose budget does not equal the fold over its declared legs refuses by name; a planted leg that raises the fold refuses the stale budget.",
        out_of_scope: "Granting any budget outside ci_budget_raise's admission (the mtcollins1 grants row owns that); the live arrival run; the install dispatch; anything that has to run on the floor.",
        handback: "An arrival-converge budget derived from the door's declared legs, so the arrival cannot fail on minutes nobody admitted."
      ), on: "2026-11-20", note: "Live read 2026-11-20, re-read after main moved: gunbc#16691 MERGED 2026-11-20T03:59:52Z (earlier read the same morning: OPEN, not draft, mergeable CONFLICTING, merge state DIRTY, updated 2026-11-19T08:59:18Z -- the rebase it needed came with the merge), branch dev/arrival-converge-budget, title 'fleet-converge: budget the arrival-converge step as a fold over the door's declared legs'. Correction to the hand-down: the brief labeled this 'live prior-life archive'; the live PR is the arrival-converge budget fold, and no prior-life archive PR is open -- the prior-life question, if it is real, opens as its own row against today's code rather than as a label on this one. The arrival-door row is its prerequisite: budgeting a fold over legs whose door can swallow a refusal budgets a reading that may never have happened.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "site-boot-and-management-edge", contribution: "The arriving host's minutes derived from the model's own declared legs, not from a hand."),
      centering: plan(text: "new_server_bringup_plan: bobo (srv15) is the first host installed through the PXE edge, and its arrival-converge step is budgeted from the legs the door declares. Target: dag/gunbc/fleet/site_pxe_edge_converge.dag and the arrival-converge step it feeds."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_5NXJ8QV2TW7Z4RCMKYD6HB3F1P",
      id: "srv15-arrival-environment-approval",
      owner: "operator",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/auth/srv15_arrival_federation_provision.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "DECISION GATE: the operator approves the srv15-arrival environment",
        displaced_cost: "Everything after it in the lane queues: the CI arrival leg, the live hpm check and the install dispatch all need credentials from an environment only the operator can create.",
        boundary: "The operator creates and approves the srv15-arrival environment that gunbc.auth.srv15_arrival_federation_provision is modeled ReadyPendingOperatorCreate for. The repository's job ends at stating the shape; the creation and the approval are not agent work.",
        first_slice: "The operator creates the srv15-arrival environment per the modeled provision; the witness that reads the provision's ReadyPendingOperatorCreate arm flips once the environment is real.",
        red_control: "A run that asks the modeled provision to act while the environment is still Pending refuses on that arm, so no lane step can pretend the environment exists.",
        out_of_scope: "Any agent-side action: creating the environment, holding its credentials, or approving it on the operator's behalf.",
        handback: "An approved srv15-arrival environment whose credentials the CI arrival leg can be issued against."
      ), on: "2026-11-20", note: "Recorded as its own row because it is the lane's only hard operator-held dependency before the host can be installed: the model is ReadyPendingOperatorCreate, and no row in this repository can close it. The module's name is itself the obligation it carries -- the row waits on a person, not on a review.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "site-boot-and-management-edge", contribution: "The operator-held half of the install path, named as a gate so the queue reads it as waiting on a person, not as stalled work."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_3KZP7YD2VQ9X48HNRCMT6B5FJW",
      id: "bobo-install-credential-and-ci-arrival-leg",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/host/network_install.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The network install's BMC credential comes through the one authority (gunbc#16715), then this lane's CI arrival leg",
        displaced_cost: "An install whose BMC credential arrives by any route other than the one authority is an install whose credential nobody can account for -- and without a CI arrival leg the host's arrival is never exercised, so the install dispatch would be dispatched by a hand rather than by the workflow meant to own it.",
        boundary: "Two things in order, and the first is done. gunbc#16715 landed 2026-11-20T08:36:47Z, producing the network install's BMC credential through the one authority and making the capability refusal name its observation. What this row still owes is this lane's own arrival leg against the approved srv15-arrival environment, so the arrival runs from CI with issued credentials.",
        first_slice: "Add the arrival leg as data over the existing arrival workflow -- the credential half arrived with gunbc#16715, so the slice is the leg itself plus one run against the approved environment's credentials.",
        red_control: "An install credential produced off the one authority refuses by name, and a capability refusal that names no observation refuses; the same leg passes with the credential through the authority and the environment's credentials bound.",
        out_of_scope: "Creating the environment (its gate row); the live hpm check; the install dispatch itself; the host's runner join, which belongs to another session's rows.",
        handback: "An install credential that comes through the one authority, and a CI-driven arrival for bobo with issued credentials."
      ), on: "2026-11-20", note: "Live read 2026-11-20, re-read after it moved: gunbc#16715 MERGED 2026-11-20T08:36:47Z as a886595e128e (earlier the same day: OPEN, not draft, mergeable MERGEABLE, merge state CLEAN, updated 2026-11-20T07:24:09Z), branch session/wise-otter-90-bmc-cap, title 'feat(ci): the network install produces its BMC credential through the one authority; the capability refusal names its observation' -- ready; wise-otter-90 is idle. Correction to the hand-down: the brief described it as 'the arrival leg', and the live PR is the install's BMC credential through the one authority; the arrival leg is the second half of this row and has no PR yet, which is why it is stated here rather than linked. The credential half of this row is landed; what remains -- the CI arrival leg -- waits on the operator's environment approval, not on review.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "site-boot-and-management-edge", contribution: "The install's credential and the host's arrival, both through the authorities that own them."),
      centering: plan(text: "new_server_bringup_plan: srv15's arrival is a modeled CI leg with a credential from the one authority, so the install path is reproducible. Target: dag/gunbc/host/network_install.dag and the arrival workflow it feeds."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_8VQD2KJ7TY5Z3N6XWHMR9C4BPF",
      id: "bobo-live-hpm-check-and-evidence",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/host/boot_medium.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The live hpm check on bobo, and the evidence PR that records it",
        displaced_cost: "A firmware check that has never been read live cannot tell an install-ready host from a host whose BMC will drop the mount mid-install -- and without the evidence PR, the next reader has no way to tell whether the check was ever done.",
        boundary: "Run the modeled hpm firmware check against bobo once, read the result, and open the evidence PR that records the reading with its provenance. The reading is data; the PR is its receipt.",
        first_slice: "One live hpm read against bobo, its result compared with the modeled expectation, and the evidence PR carrying the reading, the time and the reader.",
        red_control: "A claimed hpm standing with no live reading behind it refuses, and the same claim passes once the reading is recorded and quoted.",
        out_of_scope: "Acting on the reading: firmware updates, resets, or any repair are operator actions on the floor; a second host.",
        handback: "A live firmware reading for bobo, quoted in its evidence PR, that the install dispatch can gate on."
      ), on: "2026-11-20", note: "Ordered after the credential and arrival-leg row: the check is only meaningful once the host is arriving through the modeled chain and the reading has somewhere to be recorded."), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Narrowed by keen-dove-217 after review of gunbc#16983: this reading's consumer is the arrival door's firmware-qualification leg (gunbc#16787, through gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_firmware_hpm_read), which the install admits only after; no install decision reads it directly, and it alone does not let the install drive srv15. srv15's committed manager capture is OpenBMC 3.22.00 (artifacts/bmc/srv15-inband-recovery-2026-10-29/redfish_v1_Managers_bmc.json), and the install's capability lookup (gunbc.host.network_install_ci network_install_ci_capability_row) reads MegaRAC evidence only. The admitted boot-and-power route for this release is its own prerequisite of the dispatch, bobo-openbmc-boot-power-route-admitted.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "site-boot-and-management-edge", contribution: "The firmware truth about the host that is about to be installed, read once and recorded once."),
      centering: plan(text: "new_server_bringup_plan: an install is dispatched against evidence, not expectation. Target: dag/gunbc/host/boot_medium.dag and the hpm firmware-check standing it feeds."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_6MZT4XQK9RV2J7YDHNC8WB3FP5",
      id: "bobo-pxe-install-dispatch",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/host/network_install.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Dispatch bobo's one-shot network install over the PXE edge",
        displaced_cost: "The whole point of the lane: until a host is actually installed over the edge, srv4 is a boot edge only in the model, and every later lane (the runner join, the census reading of the edge) waits on a host that does not exist.",
        boundary: "Dispatch the modeled one-shot network install for bobo against the converged edge, then keep the install's receipt. The dispatch is the repository's act; the boot itself is the host's.",
        first_slice: "One dispatch of the modeled network install for bobo against the converged edge, its install receipt recorded and quoted back to this row.",
        red_control: "A dispatch whose target is neither the unit's designated medium nor an unformatted disk, or that lacks the edge's converged standing or the operator's GO, refuses; the same dispatch passes with all three present.",
        out_of_scope: "What the host does after first boot -- the tag:ci join and the first live build belong to their own sessions' rows; a second host's install; the edge's own Apply (its own operator gate row).",
        handback: "bobo installed over the edge with a receipt, and the edge itself demonstrated by a real install rather than asserted."
      ), on: "2026-11-20", note: "Every prerequisite is a row. The one that gates hardest is the operator's boot GO: a boot attempt is the operator's call, and the standing precedent is at dag/gunbc/auth/privileged_effect_registry.dag:553, where exactly one cold reset of mtcollins1's controller was approved and a second needs a new operator go -- so this row waits on operator-boot-or-reset-go and is not dispatched past it."), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Prerequisite edge to bmc-nfs-share-server-through-endpoint-authority removed by keen-dove-217 after review of gunbc#16983: that row resolves the MegaRAC virtual-media NFS share's server, which the PXE install path does not consume. Red control restated by keen-dove-217 under gunbc.design_ruling::install_target_is_designated_or_unformatted_2026_11_24: the pre-install target-disk identity is no longer a requirement of the dispatch; the target is the designated medium or an unformatted disk, chosen and checked inside the run. That change is owned by install-target-designated-or-unformatted, now a prerequisite of this row.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "site-boot-and-management-edge", contribution: "The install itself: the first host brought up over the modeled boot edge."),
      centering: plan(text: "new_server_bringup_plan: srv4 becomes the site's boot edge by installing something, and bobo (srv15) is the host it installs. Target: dag/gunbc/host/network_install.dag and the one-shot install dispatch it models."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_4YHB7NQM2KZ9X5VT6RJW8DC3FP",
      id: "bobo-first-boot-handoff-to-remote-build",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/compute/remote_build.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "The boundary at bobo's first boot: from there the host is remote-build's, not this lane's",
        displaced_cost: "Without a stated boundary two lanes both think they own the host: the install lane keeps reaching past first boot, and the runner lane waits for someone else to say the host is ready to join.",
        boundary: "Record the handoff, and nothing of the handoff's content. From first boot, bobo belongs to quick-lynx-508 under clever-raven-401's remote-build root, on the operator's default-approved split of 2026-11-19: the tag:ci join, the host key, the MemTotal row, the roster row and one live build. Those rows are theirs; this one is the edge where this lane stops and reaches into their work.",
        first_slice: "State the handoff on this row and link it by edge to the remote-build CI bridge the join lands in; say in the handback who owns what, by name.",
        red_control: "A first-boot claim in this lane that also claims a runner-roster or tag:ci fact is refused -- the same fact may not be owned from both sides of the boundary.",
        out_of_scope: "The tag:ci join, the host-key enrollment, the MemTotal row, the roster row and the first live build: all authored by quick-lynx-508 and clever-raven-401, never here.",
        handback: "One sentence a reader can trust: bobo is installed at first boot, and everything after that is the remote-build lane's."
      ), on: "2026-11-20", note: "The brief's instruction is explicit that this is a boundary row and not the join itself; it exists so the join has an edge to hang from without this lane authoring another session's work. The edge it draws points at the existing row remote-build-ci-bridge, which the operator's 2026-11-19 ruling admitted (landed by gunbc#16748, MERGED 2026-11-20T00:57:17Z).")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "site-boot-and-management-edge", contribution: "The lane's stopping line: the install path ends at first boot and hands the host to the remote-build lane."),
      centering: plan(text: "new_server_bringup_plan: the install path is bounded at first boot; the runner join is another lane's work on the operator's default-approved split. Target: dag/gunbc/compute/remote_build.dag, where the join lands."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7CJQ5ZKX2WN84TRHDY6MBV9FP3",
      id: "butch-executor-route-under-the-ci-ruling",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/runner/runner_host_deploy.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "butch (srv14) is the executor route only, at runner width zero, under the 2026-11-19 CI ruling",
        displaced_cost: "Read the old way, butch looks like a runner host that is merely slow to join, and the next reader spends the day chasing a width the ruling set to zero on purpose -- and the fleet charges itself for capacity that was never granted.",
        boundary: "Model what the operator's 2026-11-19 ruling (gunbc.design_ruling::hosted_ci_bridges_to_remote_builds_and_adopts_work_execution_redesign, dag/gunbc/design_ruling.dag:40, landed by gunbc#16748) narrowed gunbc#16655 to: the executor route only, runner width 0. The tailnet anchor stands; the runner capacity does not.",
        first_slice: "Land gunbc#16655 in its narrowed form: srv14's tailnet anchor, a first-contact hop admitted by exactly two modes, and the witness that says so.",
        red_control: "Any srv14 row that claims runner capacity above zero refuses while the ruling stands, and a planted executor-route claim passes.",
        out_of_scope: "Retiring mtcollins1 from its runner role, which is mtcollins1-boot-duty-retirement's own work; and ken's strata trim, which is not bobo's and landed as gunbc#16763, recorded on ken-strata-56g-reread-dissolves-build-seat-frontier; and the per-host trust policy, which is the operator's decision-gate row, not this one.",
        handback: "A srv14 that is honestly executor-only in the model, so nobody charges the fleet for capacity the ruling refused to grant."
      ), on: "2026-11-20", note: "Live read 2026-11-20: gunbc#16655 OPEN, not draft, mergeable MERGEABLE, merge state BLOCKED with its required checks pending after a push at 2026-11-20T09:20:51Z (earlier reads the same day: merge state CLEAN, updated 06:06:12Z), branch session/tidy-swift-586-tailnet-anchor, title 'B3b model: tailnet anchor for srv14; a first-contact hop admitted by exactly two modes'. What the model holds today: srv14 is the already-installed CI-only host at dag/gunbc/runner/runner_host_deploy.dag:341, and srv14_runner_host_spec refuses until its LAN address is modeled; no srv14 runner-width row exists anywhere under dag/gunbc/runner/, which is exactly the legibility this row buys. Correction to the hand-down: butch's ed25519 host key is already enrolled as a LAN endpoint host key at dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_host_key_enrollment.dag (landed by gunbc#16276, MERGED 2026-11-11T00:07:47Z, title 'enroll srv14/butch's ed25519 host key: scan-proven, first contact 2026-11-10'); what is owed is the tailnet anchor, which is this row's own subject.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "site-boot-and-management-edge", contribution: "The management half of the edge: what a host may do here is modeled, and a ruling that caps a host is legible from the model."),
      centering: plan(text: "new_server_bringup_plan: capacity decisions are recorded as model state, so a ruling that sets a host to executor-only is enforceable rather than folklore. Target: dag/gunbc/runner/runner_host_deploy.dag, where srv14's spec and its absence are already decided."),
