      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Parse formation refuses: a dropped separator cannot silently change the program",
        boundary: "Two slices, one wall. Safety: a missing list separator refuses at parse instead of parsing as element juxtaposition (the measured below-floor census row — a dropped comma silently changes list arity). Completeness: a block after a bare identifier in if-condition position parses as the block it is, closing the measured false refusal (expected-RParen on legitimate input). Probe-paired via the corpus's parser pair; grammar-owned, no host parser (census queue items 6-7).",
        displaced_cost: "The separator specimen survived regen, whole-corpus compile, fixed-point verify, and a 15-case matrix; only a human diff read caught it (review 45347).",
        first_slice: "The separator refusal with legitimate-list controls green.",
        red_control: "RED IS OBTAINED BY EXECUTION, NOT BY READING. WITNESS MODULE AND LEGS BY NAME: the legs are test fns in dag/test/claim/guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness.dag, declared module test.claim.guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness, cited as test.claim.guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness::<fn>; the probe rows they read are data in gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus, cited as gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus::floor_parse_list_separator_control_probe, ::floor_parse_list_separator_green_probe and ::floor_parse_list_separator_hole_probe under class gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus::floor_parse_list_separator_class, path v1_compile_rust_path_id. Name the module and the symbol, never a line number: `module.path::decl` per gunbc.design_argument::single_authority. THE PAIR THAT DECIDES THE NODE, each appearing BY NAME with its own verdict line in one log and its command's own exit status on its own line: test.claim.guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness::floor_parse_list_separator_doubled_separator_control_refuses, the wrong case refused with exactly 1 blocking ParseError row, and test.claim.guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness::floor_parse_list_separator_green_control_is_clean, the correct case accepted with 0 rows total. RUN EVERY LEG ON THE CLAIM ROUTE, not through the deleted claim_batch verb: invoked as `gunbc test //test/claim/guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness:<fn>` with each label its own operand and roots --source-root dag --source-root src/v2, one stage per heavy-slot acquisition on srv1, and the verdict vocabulary is HELD outcome=Pass, DID NOT HOLD and UNOBSERVED outcome=..., never PASS or FAIL. INSTRUMENT CHECK FIRST: grep -ac of the wall's diagnostic name on the binary you are about to run must read 0 before any leg runs on it, and the binary must be main's own with its sha256 read from disk in the log, never a binary built from the PR lineage. THREE OF THE NAMED LEGS ARE ADDED OR INVERTED BY THIS CHANGE, so they do not exist in their final form at red_at on main: obtain the red by overlaying the witness file's exact committed bytes onto a main tree without the wall, printing the overlaid file's sha256 on its own line beside the sha256 of git show <head>:dag/test/claim/guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness.dag, so red and green are PROVEN to have run identical witness content rather than asserted to. red_at: the main sha whose build lacks the separator refusal, where the deciding leg reports DID NOT HOLD naming the omission case; green_at: red_at or later, with every named leg reporting HELD outcome=Pass and zero UNOBSERVED. TWO LEGS IN THAT FILE ARE RUNG-DROPS AND MUST FLIP WITH THE WALL RATHER THAN BE DELETED SILENTLY: test.claim.guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness::floor_parse_list_separator_omission_is_still_silent asserts 0 ParseError rows on the omitted-separator source, and test.claim.guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness::floor_hole_receipt_records_acceptance_as_the_observation asserts observation_is_clean on that same source; both pass only while the compiler is wrong, so the change landing the refusal inverts them (the omission refused naming the missing separator, the refused count 1), and the recurring_failure_mode row carrying the hole is the record until then. The if-block fixture parses correctly and every legitimate list in the corpus still parses, so the refusal cannot be bought by widening the grammar. IF THE WALL IS ALREADY ON MAIN: report the row as already landed and obtain the observed red by breaking the invariant off current main with the RedProbe variant of gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_status::RedObservation, red_at's first parent being a main sha, pushing probe_ref red-control/floor-parse-formation-wall and never merging it.",
        out_of_scope: "Grammar redesign; lookahead classes the census does not name.",
        handback: "The two closed defects, probe flips, corpus parse receipt."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Name which parser this wall is measured on (v1 or v2; #12773 open)."), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: parser subject undecided."), on: "2026-11-24", note: "Centered on the v2 parser by measurement, not assertion. The observing instrument is #v2.compiler.parse_acceptance_census::parse_acceptance_of_text, declared at src/v2/compiler/parse_acceptance_census.dag:52, called by the probe witness shipped in gunbc#16878 at src/v2/test/claim/parse/sibling_comma_gap_probe.dag -- that witness is not on main until gunbc#16878 merges, so it is cited by file path rather than as a checked symbol. The parser binary was built at main 4cb919e4a1094b400179f749cce83b4e6a2a6a62, a main tree and never the wall of its own lineage. Both alternatives are rejected as measured blind: a claim --entry sweep parses entry closures rather than function bodies, so an undemanded new body contributes zero error lines and a parse wall cannot surface; and the stage0 seed Rust parser is grammar-inert, so no grammar edit can move it. The 2026-09-30 note citing gunbc#12773 as open is answered: gunbc#12773 is MERGED, titled v2 parse: layout derived from the stream source with RefuseOnMatch and AfterLineBreak grammar arms, so the grammar arms this wall needs live in v2. Locus is the bracketed list literal production #v2.extdeps.languages.dag::dag_grammar_comma_list_expr at src/v2/extdeps/languages/dag.dag:953; bare non-bracketed juxtaposition is the adjacent concern owned by residue-field-consequence-adoption, not this wall. The two 2026-09-30 notes above stand as written history. 2026-11-25 CRITERIA FIX BY THE LANE MANAGER, authorised by neat-badger-614 (msg_15194358): red_control REWRITTEN, so node_criteria_digest MOVES for this row; this is a criteria change, not a progress note. The text it replaces named NO executable witness - it read: The separator probe flips exactly when the refusal lands; the if-block fixture parses correctly; every legitimate list in corpus still parses - and the only probe path it cited, sibling_comma_gap_probe.dag under src/v2/test/claim/parse/, does not exist: 0 files repo-wide at origin/main 0d399a799b64, its only hit anywhere in the repo being this file. Measured with hit counts: git grep -n floor_parse_list_separator over dag/gunbc/guarantee_probe_corpus.dag = 11 hits at :185 :197 :257 :258 :259 :670 :671 :676 :677 :682 :683; dag/test/claim/guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness.dag exists at 21340 bytes carrying the legs named above. dispatch REMOVED (NotDispatchable, the convention of the 183 rows that omit the field): ladder-probe-corpus and floor-generic-field-constraint-wall both edit that witness file, so the three land in dependency order, never in parallel. ALSO 2026-11-25 (b) RE-CENTRED ON THE v1 PARSER BY MEASUREMENT, per neat-badger-614 (msg_0bdc00e2), after the row's 2026-11-24 note said the wall was centred on the v2 parser. The list-literal parser is in v1: src/v1/02_parse.dag:5762 dispatches Present { value: ShLBracket } => parse_list_literal(tokens: tokens, ctx: ctx), defined at :6841. The corpus carries exactly two route ids, guarantee_probe_corpus.dag:138 v1_compile_rust_path_id and :139 v2_infer_eval_path_id, and inside fn guarantee_probe_rows() the 39 rows split 37 / 2 across them, so no probe row exists on any v2 PARSE route: a wall landed in the v2 parser today could not be observed by any probe. The 2026-11-24 note came from the OBSERVING instrument (src/v2/compiler/parse_acceptance_census.dag, parse_acceptance_of_text at :52) and conflated which compiler reads a file with which compiler must refuse it. The v2 route's own enrolment is its own row (rn_7C9829041BF4909E8AFD14A3C6), so this row stays on v1: the refusal lands in parse_list_literal, measured by the v1-path probes named in red_control. The if-block half already has a carrier on main: dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/a_labeled_call_opening_an_if_branch_after_an_uppercase_value_is_parse_failed.dag, named here so a worker extends that row instead of minting a second home for the same defect.")),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A dropped separator cannot change the program."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7C9829041BF4909E8AFD14A3C6",
      id: "v2-parse-path-carries-no-probes-so-its-parse-walls-cannot-be-observed",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/guarantee_probe_corpus.dag"), carrier(path: "dag/test/claim/guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness.dag")),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The v2 parse route carries no probe rows, so a parse wall there could be claimed with nothing able to observe it",
        boundary: "MEASURED AT MAIN b6d515a6d4c by the lane manager, counts printed. v2 parses .dag source: src/v2/compiler/source_authority.dag:551 parse_dag_source_ast(source: Medium<String>) -> Outcome<DagSourceAst> delegates at :533 to tokenize(text: source.carried, file: compilation_unit, rules: lm.lex) then parse(tokens: token_stream, grammar: lm.grammar), with the grammar from src/v2/extdeps/languages/dag.dag:4542 dag_language_model(). The guarantee probe corpus knows two routes only: dag/gunbc/guarantee_probe_corpus.dag:138 data v1_compile_rust_path_id = \"v1-compile-rust\" and :139 data v2_infer_eval_path_id = \"v2-infer-eval\"; git grep for v2_parse, parse_path_id or v2_compile over that file returns 0 hits. Inside fn guarantee_probe_rows() there are 39 GuaranteeProbeRow rows, 37 with path: v1_compile_rust_path_id and 2 with path: v2_infer_eval_path_id, so ZERO rows run the route that actually parses .dag in v2. Expectations across those 39: 23 ExpectBlockingRefusal, 13 ExpectZeroDiagnostics, 2 ExpectSilentAcceptanceHole, 1 ExpectAcceptedCounted. Consequence, stated as the defect: every parse-class guarantee this corpus can express is a claim about the v1 parser. The v2 parse front door can accept juxtaposed list elements, accept a block where a paren is missing, or refuse a legitimate program, and no probe in the corpus can see it -- while the v2 parser is the one the successor compiler will ship. Naming the route is the whole node: without a path id there is no row, without a row there is no probe, and without a probe there is no red control, so any future claim that the v2 parser has a parse wall is unfalsifiable by construction (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed, and the leg rule that a check which cannot fail is not a check).",
        displaced_cost: "The v2 parser inherits every parse defect the v1 parser has already been measured with -- the omitted list separator that silently changes arity, the block-after-identifier false refusal -- and arrives at the shipping line with none of the instrumentation that caught them. The gap-analysis record says the separator specimen survived regen, whole-corpus compile, fixed-point verify and a 15-case matrix, and only a human diff read caught it (review 45347). That is what an unobservable parser costs, paid by the next reviewer.",
        first_slice: "Enrol one GuaranteePathId for the v2 parse route beside the two at :138-139, and the separator trio on it -- control, green, hole -- as one new class, with the same expectation grammar the v1 trio uses, so the route exists as data before anyone claims a wall on it.",
        red_control: "RedProbe (roadmap_status.dag:78) on a census claim in dag/test/claim/guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness.dag over fn guarantee_probe_rows(), asserting that every parse-named guarantee class holds a row whose path is a route that parses source. red_at: current main, where it FAILS naming floor_parse_list_separator_class -- measured, not implied: 39 rows, 37 on v1_compile_rust_path_id, 2 on v2_infer_eval_path_id, 0 on any parse route, and only two GuaranteePathIds exist. green_at: the commit enrolling the v2 parse path id and the trio on it. The batch must print rows= pass= fail= with its own exit status on its own line, name the failing class in the red run, and in the green run name the discriminating pair BY NAME: the omitted separator refused and the correct separator accepted, from the same run, so the new path is shown able to go both ways rather than green by vacuity.",
        out_of_scope: "NOT the v1 separator refusal, which belongs to floor-parse-formation-wall; NOT making the v2 parser authoritative for anything, which is a program decision and not this row; NOT the v2 infer/eval route, which already has 2 rows and is a different question; NOT the dark-suite disposition row, which covers a different axis of the same corpus.",
        handback: "The new path id and three probe rows as data, the census claim PASS log naming the class that used to fail, and the discriminating pair named in one PASS log with the batch exit status."
      )),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A parse wall on a route no probe can reach is unfalsifiable, so the route is enrolled before any wall is claimed."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
