      id: "floor-record-construction-wall",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Record construction refuses: missing required fields, bad defaults, ungrounded nominal literals",
        boundary: "A record literal missing a required field refuses at compile with the field named; defaults apply only where declared; a literal claiming a nominal type it does not ground refuses. Owns the census's record-completeness class — the declared-conformance chain owns return, data, and generic instantiation, not this. Probe-paired via the corpus's record-completeness pair. Motivating specimen: HandAuthoredDocBind's primary_work construction wall currently rests on record-completeness enforcement that is itself unmeasured.",
        displaced_cost: "A construction wall anywhere in the corpus is only as strong as required-field enforcement; this node is what makes primary_work-style walls load-bearing rather than declared.",
        first_slice: "Missing-required-field refusal, probe-paired.",
        red_control: "RED IS OBTAINED BY EXECUTION, NOT BY READING. WITNESS, MODULE AND LEGS BY NAME: dag/test/claim/anonymous_record_literal_roster_witness.dag legs an_anonymous_list_element_refuses_a_missing_field_test and an_anonymous_data_initializer_refuses_a_missing_field_test (the refused case) paired with an_anonymous_list_element_with_the_full_roster_compiles_test and an_anonymous_data_initializer_with_the_full_roster_compiles_test (the accepted case); the nominal-grounding half is dag/test/claim/record_literal_names_a_union_type_witness.dag legs a_record_literal_naming_a_union_refuses_at_a_data_binding, a_record_literal_naming_a_union_refuses_at_a_return, a_record_literal_naming_a_union_refuses_at_a_list_element, a_record_literal_naming_a_union_refuses_at_a_call_argument and a_record_literal_naming_an_alias_of_a_union_refuses, paired with the_fielded_arm_is_accepted, the_empty_arm_is_accepted and a_record_and_an_alias_of_a_record_are_accepted. RED: those refusal legs DID NOT HOLD, with their failure text recorded verbatim, when run on the CLAIM ROUTE by main's released gunbc -- sha256 read from disk in the log, never a binary built from the PR lineage -- at the main sha printed in the same log, through HEAVY_OWNER with one acquisition per stage, invoked as gunbc test //test/claim/<module>:<fn> with each label its own operand and roots --source-root dag --source-root src/v2; the verdict vocabulary is HELD outcome=Pass, DID NOT HOLD and UNOBSERVED outcome=..., never PASS or FAIL, and a required witness counts only if it appears BY NAME in the log with its command's own exit status on its own line. GREEN: the same leg names HELD outcome=Pass on the branch binary at the final head, every HELD line naming its leg and every real exit status on its own line. NAMED NEGATIVES IN THE SAME RUN, so a green cannot come from an arm that stopped judging: an_unknown_name_keeps_its_own_refusal and the_constructor_question_is_asked_before_the_fields must keep refusing. THE DECLARED-DEFAULTS HALF OF THE BOUNDARY HAS NO WITNESS AT MAIN -- whoever takes this row states that and adds the leg, rather than reading the silence as coverage. IF THE BEHAVIOUR IS ALREADY ON MAIN: report the row as already landed and obtain the observed red by breaking the invariant off current main with the RedProbe variant of gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_status::RedObservation, red_at first parent being a main sha, pushing probe_ref red-control/floor-record-construction-wall and never merging it. A control never observed red on any tree is not a control.",
        out_of_scope: "Row polymorphism; invocation default semantics (call-shape owns those).",
        handback: "The judgment site, probe flip, corpus receipt."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "The v2 twin landed in #12763."), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: v1 half scoping.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
