    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_READSETCONVPROG00000000000",
      id: "read-set-convergence",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/plans/read_set_convergence.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
        headline: "Regenerate exactly what is needed from exactly what changed (the read-set convergence program)",
        boundary: "One read-set validation authority, consumed through the existing convergence modality (gunbc.ensure ensure_decide), replaces every bespoke affected-set check: each generated product (a stage0 mirror, a seed-build artifact, a parse verdict, a required-job verdict) stays valid while nothing its generator read has changed and the generator is unchanged, and is otherwise regenerated alone. Heal's forced recheck (the emission-scope base mirror) is the remaining whole-pool cost this program owns down to the change. The authority lives in the plan gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence; this node is the roadmap lane for its executable work (gunbc.design_argument::planning_has_one_home).",
        approach: "Phase by phase (the plan's P0..P7), switch one production consumer onto the one authority and delete what it displaces; heal's remaining whole-pool cost is P7.",
        red_control: "A generated product that is regenerated when nothing it read changed, or kept stale when something it read changed, keeps this red. A fourth bespoke affected-set check outside the one authority keeps this red.",
        displaced_cost: "Heal regenerates the whole population on every same-repository pull request touching dag/**, src/v1/** or src/v2/** -- paid even for a plan-only change, because the round does no change selection and its scope reads WholePopulation. Counts (172 stage0 mirrors, 13 seed-build artifacts) are the lineage census of the plan gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence; the median 65-minute figure is the heal-generated-artifacts job wall time on the PR's own CI, e.g. run 44454974358 (03:57:47Z->05:02:58Z = 65m11s) and run 44424789306 (23:55:24Z->00:58:52Z = 63m28s).",
        handback: "Every affected-set mechanism consolidated onto the one authority or deleted, and heal's forced recheck bounded by the pull request's own diff (P7)."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "gunbc-project-root", contribution: "Converging the read set -- regenerating exactly what changed and nothing more -- is what makes the self-host round (heal) and every generated product cheap enough to run on every pull request (the plan gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence)."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_HEALFORKSEEDP7000000000000",
      id: "heal-forced-recheck-seeds-from-the-fork-point",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "heal's forced recheck seeds the base mirror from the merge-base, not main's tip (P7: heal's remaining whole-pool cost)",
        boundary: "heal's emission-scope step force-rechecks the diff between the PR head and HEAL_BASE_MIRROR_COMMIT, which the generated workflow sets to the pull request's base.sha. base.sha is main's TIP at event time, so on a branch forked days earlier the recheck is the whole distance main travelled, not the PR's change (measured on PR #16548 head 3a917e44 against main tip 5776d05cba: 156 files whole-repo / 95 in the stage0+corpus subset versus 13 across the merge-base -- the PR's own diff -- and a 22.6 GB climb that stalled 2,258 s at memory.high and was refused, run 43781205899, job 133018576398). This row's change: resolve the seed to git merge-base base.sha HEAD -- the fork point -- in ONE authority (required_regen_host::fork_point_of_base), consumed by resolve_base_mirror_authority (which reads the population and names the receipt's base_mirror_authority) and by scoped_round_base_admission (which must judge the protocol floor at the fork point it actually builds, never building a scope-blind seed). heal.yml stays unchanged: a workflow expression cannot run git merge-base, and the generator already documents the fork point as the scoped path's base, so the change belongs in the seed host that already resolves commit -> population. workflow_dispatch is covered by the same code; the checkout is fetch-depth: 0 so the fork point is always computable.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it heal's round-1 cost scales with branch staleness instead of the PR's size: a stale branch climbs past memory.high and the round that converges the seed's mirrors is refused (run 43781205899: 22.6 GB, 2,258 s at memory.high, refused), while the WholePopulation scope label hides the staleness in every round.",
        first_slice: "Pending, open in the implementation PR (#16753): resolve_base_mirror_authority seeds the population and the receipt at the fork point, and the round logs seed_commit, seed_size and seeded_from_base_sha so staleness is visible. Not done until #16753 merges and an accepted item event is recorded for this row.",
        red_control: "The change adds (in #16753) two hermetic one-function-per-process controls: cli_run::required_regen_host::regen_affected_set_tests::the_forced_recheck_seeds_from_the_fork_point_when_the_head_is_behind_main (a head behind main yields the merge-base, and the seed diff equals the branch's own change) and ::the_protocol_floor_is_judged_at_the_fork_point_a_stale_fork_point_refuses (its first assert shows a base-judged gate would admit the scope-blind base).",
        out_of_scope: "No new job, no time or memory budget change, no move onto the merge ref (heal publishes onto the head, so it still builds the head's tree); no commit-keyed mirror cache.",
        handback: "When #16753 lands: the change, its two hermetic controls with their PASS lines, the regenerated heal.yml matching its generator, and the heal round's seed-size/base line on the PR's own CI."
      ), on: "2026-11-19", note: "Pending: the change and its tests are open in the implementation PR #16753 (fix(heal): seed the forced recheck from the merge-base); not done until that merges and an accepted event is recorded. Operator approved the direction 2026-11-19.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "read-set-convergence", contribution: "P7: heal's forced recheck is bounded by the pull request's own diff, not the branch's distance from main's tip (the plan gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence)."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_CREDRECVRECEIPTHOME0000000001",
      id: "credential-recovery-receipt-under-declared-instance-dir",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_belt_tick_cli.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "belt credential-recovery receipt relocated under the declared instance receipts directory",
        boundary: "Serves gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_tick_cli belt_credential_recovery_cli. The receipt path was derived from instance_root + '/credential-acquisition-recovery.json', targeting the top level of the instance root directory which is root:root 0755 — briansrls cannot create files there. The fix introduces belt_credential_recovery_receipt_path, deriving the receipt path through instance_receipts_dir (the declared, install-owned briansrls-writable directory already created by apply_legs step instance-receipts-dir and used by the tick and obligation receipts), so the credential-recovery receipt is durable without any hand host operation and without touching /opt/gunbc's top-level ownership.",
        displaced_cost: "Without it the credential-recovery unit exits 1 on every run; the journal carries 'receipt write failed' and the recovery result — however correct — is never persisted durably for the operator.",
        first_slice: "One path derivation (belt_credential_recovery_receipt_path) in the CLI's module, and ONE claim witness over it, test.claim.belt_credential_recovery_receipt_home_witness (four test fn's: path under instance_receipts_dir; pinned bytes /opt/gunbc/receipts/credential-acquisition-recovery.json; named negatives: not homed in credential-acquisition-slots, no '..' traversal). The witness imports belt_credential_recovery_receipt_path from production, so it is the discriminating control (see red_control). The pre-fix top-level value is recorded on this row as labelled historical EVIDENCE, not as a second witness — there is no old-path witness module in the tree.",
        red_control: "Discriminating pair over the receipt path. DISCRIMINATOR = test.claim.belt_credential_recovery_receipt_home_witness, which imports belt_credential_recovery_receipt_path from gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_tick_cli (the production derivation) and instance_receipts_dir from gunbc.host.host_layout. GREEN at green_at (this row's head, and the closing commit at recording): four claims, rc 0 — the path is under instance_receipts_dir; equals /opt/gunbc/receipts/credential-acquisition-recovery.json; is not homed in credential-acquisition-slots; contains no '..' traversal. Executed mutation RED (never pushed): in a scratch worktree at the head, belt_credential_recovery_receipt_path's body is changed ONLY back to the top-level join([instance_root, '/credential-acquisition-recovery.json'], ''); the same home witness then FAILS the two value claims the_receipt_sits_in_the_instance_receipts_directory and the_receipt_path_is_the_expected_bytes, rc 1 — the control goes red when the behavior is wrong (fail_closed). Integration RED: run against red_at=56d460116d6252f6ec8dfe889ea358c804685861 the home witness cannot load because belt_credential_recovery_receipt_path does not exist — the import is refused, rc 1 — proving the control reads production. Labelled VALUE evidence for the pre-fix defect (not a discriminator): at red_at belt_credential_recovery_cli spelled the path inline as join([instance_root, '/credential-acquisition-recovery.json'], '') at roadmap_belt_tick_cli.dag:844, computing /opt/gunbc/credential-acquisition-recovery.json — the top of the root-owned instance root, NOT under instance_receipts_dir; the srv1 journal of gunbc-roadmap-belt-credential-recovery.service records 'belt_credential_recovery_cli: receipt write failed: /opt/gunbc/credential-acquisition-recovery.json' at status=1/FAILURE against /opt/gunbc root:root 0755, with the recovery itself succeeding (recovered: no credential slots).",
        out_of_scope: "No new apply leg; no directory mode change; no credential_acquisition_slots_directory relocation; no belt tick, drain or attempt launcher enablement; no touch to release_pair_delivery, release_locus, roadmap event/recorder, or fleet_converge_* planning sites.",
        handback: "Two halves. Model half: at the fix's head test.claim.belt_credential_recovery_receipt_home_witness passes four claims (rc 0); the executed mutation RED (belt_credential_recovery_receipt_path's body reverted to the top-level join in a scratch worktree, never pushed) turns its two value claims red (rc 1); and run against red_at 56d460116d6252f6ec8dfe889ea358c804685861 the witness's import of belt_credential_recovery_receipt_path is refused (rc 1); plus this roadmap row. Host half (lands ONLY after the deploy-route apply reaches the host under operator broker approval — the worker performs no host mutation): observed READ-ONLY on srv1 for the PRODUCTION unit gunbc-roadmap-belt-credential-recovery.service (instance_root=/opt/gunbc, User=briansrls), the receipt write succeeds at the declared path /opt/gunbc/receipts/credential-acquisition-recovery.json AND the unit reaches exit 0, both observed READ-ONLY after the apply; if the unit then fails for another reason the host half is not met and that is reported with the journal line rather than narrowing the row. The lab instance gunbc-srv1-lab-codex-feedback-v0-belt-credential-recovery.service (instance_root=/opt/gunbc-lab/codex-provider-feedback-v0) is a separate unit whose receipt already writes to a writable lab dir; any other failure there is out of scope for this row and not faked here."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "fabric-bringup", contribution: "The belt credential-recovery unit writes its receipt into the model-owned instance receipts directory, making the recovery result durable without a hand host operation."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_4PZ3K4FWAPEJLK22FS5C4VISAU",
      id: "citation-lens-unenforced-in-the-required-lane",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: concat(carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/declaration_index.rs"), carrier(path: "src/v1/stage0/src/bin/v1_src_dag_parse.rs")),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "The citation-integrity lens that reports 213 dangling authored references on main is wired to no required check",
        boundary: "Serves gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed and the required lane's promise that a dangling authored reference cannot reach main. THE POPULATION DISTINCTION IS THE WHOLE ROW, SO STATE IT FIRST: v2.cli.reference_check::check_references, the only reference check any merge-gate workflow runs, governs the hashtag marker spelling #module.path::decl found in annotations, extracted by std.annotation_reference::annotation_references; the lens that reports the 213 findings is declaration_index::corpus_findings (src/v1/stage0/src/declaration_index.rs:3078), which audits AUTHORED DeclarationRefs. The two populations are disjoint by construction, so a green check-references says nothing about the 213, and this row does not ask check-references to change. KNOWN EMITTER FRAGILITY, RECORDED AND NOT REQUIRED: the only check-references step in any workflow is the fast-lane step in the generated artifact .github/workflows/witnesses.yml (positions :747-752, carried beside the step name 'Check marked references with the restored native CLI (fast lane)'), and it is gated on the fast-lane skip output; its run line carries a second-binary '||' fallback that the condition makes dead. The full-run branch covers the same check in code invisible to the yml, in native_lane_runner::walk_reference_controls (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/native_lane_runner.rs:3524) with its check-references invocation beside it, and that split is pinned green by test.claim.compiler_gate_emit_build_lane_witness::the_closure_dependent_steps_run_unless_the_fast_lane_reused. None of that is a requirement of this row; the fast lane is NOT the gap. Cite, and edit NEITHER of, the two adjacent rows this one sits beside: rn_6WBAWKDJWDPYQ0C2D1746B8C9T (required-check-names-what-it-executed) and rn_8XBLW9DKZH5NCQ0RTVPMGJ4F2 (ci-executed-coverage-receipt). When the green lands, correct the ten stale prose carriers that still describe the lens as though a required phase ran it, each named by the declaration its annotation sits on: test.claim.printed_chassis_manufacturing_manifest_witness::a1_mini_catalog, test.claim.self_host_promotion_admission_witness::pa_provenance, test.claim.printed_chassis_manufacturing_manifest_livetree_witness::live_tree_disposition, test.claim.spark.engram_materialization_witness::repacked_encoding, product.printed_chassis.manufacturing_manifest::scan_printer_assets, std.machine_word::word_from_octets, gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.one_encoding_carries_a_module_body_and_a_spine_segment (its row), gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.merge_carries_prose_true_on_one_side_and_false_on_the_other (its row), gunbc.representation_boundary::RepresentationBoundary, and the frontier annotation on v2.compiler.reference_conservation_admission::ObservationFrontier.",
        displaced_cost: "A dangling authored reference -- a DeclarationRef naming a module or declaration no longer in the index -- reaches main and stays, because nothing that gates a merge reads the lens. Today that is 213 findings living on main while every required check on the same sha is green, so the number is invisible to review: the next reader has to know to run a development binary to learn what the tree actually says. One measured instance, named so it can be checked without running anything: `extdeps.apple.app_attest::attestation_verification_from_implementation` carries an admit_callers list in which two entries dangle while their sibling resolves. The lens reports `CITED-DECLARATION-ABSENT dag/extdeps/apple/app_attest.dag:204:5: extdeps.apple.app_attest cites test.claim.approval_device_redemption_witness fx_attestation, which that module does not declare` and the same at :205 for `witness_enrolment_refuses_a_refused_attestation`, while the adjacent entry naming `test.claim.approval_google_enrolment_witness::fx_attestation` does resolve because that one is declared. The device witness declares `fx_attestation_request` and `fx_attestation_failed` and no bare `fx_attestation`, and `witness_enrolment_refuses_a_refused_attestation` is declared in neither witness: one arm of an adjacent pair drifted and the other did not, and today every required check on that sha is green over both.",
        first_slice: "1. Name the lens and its single production caller in the PR description, with the counts: declaration_index::corpus_findings (src/v1/stage0/src/declaration_index.rs:3078) over declaration_index::cited_symbol_findings (:2893) and declaration_index::import_member_findings (:1960), reached from exactly one place -- the corpus_findings call inside main in src/v1/stage0/src/bin/v1_src_dag_parse.rs -- and tree-wide from no non-test, non-binary caller (print that count, not the absence of one). 2. Re-measure it on current main with the RELEASED binary (sha256 read from disk and matched to release-bins.manifest) and paste the raw per-kind counts. 3. Decide and record WHICH population the required lane governs, so the 213 are classified in-population or out-of-population in writing rather than by inference. 4. Choose the required route, one of two: either a required route calls corpus_findings and refuses above a recorded baseline, or a typed declared drop records the exemption with a bounded next-rung trigger naming the capability that would retire it. 5. Record the 213 as the baseline the chosen route carries, with the main sha it was measured at.",
        red_control: "OBSERVED RED, already executed on main at 89fc77e8733d32a2a6e789b490a7e4ce00fde12a with the released v1_src_dag_parse (sha256 841f3ae4774668e2ce642e9736859fede949f48b637e1a68c6348d72155d3cc1, disk equal to release-bins.manifest), srv1, heavy-slot acquired 07:03:22Z and 07:17:53Z: the binary exits 1 with 213 findings -- CITED-MODULE-ABSENT 60, CITED-DECLARATION-ABSENT 152, CITED-FIELD-ABSENT 1 -- over a population of 10643 files, 210257 declarations, 301023 import members and 11233 citations, while every required check on that sha is green. Deterministic: two runs produced byte-identical normalized stderr (sha da4565252d59df63 both, diff rc 0). NAMED NEGATIVE, fired in the same session: appending one parse fault to dag/test/claim/annotation_reference_witness.dag made it exit 1 with exactly one line naming that file ('152:35: expected expression, found Eof'), then the restore returned it to the 213-finding state. THE CONTROL'S OWN DOCUMENTED PLANT DOES NOT DISCRIMINATE AND MUST NOT BE REUSED: the header comment above main in src/v1/stage0/src/bin/v1_src_dag_parse.rs prescribes appending a trailing bare '//' line, and a '//' with text behaves identically -- both produced output byte-identical to clean, 214 lines, none naming the probe file, because comment trivia is invisible to this lens. Any plant must be a PARSE fault. red_at and green_at are recorded through the red-control evidence model, not by prose: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_status::RedControlEvidence, whose RedControlExecuted variant carries witness_module, witness_fn and executed_on, gated by gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_status::red_control_evidence_satisfied -- which is why a row naming a witness that was never run cannot be accepted. Break the invariant off current main so the red tree's first parent is a main sha, watch the chosen required route refuse, then show green at that base or later; the probe branch, carried as the probe_ref parameter of gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_cutover_cli::roadmap_cutover_acceptance_record_cli, is pushed to gunb-ai/gunbc as red-control/citation-lens-unenforced-in-the-required-lane and never merged. Corroborated at a second tree by another lane, as a second measurement rather than a restatement: 212 CITED-*-ABSENT sites, 184 of them spread over 80 files OUTSIDE the fleet-domain slice, the per-file list in PR 17084 body with the heaviest being test.claim.integration_concern_witness at 17, gunbc.serving_relocation at 9, test.claim.fleet_naming_witness at 8 and gunbc.integration_concern at 7, measured with the v1 parse binary sha256 278e4454 whose build inputs differ from main by zero lines. That agrees with the 213 above within the slice boundary: the difference is the slice, not the counter.",
        out_of_scope: "Does not repair the 213 findings. Does not change v2.cli.reference_check::check_references, the marker grammar, or the fast-lane decision. Does not touch declaration_index::PRE_EXISTING_CITATION_DEBT or declaration_index::FIXTURE_CARRIER_CITATION_EXEMPTIONS. Does not re-pin any released binary, does not add hand-written seed Rust, and does not re-open the fast-lane coverage question, which is pinned green elsewhere.",
        handback: "Two halves. MODEL half: at the fix's head, the witness module dag/test/claim/citation_lens_required_lane_witness.dag passes its discriminating pair -- the planted dangling authored reference REFUSED by the chosen required route, and the recorded 213-finding baseline ACCEPTED -- with the batch's own exit status pasted, and each claim by name in a PASS log. Keep only that pair: a census claim of the form 'no workflow invokes the binary' passes only while the defect exists and would go red the day the lane is fixed, so it belongs in the handback's printed evidence, not in the shipped witness. EXECUTED half: the raw per-kind counts at the main sha, the released binary's sha256 read from disk, the heavy-slot acquisition line, the deterministic repeat, the named parse-fault negative with its line, the counts for every search the ruling rests on, and the call site of the required route (named by module and symbol, or the declared drop that carries the exemption).",
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "factory", contribution: "The required lane's promises are kept by checks that actually run; a lens that only a development binary calls enforces nothing at merge."),
    ),
  ]
}

